el / strategy / window_bits / method / buffer_size, and png_set_text_compression_* equivalents. What branches exist (clamping, warnings, the \"window_bits==8 -> 9\" fix, PNG_WRITE_OPTIMIZE_CMF logic in png_deflate_claim / optimize_cmf). Also png_compress_IDAT / png_image_size and how flush interacts.\n\n5. png_write_transformations (pngwtran.c) and the shared pngtrans.c functions: the exact ORDER of transforms applied and the precise gating conditions (colour type / bit depth) for each of: user transform, packing, shift, swap (16-bit), packswap, invert_mono, bgr, swap_alpha, invert_alpha, filler. Which combinations are no-ops and which actually change data. png_do_write_transformations gating on row_info.\n\n6. png_set_filler / png_set_add_alpha on write: which branches, before/after values, and what colour types they are legal for.\n\n7. png_write_info_before_PLTE / png_write_info: the ORDER of chunks written and the exact `valid` flags gating each of gAMA, cHRM, sRGB, iCCP, sBIT, PLTE, tRNS, bKGD, hIST, pHYs, oFFs, sCAL, pCAL, tIME, tEXt/zTXt/iTXt, sPLT, eXIf, cICP, cLLI, mDCV, and unknown chunks at each PNG_HAVE_* location. Include which chunk writers have interesting internal branches (e.g. png_write_sBIT per colour type, png_write_tRNS per colour type, png_write_sCAL_s, png_write_pCAL with each equation type 0..3, png_write_iCCP compression, png_write_tEXt vs zTXt vs iTXt compression flags, png_write_cHRM_fixed, png_write_eXIf).\n\n8. png_write_png (pngwrite.c): each PNG_TRANSFORM_* flag it honours on write and the branch for each; PNG_TRANSFORM_INVERT_MONO, PACKING, PACKSWAP, SHIFT, BGR, SWAP_ALPHA, INVERT_ALPHA, SWAP_ENDIAN, STRIP_FILLER_BEFORE/AFTER. Which flags are ignored/error on write.\n\n9. png_write_row / png_write_rows / png_write_image: interlace handling (png_do_write_interlace and the 7 passes, the \"pass width 0 -> skip\" branches), the `png_ptr->row_number`/`pass` state machine, the sub-8-bit handling.\n\n10. png_write_flush / png_set_flush branc