handling in progressive mode: which passes call row_fn with what pass/row_num, and how png_read_push_finish_row works.\n7. png_set_progressive_read_fn + png_process_data_skip interaction; what the return value of png_process_data_pause means.\n8. Any state that differs based on chunk size vs buffer size (i.e. the axes: 1-byte feed, small feed, whole-buffer feed).\n\nPART D — SIMPLIFIED API:\n9. png_image_begin_read_from_memory / _from_file / _from_stdio / png_image_begin_read_from_stdio: branches, and what png_image_read_header sets (format deduction from colour type + bit depth: enumerate the exact mapping from PNG colour type/bit depth to the resulting image->format, including when PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_COLORMAP is set).\n10. png_image_finish_read: every branch. In particular:\n    - the `background` argument used vs NULL (and for which formats it matters — linear vs 8-bit, alpha present or not)\n    - positive vs negative row_stride handling\n    - colormap vs direct (buffer + colormap args)\n    - PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_* flags (PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_16BIT_sRGB, PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_COLORMAP_UNCHANGED / FAST if present) — enumerate the flags in png.h and their effect\n    - the internal png_image_read_direct vs png_image_read_colormap vs png_image_read_composite / png_image_read_background code paths and the conditions selecting each\n    - For png_image_read_colormap: enumerate every distinct case in its big switch (by input colour type/bit depth x output format), including the make_gray_colormap / make_ga_colormap / make_rgb_colormap helpers and the \"cmap_entries\" accounting.\n11. Enumerate every legal PNG_FORMAT_* value in png.h (gray, GA, AG, RGB, BGR, RGBA, ARGB, BGRA, ABGR, each LINEAR variant, each COLORMAP variant) and say which are distinct code paths in the simplified read and simplified write.\n12. png_image_write_to_memory / _to_file / _to_stdio / png_image_write_to_memory with memory==NULL size-query mode: branches; convert_to_8bit 0 vs 1; png_image_write_main's decisions (colormap input, linear input, alpha handling, the \"write 16-bit vs 8-bit\" branch, the PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_* handling); png_image_set_PLTE.\n13. png_image_free and error/longjmp handling (png_safe_execute).\n\nEnumerate rather than summarize. Long answer is fine.","uuid":"e970df9e-5901-4497-935a-b7be9d1c7a52","session_id":"e3091878-9949-4689-ad83-c0c41e6641a2"}
