{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_iyetzjbjgwjiibth67y4tylqomrhphbitgnaupyt5nobyg7qd6iq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything read. Below is the enumerated report. All line numbers refer to files under `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-kk7Dev/c_src/`.\n\n---\n\n# PART C — PROGRESSIVE READ (`src/pngpread.c`, 945 lines)\n\n## C.0 Mode constants (the complete set)\n\n`src/pngpread.c:17-25`:\n\n| constant | value | line | handler in `png_process_some_data` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `PNG_READ_SIG_MODE` | 0 | 18 | `png_push_read_sig` (`:115-119`) |\n| `PNG_READ_CHUNK_MODE` | 1 | 19 | `png_push_read_chunk` (`:121-125`) |\n| `PNG_READ_IDAT_MODE` | 2 | 20 | `png_push_read_IDAT` (`:127-131`) |\n| `PNG_READ_tEXt_MODE` | 4 | 21 | **dead**: falls into `default:` (`:133-137`) → `buffer_size = 0` |\n| `PNG_READ_zTXt_MODE` | 5 | 22 | **dead** → `default:` |\n| `PNG_READ_DONE_MODE` | 6 | 23 | `default:` → `buffer_size = 0` (all further data discarded) |\n| `PNG_READ_iTXt_MODE` | 7 | 24 | **dead** → `default:` |\n| `PNG_ERROR_MODE` | 8 | 25 | `default:`; **never assigned anywhere** |\n\nGrep-verified: the only assignments to `process_mode` in the whole tree are `:175` (→CHUNK), `:219` (→IDAT), `:254` (→DONE), `:272` (→IDAT), `:422` (→CHUNK). `tEXt/zTXt/iTXt/ERROR` modes are vestigial from libpng 1.0/1.2; text chunks are now handled synchronously inside `png_handle_chunk`. `process_mode` is `int` at `include/pngstruct.h:326`, zero-initialised (== SIG_MODE) by `png_create_read_struct`.\n\n## C.1 `png_set_progressive_read_fn` (`:922-935`) and the 3 callbacks\n\n- `:927-928` NULL-`png_ptr` guard, silent return.\n- `:930-932` unconditional stores: `png_ptr->info_fn = info_fn; row_fn; end_fn`. **No validation** — any or all may be NULL.\n- `:934` `png_set_read_fn(png_ptr, progressive_ptr, png_push_fill_buffer)` — this both stores `io_ptr = progressive_ptr` and installs `png_push_fill_buffer` as `read_data_fn`, which is what makes `png_read_chunk_header`/`png_crc_read`/`png_crc_finish` pull from the push buffers.\n- `png_get_progressive_ptr` (`:937-944`) just returns `png_ptr->io_ptr`.\n\nNULL-callback branches are in the three trampolines, each a single `!= NULL` test:\n- `png_push_have_info` (`:883-888`): `if (png_ptr->info_fn != NULL) (*info_fn)(png_ptr, info_ptr);`\n- `png_push_have_end` (`:890-895`): `if (end_fn != NULL) (*end_fn)(png_ptr, info_ptr);`\n- `png_push_have_row` (`:897-903`): `if (row_fn != NULL) (*row_fn)(png_ptr, row, png_ptr->row_number, (int)png_ptr->pass);`\n\nNote: `row_fn == NULL` does **not** skip the row-generation loops in `png_push_process_row`; the loops still run and `png_read_push_finish_row` still advances state.\n\n**Critical implicit contract**: `png_read_start_row` is only called from `png_read_update_info` (`src/pngread.c:180`) and `png_start_read_image` (`src/pngread.c:210`). Neither is called by pngpread.c. So `row_buf`/`prev_row` are only allocated if the app calls one of them from `info_fn`; otherwise `png_process_IDAT_data` sets `zstream.next_out = png_ptr->row_buf == NULL`.\n\n## C.2 The three entry points\n\n### `png_process_data` (`:49-62`)\n1. `:53-54` `if (png_ptr == NULL || info_ptr == NULL) return;` (silent).\n2. `:56` `png_push_restore_buffer(png_ptr, buffer, buffer_size)`.\n3. `:58-61` `while (png_ptr->buffer_size) png_process_some_data(png_ptr, info_ptr);`\n\nThe loop terminates only when `buffer_size` hits 0, which happens via: `png_push_fill_buffer` consuming (`:312`, `:327`), `png_push_read_IDAT` consuming (`:455`, `:481`), `png_push_save_buffer` (`:390` sets it to 0), or the `default:` arm at `:135`.\n\n### `png_process_data_pause` (`:64-89`)\n- `:67` NULL guard → returns 0.\n- `:72-73` `save != 0` → `png_push_save_buffer(png_ptr)`, returns **0** (libpng has taken a private copy of everything unconsumed; caller must not re-feed).\n- `:75-85` `save == 0` → `remaining = buffer_size; buffer_size = 0;` then `:83-84` `if (save_buffer_size < remaining) return remaining - save_buffer_size;` else fall to `:88 return 0`.\n- **Return value semantics**: number of bytes *of the caller's own current buffer* that were not consumed, i.e. how far the caller must rewind its stream before the next `png_process_data`. 0 means either \"everything consumed\" or \"everything left over was already in libpng's `save_buffer`, so re-feed nothing\". Note that when `save==0` the not-yet-consumed `save_buffer` contents are *retained* (only `buffer_size` is zeroed), so the pending saved bytes are re-counted on the next `png_push_restore_buffer` (`:399`).\n\n### `png_process_data_skip` (`:91-102`)\nFully stubbed. `png_app_warning(png_ptr, \"png_process_data_skip is not implemented in any current version of libpng\")` and `return 0`. The `TODO` at `:94-98` says the implementation was lost/abandoned. **No interaction whatsoever with `png_set_progressive_read_fn` or any state** (item 7): it reads nothing, writes nothing, and returns 0 always. `png_push_crc_skip` and `png_push_crc_finish` **do not exist** in this version (grep over `src` + `include` returns nothing); the CRC skipping is done by the shared `png_crc_finish`/`png_crc_finish_critical` in `src/pngrutil.c` (which loops over a `PNG_INFLATE_BUF_SIZE` stack buffer calling `png_crc_read` → `png_read_data` → `png_push_fill_buffer`).\n\n## C.3 `png_push_read_chunk` dispatch (`:180-288`)\n\nBuffer-guard macros (`:27-32`):\n- `PNG_PUSH_SAVE_BUFFER_IF_FULL`: `if (push_length + 4 > buffer_size) { png_push_save_buffer; return; }` — requires **whole chunk data + 4-byte CRC contiguously available**.\n- `PNG_PUSH_SAVE_BUFFER_IF_LT(N)`: `if (buffer_size < N) { png_push_save_buffer; return; }`.\n\nFlow:\n1. `:194-199` header phase: `if ((mode & PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER) == 0) { PNG_PUSH_SAVE_BUFFER_IF_LT(8); push_length = png_read_chunk_header(png_ptr); mode |= PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER; }`. `png_read_chunk_header` (`src/pngrutil.c:183-222`) reads 8 bytes via `png_read_data`, sets `chunk_name`, calls `png_reset_crc` + `png_calculate_crc(buf+4,4)`, and `png_chunk_error`s on `buf[0] >= 0x80` (\"bad header (invalid length)\") or bad type (`check_chunk_name`).\n2. `:203-230` **IDAT pre-pass** (runs before the dispatch below, for `chunk_name == png_IDAT`):\n   - `:205-206` if `PNG_AFTER_IDAT` → set `PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_AFTER_IDAT`.\n   - `:212-213` `png_error(\"Missing IHDR before IDAT\")`.\n   - `:215-217` `png_error(\"Missing PLTE before IDAT\")` for palette images.\n   - `:219` `process_mode = PNG_READ_IDAT_MODE`.\n   - `:221-224` **zero-length-IDAT special case**: `if (HAVE_IDAT && !HAVE_CHUNK_AFTER_IDAT && push_length == 0) return;` — early return *leaving `PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER` set*, so `png_push_read_IDAT` skips its own header read and (with `idat_size == 0`) goes straight to `:486-493` to consume the 4-byte CRC.\n   - `:226` set `PNG_HAVE_IDAT`; `:228-229` `png_benign_error(\"Too many IDATs found\")` if already `PNG_AFTER_IDAT`.\n3. `:232-238` non-IDAT chunk after IDAT → `mode |= PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_AFTER_IDAT | PNG_AFTER_IDAT`.\n4. Dispatch chain (order matters):\n   - `:240-247` `png_IHDR`: length must be exactly 13 else `png_error(\"Invalid IHDR length\")`; then `PNG_PUSH_SAVE_BUFFER_IF_FULL`, `png_handle_chunk(...)`.\n   - `:249-256` `png_IEND`: `PNG_PUSH_SAVE_BUFFER_IF_FULL`, `png_handle_chunk`, `process_mode = PNG_READ_DONE_MODE`, `png_push_have_end(png_ptr, info_ptr)`.\n   - `:258-267` `#ifdef PNG_HANDLE_AS_UNKNOWN_SUPPORTED`: `keep = png_chunk_unknown_handling(...) != 0` → `PNG_PUSH_SAVE_BUFFER_IF_FULL`, `png_handle_unknown(..., keep)`; `:264-265` if `png_PLTE` also `mode |= PNG_HAVE_PLTE`. **This branch precedes the IDAT branch**, so an app that marks IDAT as handled-as-unknown would divert it here.\n   - `:269-279` `png_IDAT` (the real IDAT entry): `idat_size = push_length`; `process_mode = PNG_READ_IDAT_MODE`; **`png_push_have_info(png_ptr, info_ptr)`** (this is where `info_fn` fires — exactly once, at the first IDAT); `zstream.avail_out = PNG_ROWBYTES(pixel_depth, iwidth) + 1`; `zstream.next_out = row_buf`; **`return`** — note this path does *not* clear `PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER` (deliberate: `png_push_read_IDAT` needs it set so it doesn't re-read the header).\n   - `:281-285` everything else: `PNG_PUSH_SAVE_BUFFER_IF_FULL`, `png_handle_chunk(png_ptr, info_ptr, push_length)`.\n5. `:287` `mode &= ~PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER;` (reached by IHDR/IEND/unknown/default paths only).\n\n**Inline vs `png_handle_*`**: only IDAT is truly inline (`:269-279`). IHDR, IEND and all other known chunks go through the single table-driven `png_handle_chunk` (`src/pngrutil.c:3106-3216`), which does position (`pos_before`/`pos_after`), duplicate, min-length and max-length (`NoCheck`/`Limit`/explicit) checks and then calls `read_chunks[chunk_index].handler`. Unknown/handled-as-unknown chunks go through `png_handle_unknown`. So unlike libpng 1.2/1.4 there is no per-chunk `png_handle_tEXt`/`png_handle_zTXt` switch in pngpread.c any more.\n\n### Buffer plumbing\n\n- `png_push_fill_buffer` (`:290-331`, `PNGCBAPI` — installed as `read_data_fn`, also called directly at `:158` and `:413`):\n  - `:295-296` NULL guard.\n  - `:299-315` first drain `save_buffer`: `save_size = min(length, save_buffer_size)`, `memcpy`, then decrement `length`, `buffer_size`, `save_buffer_size`, advance `ptr`, `save_buffer_ptr`.\n  - `:316-330` then drain `current_buffer`: same pattern, decrementing `buffer_size`, `current_buffer_size`, advancing `current_buffer_ptr`.\n  - **No short-read detection**: if `length` exceeds `buffer_size` it silently returns partially-filled data. All callers are required to have pre-checked with the `PNG_PUSH_SAVE_BUFFER_IF_*` macros. This is the invariant that ties chunk size to buffer size.\n- `png_push_save_buffer` (`:333-391`):\n  - `:336-351` if `save_buffer_ptr != save_buffer`, byte-by-byte move the `save_buffer_size` unconsumed bytes down to offset 0.\n  - `:352-381` if `save_buffer_size + current_buffer_size > save_buffer_max`: overflow check `:358-362` (`png_error(\"Potential overflow of save_buffer\")`), `new_max = save_buffer_size + current_buffer_size + 256` (`:364`), `png_malloc_warn`, `:369-373` on NULL → free old + `png_error(\"Insufficient memory for save_buffer\")`, `:375-378` copy old contents (or `png_error(\"save_buffer error\")` if `old_buffer == NULL && save_buffer_size != 0`), `png_free(old)`, `save_buffer_max = new_max`.\n  - `:382-388` append all of `current_buffer` to the end of `save_buffer`, `save_buffer_size += current_buffer_size`, `current_buffer_size = 0`.\n  - `:389-390` `save_buffer_ptr = save_buffer; buffer_size = 0;` — the `buffer_size = 0` is what breaks the `while` loop in `png_process_data`.\n- `png_push_restore_buffer` (`:393-401`): `current_buffer = buffer; current_buffer_size = buffer_length; buffer_size = buffer_length + save_buffer_size; current_buffer_ptr = current_buffer;`. Note `buffer_size` is the **sum** of saved + new.\n\n## C.4 IDAT path\n\n### `png_push_read_IDAT` (`:403-494`)\n1. `:406-431` header phase, only if `PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER` clear:\n   - `:412` `PNG_PUSH_SAVE_BUFFER_IF_LT(8)`.\n   - `:413-414` `png_push_fill_buffer(chunk_length, 4)`, `push_length = png_get_uint_31(...)`.\n   - `:415-417` `png_reset_crc`, `png_crc_read(chunk_tag, 4)`, `chunk_name = PNG_CHUNK_FROM_STRING(chunk_tag)`. (Note: this duplicates `png_read_chunk_header` but **skips** the `buf[0] >= 0x80` and `check_chunk_name` validation — the `TODO` at `:411` acknowledges the duplication.)\n   - `:418` set `PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER`.\n   - `:420-428` if `chunk_name != png_IDAT`: `process_mode = PNG_READ_CHUNK_MODE`; if `(flags & PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_ENDED) == 0` → `png_error(\"Not enough compressed data\")`; `return`.\n   - `:430` `idat_size = push_length`.\n2. `:433-458` **save_buffer half**: if `idat_size != 0 && save_buffer_size != 0`: compute `save_size = min(idat_size, save_buffer_size)` with the careful type-dance at `:444-448`; `png_calculate_crc`; `png_process_IDAT_data(save_buffer_ptr, save_size)`; decrement `idat_size`, `buffer_size`, `save_buffer_size`; advance `save_buffer_ptr`.\n3. `:460-484` **current_buffer half**: identical logic against `current_buffer_ptr`/`current_buffer_size`.\n4. `:486-493` if `idat_size == 0`: `PNG_PUSH_SAVE_BUFFER_IF_LT(4)`; `png_crc_finish(png_ptr, 0)`; clear `PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER`; set `PNG_AFTER_IDAT`; `zowner = 0`.\n\n### `png_process_IDAT_data` (`:496-606`)\n- `:501-502` `if (!(buffer_length > 0) || buffer == NULL) png_error(\"No IDAT data (internal error)\")`.\n- `:508-510` `zstream.next_in = buffer; avail_in = (uInt)buffer_length;` (truncation `TODO` at `:509`).\n- `:515-598` loop `while (avail_in > 0 && !(flags & PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_ENDED))`:\n  - `:525-532` if `avail_out == 0`, re-arm `avail_out = PNG_ROWBYTES(pixel_depth, iwidth) + 1`, `next_out = row_buf`.\n  - `:541` `ret = PNG_INFLATE(png_ptr, Z_SYNC_FLUSH)`.\n  - `:544-567` error arm: set `PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_ENDED`, `zowner = 0`; if `row_number >= num_rows || pass > 6` → `png_warning(\"Truncated compressed data in IDAT\")`; else if `ret == Z_DATA_ERROR` → `png_benign_error(\"IDAT: ADLER32 checksum mismatch\")`; else `png_error(\"Decompression error in IDAT\")`; then `return`.\n  - `:570-593` if `next_out != row_buf` (output produced): `:576-588` if `row_number >= num_rows || pass > 6` → `png_warning(\"Extra compressed data in IDAT\")`, set ZSTREAM_ENDED, `zowner = 0`, `return`; `:591-592` if `avail_out == 0` → **`png_push_process_row(png_ptr)`**.\n  - `:596-597` if `ret == Z_STREAM_END` set `PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_ENDED`.\n- `:604-605` leftover `avail_in > 0` → `png_warning(\"Extra compression data in IDAT\")`.\n\n### `png_push_process_row` (`:608-836`)\n- `:611-619` builds a **local** `png_row_info` (moved out of png_struct in 1.5.6): `width = iwidth`, `color_type`, `bit_depth`, `channels`, `pixel_depth`, `rowbytes = PNG_ROWBYTES(pixel_depth, iwidth)`.\n- `:621-628` unfilter: if `row_buf[0] > PNG_FILTER_VALUE_NONE` then if `< PNG_FILTER_VALUE_LAST` → `png_read_filter_row(...)` else `png_error(\"bad adaptive filter value\")`.\n- `:635` `memcpy(prev_row, row_buf, row_info.rowbytes + 1)` (interlaced row count only, per the 1.5.6 comment).\n- `:637-640` `if (transformations != 0) png_do_read_transformations(png_ptr, &row_info)`.\n- `:643-651` depth consistency: first row sets `transformed_pixel_depth` and errors `\"progressive row overflow\"` if `> maximum_pixel_depth`; later rows error `\"internal progressive row size calculation error\"` on mismatch.\n- `:654-829` interlace expansion branch, taken iff `interlaced != 0 && (transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) != 0`; `:659-661` `if (pass < 6) png_do_read_interlace(...)`; then the big `switch (png_ptr->pass)` (see C.6).\n- `:830-835` else (non-interlaced, or app doing its own interlace handling): single `png_push_have_row(png_ptr, row_buf + 1); png_read_push_finish_row(png_ptr);`.\n\n## C.5 `png_progressive_combine_row` (`:906-919`)\n\nGuarded by `#ifdef PNG_READ_INTERLACING_SUPPORTED` (`:905`, `:920`). Only two branches:\n- `:910-911` `if (png_ptr == NULL) return;`\n- `:917-918` `if (new_row != NULL) png_combine_row(png_ptr, old_row, 1/*blocky display*/);`\n\nSo:\n- **`new_row == NULL`** → no-op. `new_row` is used purely as a flag (\"the app callback was called for a synthesised empty row\"), per the comment at `:913-916`. The actual pixel source is always `png_ptr->row_buf + 1`, read internally by `png_combine_row`.\n- **No `old_row == NULL` branch** — passing NULL `old_row` with non-NULL `new_row` will be dereferenced by `png_combine_row` (`src/pngrutil.c:3225`+) as `dp`.\n- **No sparkle/block choice**: the `display` argument is hard-coded to `1` (blocky). The historical sparkle path (`display == 0`) is unreachable from the progressive API in this version; only `png_read_row`'s `dsp_row`/`row` pair distinction still exercises `display == 0` in the sequential reader.\n- There is no separate \"interlaced pass\" branch here; `png_combine_row` itself reads `png_ptr->pass` internally (`src/pngrutil.c:3230`) and errors on `transformed_pixel_depth == 0` (`:3239`), `info_rowbytes` mismatch (`:3246`), `row_width == 0` (`:3252`).\n\n## C.6 Interlace handling — which passes call `row_fn` with what, and `png_read_push_finish_row`\n\n`png_read_push_finish_row` (`:838-881`):\n- `:841-843` `row_number++`; if `row_number < num_rows` return (nothing else changes).\n- `:846-879` `#ifdef PNG_READ_INTERLACING_SUPPORTED` + `if (interlaced != 0)`:\n  - `:848` `row_number = 0`; `:849` `memset(prev_row, 0, rowbytes + 1)`.\n  - `:851-878` `do { pass++; ...` :\n    - `:854-857` skip degenerate passes: `(pass==1 && width<5) || (pass==3 && width<3) || (pass==5 && width<2)` → `pass++` again.\n    - `:859-860` `if (pass > 7) pass--;`\n    - `:862-863` `if (pass >= 7) break;`\n    - `:865-868` `iwidth = (width + png_pass_inc[pass] - 1 - png_pass_start[pass]) / png_pass_inc[pass]`.\n    - `:870-871` **`if ((transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) != 0) break;`** ← key: when libpng is doing the interlace expansion, `num_rows` is **never** recomputed, so it stays at `height` (set by `png_read_start_row`, `src/pngrutil.c:4424`). Every pass therefore delivers exactly `height` `row_fn` calls with `row_num` running 0..height-1.\n    - `:873-876` else (app handles interlace) recompute `num_rows = (height + png_pass_yinc[pass] - 1 - png_pass_ystart[pass]) / png_pass_yinc[pass]`.\n    - `:878` `while (iwidth == 0 || num_rows == 0)`.\n- The static interlace tables are `png_pass_start[7]={0,4,0,2,0,1,0}`, `png_pass_inc={8,8,4,4,2,2,1}`, `png_pass_ystart={0,0,4,0,2,0,1}`, `png_pass_yinc={8,8,8,4,4,2,2}` (`:38-44`), duplicated from pngrutil.c (`TODO` at `:46`).\n\n`row_fn` invocation pattern, from the `switch (png_ptr->pass)` in `png_push_process_row` (`:663-828`). In every case `png_push_have_row` passes the *current* `row_number`/`pass`, and `png_read_push_finish_row` then bumps them, so the reported `row_num` advances 1 per call:\n\n- **case 0** (`:665-699`): 8× `row_buf+1` while `pass==0` (`:668-672`); then `:674-681` if `pass==2` (pass 1 was empty, width<5): 4× `NULL`; `:683-690` if `pass==4 && height<=4`: 2× `NULL`; `:692-696` if `pass==6 && height<=4`: 1× `NULL`.\n- **case 1** (`:701-720`): 8× `row_buf+1` while `pass==1`; then `:710-717` if `pass==2`: 4× `NULL` (\"skip top 4 generated rows\").\n- **case 2** (`:722-748`): 4× `row_buf+1` while `pass==2` (`:726-730`); 4× `NULL` while `pass==2` (`:732-736`); `:738-745` if `pass==4` (pass 3 empty): 2× `NULL`.\n- **case 3** (`:750-770`): 4× `row_buf+1`; then `:760-767` if `pass==4`: 2× `NULL`.\n- **case 4** (`:772-795`): 2× `row_buf+1`; 2× `NULL`; `:788-792` if `pass==6` (pass 5 empty): 1× `NULL`.\n- **case 5** (`:797-814`): 2× `row_buf+1`; `:807-811` if `pass==6`: 1× `NULL`.\n- **default / case 6** (`:816-827`): 1× `row_buf+1` + finish; `:822-823` `if (pass != 6) break;` else 1× `NULL` + finish. (Fallthrough-style: `default` and `6` share the body.)\n\nSo the total `row_fn` call count per decoded interlaced row is 8/8/4/4/2/2/1 for passes 0..6 in the \"real row\" position, plus the `NULL` (empty) calls that let a display update the replicated rows. The app is expected to call `png_progressive_combine_row(png_ptr, my_row_ptr[row_num], new_row)` and rely on the NULL check at `:917`.\n\nNon-interlaced (or `PNG_INTERLACE` not in `transformations`): exactly one `row_fn` per row at `:833-834`, `pass` will be whatever `png_ptr->pass` is (0 for non-interlaced).\n\n## C.7 (see C.2 for `png_process_data_pause`/`_skip`)\n\n`png_set_progressive_read_fn` and `png_process_data_skip` have **zero** interaction: `_skip` never touches `info_fn`/`row_fn`/`end_fn`, `io_ptr`, `read_data_fn`, `process_mode`, or any buffer. It is a warn-and-return-0 stub.\n\n## C.8 State that differs by chunk size vs buffer size (the 1-byte / small / whole-buffer axes)\n\nThe observable-behaviour differences all come from three contiguity requirements plus one incremental path:\n\n1. **8-byte chunk header** — `PNG_PUSH_SAVE_BUFFER_IF_LT(8)` at `:196` (`png_push_read_chunk`) and `:412` (`png_push_read_IDAT`). Feeding <8 bytes at a time forces a `png_push_save_buffer` on every call until 8 bytes have accumulated. `png_read_chunk_header` (`src/pngrutil.c:183`) then consumes them via `png_push_fill_buffer`.\n2. **whole non-IDAT chunk + CRC** — `PNG_PUSH_SAVE_BUFFER_IF_FULL` (`push_length + 4 > buffer_size`) at `:245`, `:251`, `:261`, `:283`. A large ancillary chunk (e.g. a big `zTXt`) must be *entirely* buffered before `png_handle_chunk` runs, so with 1-byte feeding `save_buffer` grows to `push_length + 4` via repeated `+256` reallocs (`:364`). Consequences: peak memory is `O(largest ancillary chunk)` regardless of feed size; `png_malloc_warn` failure → `png_error(\"Insufficient memory for save_buffer\")`; the `png_error(\"Potential overflow of save_buffer\")` at `:361`.\n3. **4-byte IDAT CRC** — `PNG_PUSH_SAVE_BUFFER_IF_LT(4)` at `:488`. Note this is reached *after* the two consume-halves have already run and mutated `idat_size`/`buffer_size`, so on a partial feed the function returns having already inflated data, and re-enters at `:406` with `PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER` still set and `idat_size == 0` — the `:433`/`:460` blocks are skipped and it retries the CRC. This re-entry is idempotent.\n4. **IDAT payload is fully incremental** — no contiguity requirement. `png_push_read_IDAT` splits the work into the save_buffer half (`:433-458`) and the current_buffer half (`:460-484`), each clamped by `min(idat_size, <that buffer's size>)`. So:\n   - *1-byte feed*: `png_process_IDAT_data` is called with `buffer_length == 1`, once per byte → one `inflate(Z_SYNC_FLUSH)` per byte. Semantically identical output, but `avail_out` re-arming at `:525-532` and the `next_out != row_buf` test at `:570` mean partial rows accumulate in `row_buf` and `png_push_process_row` only fires when `avail_out` reaches 0 exactly (`:591`).\n   - *small feed spanning the IDAT boundary*: both halves execute in one call — first draining leftovers from `save_buffer`, then the fresh bytes — so a single `png_process_data` can produce two `png_process_IDAT_data` calls and hence two `png_calculate_crc` calls on disjoint ranges.\n   - *whole-buffer feed*: one `png_process_IDAT_data` per IDAT chunk, `save_buffer` stays empty and is never allocated.\n5. **`save_buffer` residency changes `png_process_data_pause`'s return value** (`:83-84`): with whole-buffer feeding after a `SAVE_BUFFER_IF_FULL` trip, `save_buffer_size` may equal `remaining`, so pause returns 0 rather than a byte count.\n6. **The zero-length-IDAT early return** at `:221-224` leaves `PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER` set; whether the following CRC is consumed in the same `png_process_data` call depends purely on whether ≥4 further bytes are in the buffer.\n\n---\n\n# PART D — SIMPLIFIED API\n\n## D.9 `png_image_begin_read_from_*` and `png_image_read_header`\n\n### Shared init: `png_image_read_init` (`src/pngread.c:1127-1172`)\n`static`, deliberately png_error-free (uses `png_malloc_warn`).\n- `:1129` `if (image->opaque == NULL)` … else `:1171` `return png_image_error(image, \"png_image_read: opaque pointer not NULL\")`.\n- `:1131-1132` `png_create_read_struct(PNG_LIBPNG_VER_STRING, image, png_safe_error, png_safe_warning)`.\n- `:1137-1138` **`memset(image, 0, sizeof *image); image->version = PNG_IMAGE_VERSION;`** — note this wipes `flags`, which is why png.h `:3216-3217` says `PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_16BIT_sRGB` can only be set *after* the begin_read call.\n- `:1140-1160` nested allocation: `png_create_info_struct` → `png_malloc_warn` for the `png_control` → `memset(control,0)`, `control->png_ptr`, `control->info_ptr`, **`control->for_write = 0`**, `image->opaque = control`, `return 1`.\n- `:1163-1166` unwind: `png_destroy_info_struct`, `png_destroy_read_struct`, `return png_image_error(image, \"png_image_read: out of memory\")`.\n\n### `png_image_begin_read_from_stdio` (`:1336-1364`, `#ifdef PNG_STDIO_SUPPORTED`)\nBranches: `image != NULL && version == PNG_IMAGE_VERSION` → `file != NULL` → `png_image_read_init != 0` → `:1347` **`image->opaque->png_ptr->io_ptr = file;`** (direct poke, comment `:1343-1346` \"slightly evil\", avoids needing a safe wrapper for `png_init_io`) → `:1348 return png_safe_execute(image, png_image_read_header, image)`. Else-paths: `\"...invalid argument\"` (`:1353`), `\"...incorrect PNG_IMAGE_VERSION\"` (`:1357`), and a bare `return 0` at `:1360` for `image == NULL` **and also when `png_image_read_init` fails** (init already logged the error).\n\n### `png_image_begin_read_from_file` (`:1366-1401`, `#ifdef PNG_STDIO_SUPPORTED`)\nSame shape plus: `:1374 fopen(file_name, \"rb\")`; on success + init success `:1378-1379` sets `io_ptr = fp` **and `image->opaque->owned_file = 1`** (this is what makes `png_image_free_function` `fclose` it, `src/png.c:3970-3983`); `:1384` `(void)fclose(fp)` if init failed; `:1388` `png_image_error(image, strerror(errno))` if fopen failed.\n\n### `png_image_begin_read_from_memory` (`:1435-1466`) + `png_image_memory_read` (`:1405-1432`)\n- `:1439` `memory != NULL && size > 0` else `\"...invalid argument\"`.\n- `:1443-1449` sets `opaque->memory`, `opaque->size`, **`png_ptr->io_ptr = image`** (not the memory!), **`png_ptr->read_data_fn = png_image_memory_read`** — again a direct struct poke instead of `png_set_read_fn`.\n- `png_image_memory_read` branches: NULL `png_ptr` → return; NULL `image` → falls through to `png_error(\"invalid memory read\")`; NULL `cp` → same; `memory != NULL && size >= need` → `memcpy` + advance `cp->memory`/`cp->size`; otherwise `png_error(\"read beyond end of data\")`.\n\n### `png_image_read_header` (`:1275-1334`) — the format deduction\nExecuted inside `png_safe_execute`.\n- `:1279-1281` `png_set_benign_errors(png_ptr, 1/*warn*/)` (`#ifdef PNG_BENIGN_ERRORS_SUPPORTED`).\n- `:1282` `png_read_info(png_ptr, info_ptr)`.\n- `:1285-1286` `image->width = png_ptr->width; image->height = png_ptr->height;` (read straight out of png_struct).\n- `:1289-1301` `format = png_image_format(png_ptr); image->format = format;` and `:1303-1305` `if ((format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_COLOR) != 0 && png_image_is_not_sRGB(png_ptr)) image->flags |= PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_COLORSPACE_NOT_sRGB;` (grayscale never gets the flag, per the comment `:1299-1302`).\n- `:1310-1332` `colormap_entries`: `switch (png_ptr->color_type)` — `PNG_COLOR_TYPE_GRAY` → `1U << bit_depth`; `PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE` → `num_palette`; `default:` → `256`; then `:1327-1328` clamp to 256.\n\n`png_image_format` (`:1176-1201`) is the deduction:\n- `:1180-1181` `COLOR` iff `color_type & PNG_COLOR_MASK_COLOR`\n- `:1183-1184` `ALPHA` iff `color_type & PNG_COLOR_MASK_ALPHA`; `:1191-1192` **else if** `png_ptr->num_trans > 0` → `ALPHA` (comment `:1186-1190` explains why `png_ptr` and not `info_ptr` is used)\n- `:1194-1195` `LINEAR` iff `bit_depth == 16`\n- `:1197-1198` `COLORMAP` iff `color_type & PNG_COLOR_MASK_PALETTE`\n- `BGR`, `AFIRST`, `ASSOCIATED_ALPHA` are **never** deduced.\n\nExact PNG → `image->format` table:\n\n| PNG colour type | bit depth | tRNS? | resulting `image->format` | named macro |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 GRAY | 1,2,4,8 | no | `0` | `PNG_FORMAT_GRAY` |\n| 0 GRAY | 1,2,4,8 | yes | `ALPHA` | `PNG_FORMAT_GA` |\n| 0 GRAY | 16 | no | `LINEAR` | `PNG_FORMAT_LINEAR_Y` |\n| 0 GRAY | 16 | yes | `ALPHA|LINEAR` | `PNG_FORMAT_LINEAR_Y_ALPHA` |\n| 2 RGB | 8 | no | `COLOR` | `PNG_FORMAT_RGB` |\n| 2 RGB | 8 | yes | `COLOR|ALPHA` | `PNG_FORMAT_RGBA` |\n| 2 RGB | 16 | no | `COLOR|LINEAR` | `PNG_FORMAT_LINEAR_RGB` |\n| 2 RGB | 16 | yes | `COLOR|ALPHA|LINEAR` | `PNG_FORMAT_LINEAR_RGB_ALPHA` |\n| 3 PALETTE | 1,2,4,8 | no | `COLOR|COLORMAP` | `PNG_FORMAT_RGB_COLORMAP` |\n| 3 PALETTE | 1,2,4,8 | yes | `COLOR|ALPHA|COLORMAP` | `PNG_FORMAT_RGBA_COLORMAP` |\n| 4 GRAY_ALPHA | 8 | (ignored) | `ALPHA` | `PNG_FORMAT_GA` |\n| 4 GRAY_ALPHA | 16 | (ignored) | `ALPHA|LINEAR` | `PNG_FORMAT_LINEAR_Y_ALPHA` |\n| 6 RGBA | 8 | (ignored) | `COLOR|ALPHA` | `PNG_FORMAT_RGBA` |\n| 6 RGBA | 16 | (ignored) | `COLOR|ALPHA|LINEAR` | `PNG_FORMAT_LINEAR_RGB_ALPHA` |\n\n`PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_COLORMAP` is set **only** for PNG colour type 3, and never together with `LINEAR` (palette bit depth ≤ 8). Palette images always get `COLOR` set. The application may then overwrite `image->format` with anything before `png_image_finish_read`.\n\nSupporting helpers: `chromaticities_match_sRGB` (`:1204-1226`, `sRGB_TOLERANCE 1000`, ITU-R BT.709-3 `sRGB_xy`), `png_gamma_not_sRGB` (`:1234-1241`, returns 0 for `g < PNG_LIB_GAMMA_MIN || g > PNG_LIB_GAMMA_MAX` including 0, else `png_gamma_significant((g*11+2)/5)`), `png_image_is_not_sRGB` (`:1248-1273`, priority: `cICP`/`mDCV` → chromaticity check; `sRGB` chunk → 0; `cHRM` → chromaticity check; default 0), and `png_image_skip_unused_chunks` / `PNG_SKIP_CHUNKS` (`:1473-1519`, keeps only bKGD/cHRM/cICP/gAMA/mDCV/sBIT/sRGB as-default, everything else `PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_NEVER`).\n\n## D.10 `png_image_finish_read` (`:4087-4202`) — every branch\n\nArgument validation, outermost to innermost:\n1. `:4091` `image != NULL && image->version == PNG_IMAGE_VERSION`; `:4197-4199` else-if `image != NULL` → `\"damaged PNG_IMAGE_VERSION\"`; `:4201` else `return 0`.\n2. `:4097` `channels = PNG_IMAGE_PIXEL_CHANNELS(image->format)` (1 for colormap formats, per `PNG_IMAGE_PIXEL_` in png.h `:3126-3130`).\n3. `:4105` `if (image->width <= 0x7fffffffU/channels)` else `:4193` `\"row_stride too large\"`.\n4. `:4110-4111` **`row_stride == 0` → defaulted** to `image->width * channels`.\n5. `:4113-4117` **negative row_stride**: `check = -(png_uint_32)row_stride` (absolute value); positive: `check = row_stride`.\n6. `:4123` `image->opaque != NULL && buffer != NULL && check >= png_row_stride` else `:4188` `\"invalid argument\"`.\n7. `:4141-4142` `image->height <= 0xffffffffU / PNG_IMAGE_PIXEL_COMPONENT_SIZE(format) / check` else `:4183` `\"image too large\"`.\n8. `:4144-4145` **colormap gate**: `(format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_COLORMAP) == 0 || (image->colormap_entries > 0 && colormap != NULL)` else `:4178` `\"png_image_finish_read[color-map]: no color-map\"`.\n9. `:4150-4156` build the `png_image_read_control` on the stack: `memset` 0, then `image`, `buffer`, `row_stride`, `colormap`, `background`, `local_row = NULL`.\n10. `:4161-4171` **the path split**:\n    - `(format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_COLORMAP) != 0` → `png_safe_execute(image, png_image_read_colormap, &display) && png_safe_execute(image, png_image_read_colormapped, &display)` — **two** separate safe_execute calls, short-circuited.\n    - else → `png_safe_execute(image, png_image_read_direct, &display)`.\n11. `:4173-4174` `png_image_free(image); return result;` — always frees, success or failure.\n\n### The `background` argument: exactly when it matters\nRead-path uses, with conditions:\n- **Colormap path**, `png_image_read_colormap:1989-2021`: `background` is only consulted when *(input has alpha or tRNS)* **and** *(output format lacks `PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_ALPHA`)*. Within that:\n  - `output_encoding == P_LINEAR` (i.e. output format has `LINEAR`) → `back_r=back_g=back_b=0` (**compose on black; `background` ignored entirely**), `:1993-1994`.\n  - else `display->background == NULL` → **`png_error(\"background color must be supplied to remove alpha/transparency\")`** (`:1996-1998`). This is the one hard requirement.\n  - else `:2004-2014` copy: `back_g = background->green` always; if output has `COLOR`, also `back_r = background->red`, `back_b = background->blue`; otherwise `back_b = back_r = back_g` (green channel used for gray).\n  - `:2017-2021` when there is nothing to remove: `back_* = 65535` (P_LINEAR) or `255` (P_sRGB) — unused defaults.\n- **Direct path**, `png_image_read_direct:3778-3830`, only when `change & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_ALPHA` and `base_format` has ALPHA (i.e. alpha is being *removed*):\n  - `do_local_background != 0` → `do_local_background = 2` (`:3791-3792`); `background` handled later in `png_image_read_background`.\n  - else `linear != 0` → `png_set_strip_alpha` (`:3795-3796`) — **16-bit output composites on black by pre-multiplication; `background` ignored**.\n  - else `display->background != NULL` → `:3799-3818` build a `png_color_16` (`red/green/blue` from background, **`gray = background->green`**, per the comment `:3809-3814`) and `png_set_background_fixed(..., PNG_BACKGROUND_GAMMA_SCREEN, 0/*need_expand*/, 0)`.\n  - else (`background == NULL`, 8-bit) → `:3820-3829` `do_local_compose = 1; mode = PNG_ALPHA_OPTIMIZED;` — **compose onto whatever is already in the caller's buffer**, done by `png_image_read_composite`.\n- **`png_image_read_background`** (`:3341-3614`), bit_depth 8 case: `:3426` `if (display->background == NULL)` → compose against `outrow[0]` (`:3440-3464`); `:3468-3509` else constant `background8 = display->background->green`, `background = png_sRGB_table[background8]`, and fully-transparent pixels get `outrow[0] = background8` (`:3503-3504`). bit_depth 16 case (`:3514-3605`) **never looks at `background`** — it only pre-multiplies and optionally keeps alpha.\n\nSummary of the matrix: `background` matters only for **8-bit (non-LINEAR) output with the alpha channel being dropped**; it is *mandatory* for the colormap + 8-bit + drop-alpha combination, *optional* (NULL ⇒ compose on the existing buffer contents) for the direct 8-bit case, and *always ignored* for LINEAR output and whenever the output keeps alpha.\n\n### Positive vs negative `row_stride`\nTwo places, identical idiom:\n- `png_image_read_colormapped:3081-3097`: `row_step = display->row_stride`; `if (row_step < 0) { ptr = buffer; ptr += (image->height-1) * (-row_step); first_row = ptr; }`; store `first_row`, `row_step`.\n- `png_image_read_direct:4002-4021`: same, but with `if (linear != 0) row_step *= 2;` **before** the sign test (`:4006-4007`), so `row_step` is in bytes while the API argument is in components.\nThen all inner loops do `outrow = first_row + y * row_step` (e.g. `:2874`, `:3255`, `:3432`) or `row += row_step` (`:4079`), which walks upward in memory for positive stride and downward for negative. `png_image_read_background`'s 16-bit case divides back: `ptrdiff_t row_step = display->row_step / 2;` (`:3525`, with the comment at `:3522-3524`).\n\n### `PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_*` — complete enumeration (png.h `:3180-3217`)\n| flag | value | line | effect |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_COLORSPACE_NOT_sRGB` | `0x01` | `include/png.h:3185` | **Read**: *set by* `png_image_read_header` (`pngread.c:3103-3105`) when the image has COLOR and `png_image_is_not_sRGB()`. **Write**: read by `png_image_write_main` (`pngwrite.c:2094`, `:2104`) — if clear, writes `cHRM` (16-bit) or `sRGB` (8-bit); if set, writes only `gAMA` (`PNG_GAMMA_LINEAR` for 16-bit at `:2092`, `PNG_GAMMA_sRGB_INVERSE` for 8-bit at `:2111`) and no `cHRM`/`sRGB`. |\n| `PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_FAST` | `0x02` | `include/png.h:3190` | **Write only**: `pngwrite.c:2173-2184` → `png_set_filter(png_ptr, PNG_FILTER_TYPE_BASE, PNG_NO_FILTERS)` and `png_set_compression_level(png_ptr, 3)` (`#ifdef PNG_WRITE_CUSTOMIZE_COMPRESSION_SUPPORTED`). No read effect. |\n| `PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_16BIT_sRGB` | `0x04` | `include/png.h:3201` | **Read only**, app-settable after begin_read. Two uses: `png_image_read_colormap:2032-2037` (`bit_depth == 16 && !16BIT_sRGB` → `png_ptr->default_gamma = PNG_GAMMA_LINEAR`, else `PNG_GAMMA_sRGB_INVERSE`) and `png_image_read_direct:3690-3694` (`base_format & LINEAR && !16BIT_sRGB` → `input_gamma_default = PNG_GAMMA_LINEAR`, else `PNG_DEFAULT_sRGB`). |\n\nThere is **no** `PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_COLORMAP_UNCHANGED` and no `PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_..._FAST` read flag in this version — grep confirms only these three `PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_*` defines exist. (`PNG_IMAGE_WARNING = 1` / `PNG_IMAGE_ERROR = 2` / `PNG_IMAGE_FAILED()` at `include/png.h:2939-2950` are `warning_or_error` bits, not `flags`.)\n\n### The five internal read row-loop routines and their selection conditions\nAll selected inside `png_image_read_direct` (`:4023-4084`) or `png_image_read_colormapped` (`:3099-3129`):\n\n1. **`png_image_read_and_map`** (`:2812-2999`) — colormap path, chosen at `:3099` when `passes == 0`, i.e. when `colormap_processing != PNG_CMAP_NONE` (because `passes` is only set by `png_set_interlace_handling` at `:3020`, guarded by `if (colormap_processing == PNG_CMAP_NONE)`). Allocates a `png_get_rowbytes`-sized `local_row` (`:3102`) and runs a nested `png_safe_execute`. Inner `switch (proc)`: `PNG_CMAP_GA` (`:2887-2914`), `PNG_CMAP_TRANS` (`:2916-2931`), `PNG_CMAP_RGB` (`:2933-2939`), `PNG_CMAP_RGB_ALPHA` (`:2941-2989`), `default: break`.\n2. **direct colormap loop** (`:3112-3129`) — colormap path, `PNG_CMAP_NONE`: reads straight into the user buffer, `passes` iterations of `height` `png_read_row` calls.\n3. **`png_image_read_composite`** (`:3188-3325`) — `do_local_compose != 0` (`:4023`), i.e. 8-bit output, alpha being removed, `background == NULL`. Branches inside: interlace `NONE`/`ADAM7`/error (`:3197-3209`), `channels = COLOR ? 3 : 1` (`:3215-3216`), `optimize_alpha = (png_ptr->flags & PNG_FLAG_OPTIMIZE_ALPHA) != 0` (`:3217`), per-pixel `alpha > 0` / `alpha < 255` / `optimize_alpha` two-way split (`:3274-3311`, the second arm being the CVE-2025-66293 belt-and-suspenders clamp at `:3290-3291` plus the non-gamma-correct sRGB-space composite at `:3307-3310`).\n4. **`png_image_read_background`** (`:3340-3614`) — `do_local_background == 2` (`:4036`). Entry assertions: `png_error(\"lost rgb to gray\")` if `!(transformations & PNG_RGB_TO_GRAY)` (`:3357`), `\"unexpected compose\"` if `PNG_COMPOSE` set (`:3360`), `\"lost/gained channels\"` if `png_get_channels != 2` (`:3363`), `\"unexpected 8-bit transformation\"` if `!LINEAR && ALPHA` (`:3367`). Then `switch (info_ptr->bit_depth)`: `8` (`:3392-3512`, background NULL vs constant as above), `16` (`:3514-3605`, `preserve_alpha`, `outchannels = 1 + preserve_alpha`, `swap_alpha` under `PNG_SIMPLIFIED_READ_AFIRST_SUPPORTED` at `:3531-3535`), `default: png_error(\"unexpected bit depth\")` (`#ifdef __GNUC__`).\n5. **`png_image_read_direct_scaled`** (`:3133-3185`) — `do_local_scale != 0` (`:4049`), set only at `:3770-3771` when the bit depth is being reduced 16→8 **and** `png_ptr->interlaced != 0`. Copies `row_bytes` from `local_row` into the user buffer per row, advancing by `row_step`. (This is the newer overflow fix for `png_combine_row` writing at IHDR bit depth.)\n6. **plain direct loop** (`:4067-4084`) — none of the above; `passes` × `height` `png_read_row(png_ptr, row, NULL)` straight into the user buffer.\n\nNote `passes` is only non-zero when `do_local_compose == 0 && do_local_background != 2` (`:3936-3937`), so paths 3 and 4 do their own interlace pass loops; path 5 does too (`:3147-3160`) even though `passes` was set.\n\n`png_image_read_direct`'s transform-setup decisions, in order: `png_set_expand` (`:3637`); `base_format = png_image_format(png_ptr) & ~PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_COLORMAP`, `change = format ^ base_format` (`:3641-3643`); COLOR change → `png_set_gray_to_rgb` or (`png_set_rgb_to_gray_fixed` + `do_local_background = 1` if input has alpha) (`:3648-3677`); input gamma default via `png_set_alpha_mode_fixed(PNG_ALPHA_PNG, ...)` (`:3681-3700`); `mode`/`output_gamma` = `PNG_ALPHA_STANDARD`+`PNG_GAMMA_LINEAR` / `PNG_ALPHA_PNG`+`PNG_GAMMA_LINEAR` / `PNG_ALPHA_PNG`+`PNG_DEFAULT_sRGB` (`:3702-3720`); `ASSOCIATED_ALPHA` change → `mode = PNG_ALPHA_OPTIMIZED` (`:3722-3726`); the `do_local_background` gamma-threshold refinement 1→0 or 1→2 (`:3734-3755`); LINEAR change → `png_set_expand_16` or `png_set_scale_16` (+`do_local_scale`) (`:3758-3775`); ALPHA change (see background matrix above, plus the add-alpha `filler`/`PNG_FILLER_BEFORE|AFTER` arm at `:3832-3860`); `png_set_alpha_mode_fixed(mode, output_gamma)` unconditionally (`:3870`); BGR (`:3872-3886`, cleared from `format` if output is gray); AFIRST (`:3888-3910`, suppressed when `do_local_background == 2`, cleared from `format` if no alpha); host-endian `png_set_swap` for 16-bit output (`:3915-3921`); and finally `if (change != 0) png_error(\"png_read_image: unsupported transformation\")` (`:3924-3925`). The post-`png_read_update_info` re-derivation and `if (info_format != format) png_error(\"png_read_image: invalid transformations\")` is at `:3941-3995`.\n\n### `png_image_read_colormap` (`:1959-2809`) — every distinct case\n\nPreamble: `output_format = image->format`, `output_encoding = (LINEAR) ? P_LINEAR : P_sRGB` (`:1967-1969`); encodings `P_NOTSET 0 / P_sRGB 1 / P_LINEAR 2 / P_FILE 3 / P_LINEAR8 4` (`:1082-1086`); processing options `PNG_CMAP_NONE 0 / GA 1 / TRANS 2 / RGB 3 / RGB_ALPHA 4` (`:1090-1094`) with documented background indices `NONE 256 / GA 231 / TRANS 254 / RGB 256 / RGB_ALPHA 216` (`:1098-1102`). `back_r/g/b` setup at `:1989-2021` (see background matrix). `default_gamma` set at `:2032-2037`.\n\n`switch (png_ptr->color_type)`:\n\n**A. `PNG_COLOR_TYPE_GRAY`, bit_depth ≤ 8** (`:2046-2112`)\n- `cmap_entries = 1U << bit_depth` (1/4/16/256); `png_error(\"gray[8] color-map: too few entries\")` if it exceeds `image->colormap_entries`.\n- `step = 255/(cmap_entries-1)`; `output_processing = PNG_CMAP_NONE`; `data_encoding = P_FILE`.\n- tRNS sub-branch (`:2064-2070`): `trans = png_ptr->trans_color.gray`; if output has no ALPHA, `back_alpha = P_LINEAR ? 65535 : 255`.\n- Loop `:2079-2100`: `i != trans` → `png_create_colormap_entry(display, i, val,val,val, 255, P_FILE)`; `i == trans` → entry with `back_r/g/b, back_alpha, output_encoding`.\n- `:2110-2111` `if (bit_depth < 8) png_set_packing(png_ptr)`.\n\n**B. `PNG_COLOR_TYPE_GRAY`, bit_depth == 16** (`:2114-2214`)\n- `data_encoding = P_sRGB`; requires `PNG_GRAY_COLORMAP_ENTRIES (256)` (`png_error(\"gray[16] color-map: too few entries\")`); `cmap_entries = make_gray_colormap(display)` = 256.\n- No tRNS → `output_processing = PNG_CMAP_NONE` (`:2212-2213`).\n- tRNS + output has ALPHA → `back_alpha = 0`, falls to the `PNG_CMAP_TRANS` block below.\n- tRNS + no output ALPHA + **gray background** (`back_r == back_g == back_b`, `:2148-2183`) → possibly rewrite entry `gray = PNG_sRGB_FROM_LINEAR(gray*255)` for P_LINEAR, `png_set_background_fixed(..., PNG_BACKGROUND_GAMMA_SCREEN, 0, 0)`, `output_processing = PNG_CMAP_NONE`, **`break`** out of the whole switch.\n- tRNS + no output ALPHA + non-gray background → `back_alpha = P_LINEAR ? 65535 : 255`.\n- The `PNG_CMAP_TRANS` tail (`:2201-2209`): `expand_tRNS = 1`, `output_processing = PNG_CMAP_TRANS`, `background_index = 254`, and entry 254 overwritten with the full-precision background (\"sacrifice gray level 254\", comment `:2116-2131`).\n\n**C. `PNG_COLOR_TYPE_GRAY_ALPHA`** (`:2217-2371`), `data_encoding = P_sRGB` always\n- C1 output **has** ALPHA (`:2230-2239`): needs `PNG_GA_COLORMAP_ENTRIES (256)` (`\"gray+alpha color-map: too few entries\"`); `cmap_entries = make_ga_colormap(display)` = 256; `background_index = PNG_CMAP_GA_BACKGROUND (231)`; `output_processing = PNG_CMAP_GA`.\n- C2 output has no ALPHA and (**output is gray** or **background is gray**) (`:2259-2291`): needs 256 (`\"gray-alpha color-map: too few entries\"`); `make_gray_colormap`; for P_LINEAR recompute `gray = PNG_sRGB_FROM_LINEAR(back_g*255)` and overwrite that entry; `png_set_background_fixed`; `output_processing = PNG_CMAP_NONE`.\n- C3 output is colour with a non-gray background (`:2293-2369`): hand-rolled \"ga colormap with opaque entries\" — needs 256 (`\"ga-alpha color-map: too few entries\"`); 231 gray entries `(i*256+115)/231` (`:2304-2309`); `background_index = i` then one full-precision background entry (`:2314-2323`); if `output_encoding == P_sRGB` convert `back_*` through `png_sRGB_table` (`:2333-2342`); then 4×6 = 24 composited entries for `a=1..4`, `g=0..5` (`:2344-2365`); `cmap_entries = i` (= 256); `output_processing = PNG_CMAP_GA`.\n\n**D. `PNG_COLOR_TYPE_RGB` / `PNG_COLOR_TYPE_RGB_ALPHA`** (`:2373-2670`)\n- D-gray: output has **no** `COLOR` (`:2378-2507`) → `png_set_rgb_to_gray_fixed(PNG_ERROR_ACTION_NONE, -1, -1)` (`:2388-2389`), `data_encoding = P_sRGB`.\n  - D1 (`:2395-2411`) input has alpha/tRNS **and** output has ALPHA: `expand_tRNS = 1`; needs 256 (`\"rgb[ga] color-map: too few entries\"`); `make_ga_colormap`; `background_index = 231`; `PNG_CMAP_GA`.\n  - D2 (`:2413-2506`) otherwise: needs 256 (`\"rgb[gray] color-map: too few entries\"`).\n    - D2a (`:2435-2441`) input has alpha/tRNS **and** `png_gamma_not_sRGB(gamma)` → `make_gray_file_colormap` (256 file-gamma entries) and `data_encoding = P_FILE` — the double-gamma-correction workaround described at `:2424-2433`.\n    - D2b (`:2443-2444`) else `make_gray_colormap`.\n    - D2c (`:2448-2503`) if input has alpha/tRNS: fix up the background entry — three sub-cases: `data_encoding == P_FILE` (`:2459-2477`, gray pushed through `png_sRGB_table` then `PNG_DIV257(png_gamma_16bit_correct(gray, gamma))`), `output_encoding == P_LINEAR` (`:2479-2487`), or neither; then `expand_tRNS = 1` and `png_set_background_fixed` (`:2499-2502`, with the \"apparently a bug in libpng\" note at `:2495-2498`).\n    - `output_processing = PNG_CMAP_NONE` (`:2505`).\n- D-colour: output **has** `COLOR` (`:2509-2669`), `data_encoding = P_sRGB`.\n  - D3 (`:2525-2563`) input has alpha/tRNS **and** output has ALPHA: needs `216+1+27 = 244` (`\"rgb+alpha color-map: too few entries\"`); `make_rgb_colormap` (216); one transparent entry at 216 → `background_index = 216` (= `PNG_CMAP_RGB_ALPHA_BACKGROUND`); then 27 entries (`r,g,b ∈ {0,127,255}`) with alpha 128 via the `for (r=0; r<256; r = (r<<1)|0x7f)` idiom (`:2544-2559`); `expand_tRNS = 1`; `PNG_CMAP_RGB_ALPHA`.\n  - D4 (`:2565-2655`) input has alpha/tRNS, output has **no** ALPHA: needs 244 (`\"rgb-alpha color-map: too few entries\"`); `make_rgb_colormap`; write a candidate background entry at index 216; compute sRGB `r,g,b`; `memcmp` that entry against `colormap[PNG_RGB_INDEX(r,g,b)]` (`:2605-2609`):\n    - **differ** → `background_index = cmap_entries++` (216) and 27 composed entries via `png_colormap_compose(..., 128, back_*, output_encoding)` (`:2617-2634`); `expand_tRNS = 1`; `PNG_CMAP_RGB_ALPHA` (`cmap_entries` = 244).\n    - **match** → `png_set_background_fixed` with `c.red/green/blue/gray` from `back_*` (`:2642-2651`); `output_processing = PNG_CMAP_RGB`; `cmap_entries` stays 216, `background_index` stays 256.\n  - D5 (`:2658-2668`) no alpha/tRNS at all: needs `PNG_RGB_COLORMAP_ENTRIES (216)` (`\"rgb color-map: too few entries\"`); `make_rgb_colormap`; `PNG_CMAP_RGB`.\n\n**E. `PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE`** (`:2672-2735`)\n- `output_processing = PNG_CMAP_NONE`, `data_encoding = P_FILE` (\"Don't change from color-map indices\"), `cmap_entries = min(num_palette, 256)`; `png_error(\"palette color-map: too few entries\")` if it exceeds `image->colormap_entries`.\n- `do_background = trans != NULL && (output_format & ALPHA) == 0` (`:2680-2681`); `trans == NULL` forces `num_trans = 0` (`:2685-2686`).\n- Per entry `:2697-2727`: if `do_background && i < num_trans && trans[i] < 255` → `trans[i] == 0` gives the flat background entry (`:2701-2703`), else three `png_colormap_compose(display, colormap[i].{red,green,blue}, P_FILE, trans[i], back_*, output_encoding)` calls with alpha `trans[i]*257` (P_LINEAR) or `trans[i]` (`:2710-2719`); otherwise the plain `P_FILE` entry with alpha `i < num_trans ? trans[i] : 255` (`:2724-2726`).\n- `:2732-2733` `if (bit_depth < 8) png_set_packing(png_ptr)`.\n\n**F. `default:`** (`:2737-2739`) `png_error(\"invalid PNG color type\")`.\n\nEpilogue:\n- `:2743-2745` `if (expand_tRNS && num_trans > 0 && !(color_type & MASK_ALPHA)) png_set_tRNS_to_alpha(png_ptr)`.\n- `:2747-2763` `switch (data_encoding)`: `P_sRGB` → `png_set_alpha_mode_fixed(PNG_ALPHA_PNG, PNG_GAMMA_sRGB)` then **fallthrough**; `P_FILE` → `if (bit_depth > 8) png_set_scale_16(png_ptr)`; `#ifdef __GNUC__ default: png_error(\"bad data option (internal error)\")`.\n- `:2765-2766` `if (cmap_entries > 256 || cmap_entries > image->colormap_entries) png_error(\"color map overflow (BAD internal error)\")`.\n- `:2768` **`image->colormap_entries = cmap_entries;`** (this is the documented \"may be less than the original value\" update).\n- `:2771-2804` cross-check `switch (output_processing)` against `background_index`: NONE↔256, GA↔231, TRANS↔254 *and* `< cmap_entries`, RGB↔256, RGB_ALPHA↔216; mismatch → `png_error(\"bad background index (internal error)\")`, unknown → `\"bad processing option (internal error)\"`.\n- `:2806` `display->colormap_processing = output_processing`.\n\n**cmap_entries accounting summary**: A `1<<bit_depth`; B 256 (+ entry 254 stolen); C1/C2 256; C3 231 + 1 background + 24 composed = 256; D1 256; D2 256; D3 216 + 1 + 27 = 244; D4 216 (match) or 244 (differ); D5 216; E `min(num_palette, 256)`.\n\n**Helpers**: `make_gray_file_colormap` (`:1852-1861`, 256× `P_FILE`, returns 256), `make_gray_colormap` (`:1863-1873`, 256× `P_sRGB`, `PNG_GRAY_COLORMAP_ENTRIES 256` at `:1874`), `make_ga_colormap` (`:1875-1927`, 231 grays `(i*256+115)/231` + 1 transparent white + 4×6 partial-alpha = 256, `PNG_GA_COLORMAP_ENTRIES 256` at `:1929`; the index algorithm is documented in the comment at `:1881-1901` and duplicated in code at `:2899-2910`), `make_rgb_colormap` (`:1930-1953`, 6×6×6 = 216, `PNG_RGB_COLORMAP_ENTRIES 216` at `:1954`, `PNG_RGB_INDEX(r,g,b)` at `:1957-1958`). Entry writer `png_create_colormap_entry` (`:1631-1851`) with `PNG_DIV51` (`:1524`), `set_file_encoding` (`:1527-1553`), `decode_gamma` (`:1555-1591`), `png_colormap_compose` (`:1594-1626`).\n\n`png_image_read_colormapped` (`:3001-3130`) then validates the promised libpng output before reading: `PNG_CMAP_NONE` → colour type PALETTE or GRAY at depth 8 (`:3031-3034`); `PNG_CMAP_TRANS`/`PNG_CMAP_GA` → GRAY_ALPHA, depth 8, `screen_gamma == PNG_GAMMA_sRGB`, `colormap_entries == 256` (`:3044-3048`); `PNG_CMAP_RGB` → RGB, depth 8, sRGB, 216 (`:3054-3058`); `PNG_CMAP_RGB_ALPHA` → RGB_ALPHA, depth 8, sRGB, **244** (`:3064-3067`); anything else → `png_error(\"bad color-map processing (internal error)\")` (`:3072-3074`).\n\n## D.11 Every legal `PNG_FORMAT_*` value and whether it is a distinct code path\n\nFlags (png.h `:3025-3038`): `ALPHA 0x01`, `COLOR 0x02`, `LINEAR 0x04`, `COLORMAP 0x08`, `BGR 0x10` (`#ifdef PNG_FORMAT_BGR_SUPPORTED`), `AFIRST 0x20` (`#ifdef PNG_FORMAT_AFIRST_SUPPORTED`), `ASSOCIATED_ALPHA 0x40`. The header states \"All combinations are valid\" (`:3005`).\n\nNamed macros (png.h `:3044-3073`) with values:\n\n| macro | value | line |\n|---|---|---|\n| `PNG_FORMAT_GRAY` | `0x00` | 3044 |\n| `PNG_FORMAT_GA` | `0x01` | 3045 |\n| `PNG_FORMAT_AG` | `0x21` | 3046 |\n| `PNG_FORMAT_RGB` | `0x02` | 3047 |\n| `PNG_FORMAT_BGR` | `0x12` | 3048 |\n| `PNG_FORMAT_RGBA` | `0x03` | 3049 |\n| `PNG_FORMAT_ARGB` | `0x23` | 3050 |\n| `PNG_FORMAT_BGRA` | `0x13` | 3051 |\n| `PNG_FORMAT_ABGR` | `0x33` | 3052 |\n| `PNG_FORMAT_LINEAR_Y` | `0x04` | 3057 |\n| `PNG_FORMAT_LINEAR_Y_ALPHA` | `0x05` | 3058 |\n| `PNG_FORMAT_LINEAR_RGB` | `0x06` | 3059 |\n| `PNG_FORMAT_LINEAR_RGB_ALPHA` | `0x07` | 3060-3061 |\n| `PNG_FORMAT_RGB_COLORMAP` | `0x0A` | 3068 |\n| `PNG_FORMAT_BGR_COLORMAP` | `0x1A` | 3069 |\n| `PNG_FORMAT_RGBA_COLORMAP` | `0x0B` | 3070 |\n| `PNG_FORMAT_ARGB_COLORMAP` | `0x2B` | 3071 |\n| `PNG_FORMAT_BGRA_COLORMAP` | `0x3B` | 3072 |\n| `PNG_FORMAT_ABGR_COLORMAP` | `0x3B`… wait, `ABGR|COLORMAP` = `0x3B` | 3073 |\n\n(`BGRA_COLORMAP` = `0x1B`, `ABGR_COLORMAP` = `0x3B`; both distinct.) There are **no** named `GRAY_COLORMAP` / `GA_COLORMAP` / `LINEAR_*_COLORMAP` macros, but `PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_COLORMAP` may legally be OR-ed onto any of them (e.g. `PNG_FORMAT_GRAY|COLORMAP` = `0x08`, `PNG_FORMAT_LINEAR_Y|COLORMAP` = `0x0C`).\n\n**Distinct code paths — read** (the axes that actually branch):\n- `COLORMAP` (0x08) — the top-level split at `pngread.c:4161`: colormap → `read_colormap` + `read_colormapped`; else `read_direct`. **Fully distinct.**\n- `LINEAR` (0x04) — distinct throughout: `output_encoding = P_LINEAR` in the colormap code (`:1968`), 16-bit vs 8-bit colormap entry writers (`:1745` vs `:1826` in `png_create_colormap_entry`), `row_step *= 2` (`:4007`), `png_set_expand_16` vs `png_set_scale_16` (`:3760-3772`), `PNG_ALPHA_STANDARD` vs `PNG_ALPHA_PNG` (`:3707-3711`), `png_set_swap` (`:3915-3921`), background-on-black vs supplied-background (`:1993`, `:3795`), and `read_background`'s bit-depth 8 vs 16 arms (`:3392` / `:3514`). **Fully distinct.**\n- `ALPHA` (0x01) — distinct: drives `change & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_ALPHA` (`:3778`), add-alpha vs remove-alpha, `PNG_CMAP_GA` vs the background variants, `preserve_alpha` (`:3526`). **Fully distinct.**\n- `COLOR` (0x02) — distinct: `png_set_gray_to_rgb` vs `png_set_rgb_to_gray_fixed` (`:3651-3674`), `channels = COLOR ? 3 : 1` (`:3215-3216`), `convert_to_Y` in colormap entries (`:1636-1637`), and it also gates BGR (`:3878-3882`). **Fully distinct.**\n- `BGR` (0x10) — **only distinct when `COLOR` is also set**. `png_image_read_direct:3878-3882` calls `png_set_bgr` if COLOR, otherwise silently clears the bit from the local `format` (so `PNG_FORMAT_GRAY|BGR` behaves exactly as `PNG_FORMAT_GRAY`). In the colormap path `bgr` is only used at `:1758`/`:1839` for `channels >= 3`. So `RGB` vs `BGR`, `RGBA` vs `BGRA`, `ARGB` vs `ABGR` are distinct; `GRAY|BGR` and `GA|BGR` are not.\n- `AFIRST` (0x20) — **only distinct when `ALPHA` is also set**. `:3889-3909` calls `png_set_swap_alpha` only if ALPHA, otherwise clears the bit; also affects `png_set_add_alpha(..., PNG_FILLER_BEFORE)` at `:3849-3853`, and is *suppressed* when `do_local_background == 2` (`:3901-3902`) with `read_background` doing the swap itself via `swap_alpha` (`:3531-3535`, `:3596-3598`). So `GA` vs `AG`, `RGBA` vs `ARGB`, `BGRA` vs `ABGR` are distinct; `GRAY|AFIRST`, `RGB|AFIRST` are not.\n- `ASSOCIATED_ALPHA` (0x40) — distinct only via `:3722-3726` (`mode = PNG_ALPHA_OPTIMIZED`) and `:3962-3964`. Not part of any named macro.\n- **Colormap-format sub-note**: `BGR`/`AFIRST` in a colormap format affect only the layout of the *colormap entries* (`png_create_colormap_entry:1741-1832`), never the index bytes; the index-generation switch in `png_image_read_and_map` is identical for all of `RGB_COLORMAP`/`BGR_COLORMAP`/`RGBA_COLORMAP`/`ARGB_COLORMAP`/`BGRA_COLORMAP`/`ABGR_COLORMAP`. In `png_image_write_main`, `:2132` and `:2141` explicitly skip `png_set_bgr`/`png_set_swap_alpha` when `colormap != 0`.\n\n**Distinct code paths — write** (`pngwrite.c:1997-2228`):\n- `COLORMAP` — distinct: `png_set_IHDR(PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE)` with bit depth `entries>16?8:(>4?4:(>2?2:1))` + `png_image_set_PLTE` (`:2057-2074`); also forces `linear = alpha = write_16bit = 0` (`:2009-2011`), and `png_set_packing` when `colormap_entries <= 16` (`:2150-2151`).\n- `LINEAR` — distinct, and cross-cut by `convert_to_8bit`: `write_16bit = linear && !convert_to_8bit` (`:2011`) drives the IHDR bit depth (`:2078`), `gAMA`/`cHRM` vs `sRGB` (`:2089-2111`), `png_set_swap` (`:2121-2127`), `row_step *= 2` (`:2162-2163`), and the pre-transform gate `if (linear && (alpha || convert_to_8bit))` (`:2190`).\n- `ALPHA` — distinct: `PNG_COLOR_MASK_ALPHA` in IHDR (`:2080`), and it is the *only* thing that makes `png_write_image_16bit` legal (that function `png_error`s \"png_write_image: internal call error\" at `:1629` if ALPHA is not set) and selects the alpha vs no-alpha arms of `png_write_image_8bit` (`:1769` vs `:1823`).\n- `COLOR` — distinct: `PNG_COLOR_MASK_COLOR` in IHDR (`:2079`), `channels = COLOR ? 3 : 1` (`:1607`, `:1766`), and gates BGR (`:2132`).\n- `BGR` — only distinct for `colormap == 0 && COLOR` (`png_set_bgr`, `:2130-2135`) or, for colormap input, `channels >= 3` inside `png_image_set_PLTE` (`:1871-1875`, `:1899-1904`, `:1931-1936`, `:1959-1961`). Bit is always cleared from the local `format` afterwards (`:2134`).\n- `AFIRST` — only distinct for `colormap == 0 && ALPHA` (`png_set_swap_alpha`, `:2139-2144`) or, for colormap input, in `png_image_set_PLTE`'s `afirst` (`:1863-1869`, `:1914`, `:1954`, `:1965`, `:1971`); plus `aindex = -1` + pointer pre-increment in `png_write_image_16bit`/`_8bit` (`:1614-1625`, `:1774-1784`).\n- `ASSOCIATED_ALPHA` (0x40) and `LINEAR` residue are the only bits the final check tolerates: `:2154-2156` `if ((format & ~(COLOR|LINEAR|ALPHA|COLORMAP)) != 0) png_error(\"png_write_image: unsupported transformation\")` — so an app setting `PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_ASSOCIATED_ALPHA` on **write** hits this error, since nothing clears 0x40.\n\n## D.12 `png_image_write_*` branches\n\n### `png_image_write_to_memory` (`:2278-2342`)\n- `:2284` `image != NULL && version == PNG_IMAGE_VERSION` else `:2337` `\"...incorrect PNG_IMAGE_VERSION\"` / `:2341 return 0`.\n- `:2286` `memory_bytes != NULL && buffer != NULL` else `:2332-2333` `\"...invalid argument\"`. Note `buffer` is required even in size-query mode.\n- `:2291-2292` **size-query mode**: `if (memory == NULL) *memory_bytes = 0;` (defensive, per comment `:2288-2290`).\n- `:2294` `png_image_write_init` else `:2328 return 0`.\n- `:2299-2307` display init: `image`, `buffer`, `row_stride`, `colormap`, `convert_to_8bit`, `memory`, `memory_bytes = *memory_bytes`, `output_bytes = 0`.\n- `:2309-2310` `png_safe_execute(image, png_image_write_memory, &display)` then `png_image_free(image)`.\n- `:2313-2322` post-processing: if `result`, then `if (memory != NULL && display.output_bytes > *memory_bytes) result = 0;` and **always** `*memory_bytes = display.output_bytes`. So the two failure modes are distinguishable exactly as png.h `:3355-3362` documents: `*memory_bytes` unchanged ⇒ genuine write error; `*memory_bytes` changed (or non-zero when `memory == NULL`) ⇒ buffer too small, and it now holds the required size.\n- `png_image_write_memory` (`:2262-2276`) installs `png_set_write_fn(png_ptr, display, image_memory_write, image_memory_flush)` then tail-calls `png_image_write_main`.\n- `image_memory_write` (`:2231-2254`): overflow guard `size <= ((png_alloc_size_t)-1) - ob` else `png_error(\"png_image_write_to_memory: PNG too big\")`; `if (size > 0)` then **`if (display->memory_bytes >= ob