`:2021-2054` row_stride validation, mirroring the read side: `channels = PNG_IMAGE_PIXEL_CHANNELS`; `width <= 0x7fffffffU/channels` else `png_error(\"image row stride too large\")`; **`row_stride == 0` → defaulted** to `width*channels` (`:2029-2030`); `check = |row_stride|` (`:2032-2036`); `check >= png_row_stride` else `png_error(\"supplied row stride too small\")`; `height > 0xffffffffU/png_row_stride` → `png_error(\"memory image too large\")`.\n- `:2057-2074` **colormap input**: `display->colormap != NULL && colormap_entries > 0` → `png_set_IHDR(..., entries>16?8:(entries>4?4:(entries>2?2:1)), PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE, PNG_INTERLACE_NONE, ...)` + `png_image_set_PLTE(display)`; else `png_error(\"no color-map for color-mapped image\")`.\n- `:2076-2081` **non-colormap**: `png_set_IHDR(..., write_16bit ? 16 : 8, (COLOR?PNG_COLOR_MASK_COLOR:0) + (ALPHA?PNG_COLOR_MASK_ALPHA:0), PNG_INTERLACE_NONE, ...)` — interlacing is never written.\n- Colour-space chunks, three-way (`:2089-2111`): `write_16bit` → `png_set_gAMA_fixed(PNG_GAMMA_LINEAR)` + `png_set_cHRM_fixed(sRGB primaries)` if `COLORSPACE_NOT_sRGB` clear; else if `COLORSPACE_NOT_sRGB` clear → `png_set_sRGB(PNG_sRGB_INTENT_PERCEPTUAL)`; else → `png_set_gAMA_fixed(PNG_GAMMA_sRGB_INVERSE)`.\n- `:2114` `png_write_info(png_ptr, info_ptr)` — **transforms must be set after this**, per the comment `:2083-2087`/`:2116-2120`.\n- `:2121-2127` `write_16bit` + little-endian host → `png_set_swap`.\n- `:2129-2136` `#ifdef PNG_SIMPLIFIED_WRITE_BGR_SUPPORTED`: `BGR` set → `png_set_bgr` iff `colormap == 0 && COLOR`; always `format &= ~BGR`.\n- `:2138-2145` `#ifdef PNG_SIMPLIFIED_WRITE_AFIRST_SUPPORTED`: `AFIRST` set → `png_set_swap_alpha` iff `colormap == 0 && ALPHA`; always `format &= ~AFIRST`.\n- `:2150-2151` `colormap != 0 && colormap_entries <= 16` → `png_set_packing`.\n- `:2154-2156` residual-flag check → `png_error(\"png_write_image: unsupported transformation\")`.\n- `:2158-2170` first_row/row_step: `row_step = row_stride`; `if (linear) row_step *= 2`; `if (row_step < 0) row += (height-1)*(-row_step)`.\n- `:2173-2184` `PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_FAST` → `png_set_filter(PNG_FILTER_TYPE_BASE, PNG_NO_FILTERS)` + `png_set_compression_level(png_ptr, 3)`.\n- **The \"16-bit vs 8-bit\" write branch** (`:2190-2224`): `if (linear != 0 && (alpha != 0 || convert_to_8bit != 0))` → allocate `local_row` of `png_get_rowbytes` and `png_safe_execute` either `png_write_image_16bit` (`write_16bit != 0`) or `png_write_image_8bit`; free; `if (result == 0) return 0` (skips `png_write_end`). Otherwise (`:2213-2224`) the plain loop: `height` × `png_write_row(png_ptr, row); row += row_step;`.\n  - Reachability: `linear && alpha && !convert_to_8bit` → 16bit writer; `linear && convert_to_8bit` (alpha or not) → 8bit writer; `linear && !alpha && !convert_to_8bit` → plain loop (16-bit data written verbatim with byte swapping); `!linear` → plain loop.\n- `:2226` `png_write_end(png_ptr, info_ptr); return 1;`\n\n`png_write_image_16bit` (`:1595-1697`): un-premultiplies 16-bit associated alpha with a 15-bit reciprocal (`:1655-1656`, `:1670-1681`), `aindex = -1` + pre-incremented row pointers for AFIRST (`:1614-1620`) else `aindex = channels`; `png_error(\"png_write_image: internal call error\")` if ALPHA is not set (`:1628-1629`); advances `input_row += display->row_step / 2` (`:1693`).\n`png_write_image_8bit` (`:1754-1849`): two arms — with alpha (`:1769-1821`, `alphabyte = PNG_DIV257(alpha)`, `UNP_RECIPROCAL` at `:1707`, `png_unpremultiply` at `:1709-1752` with its `component >= alpha || alpha < 128 → 255` and `alpha < 65407` sub-branches) and without alpha (`:1823-1846`, plain `component *= 255; PNG_sRGB_FROM_LINEAR`).\n\n### `png_image_set_PLTE` (`:1851-1995`)\n- `entries = min(colormap_entries, 256)` (`:1856-1857`); `channels = PNG_IMAGE_SAMPLE_CHANNELS(format)`; `afirst` (`:1863-1869`, requires **both** `PNG_FORMAT_BGR_SUPPORTED` and `PNG_SIMPLIFIED_WRITE_AFIRST_SUPPORTED` — note the odd conjunction) and `bgr` (`:1871-1875`).\n- `:1881-1882` `memset(tRNS, 255, 256); memset(palette, 0, sizeof palette);` — both are 256-entry stack arrays.\n- Per entry, top-level split on `format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_LINEAR` (`:1889`):\n  - **LINEAR** (`:1889-1943`): `if ((channels & 1) != 0)` (no alpha) → `channels >= 3` RGB via `PNG_sRGB_FROM_LINEAR(255*entry[...])` with `bgr`/`(2^bgr)` indexing, else gray from `*entry`. Alpha case → `alpha = entry[afirst ? 0 : channels-1]`, `alphabyte = PNG_DIV257(alpha)`, reciprocal `:1922-1923`, `tRNS[i] = alphabyte`, `num_trans = i+1` if `< 255`, then `png_unpremultiply` per channel (RGB at `:1929-1937`, gray at `:1939-1941`).\n  - **sRGB** (`:1945-1977`): `switch (channels)` with fallthroughs — `4` sets `tRNS[i] = entry[afirst?0:3]` then falls into `3` (`blue = entry[afirst+(2^bgr)]`, `green = entry[afirst+1]`, `red = entry[afirst+bgr]`); `2` sets `tRNS[i] = entry[1^afirst]` then falls into `1` (gray from `entry[afirst]`); `default: break`.\n- `:1987-1988` `png_set_PLTE(...)`; `:1990-1992` `if (num_trans > 0) png_set_tRNS(..., tRNS, num_trans, NULL)`; `:1994` **`image->colormap_entries = (png_uint_32)entries;`**.\n- The caller's contract is documented at `:1859`: \"the caller must check for cmap != NULL and entries != 0\" — enforced at `:2059`.\n\n## D.13 `png_image_free`, `png_safe_execute` and longjmp handling\n\n- `png_safe_execute` (`src/pngerror.c:814-847`): saves `image->opaque->error_buf`, `setjmp(safe_jmpbuf)`; on the 0 return installs `error_buf = safe_jmpbuf`, calls `function(arg)`, restores `error_buf`, and `if (result) return 1`. On the failure fallthrough (both a plain `return 0` from the function and an actual `longjmp`), `error_buf` is restored again (`:840`) and **`if (saved_error_buf == NULL) png_image_free(image);`** (`:844-845`) — i.e. only the *outermost* safe_execute frees, which is why the nested `png_safe_execute` calls (e.g. `pngread.c:3105`, `:4029`, `:4042`, `:4060`; `pngwrite.c:2198`, `:2200`) can propagate failure without double-freeing. Returns 0