`PNG_Z_DEFAULT_STRATEGY = 1 (Z_FILTERED)`, `PNG_Z_DEFAULT_NOFILTER_STRATEGY = 0 (Z_DEFAULT_STRATEGY)`, `PNG_TEXT_Z_DEFAULT_COMPRESSION = -1`, `PNG_TEXT_Z_DEFAULT_STRATEGY = 0` (`pnglibconf.h:209-229`).\n\n---\n\n# 1. `png_write_IHDR` — pngwutil.c:688-852\n\n## 1a. Colour-type / bit-depth acceptance matrix (`switch (color_type)` at :699)\n\n| color_type | line | accepted bit_depth | sets `png_ptr->channels` | error branch |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `GRAY` (0) | 701-717 | 1, 2, 4, 8, **16** (16 only under `WRITE_16BIT`, :709) | 1 | `default:` :713 → \"Invalid bit depth for grayscale image\" |\n| `RGB` (2) | 719-728 | 8, **16** (:721-723) | 3 | :724 \"Invalid bit depth for RGB image\" |\n| `PALETTE` (3) | 730-743 | 1, 2, 4, 8 (**never 16**) | 1 | :741 \"Invalid bit depth for paletted image\" |\n| `GRAY_ALPHA` (4) | 745-754 | 8, **16** | 2 | :750 \"Invalid bit depth for grayscale+alpha image\" |\n| `RGB_ALPHA` (6) | 756-765 | 8, **16** | 4 | :761 \"Invalid bit depth for RGBA image\" |\n| anything else (1,5,7,…) | 767-768 | — | — | \"Invalid image color type specified\" |\n\n**→ 15 valid (color_type, bit_depth) rows**: GRAY×{1,2,4,8,16}=5, PALETTE×{1,2,4,8}=4, RGB×{8,16}=2, GRAY_ALPHA×{8,16}=2, RGB_ALPHA×{8,16}=2.\n\n## 1b. Other validation branches (all *warning-only*, i.e. reachable and non-fatal)\n\n* `:771-775` `compression_type != PNG_COMPRESSION_TYPE_BASE(0)` → `png_warning(\"Invalid compression type specified\")` **and silently coerces to 0**.\n* `:786-798` filter_type. The composite condition means `filter_type` is accepted without warning iff:\n  * `filter_type == PNG_FILTER_TYPE_BASE (0)`, **or**\n  * all five MNG conditions hold: `mng_features_permitted & PNG_FLAG_MNG_FILTER_64`, `(mode & PNG_HAVE_PNG_SIGNATURE) == 0`, `color_type ∈ {RGB, RGB_ALPHA}`, `filter_type == PNG_INTRAPIXEL_DIFFERENCING (64)`.\n  * else `png_warning(\"Invalid filter type specified\")` + coerce to 0.\n  * **Note the interaction with `png_write_sig`**: `png_write_sig` (:81-82) only sets `PNG_HAVE_PNG_SIGNATURE` `if (png_ptr->sig_bytes < 3)`. So filter-64 is only reachable when the app called `png_set_sig_bytes(png_ptr, >=3)` (i.e. embedded-in-MNG). Distinct test row.\n* `:800-809` interlace. Under `WRITE_INTERLACING`: `interlace_type ∉ {NONE(0), ADAM7(1)}` → `png_warning(\"Invalid interlace type specified\")` and **coerced to ADAM7**, not NONE.\n\n## 1c. What it sets (:811-827)\n\n`bit_depth`, `color_type`, `interlaced`, `filter_type` (only under `MNG_FEATURES`, :816), `compression_type`, `width`, `height`,\n`pixel_depth = bit_depth * channels`, `rowbytes = PNG_ROWBYTES(pixel_depth, width)`,\n`usr_width = width`, **`usr_bit_depth = bit_depth`**, **`usr_channels = channels`**.\n\nThis is the point at which `usr_*` are reset. Anything that mutates `usr_bit_depth`/`usr_channels` (`png_set_packing` → `usr_bit_depth=8`; `png_set_filler` → `usr_channels=2/4`) must be called **after** `png_write_info`/`png_write_IHDR` or it is wiped. **Ordering axis for the matrix.**\n\nWrites the 13-byte chunk at :839. Then `:851` **`png_ptr->mode = PNG_HAVE_IHDR;` (plain assignment)** — this *clears* `PNG_HAVE_PNG_SIGNATURE` and every other mode bit. `png_write_info_before_PLTE` then re-adds `PNG_WROTE_INFO_BEFORE_PLTE` at pngwrite.c:218.\n\n## 1d. Default filter selection — pngwutil.c:841-849\n\n```c\nif ((png_ptr->do_filter) == PNG_NO_FILTERS)   /* i.e. do_filter == 0 */\n{\n   if (png_ptr->color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE ||\n       png_ptr->bit_depth < 8)\n      png_ptr->do_filter = PNG_FILTER_NONE;   /* 0x08 */\n   else\n      png_ptr->do_filter = PNG_ALL_FILTERS;   /* 0xF8 */\n}\n```\n\nNote the predicate is on colour type / bit depth **only — image width and height are irrelevant here** (the shape-based reduction happens later, in `png_write_start_row`, §3/§9).\n\nResulting default `do_filter` per row of the 15-row matrix:\n\n| color_type / bit_depth | default `do_filter` |\n|---|---|\n| GRAY 1, 2, 4 | `PNG_FILTER_NONE` (0x08) |\n| GRAY 8, 16 | `PNG_ALL_FILTERS` (0xF8) |\n| PALETTE 1, 2, 4, 8 | `PNG_FILTER_NONE` (all four, because of the PALETTE test) |\n| RGB 8, 16 | `PNG_ALL_FILTERS` |\n| GRAY_ALPHA 8, 16 | `PNG_ALL_FILTERS` |\n| RGB_ALPHA 8, 16 | `PNG_ALL_FILTERS` |\n\nSo: 6 rows get `PNG_FILTER_NONE` (GRAY@1/2/4 + PALETTE@1/2/4/8 — that's 7 actually: 3+4), 8 rows get `PNG_ALL_FILTERS`.\n\nThird branch: **`do_filter != 0` on entry** (app called `png_set_filter` before `png_write_info`) → IHDR leaves it alone. Note that `png_set_filter(png_ptr, 0, PNG_NO_FILTERS)` leaves `do_filter == 0`, so it is **indistinguishable from \"never called\"** and gets overwritten by the defaults above. Same for `png_set_filter(..., PNG_FILTER_VALUE_NONE)` since that constant is also 0. Distinct test rows.\n\n`png_deflate_claim` reads `do_filter` to pick the zlib strategy (§4), so the IHDR default choice also changes the compression strategy: PALETTE/low-bit-depth default → `do_filter == PNG_FILTER_NONE` → `PNG_Z_DEFAULT_NOFILTER_STRATEGY (0)`; everything else → `PNG_Z_DEFAULT_STRATEGY (1)`.\n\n---\n\n# 2. `png_set_filter` — pngwrite.c:1057-1181\n\nSignature: `void png_set_filter(png_structrp, int method, int filters)`.\n\n## 2a. Method check\n\n* `:1062-1063` `png_ptr == NULL` → return.\n* `:1065-1069` (MNG) `if ((mng_features_permitted & PNG_FLAG_MNG_FILTER_64) != 0 && method == PNG_INTRAPIXEL_DIFFERENCING (64)) method = PNG_FILTER_TYPE_BASE;` — i.e. method 64 is *silently accepted* when MNG filter-64 is permitted.\n* `:1071` `method == PNG_FILTER_TYPE_BASE (0)` → the main path.\n* `:1179-1180` **else → `png_error(\"Unknown custom filter method\")`** (hard error, not app_error). So method ∈ {0} always, {0, 64} with MNG permitted.\n\n## 2b. `switch (filters & (PNG_ALL_FILTERS | 0x07))` — :1073\n\n`PNG_ALL_FILTERS = 0xF8`, so the mask is `0xFF`. Cases:\n\n| case | line | action |\n|---|---|---|\n| 5, 6, 7 | 1076-1078 | `png_app_error(\"Unknown row filter for method 0\")` (**fatal in this build**), then FALLTHROUGH |\n| `PNG_FILTER_VALUE_NONE` (0) | 1081-1082 | `do_filter = PNG_FILTER_NONE (0x08)` |\n| `PNG_FILTER_VALUE_SUB` (1) | 1085-1086 | `do_filter = PNG_FILTER_SUB (0x10)` |\n| `PNG_FILTER_VALUE_UP` (2) | 1088-1089 | `do_filter = PNG_FILTER_UP (0x20)` |\n| `PNG_FILTER_VALUE_AVG` (3) | 1091-1092 | `do_filter = PNG_FILTER_AVG (0x40)` |\n| `PNG_FILTER_VALUE_PAETH` (4) | 1094-1095 | `do_filter = PNG_FILTER_PAETH (0x80)` |\n| default (all mask forms 0x08..0xF8, and 0) | 1097-1098 | `do_filter = (png_byte)filters` |\n\n**Important, load-bearing quirk:** with `PNG_WRITE_FILTER_SUPPORTED` defined, control falls out of the switch into the block at :1105-1177, whose **last statement (:1176) is `png_ptr->do_filter = (png_byte)filters;` — unconditionally overwriting everything the switch just assigned.**\n\nSo the *effective* semantics of `png_set_filter` in this build is `do_filter = (png_byte)filters`, and the `PNG_FILTER_VALUE_*` translation at :1081-1095 is dead. Concretely:\n\n* `png_set_filter(p, 0, PNG_FILTER_VALUE_SUB /*1*/)` → `do_filter == 1`, **not** `0x10`. In `png_write_find_filter` `filter_to_do = 1` matches no `PNG_FILTER_*` bit at all, so the row is written unfiltered with filter byte 0. Same for values 2, 3, 4.\n* `png_set_filter(p, 0, PNG_FILTER_VALUE_NONE /*0*/)` → `do_filter == 0 == PNG_NO_FILTERS`, which then gets re-defaulted by `png_write_IHDR` if called before `png_write_info` (§1d).\n* Values 5/6/7 are fatal (`png_app_error`) before that.\n\n**Test rows for `filters`**: `PNG_NO_FILTERS(0)`, each single mask bit `0x08/0x10/0x20/0x40/0x80`, `PNG_FAST_FILTERS(0x38)`, `PNG_ALL_FILTERS(0xF8)`, mixed pairs, plus the value forms `1,2,3,4` (all behave as \"no filtering\"), plus `5,6,7` (fatal).\n\n## 2c. Before vs after `png_write_IHDR`/`png_write_info` — three distinct states\n\nThe `if (png_ptr->row_buf != NULL)` block (:1119-1175) discriminates:\n\n1. **Before `png_write_info`**: `row_buf == NULL`, `usr_channels`/`usr_bit_depth`/`width`/`height` all still 0. Block skipped. `do_filter = filters`. Then `png_write_IHDR` re-defaults it **only if `filters == 0`**.\n2. **After `png_write_info` but before the first `png_write_row`**: `row_buf` is still NULL (it is allocated in `png_write_start_row`, called from `png_write_row` at pngwrite.c:802). Block still skipped, but `width`/`height`/`usr_*` are now valid. `do_filter = filters` and IHDR will not touch it. **This is the normal, intended call site.**\n3. **After the first `png_write_row`** (`row_buf != NULL`), i.e. mid-image: the full block runs:\n   * `:1128-1129` `if (height == 1) filters &= ~(UP|AVG|PAETH)`\n   * `:1131-1132` `if (width == 1) filters &= ~(SUB|AVG|PAETH)`\n   * `:1134-1143` `if ((filters & (UP|AVG|PAETH)) != 0 && prev_row == NULL)` → `png_app_warning(\"png_set_filter: UP/AVG/PAETH cannot be added after start\")` (**fatal in this build unless benign errors allowed**) then `filters &= ~(UP|AVG|PAETH)`. Reachable with fully valid input: start with `PNG_FILTER_NONE`, write one row, then try to add `PNG_FILTER_UP`. `prev_row` is only allocated (pngwutil.c:1993-1995) if the *initial* filter set contained AVG|UP|PAETH.\n   * `:1145-1157` `num_filters` count over SUB/UP/AVG/PAETH (0..4).\n   * `:1162-1163` `buf_size = PNG_ROWBYTES(usr_channels * usr_bit_depth, width) + 1`\n   * `:1165-1167` `if (try_row == NULL)` → malloc.\n   * `:1169-1174` `if (num_filters > 1 && tst_row == NULL)` → malloc.\n   * `:1176` `do_filter = filters`.\n\n   Note: with a `PNG_FILTER_VALUE_*` argument (1..4) in this state, `filters & (UP|AVG|PAETH) == 0`, so the warning branch is *not* taken — another distinct path.\n\n## 2d. Weighted filtering / `png_set_filter_heuristics`\n\n`PNG_WRITE_WEIGHTED_FILTER_SUPPORTED` **is** defined (`pnglibconf.h:161`), but in this version the feature is **completely gutted**:\n\n* `pngwrite.c:1183-1212`: `png_set_filter_heuristics` (`:1186-1196`, `PNG_FLOATING_POINT_SUPPORTED`) and `png_set_filter_heuristics_fixed` (`:1200-1210`, `PNG_FIXED_POINT_SUPPORTED`) are **pure no-op stubs** — bodies are nothing but `PNG_UNUSED(...)` for all five parameters. They do not validate `heuristic_method`, do not store weights or costs, do not warn, and cannot fail. There are **zero branches** in them (only the `png_ptr == NULL`-less body).\n* There is **no weighted-filter code in `png_write_find_filter`** at all (pngwutil.c:2548-2741 contains no `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_WEIGHTED_FILTER_SUPPORTED`). No `filter_weights`, `filter_costs`, `inv_filter_weights`, `heuristic_method` or `num_prev_filters` fields are referenced anywhere in the write path.\n\n**→ For the matrix: `png_set_filter_heuristics{,_fixed}` needs exactly one row each (\"calling it has no observable effect, whatever the arguments\"), and there are no weighted-filter branches to cover in `png_write_find_filter`.**\n\n---\n\n# 3. `png_write_find_filter` — pngwutil.c:2548-2741\n\nTwo top-level compile variants; in this build the `#else` (`PNG_WRITE_FILTER_SUPPORTED`) arm at :2553-2740 is live. (`:2552` is the no-filter build: unconditional `png_write_filtered_row(png_ptr, row_buf, rowbytes+1)`.)\n\nSetup:\n* `:2554` `filter_to_do = png_ptr->do_filter`\n* `:2564` **`bpp = (row_info->pixel_depth + 7) >> 3`** — this is the entire `pixel_depth < 8` handling: for pixel_depth 1, 2, 4 and 8 `bpp == 1`, so Sub/Avg/Paeth compare against the immediately-preceding *byte*. There is no other sub-8-bit special-casing anywhere in the filter code. (For 16-bit RGBA `bpp == 8`, 16-bit RGB `6`, 16-bit GA `4`, 16-bit G `2`, 8-bit RGB `3`, 8-bit RGBA `4`, 8-bit GA `2`.)\n* `:2567` `mins = PNG_SIZE_MAX - 256`\n* `:2598` `best_row = png_ptr->row_buf`\n\n## Branch enumeration\n\n**A. Overflow guard — `:2600-2606`** `if (PNG_SIZE_MAX/128 <= row_bytes)` → `filter_to_do &= 0U - filter_to_do` (keep only the lowest set bit) and `mins` stays at its huge initial value. On LP64 this needs `row_bytes >= 2^57`; **unreachable with valid input**. On a 32-bit build it needs `row_bytes >= 33554432`.\n\n**B. \"None\" cost loop — `:2607-2631`** `else if ((filter_to_do & PNG_FILTER_NONE) != 0 && filter_to_do != PNG_FILTER_NONE)` — i.e. NONE is in the set **and it is not the only member**. Sums `min(v, 256-v)` over the whole row (`:2619-2627`, `PNG_USE_ABS` variant at :2623 vs the ternary at :2625) and sets `mins = sum`.\n   * The third sub-case (`filter_to_do == PNG_FILTER_NONE` exactly, i.e. 0x08) skips this loop entirely — `mins` stays huge, `best_row` stays `row_buf`, and none of the SUB/UP/AVG/PAETH branches fire → fast path, no cost computation at all. **This is the \"filter_none only\" fast path.**\n   * A fourth sub-case: `filter_to_do` with NONE absent (e.g. `PNG_FILTER_SUB|PNG_FILTER_UP` = 0x30) → also skips the loop, `mins` huge, so the first candidate filter tested always wins its `sum < mins` comparison.\n\n**C. Sub — `:2634-2658`**\n   * `:2634` `filter_to_do == PNG_FILTER_SUB` (exactly 0x10) → `png_setup_sub_row_only(png_ptr, bpp, row_bytes)` (:2316-2336, no cost accumulation, no early exit), `best_row = try_row`.\n   * `:2641` `else if ((filter_to_do & PNG_FILTER_SUB) != 0)` → `png_setup_sub_row(png_ptr, bpp, row_bytes, lmins=mins)` (:2277-2314). Two inner loops: `i < bpp` (raw copy, :2288-2297) then `i < row_bytes` (`*rp - *lp`, :2299-2311) with **early `break` when `sum > lmins`** (:2309-2310). Then `if (sum < mins)` → update `mins`, `best_row = try_row`, and if `tst_row != NULL` swap `try_row`/`tst_row` (:2652-2656).\n   * Neither → skipped.\n\n**D. Up — `:2661-2684`** same three-way shape: `== PNG_FILTER_UP` → `png_setup_up_row_only` (:2365-2379); `& PNG_FILTER_UP` → `png_setup_up_row` (:2338-2363, single loop over `row_bytes`, `*rp - *pp`, early break on `sum > lmins`); else skip. **Requires `prev_row != NULL`** (allocated in `png_write_start_row` only when the filter set includes AVG|UP|PAETH) — hence the `png_set_filter` guard in §2c.\n\n**E. Avg — `:2687-2710`** `== PNG_FILTER_AVG` → `png_setup_avg_row_only` (:2421-2441); `& PNG_FILTER_AVG` → `png_setup_avg_row` (:2381-2419) — first loop `i < bpp` uses `*rp - *pp/2` (no left neighbour), second uses `*rp - (*pp + *lp)/2`, early break; else skip.\n\n**F. Paeth — `:2713-2735`** `== PNG_FILTER_PAETH` → `png_setup_paeth_row_only` (:2504-2545); `& PNG_FILTER_PAETH` → `png_setup_paeth_row` (:2443-2503) — first loop `i < bpp` uses `*rp - *pp`, second computes the Paeth predictor (`:2469-2490`, three-way `p = (pa <= pb && pa <= pc) ? a : (pb <= pc) ? b : c` — three sub-branches, plus the `PNG_USE_ABS` vs manual-abs variants at :2478-2486), early break; else skip.\n   * **Bug worth a dedicated test row:** the Paeth acceptance block at `:2726-2734` updates `best_row` (and swaps try/tst) **but does not assign `mins = sum`**, unlike Sub/Up/Avg. Benign only because Paeth is evaluated last; a test that asserts on the chosen filter byte for rows where Paeth wins is still meaningful.\n\n**G. Write — `:2738`** `png_write_filtered_row(png_ptr, best_row, row_info->rowbytes + 1)`.\n\n`png_write_filtered_row` (:2745-2779) branches:\n* `:2753` `png_compress_IDAT(..., Z_NO_FLUSH)`.\n* `:2757-2764` `if (prev_row != NULL)` → swap `prev_row` ↔ `row_buf`. (Under `WRITE_FILTER` only.)\n* `:2768` `png_write_finish_row`.\n* `:2771-2777` (`WRITE_FLUSH`) `flush_rows++`; `if (flush_dist > 0 && flush_rows >= flush_dist) png_write_flush(png_ptr)`.\n\n**Distinct `do_filter` values that produce structurally different paths**: `0x08` (fast path), `0x10`, `0x20`, `0x40`, `0x80` (each the \"_only\" no-cost path), and every multi-bit combination — with the special sub-case of \"NONE present + ≥1 other\" vs \"NONE absent + ≥2 others\" (whether `mins` is seeded). Also `do_filter ∈ {1,2,3,4}` from the `PNG_FILTER_VALUE_*` quirk (§2b): no branch fires, `best_row == row_buf`, filter byte 0.\n\n---\n\n# 4. Compression configuration\n\n## 4a. Setters — pngwrite.c\n\nAll under `PNG_WRITE_CUSTOMIZE_COMPRESSION_SUPPORTED` (:1214-1299):\n\n| function | line | branches |\n|---|---|---|\n| `png_set_compression_level` | 1215-1224 | only `png_ptr == NULL`. **No clamping, no validation** — stores `zlib_level` verbatim; an out-of-range value fails later inside `deflateInit2` → `png_zstream_error`. |\n| `png_set_compression_mem_level` | 1226-1235 | only NULL check. **No clamping.** |\n| `png_set_compression_strategy` | 1237-1249 | only NULL check; **always sets `PNG_FLAG_ZLIB_CUSTOM_STRATEGY`** then `zlib_strategy = strategy`. The flag is the branch driver in `png_deflate_claim` (:353). Note there is **no way to unset the flag** once set. |\n| `png_set_compression_window_bits` | 1254-1281 | 3 branches: `>15` → `png_warning(\"Only compression windows <= 32k supported by PNG\")` + clamp to 15 (:1268-1272); `<8` → `png_warning(\"Only compression windows >= 256 supported by PNG\")` + clamp to 8 (:1274-1278); else store as-is. Range 8..15. |\n| `png_set_compression_method` | 1283-1298 | `method != 8` → `png_warning(\"Only compression method 8 is supported by PNG\")` **but stores it anyway** (:1297) → later `deflateInit2` failure. |\n\nText equivalents under `PNG_WRITE_CUSTOMIZE_ZTXT_COMPRESSION_SUPPORTED` (:1302-1375) are byte-for-byte parallel: `png_set_text_compression_level` (:1303, no validation), `_mem_level` (:1314, no validation), `_strategy` (:1325, **no `CUSTOM_STRATEGY` flag** — text strategy is always taken from `zlib_text_strategy`), `_window_bits` (:1339-1360, same two warn+clamp branches), `_method` (:1362-1374, same warn-but-store).\n\n`png_set_compression_buffer_size` — **pngset.c:1796-1857**. Branches:\n* `size == 0 || size > PNG_UINT_31_MAX` → `png_error(\"invalid compression buffer size\")` (:1804-1805).\n* read struct → sets `IDAT_read_size`, return (:1808-1813).\n* write struct (:1820): `zowner != 0` → `png_warning(\"Compression buffer size cannot be changed because it is in use\")` + return (:1822-1828). **So the call is a no-op once IDAT compression has started.**\n* `size > ZLIB_IO_MAX ((uInt)-1)` → `png_warning(\"Compression buffer size limited to system maximum\")` + clamp (:1830-1836). Unreachable on 32-bit `uInt` + `size_t == 64-bit` only via overflow.\n* `size < 6` → `png_warning(\"Compression buffer size cannot be reduced below 6\")` + **return without changing anything** (:1838-1847). (Comment: deflate can loop forever on `SYNC_FLUSH` below 6.)\n* `zbuffer_size != size` → free `zbuffer_list` and set new `zbuffer_size` (:1849-1853); else no-op.\n\nDefault `zbuffer_size = PNG_ZBUF_SIZE = 8192` (pngwrite.c:571). This directly determines IDAT chunk sizes (`png_compress_IDAT` emits one IDAT per full buffer), so it's a strong observable-output axis: e.g. `{6, 7, 1024, 8192 (default), 65536}`.\n\n## 4b. `png_deflate_claim` — pngwutil.c:308-452\n\n* `:312-341` `zowner != 0` (stream already claimed). Builds the \"`<chunk>: <owner> using zstream`\" message (:315-325). Then **`#if PNG_RELEASE_BUILD`** … `#else png_error(png_ptr, msg)` — since `PNG_RELEASE_BUILD == 0` in this build, **this is a hard `png_error`**; the release-only recovery path (warn; refuse to steal from `png_IDAT` returning `Z_STREAM_ERROR`; else `zowner = 0`) at :328-337 is **dead code here**. Reachable only via an internal-ordering bug, not valid input.\n* `:344-347` seeds `level/method/windowBits/memLevel` from the IDAT set.\n* `:351-361` **`owner == png_IDAT`** strategy selection — three branches:\n  1. `flags & PNG_FLAG_ZLIB_CUSTOM_STRATEGY` → `strategy = zlib_strategy`.\n  2. `else if (do_filter != PNG_FILTER_NONE)` → `PNG_Z_DEFAULT_STRATEGY (1 = Z_FILTERED)`.\n  3. `else` → `PNG_Z_DEFAULT_NOFILTER_STRATEGY (0 = Z_DEFAULT_STRATEGY)`.\n  Note branch 2's test is `!= PNG_FILTER_NONE` (`!= 0x08`), so `do_filter == 0`, `1..4`, or any multi-bit set all take branch 2 even when no filtering actually occurs.\n* `:363-379` **`owner != png_IDAT`** (iCCP/zTXt/iTXt): under `WRITE_CUSTOMIZE_ZTXT_COMPRESSION` (live) *all five* params are replaced by the `zlib_text_*` values (:366-370). The `#else` arm (:377) would only override `strategy`.\n* `:388-402` **window-bits reduction**: `if (data_size <= 16384)` then `half_window_size = 1U << (windowBits-1); while (data_size + 262 <= half_window_size) { half >>= 1; --windowBits; }`. The `+262` accounts for deflate's extra window need. This is where a small image silently gets a smaller `windowBits` than requested. Note `windowBits` can be driven down to **8**; when `windowBits == 8` zlib's `deflateInit2` internally promotes to 9 — see 4c.\n* `:405-416` **re-init check**: `if ((flags & PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_INITIALIZED) && any of zlib_set_{level,method,window_bits,mem_level,strategy} differs)` → `deflateEnd`; `if (deflateEnd != Z_OK) png_warning(\"deflateEnd failed (ignored)\")`; clear the INITIALIZED flag.\n* `:421-424` clears `next_in/avail_in/next_out/avail_out`.\n* `:429-439` `if (INITIALIZED) ret = deflateReset(...)` **else** `ret = deflateInit2(&zstream, level, method, windowBits, memLevel, strategy)`; on `Z_OK` set INITIALIZED.\n* `:444-448` `ret == Z_OK` → `zowner = owner`; else `png_zstream_error(png_ptr, ret)`.\n\n**Matrix implication:** the pairing (IDAT compression settings, text compression settings) matters because the *same* z_stream is reused; writing a zTXt with different params than IDAT forces a `deflateEnd`+`deflateInit2` cycle (:412) rather than a `deflateReset` (:430). Two distinct paths, both reachable with valid input. Note the fields `zlib_set_*` are never assigned in this file — grep shows they are only *read* at :406-410, so the \"check against previous initialized values\" comparison uses whatever they were initialised to (0) and will therefore fire a `deflateEnd` on the second claim whenever any of level/method/windowBits/memLevel/strategy is non-zero. Worth an explicit test row.\n\n## 4c. `optimize_cmf` — pngwutil.c:266-304 (`PNG_WRITE_OPTIMIZE_CMF_SUPPORTED`)\n\nPost-hoc rewrite of the two-byte zlib header to advertise a smaller window:\n* `:272` `if (data_size <= 16384)` — else no change (windowBits must stay 15).\n* `:276` `if ((z_cmf & 0x0f) == 8 && (z_cmf & 0xf0) <= 0x70)` — CM must be deflate(8) and CINFO ≤ 7; else no change.\n* `:284` `if (data_size <= half_z_window_size)` (where `half_z_window_size = 1 << (z_cinfo + 7)`) — else no change.\n* `:288-293` `do { half >>= 1; --z_cinfo; } while (z_cinfo > 0 && data_size <= half)` — the loop stops at `z_cinfo == 0`, i.e. **windowBits 8 is representable in the header even though zlib's deflateInit2 promotes 8→9 internally**; this is exactly the \"window_bits == 8 → 9\" issue, and `optimize_cmf` is what makes the emitted stream self-consistent.\n* `:295-300` rewrite `data[0]` (CMF) and `data[1]` (FLG) fixing the mod-31 check value: `tmp = data[1] & 0xe0; tmp += 0x1f - ((z_cmf << 8) + tmp) % 0x1f;`\n\nCall sites — three, all conditional:\n1. `png_text_compress`, pngwutil.c:636-639 — only on the success path (`ret == Z_STREAM_END && input_len == 0`), called with `comp->output` and **`comp->input_len`** (uncompressed length).\n2. `png_compress_IDAT`, :1000-1004 — `if ((mode & PNG_HAVE_IDAT) == 0 && compression_type == PNG_COMPRESSION_TYPE_BASE)` i.e. only the *first* IDAT buffer, with `png_image_size(png_ptr)`.\n3. `png_compress_IDAT`, :1047-1051 — same guard, on the `Z_STREAM_END && flush == Z_FINISH` tail (small images where the first and last IDAT are the same buffer).\n\n## 4d. `png_image_size` — pngwutil.c:220-257\n\n* `:228` `if (rowbytes < 32768 && h < 32768)`:\n  * `:230` `interlaced != 0` → loop `pass 0..6`, `pw = PNG_PASS_COLS(w, pass)`, `if (pw > 0) cb_base += (PNG_ROWBYTES(pd, pw)+1) * PNG_PASS_ROWS(h, pass)` — the `pw == 0` skip is a real branch for narrow images (width < 5 skips pass 1, < 3 skips pass 3, < 2 skips pass 5).\n  * `:252` else `return (rowbytes + 1) * h`.\n* `:256` else `return 0xffffffffU` (forces windowBits 15 and disables `optimize_cmf`).\n\n**Matrix axis:** images straddling `rowbytes < 32768`, `height < 32768`, and total sizes straddling 16384 and each `1 << (windowBits-1) - 262` boundary produce different emitted zlib headers.\n\n## 4e. `png_compress_IDAT` — pngwutil.c:931-1070\n\n* `:935` `if (zowner != png_IDAT)` — first-call init:\n  * `:942-947` `if (zbuffer_list == NULL)` malloc one buffer; `else png_free_buffer_list(&zbuffer_list->next)` (trim to one).\n  * `:953-954` `if (png_deflate_claim(png_ptr, png_IDAT, png_image_size(png_ptr)) != Z_OK) png_error(...)`.\n  * `:959-960` set `next_out`/`avail_out`.\n* Main `for(;;)` loop `:969-1069`:\n  * `:974-980` chunk the input to `ZLIB_IO_MAX` per `deflate` call.\n  * `:982` `deflate(&zstream, input_len > 0 ? Z_NO_FLUSH : flush)` — **flush is `Z_NO_FLUSH` for every non-final sub-chunk regardless of the caller's `flush`**.\n  * `:992` `if (avail_out == 0)` → emit an IDAT: `optimize_cmf` guard (:1001), `if (size > 0) png_write_complete_chunk(png_IDAT, ...)` (:1006-1007), `mode |= PNG_HAVE_IDAT`, reset `next_out`/`avail_out`; then `:1017-1018` `if (ret == Z_OK && flush != Z_NO_FLUSH) continue;`\n  * `:1024-1037` `ret == Z_OK`: `if (input_len == 0) { if (flush == Z_FINISH) png_error(\"Z_OK on Z_FINISH with output space\"); return; }` — else loop again.\n  * `:1039-1061` `ret == Z_STREAM_END && flush == Z_FINISH`: emit the tail IDAT (`size = zbuffer_size - avail_out`, `if (size > 0)` guard at :1053 — a zero-size tail emits **no** trailing IDAT), set `mode |= PNG_HAVE_IDAT | PNG_AFTER_IDAT`, **`zowner = 0`** (release), return.\n  * `:1063-1068` else → `png_zstream_error` + `png_error`.\n\nCallers/flush values: `Z_NO_FLUSH` from `png_write_filtered_row` (:2753); `Z_SYNC_FLUSH` from `png_write_flush` (pngwrite.c:979); `Z_FINISH` from `png_write_finish_row` (:2091). **The `Z_SYNC_FLUSH` path is the only one that can leave `zowner == png_IDAT` while emitting a complete IDAT and re-entering — this is exactly the flush interaction to test** (see §10).\n\n---\n\n# 5. `png_do_write_transformations` (pngwtran.c:499-572) + pngtrans.c\n\n## 5a. Gating in `png_write_row`\n\npngwrite.c:907-911: `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_TRANSFORMS_SUPPORTED` `if (png_ptr->transformations != 0) png_do_write_transformations(png_ptr, &row_info);`\n\n`row_info` is built fresh **per row** at pngwrite.c:875-880 from `color_type`, `usr_width`, `usr_channels`, `usr_bit_depth`, with `pixel_depth = bit_depth*channels` and `rowbytes = PNG_ROWBYTES(pixel_depth, width)`. If interlacing with `PNG_INTERLACE` set, `png_do_write_interlace` has already rewritten `row_info.width`/`rowbytes` (pngwrite.c:897).\n\nPost-condition check at pngwrite.c:916-918: `if (row_info.pixel_depth != png_ptr->pixel_depth || row_info.pixel_depth != png_ptr->transformed_pixel_depth) png_error(\"internal write transform logic error\")`. `transformed_pixel_depth` is set to `png_ptr->pixel_depth` in `png_write_start_row` (pngwutil.c:1944). **This means the *net* effect of all transformations must bring `pixel_depth` back to the IHDR value** — e.g. PACK must be used with `usr_bit_depth == 8` and IHDR bit_depth < 8; FILLER must be used with `usr_channels == channels+1`. Any mismatch is a fatal error, and this is the single most common way a \"valid-looking\" configuration blows up.\n\n## 5b. Exact order and gating (pngwtran.c)\n\n| # | line | transform | flag | gate inside the do_ function | no-op when |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 507-521 | user transform | `PNG_USER_TRANSFORM` | `write_user_transform_fn != NULL` (:509) | fn is NULL |\n| 2 | 523-527 | filler strip | `PNG_FILLER` | `png_do_strip_channel(row_info, buf, !(flags & PNG_FLAG_FILLER_AFTER))` | see below |\n| 3 | 529-532 | packswap | `PNG_PACKSWAP` | `png_do_packswap` requires `row_info->bit_depth < 8` (pngtrans.c:487) and ∈{1,2,4} (:493-503) | bit_depth ≥ 8, or 3/5/6/7 |\n| 4 | 534-538 | pack | `PNG_PACK` | `png_do_pack` requires `row_info->bit_depth == 8 && row_info->channels == 1` (pngwtran.c:28-29), and `bit_depth` arg (= `png_ptr->bit_depth`) ∈ {1,2,4} (:31-152, `default: break` at :150) | channels ≠ 1, row bit_depth ≠ 8, or target depth 8/16 |\n| 5 | 540-545 | 16-bit byte swap | `PNG_SWAP_BYTES` | `png_do_swap` requires `row_info->bit_depth == 16` (pngtrans.c:351) | bit_depth ≠ 16 |\n| 6 | 547-551 | shift | `PNG_SHIFT` | `png_do_shift` requires `row_info->color_type != PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE` (pngwtran.c:176) | palette |\n| 7 | 553-556 | swap alpha | `PNG_SWAP_ALPHA` | `png_do_write_swap_alpha` requires `color_type ∈ {RGB_ALPHA, GRAY_ALPHA}` (pngwtran.c:314, :359) | GRAY/RGB/PALETTE |\n| 8 | 558-561 | invert alpha | `PNG_INVERT_ALPHA` | `png_do_write_invert_alpha` requires `color_type ∈ {RGB_ALPHA, GRAY_ALPHA}` (pngwtran.c:408, :455) | GRAY/RGB/PALETTE |\n| 9 | 563-566 | bgr | `PNG_BGR` | `png_do_bgr` requires `color_type & PNG_COLOR_MASK_COLOR` and `bit_depth ∈ {8,16}` and `color_type ∈ {RGB, RGB_ALPHA}` (pngtrans.c:652-718) | GRAY/GRAY_ALPHA; **PALETTE has the COLOR mask set but matches neither inner `color_type` test → no-op** |\n| 10 | 568-571 | invert mono | `PNG_INVERT_MONO` | `png_do_invert`: `GRAY` → invert all `rowbytes` (any bit depth, pngtrans.c:297); `GRAY_ALPHA && bit_depth==8` → every 2nd byte (:310); `GRAY_ALPHA && bit_depth==16` → bytes 0,1 of each 4 (:325) | RGB, RGB_ALPHA, PALETTE |\n\n## 5c. Combinations that are silent no-ops (high-value negative test rows)\n\n* **PACKSWAP + PACK together**: `png_set_packing` sets `usr_bit_depth = 8` (pngtrans.c:60), so `row_info->bit_depth == 8` when packswap runs at step 3, and `png_do_packswap`'s `bit_depth < 8` test fails ⇒ **packswap is a no-op whenever packing is also enabled**. Only after step 4 is the row actually sub-8-bit. This ordering (packswap *before* pack) is a genuine libpng quirk.\n* **PACKSWAP alone with a sub-8-bit IHDR and no packing**: `png_set_packswap` only sets the flag `if (png_ptr->bit_depth < 8)` (pngtrans.c:76), so it is a no-op unless `png_write_info` already ran with bit_depth ∈ {1,2,4}. Ordering axis.\n* **SWAP alone**: `png_set_swap` only sets the flag `if (png_ptr->bit_depth == 16)` (pngtrans.c:41). Ordering axis (must be after `png_write_info`).\n* **PACK alone with IHDR bit_depth 8 or 16**: flag never set (pngtrans.c:56).\n* **SHIFT on PALETTE**: flag set (`png_set_shift` does not exclude palette; pngtrans.c:95-106 validates against `bit_depth` only), but `png_do_shift` returns immediately (:176) ⇒ no-op.\n* **BGR on PALETTE**: no-op (see table).\n* **INVERT_MONO on GRAY_ALPHA with bit_depth 1/2/4**: impossible (IHDR rejects), but INVERT_MONO on RGB/RGBA/PALETTE is a silent no-op.\n* **SWAP_ALPHA / INVERT_ALPHA on non-alpha types**: silent no-ops.\n* **SWAP + SHIFT at 16-bit**: SWAP runs *first* (step 5) then SHIFT (step 6) reads via `png_get_uint_16` (big-endian, pngwtran.c:288) — so the shift operates on byte-swapped data. Deterministic but almost certainly not what a caller intends; a distinct data-changing row.\n* **FILLER + PACK**: `png_set_filler` rejects low-bit-depth gray outright (pngtrans.c:196-206, `png_app_error`), so the combination is not constructible for GRAY<8.\n\n## 5d. `png_do_shift` internal branches (pngwtran.c:170-304)\n\nPer-channel `shift_start[]`/`shift_dec[]` construction: colour (`COLOR_MASK_COLOR`) → 3 entries from red/green/blue (:181-194), else 1 entry from gray (:196-201); plus 1 entry from alpha if `COLOR_MASK_ALPHA` (:203-208). So `channels` ∈ {1,2,3,4}.\n\nThen three mutually exclusive depth paths:\n* `:211-246` `bit_depth < 8` (gray only). Mask sub-branches: `bit_depth->gray == 1 && row bit_depth == 2` → `mask = 0x55`; `row bit_depth == 4 && gray == 3` → `mask = 0x11`; else `mask = 0xff` (:218-225). Inner replication loop `for (j = shift_start[0]; j > -shift_dec[0]; j -= shift_dec[0])` with `j > 0` / `j <= 0` sub-branches (:235-242).\n* `:248-274` `bit_depth == 8`: per-byte over `channels * width`, `c = i % channels`.\n* `:276-302` `bit_depth == 16`: per-16-bit-word.\n\n## 5e. `png_do_strip_channel` (pngtrans.c:521-642) — the FILLER worker\n\nDriven by `at_start = !(flags & PNG_FLAG_FILLER_AFTER)`, i.e. `at_start != 0` ⇔ `PNG_FILLER_BEFORE`.\n* `channels == 2` (:539): `bit_depth == 8` (:541) → strip byte; `at_start != 0` → `++sp`, else `sp += 2; ++dp`. Sets `pixel_depth = 8`. `bit_depth == 16` (:559) → `sp += 2` / `sp += 4; dp += 2`; `pixel_depth = 16`. Any other depth → **`return` without touching rowbytes** (:576-577).\n  Then `channels = 1` and `if (color_type == GRAY_ALPHA) color_type = GRAY` (:582-583).\n* `channels == 4` (:587): parallel, `pixel_depth = 24` / `48`; other depth → `return`; then `channels = 3`, `if (color_type == RGB_ALPHA) color_type = RGB`.\n* `else` (:637-638) → `return` (\"the filler channel has gone already\"): **channels 1 and 3 make FILLER a no-op**.\n* `:641` `row_info->rowbytes = (size_t)(dp - row)`.\nNote the \"For a 1 pixel wide image there is nothing to do\" comment at :550 — `width == 1` is a distinct sub-path (`sp` already ≥ `ep`).\n\n---\n\n# 6. `png_set_filler` / `png_set_add_alpha` on write — pngtrans.c:147-244\n\n`png_set_filler(png_structrp, png_uint_32 filler, int filler_loc)`:\n* `:152-153` NULL → return.\n* `:158` `mode & PNG_IS_READ_STRUCT` → read path (stores `png_ptr->filler`).\n* `:177` **write path** — `switch (png_ptr->color_type)`:\n\n| color_type | line | outcome |\n|---|---|---|\n| `PNG_COLOR_TYPE_RGB` (2) | 185-187 | `usr_channels = 4` — legal |\n| `PNG_COLOR_TYPE_GRAY` (0), `bit_depth >= 8` | 189-194 | `usr_channels = 2` — legal |\n| `PNG_COLOR_TYPE_GRAY`, `bit_depth < 8` | 196-206 | `png_app_error(\"png_set_filler is invalid for low bit depth gray output\")` + return (**fatal in this build**) |\n| PALETTE (3), GRAY_ALPHA (4), RGB_ALPHA (6) | 208-211 | `png_app_error(\"png_set_filler: inappropriate color type\")` + return |\n\n* On success `:222` `transformations |= PNG_FILLER`, then `:224-228` `if (filler_loc == PNG_FILLER_AFTER) flags |= PNG_FLAG_FILLER_AFTER; else flags &= ~PNG_FLAG_FILLER_AFTER;` — **any `filler_loc` other than `PNG_FILLER_AFTER (1)` means BEFORE, including bogus values; no validation.**\n* The `filler` value itself is **completely ignored on write** (only used on read) — it's a strip, not a fill.\n\n**→ legal write configurations: `{RGB, GRAY@8, GRAY@16} × {PNG_FILLER_BEFORE, PNG_FILLER_AFTER}` = 6 rows.** Before/after values: `usr_channels` goes `3 → 4` (RGB) or `1 → 2` (GRAY); `usr_bit_depth` unchanged; `png_ptr->channels`/`pixel_depth`/`rowbytes` unchanged. Ordering: must be called **after** `png_write_info` (before it, `color_type` is 0 = GRAY and `bit_depth` is 0 < 8 ⇒ fatal `png_app_error`), and after it `usr_channels` survives because IHDR already ran.\n\n`png_set_add_alpha` (:232-244): calls `png_set_filler`, then `if ((transformations & PNG_FILLER) != 0) transformations |= PNG_ADD_ALPHA`. On write `PNG_ADD_ALPHA` is **never read** by any write-path code — so on write `png_set_add_alpha` ≡ `png_set_filler`. Two branches: filler succeeded / filler already-set-from-a-previous-call.\n\n---\n\n# 7. Chunk write order and `valid` gating\n\n## 7a. `png_write_info_before_PLTE` — pngwrite.c:82-220\n\nGuard `:90` `if ((png_ptr->mode & PNG_WROTE_INFO_BEFORE_PLTE) == 0)` — the whole body is idempotent; a second call is a no-op. Order:\n\n1. `:93` `png_write_sig(png_ptr)` — unconditional.\n2. `:96-102` (MNG) `if ((mode & PNG_HAVE_PNG_SIGNATURE) != 0 && mng_features_permitted != 0)` → `png_warning(\"MNG features are not allowed in a PNG datastream\")` and **`mng_features_permitted = 0`**. Reachable with valid input: `png_permit_mng_features(...)` + default `sig_bytes == 0`. This is what makes filter-64 require `png_set_sig_bytes(>=3)`.\n3. `:106-114` `png_write_IHDR(...)` from `info_ptr->{width,height,bit_depth,color_type,compression_type,filter_type,interlace_type}`.\n4. `:140` **unknown chunks at `PNG_HAVE_IHDR`** — written *first*, before all colourspace chunks (PNG v3 precedence rationale in the comment at :131-139).\n5. `:152-153` **sBIT** — `info_ptr->valid & PNG_INFO_sBIT`. Deliberately before cICP (comment :144-151).\n6. `:167-170` **cLLI** — `PNG_INFO_cLLI`.\n7. `:173-181` **mDCV** — `PNG_INFO_mDCV`.\n8. `:185-192` **cICP** — `PNG_INFO_cICP` (\"Priority 4\").\n9. `:196-200` **iCCP** — `PNG_INFO_iCCP` (\"Priority 3\").\n10. `:204-205` **sRGB** — `PNG_INFO_sRGB` (\"Priority 2\").\n11. `:209-210` **gAMA** — `PNG_INFO_gAMA` (\"Priority 1\").\n12. `:214-215` **cHRM** — `PNG_INFO_cHRM` (\"also priority 1\").\n13. `:218` `mode |= PNG_WROTE_INFO_BEFORE_PLTE`.\n\nNote: unlike older libpng there is **no `PNG_COLORSPACE_INVALID` re-check** in the emitted code (the comment at :123-128 refers to it but the `valid` flag is the only gate).\n\n## 7b. `png_write_info` — pngwrite.c:222-384\n\n1. `:234` `png_write_info_before_PLTE(png_ptr, info_ptr)`.\n2. `:236-241` **PLTE**: `valid & PNG_INFO_PLTE` → `png_write_PLTE`; **`else if (info_ptr->color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE) png_error(\"Valid palette required for paletted images\")`**; else nothing.\n3. `:244-264` **tRNS**: `valid & PNG_INFO_tRNS`. Nested sub-branch `:248-260` (`WRITE_INVERT_ALPHA`): `if ((transformations & PNG_INVERT_ALPHA) != 0 && info_ptr->color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE)` → **in-place inverts `info_ptr->trans_alpha[0..min(num_trans, PNG_MAX_PALETTE_LENGTH)-1]` to `255 - x`**. This mutates the caller's info struct and is *not* idempotent — a distinct and important test row (palette + `png_set_invert_alpha` + tRNS). Then `png_write_tRNS`.\n4. `:267-268` **bKGD** — `PNG_INFO_bKGD`.\n5. `:272-276` **eXIf** — `PNG_INFO_eXIf`; sets `mode |= PNG_WROTE_eXIf`.\n6. `:280-281` **hIST** — `PNG_INFO_hIST`, passes `info_ptr->num_palette` as `num_hist`.\n7. `:285-287` **oFFs** — `PNG_INFO_oFFs`.\n8. `:291-294` **pCAL** — `PNG_INFO_pCAL`.\n9. `:298-300` **sCAL** — `PNG_INFO_sCAL`.\n10. `:304-306` **pHYs** — `PNG_INFO_pHYs`.\n11. `:310-314` **tIME** — `PNG_INFO_tIME`; sets `mode |= PNG_WROTE_tIME`.\n12. `:318-320` **sPLT** — `PNG_INFO_sPLT`, loops `i < info_ptr->splt_palettes_num`.\n13. `:325-378` **text loop** `for (i = 0; i < info_ptr->num_text; i++)` — **not gated by any `valid` flag**, gated per-entry on `info_ptr->text[i].compression`:\n    * `> 0` → `png_write_iTXt` (:334-339); then `compression` is rewritten to `PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_NONE_WR` or `_zTXt_WR` (:341-344) so the entry is not re-written by `png_write_end`.\n    * `== PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt (1)` → `png_write_zTXt` (:355-356), mark `_zTXt_WR`.\n    * `== PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_NONE (-1)` → `png_write_tEXt` (:368-370), mark `_NONE_WR`.\n    * anything else (already-`_WR` values, i.e. `-3`/`-2`) → **no chunk written**.\n14. `:382` **unknown chunks at `PNG_HAVE_PLTE`**.\n\n## 7c. Interesting internal branches of the chunk writers (pngwutil.c)\n\n* **`png_write_PLTE` :858-912** — `max_palette_length = (color_type == PALETTE) ? (1 << bit_depth) : PNG_MAX_PALETTE_LENGTH` (:868). Then `:871-887`: `(!(MNG empty-PLTE permitted) && num_pal == 0) || num_pal > max` → PALETTE ⇒ `png_error(\"Invalid number of colors in palette\")`; non-PALETTE ⇒ `png_warning` + **return**. `:889-895` `(color_type & PNG_COLOR_MASK_COLOR) == 0` → `png_warning(\"Ignoring request to write a PLTE chunk in grayscale PNG\")` + return. Sets `num_palette` (:897) — **this is what `png_write_tRNS`, `png_write_hIST` and `png_write_bKGD` validate against**, so PLTE must precede them (it does). `mode |= PNG_HAVE_PLTE` (:911). Test rows: PALETTE@1 with 2/3 entries, @2 with 4/5, @4 with 16/17, @8 with 256/257; RGB with a suggested PLTE.\n* **`png_write_sBIT` :1234-1288** — per colour type: `(color_type & COLOR_MASK_COLOR) != 0` (:1243) → `maxbits = (color_type == PALETTE ? 8 : usr_bit_depth)`; validates red/green/blue each in `1..maxbits` else `png_warning(\"Invalid sBIT depth specified\")` + return; `size = 3`. Else (:1264) validates `gray` in `1..usr_bit_depth`; `size = 1`. Then `(color_type & COLOR_MASK_ALPHA) != 0` (:1276) → validates `alpha`; `buf[size++] = alpha`. **Emitted sizes: GRAY→1, GRAY_ALPHA→2, RGB→3, PALETTE→3, RGB_ALPHA→4.** Note the check is against **`usr_bit_depth`**, so calling `png_set_packing` before `png_write_info` (which resets `usr_bit_depth`) vs after changes the accepted sBIT range.\n* **`png_write_tRNS` :1319-1380** — four colour-type arms:\n  * PALETTE (:1327): `num_trans <= 0 || num_trans > (int)png_ptr->num_palette` → `png_app_warning(\"Invalid number of transparent colors specified\")` + return (**fatal in this build**); else writes `trans_alpha` raw, length `num_trans`.\n  * GRAY (:1341): `tran->gray >= (1 << bit_depth)` → `png_app_warning(\"Ignoring attempt to write tRNS chunk out-of-range for bit_depth\")` + return; else 2 bytes.\n  * RGB (:1356): builds 6 bytes then `if (bit_depth == 8 && (buf[0]|buf[2]|buf[4]) != 0)` → `png_app_warning(\"Ignoring attempt to write 16-bit tRNS chunk when bit_depth is 8\")` + return; else 6 bytes. (Non-`WRITE_16BIT` variant at :1365 drops the depth test.)\n  * GRAY_ALPHA / RGB_ALPHA (:1376) → `png_app_warning(\"Can't write tRNS with an alpha channel\")`, nothing written.\n* **`png_write_bKGD` :1385-1443** — PALETTE arm (:1392) with the MNG empty-PLTE composite guard at :1394-1403 (`png_warning(\"Invalid background palette index\")` + return), 1 byte. Colour arm (:1409): 6 bytes with the same `bit_depth == 8 && high bytes nonzero` warn+return (:1415-1425). Gray arm (:1430): `back->gray >= (1 << bit_depth)` warn+return, else 2 bytes.\n* **`png_write_hIST` :1537-1563** — `num_hist > (int)png_ptr->num_palette` → `png_warning(\"Invalid number of histogram entries specified\")` + return. Writes `num_hist * 2` bytes one 16-bit value at a time.\n* **`png_write_sCAL_s` :1847-1872** — `total_len = strlen(width) + strlen(height) + 2`; **`if (total_len > 64) png_warning(\"Can't write sCAL (buffer too small)\") + return`** (:1860-1863). Reachable with valid input (long ASCII-float strings). Boundary rows at 63/64/65.\n* **`png_write_pCAL` :1782-1842** — `type >= PNG_EQUATION_LAST (4)` → `png_error(\"Unrecognized equation type for pCAL chunk\")` (:1796). Types 0..3 are all accepted and produce **identical control flow**; only `buf[8]` differs. Real branches: `units_len = strlen(units) + (nparams == 0 ? 0 : 1)` (:1807) and the per-parameter `params_len[i] = strlen(params[i]) + (i == nparams-1 ? 0 : 1)` (:1819). `nparams == 0` is a distinct row (mallocs a zero-size array at :1811). Chunk layout: purpose+NUL, X0, X1, type, nparams, units, params.\n* **`png_write_sRGB` :1099-1112** — `srgb_intent >= PNG_sRGB_INTENT_LAST (4)` → `png_warning(\"Invalid sRGB rendering intent specified\")` **but writes the byte anyway**. Valid rows: 0,1,2,3.\n* **`png_write_oFFs` :1762-1778** — `unit_type >= PNG_OFFSET_LAST (2)` → `png_warning` but writes anyway. Valid: 0,1.\n* **`png_write_pHYs` :1877-1894** — `unit_type >= PNG_RESOLUTION_LAST (2)` → `png_warning` but writes anyway. Valid: 0,1.\n* **`png_write_tIME` :1901-1924** — `month > 12 || month < 1 || day > 31 || day < 1 || hour > 23 || second > 60` → `png_warning(\"Invalid time specified for tIME chunk\")` + return. **`minute` is never validated** and `year` is never validated. Boundary rows: second == 60 (leap second, accepted), second == 61 (rejected), minute == 99 (accepted!).\n* **`png_write_cHRM_fixed` :1293-1314** — **no branches at all**; 8 × `png_save_int_32` into a 32-byte buffer, order `whitex, whitey, redx, redy, greenx, greeny, bluex, bluey`. All validation lives in `png_set_cHRM_fixed`/`png_colorspace_set_chromaticities`.\n* **`png_write_gAMA_fixed` :1084-1094** — no branches, 4 bytes.\n* **`png_write_cICP` :1448-1466** — no branches, 4 bytes (`colour_primaries, transfer_function, matrix_coefficients, video_full_range_flag`).\n* **`png_write_cLLI_fixed` :1470-1482** — no branches, 8 bytes (maxCLL, maxFALL).\n* **`png_write_mDCV_fixed` :1486-1510** — no branches, 24 bytes (8 × uint16 chromaticities then maxDL, minDL as uint32).\n* **`png_write_eXIf` :1515-1532** — no branches; **writes `num_exif` bytes one at a time in a loop** (:1525-1529), i.e. `num_exif` calls to `png_write_chunk_data`. `num_exif == 0` produces a zero-length eXIf. Performance/behaviour axis.\n* **`png_write_iCCP` :1117-1174** — five `png_error` validations, all reachable only with a malformed profile (so out of scope for \"valid configurations\", but they define what \"valid\" means): `profile == NULL` (:1131), `profile_len < 132` (:1134), `png_get_uint_32(profile) != profile_len` (:1137), `*(profile+8) > 3 && (profile_len & 3)` (:1140-1142), redundant embedded-length recheck (:1145-1148), `png_check_keyword` returning 0 (:1153). Then `new_name[++name_len] = PNG_COMPRESSION_TYPE_BASE; ++name_len;` and `png_text_compress(png_iCCP, &comp, name_len)`. **The compression parameters used are the `zlib_text_*` set**, not the IDAT set (see §4b). Chunk = keyword+NUL+method+deflate stream.\n* **`png_write_sPLT` :1179-1229** — `entry_size = (spalette->depth == 8 ? 6 : 10)` (:1185) — two distinct layouts, `:1207` 8-bit packs bytes + uint16 frequency, `:1216` else five uint16s. `png_check_keyword == 0` → `png_error(\"sPLT: invalid keyword\")`. `nentries == 0` is a valid distinct row.\n* **`png_write_tEXt` :1568-1606** — `png_check_keyword == 0` → `png_error(\"tEXt: invalid keyword\")`. `:1582-1586` `if (text == NULL || *text == '\\0') text_len = 0; else text_len = strlen(text)` — **the caller's `text_len` argument is always discarded** (all call sites pass 0 anyway). `:1588` `text_len > PNG_UINT_31_MAX - (key_len+1)` → `png_error(\"tEXt: text too long\")`. `:1602` `if (text_len != 0)` guards the second data write. Rows: NULL text, \"\" text, normal text.\n* **`png_write_zTXt` :1611-1657** — `:1621-1625` **`compression == PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_NONE (-1)` → delegates to `png_write_tEXt` and returns** (writes a tEXt, not a zTXt!). `:1627-1628` `compression != PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt (1)` → `png_error(\"zTXt: invalid compression type\")`. Note `png_write_end` reaches this with `compression >= PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt` (pngwrite.c:448), so values ≥ 2 are fatal from that path. Then keyword+NUL+method+deflate.\n* **`png_write_iTXt` :1662-1757** — `switch (compression)` at :1679:\n  * `PNG_ITXT_COMPRESSION_NONE (0)` / `PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_NONE (-1)` → `compression = new_key[++key_len] = 0`;\n  * `PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt (1)` / `PNG_ITXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt (2)` → `compression = new_key[++key_len] = 1`;\n  * `default:` → `png_error(\"iTXt: invalid compression\")`.\n  Then `:1708-1712` three NULL-defaulting branches (`lang → \"\"`, `lang_key → \"\"`, `text → \"\"`), `:1715-1723` two `PNG_UINT_31_MAX` saturation branches for `prefix_len`. `:1727` `if (compression != 0)` → `png_text_compress` (may `png_error` with `zstream.msg`) else `:1735-1739` `if (comp.input_len > PNG_UINT_31_MAX - prefix_len) png_error(\"iTXt: uncompressed text too long\")` and `output_len = input_len`. `:1750-1754` mirrored branch for emitting compressed vs raw text. Layout = key+NUL, compression_flag, compression_method, lang+NUL, lang_key+NUL, text.\n* **`png_check_keyword` (pngset.c:1981-2054)** — shared by iCCP/sPLT/tEXt/zTXt/iTXt/pCAL. Branches: `key == NULL` → return 0 (:1993); the `while (*key && key_len < 79)` loop with three arms (valid char `(ch > 32 && ch <= 126) || ch >= 161`; a space/invalid char after a non-space → emit one 0x20 and record `bad_character` if `ch != 32`; else skip and record the first bad char); trailing-space trim (:2022-2027); `key_len == 0` → return 0 (which every caller turns into a `png_error`); warnings `\"keyword truncated\"` if `*key != 0` (:2040) and the formatted `\"keyword \\\"@1\\\": bad character '0x@2'\"` (:2042-2051). **Test rows: 1-char key, 79-char key, 80-char key (truncated warning), leading space, trailing space, double internal space, 0x80 char, 0xA0 char, 0xA1 char, all-space key (→ length 0 → png_error).**\n* **`png_write_compressed_data_out` :653-681** — the `for(;;)` shipping loop over `comp->output[1024]` then the `zbuffer_list` chain; `:679-680` `if (output_len > 0) png_error(\"error writing ancillary chunked compressed data\")` (internal error). Reachable configurations differ by whether the compressed text exceeds 1024 bytes (one chunk-data write vs many) and whether it exceeds `1024 + n*zbuffer_size`.\n* **`png_text_compress` :504-650** — `png_deflate_claim` failure early-return (:522); the `do{}while(ret == Z_OK)` loop with the `avail_out == 0` buffer-extension block (:555-594: `output_len + prefix_len > PNG_UINT_31_MAX` → `Z_MEM_ERROR`; reuse an existing `*end` buffer vs malloc a new one; malloc failure → `Z_MEM_ERROR`); `deflate(..., input_len > 0 ? Z_NO_FLUSH : Z_FINISH)` (:597); the final `output_len + prefix_len >= PNG_UINT_31_MAX` check (:619); `zowner = 0` (:629); `ret == Z_STREAM_END && input_len == 0` → `optimize_cmf` + **return `Z_OK`** (:634-645), else return `ret`. Note: **empty input (`input_len == 0`) is explicitly supported** (\"may be zero!\", :533) — a zTXt/iTXt with empty text is a valid row.\n\n## 7d. `png_write_end` — pngwrite.c:391-504\n\n* `:396-397` `png_ptr == NULL` → return.\n* `:399-400` `(mode & PNG_HAVE_IDAT) == 0` → `png_error(\"No IDATs written into file\")`.\n* `:402-406` (`WRITE_CHECK_FOR_INVALID_INDEX`) `color_type == PALETTE && num_palette_max >= num_palette` → **`png_benign_error(\"Wrote palette index exceeding num_palette\")` — fatal in this build** (see §0). `num_palette_max` defaults to 0 (zeroed struct) so the check is *on* by default; `png_set_check_for_invalid_index(png_ptr, 0)` (pngset.c:1955-1965) sets it to −1 to disable. **Reachable with a perfectly well-formed PLTE if any pixel index ≥ num_palette.** Distinct, high-value test rows: PALETTE@1 with num_palette 2 and pixel value 1 (ok) vs num_palette 1 and pixel value 1 (fatal).\n* `:409` **`if (info_ptr != NULL)`** — the whole trailer block. Passing `NULL` skips tIME, text, eXIf and after-IDAT unknown chunks entirely. Two top-level rows.\n  * `:416-418` tIME: `valid & PNG_INFO_tIME && (mode & PNG_WROTE_tIME) == 0` → write. (So tIME appears before IDAT if `png_write_info` saw it, after IDAT only if it was set between `png_write_info` and `png_write_end`.)\n  * `:423-473` text loop, same 3-way dispatch as `png_write_info` **except** the zTXt arm tests `compression >= PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt` (:448) rather than `==`.\n  * `:477-479` eXIf: `valid & PNG_INFO_eXIf && (mode & PNG_WROTE_eXIf) == 0`.\n  * `:483` unknown chunks at `PNG_AFTER_IDAT`.\n* `:487` `mode |= PNG_AFTER_IDAT`; `:490` `png_write_IEND`.\n* `:499-503` `PNG_WRITE_FLUSH_SUPPORTED && PNG_WRITE_FLUSH_AFTER_IEND_SUPPORTED` → `png_flush`. **`PNG_WRITE_FLUSH_AFTER_IEND_SUPPORTED` is not in pnglibconf.h ⇒ no flush after IEND in this build.**\n\n---\n\n# 8. `png_write_png` — pngwrite.c:1406-1527 (`PNG_INFO_IMAGE_SUPPORTED`)\n\n* `:1412-1413` either pointer NULL → return.\n* `:1415-1419` `(info_ptr->valid & PNG_INFO_IDAT) == 0` → `png_app_error(\"no rows for png_write_image to write\")` + return (fatal in this build). Set by `png_set_rows` (pngset.c:1777).\n* `:1422` `png_write_info(png_ptr, info_ptr)` — **transforms are applied *after* the header is written** (unlike the read side).\n\nThen, in exactly this order:\n\n| order | line | flag (value) | action | notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 1427-1432 | `PNG_TRANSFORM_INVERT_MONO` (0x0020) | `png_set_invert_mono` | unconditional |\n| 2 | 1437-1443 | `PNG_TRANSFORM_SHIFT` (0x0040) | **`if ((info_ptr->valid & PNG_INFO_sBIT) != 0) png_set_shift(png_ptr, &info_ptr->sig_bit)`** | nested `if` with no `else` — requesting SHIFT without sBIT is a **silent no-op**. Distinct row. |\n| 3 | 1446-1451 | `PNG_TRANSFORM_PACKING` (0x0004) | `png_set_packing` | itself gated on `bit_depth < 8` |\n| 4 | 1454-1459 | `PNG_TRANSFORM_SWAP_ALPHA` (0x0100) | `png_set_swap_alpha` | |\n| 5 | 1465-1484 | `PNG_TRANSFORM_STRIP_FILLER_{BEFORE(0x0800), AFTER(0x1000)}` | see below | |\n| 6 | 1487-1492 | `PNG_TRANSFORM_BGR` (0x0080) | `png_set_bgr` | |\n| 7 | 1495-1500 | `PNG_TRANSFORM_SWAP_ENDIAN` (0x0200) | `png_set_swap` | gated on `bit_depth == 16` |\n| 8 | 1503-1508 | `PNG_TRANSFORM_PACKSWAP` (0x0008) | `png_set_packswap` | gated on `bit_depth < 8`; **and note ordering vs PACKING in §5c** |\n| 9 | 1511-1516 | `PNG_TRANSFORM_INVERT_ALPHA` (0x0400) | `png_set_invert_alpha` | |\n\nThe STRIP_FILLER block (:1465-1484), three sub-branches:\n* `AFTER` set **and** `BEFORE` set → `png_app_error(\"PNG_TRANSFORM_STRIP_FILLER: BEFORE+AFTER not supported\")` (fatal here; the comment at :1475 says \"Continue if ignored - this is the pre-1.6.10 behavior\") **then still calls `png_set_filler(png_ptr, 0, PNG_FILLER_AFTER)`**.\n* `AFTER` only → `png_set_filler(png_ptr, 0, PNG_FILLER_AFTER)`.\n* `BEFORE` only (:1479-1480) → `png_set_filler(png_ptr, 0, PNG_FILLER_BEFORE)`.\n\nThen `:1521` `png_write_image(png_ptr, info_ptr->row_pointers)`, `:1524` `png_write_end(png_ptr, info_ptr)`, `:1526` `PNG_UNUSED(params)` — **the `params` argument is required to be NULL by convention but is never checked or used.**\n\n**Flags with no code path at all in `png_write_png` — silently ignored on write** (no error, no warning): `PNG_TRANSFORM_IDENTITY` (0x0000), `STRIP_16` (0x0001), `STRIP_ALPHA` (0x0002), `EXPAND` (0x0010), `GRAY_TO_RGB` (0x2000), `EXPAND_16` (0x4000), `SCALE_16` (0x8000). Since every write-supported feature is compiled in, **none of the `png_app_error(\"PNG_TRANSFORM_X not supported\")` `#else` arms is reachable in this build.**\n\nNote `png_write_png` never calls `png_set_interlace_handling`; `png_write_image` does it internally (:664).\n\n---\n\n# 9. `png_write_row` / `png_write_rows` / `png_write_image` and interlacing\n\n## 9a. `png_write_rows` — pngwrite.c:626-643\nOnly branches: `png_ptr == NULL` → return; the `for (i = 0; i < num_rows; i++)` loop. `num_rows == 0` is a no-op row.\n\n## 9b. `png_write_image` — pngwrite.c:648-677\n* `:655` NULL → return.\n* `:664` `num_pass = png_set_interlace_handling(png_ptr)` (pngtrans.c:126-138: returns **7** if `png_ptr->interlaced != 0` and sets `transformations |= PNG_INTERLACE`, else **1** and sets nothing).\n* `:669-676` `for (pass = 0; pass < num_pass; pass++) for (i = 0; i < png_ptr->height; i++) png_write_row(png_ptr, image[i]);` — **the full image is passed 7 times for an interlaced write**; row selection happens inside `png_write_row`.\n\n## 9c. `png_write_row` — pngwrite.c:745-951\n\n**First-row init**, `:758` `if (png_ptr->row_number == 0 && png_ptr->pass == 0)`:\n* `:761-763` `(mode & PNG_WROTE_INFO_BEFORE_PLTE) == 0` → `png_error(\"png_write_info was never called before png_write_row\")`.\n* `:766-800` seven \"transform set but compiled out\" `png_warning` blocks — **all dead in this build** (every `PNG_WRITE_*_SUPPORTED` is defined).\n* `:802` `png_write_start_row(png_ptr)`.\n\n**Interlace row-skip state machine**, `:807-871`, gated on `interlaced != 0 && (transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) != 0` — `switch (png_ptr->pass)`:\n\n| pass | line | skip condition (→ `png_write_finish_row(); return;`) | kept rows | min width |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 812-818 | `(row_number & 0x07) != 0` | y ≡ 0 mod 8 | — |\n| 1 | 820-826 | `(row_number & 0x07) != 0 \\|\\| png_ptr->width < 5` | y ≡ 0 mod 8 | width ≥ 5 |\n| 2 | 828-834 | `(row_number & 0x07) != 4` | y ≡ 4 mod 8 | — |\n| 3 | 836-842 | `(row_number & 0x03) != 0 \\|\\| png_ptr->width < 3` | y ≡ 0 mod 4 | width ≥ 3 |\n| 4 | 844-850 | `(row_number & 0x03) != 2` | y ≡ 2 mod 4 | — |\n| 5 | 852-858 | `(row_number & 0x01) != 0 \\|\\| png_ptr->width < 2` | y ≡ 0 mod 2 | width ≥ 2 |\n| 6 | 860-866 | `(row_number & 0x01) == 0` | y odd | — |\n| ≥7 | 868-869 | `default:` — \"error: ignore it\", falls through and writes | | |\n\n**These are the \"pass width 0 → skip\" branches.** Note the height-driven empty passes are *not* handled here — passes 2/4/6 have no width guard, so for `height == 1` pass 2 never matches `row_number == 4` and is naturally empty; for `width == 1` passes 1/3/5 are skipped by the explicit width tests.\n\n**Per-row setup** `:875-887` (see §5a), `:890` `memcpy(png_ptr->row_buf + 1, row, row_info.rowbytes)`.\n\n**Interlace extraction** `:894-904`: `if (png_ptr->interlaced && png_ptr->pass < 6 && (transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) != 0)` → `png_do_write_interlace(&row_info, row_buf+1, pass)`; then `if (row_info.width == 0) { png_write_finish_row(); return; }` (:899-903, \"should always get caught above, but still …\").\n\n**Transforms** `:907-911`; **depth assertion** `:916-918`.\n\n**MNG intrapixel** `:930-935`: `(mng_features_permitted & PNG_FLAG_MNG_FILTER_64) != 0 && filter_type == PNG_INTRAPIXEL_DIFFERENCING` → `png_do_write_intrapixel(&row_info, row_buf+1)`. That function (`:681-741`) branches on `color_type & COLOR_MASK_COLOR`, then `bit_depth == 8` (RGB → bpp 3, RGB_ALPHA → bpp 4, else return) and `bit_depth == 16` (RGB → 6, RGB_ALPHA → 8, else return). 4 live combinations.\n\n**Palette index check** `:939-943`: `row_info.color_type == PALETTE && num_palette_max >= 0` → `png_do_check_palette_indexes(png_ptr, &row_info)` (pngtrans.c:727-826). That function: `if (num_palette < (1 << row_info->bit_depth) && num_palette > 0)` then `switch (row_info->bit_depth)` with cases 1, 2, 4, 8 and `default: break`; uses `padding = PNG_PADBITS(pixel_depth, width)` for the last byte. **Four distinct sub-8/8 code paths, and the outer condition means the check is skipped entirely when the palette is exactly full (`num_palette == 1<<bit_depth`) or empty.**\n\n**`png_write_find_filter`** `:947`; then `:949-950` `if (write_row_fn != NULL) (*write_row_fn)(png_ptr, row_number, pass)`.\n\n## 9d. `png_write_start_row` — pngwutil.c:1928-2024\n\n* `:1940-1941` `usr_pixel_depth = usr_channels * usr_bit_depth`; `buf_size = PNG_ROWBYTES(usr_pixel_depth, width) + 1`.\n* `:1944-1945` `transformed_pixel_depth = pixel_depth`; `maximum_pixel_depth = usr_pixel_depth`.\n* `:1948` malloc `row_buf`; `:1950` `row_buf[0] = PNG_FILTER_VALUE_NONE`.\n* **Shape-driven filter reduction** (`WRITE_FILTER`, :1952-1996):\n  * `:1955-1956` `if (height == 1) filters &= ~(UP|AVG|PAETH)`\n  * `:1958-1959` `if (width == 1) filters &= ~(SUB|AVG|PAETH)`\n  * `:1961-1962` `if (filters == 0) filters = PNG_FILTER_NONE` — so a 1×1 image with `PNG_ALL_FILTERS` ends up `PNG_FILTER_NONE`; a 1-row image with `PNG_FILTER_UP` alone ends up `PNG_FILTER_NONE`.\n  * `:1964` `do_filter = filters` (write-back).\n  * `:1966-1988` `if ((filters & (SUB|UP|AVG|PAETH)) != 0 && try_row == NULL)` → malloc `try_row`; count `num_filters` (:1969-1984); `if (num_filters > 1)` malloc `tst_row` (:1985-1987).\n  * `:1993-1995` `if ((filters & (AVG|UP|PAETH)) != 0)` → **`png_calloc` `prev_row`** (zero-filled, which is what makes UP/AVG/PAETH correct for row 0).\n* **Pass 0 dimensions** (`WRITE_INTERLACING`, :1998-2023): `interlaced != 0`:\n  * `(transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) == 0` (app supplies pre-reduced sub-images) → `num_rows = (height + 8 - 1 - 0)/8`, `usr_width = (width + 8 - 1 - 0)/8`.\n  * else `num_rows = height`, `usr_width = width`.\n  * non-interlaced → `num_rows = height`, `usr_width = width`.\n\n**→ Test-matrix shape axis: `{1×1, 1×N, N×1, N×M}` × `{interlaced, not}` × `{PNG_INTERLACE set (png_set_interlace_handling / png_write_image), not set}` × initial filter set.**\n\n## 9e. `png_write_finish_row` — pngwutil.c:2027-2092\n\n* `:2033` `row_number++`; `:2036-2037` `if (row_number < num_rows) return`.\n* `:2041` `if (interlaced != 0)`: `row_number = 0`;\n  * `:2044-2047` `(transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) != 0` → just `pass++` (no width/height recompute — the caller feeds full rows).\n  * `:2049-2074` else: `do { pass++; if (pass >= 7) break; recompute usr_width and num_rows from png_pass_inc/png_pass_start/png_pass_yinc/png_pass_ystart; if ((transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) != 0) break; } while (usr_width == 0 || num_rows == 0);` — **this is the \"pass width/height 0 → skip the whole pass\" loop** for the app-supplies-sub-images mode. (The inner `PNG_INTERLACE` break at :2069-2070 is unreachable in this arm.)\n  * `:2077-2085` `if (pass < 7) { if (prev_row != NULL) memset(prev_row, 0, PNG_ROWBYTES(usr_channels*usr_bit_depth, width)+1); return; }` — **`prev_row` is reset between passes**, so filters are per-pass.\n* `:2091` fall-through (non-interlaced last row, or pass reached 7) → `png_compress_IDAT(png_ptr, NULL, 0, Z_FINISH)`.\n\n## 9f. `png_do_write_interlace` — pngwutil.c:2102-2264\n\n* `:2108` `if (pass < 6)` — **pass 6 is a complete no-op (no data movement, no width/rowbytes update)**.\n* `switch (row_info->pixel_depth)` — four arms:\n  * `case 1` :2113-2149 — bit gather, `shift` 7→0, final `if (shift != 7) *dp = d`.\n  * `case 2` :2151-2186 — `shift` 6, step 2, final `if (shift != 6)`.\n  * `case 4` :2188-2222 — `shift` 4, step 4, final `if (shift != 4)`.\n  * `default:` :2224-2253 — `pixel_bytes = pixel_depth >> 3`; `memcpy` per pixel with `if (dp != sp)` guard (:2246). Covers pixel_depth 8, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64.\n* `:2256-2262` `row_info->width = (width + png_pass_inc[pass] - 1 - png_pass_start[pass]) / png_pass_inc[pass]`; `rowbytes = PNG_ROWBYTES(pixel_depth, width)`.\n\nArrays: `png_pass_start = {0,4,0,2,0,1,0}`, `png_pass_inc = {8,8,4,4,2,2,1}`, `png_pass_ystart = {0,0,4,0,2,0,1}`, `png_pass_yinc = {8,8,8,4,4,2,2}` (pngwutil.c:24-30).\n\n**→ interlace test rows: 7 passes × 4 pixel-depth arms (1/2/4/other) × the \"final partial byte\" boundary (width not a multiple of the pass stride × 8/shift-count) × `{width<2, width<3, width<5, width≥5}` for empty-pass behaviour.**\n\n---\n\n# 10. Flush, end, signature, low-level chunk writers\n\n* **`png_set_flush`** — pngwrite.c:955-964 (`WRITE_FLUSH`). Branches: NULL → return; `flush_dist = (nrows < 0 ? 0 : (png_uint_32)nrows)`. So `nrows <= 0` disables flushing (`flush_dist == 0` is tested at pngwutil.c:2773). Rows: negative, 0, 1, 2, > height.\n* **`png_write_flush`** — pngwrite.c:967-982. Branches: NULL → return; **`if (png_ptr->row_number >= png_ptr->num_rows) return`** (:976-977 — \"already written out all of the data\", so a manual flush after the last row of a pass is a no-op); else `png_compress_IDAT(png_ptr, NULL, 0, Z_SYNC_FLUSH)`, `flush_rows = 0`, `png_flush(png_ptr)`. Note the automatic call site (pngwutil.c:2771-2777) increments `flush_rows` *after* `png_write_finish_row`, so on the last row of a pass `row_number` has already wrapped and the early return fires. `png_flush` (pngwio.c:66-71) branches on `output_flush_fn != NULL`.\n* **`png_write_sig`** — pngwutil.c:67-83. `io_state = PNG_IO_WRITING|PNG_IO_SIGNATURE` (`PNG_IO_STATE_SUPPORTED`); writes `&png_signature[sig_bytes]`, length `8 - sig_bytes`; `if (sig_bytes < 3) mode |= PNG_HAVE_PNG_SIGNATURE`. **Rows: `sig_bytes` = 0 (normal), 1, 2, 3 (boundary: signature flag not set → MNG filter-64 becomes legal), 8 (writes nothing).** No bounds check on `sig_bytes`.\n* **`png_write_chunk_header`** (static) — pngwutil.c:89-129. `png_ptr == NULL` → return; sets `io_state = WRITING|CHUNK_HDR`, writes 8 bytes (length + name), sets `png_ptr->chunk_name`, `png_reset_crc`, `png_calculate_crc(buf+4, 4)`, sets `io_state = WRITING|CHUNK_DATA`.\n* **`png_write_chunk_start`** — :131-136. Thin wrapper: `png_write_chunk_header(png_ptr, PNG_CHUNK_FROM_STRING(chunk_string), length)`. No validation of the name at all.\n* **`png_write_chunk_data`** — :143-159. `png_ptr == NULL` → return; **`if (data != NULL && length > 0)`** → write + `png_calculate_crc`. So `data == NULL` or `length == 0` is a silent no-op (CRC unaffected). Multiple calls per chunk are legal and must sum to the header length — no check.\n* **`png_write_chunk_end`** — :162-180. NULL → return; `io_state = WRITING|CHUNK_CRC`; writes the 4-byte CRC in one call.\n* **`png_write_complete_chunk`** (static) — :191-205. NULL → return; **`if (length > PNG_UINT_31_MAX) png_error(\"length exceeds PNG maximum\")`** (64-bit only); then header+data+end.\n* **`png_write_chunk`** — :208-214. Public wrapper over `png_write_complete_chunk`.\n* **`png_write_IEND`** — :1073-1080. No branches: `png_write_complete_chunk(png_IEND, NULL, 0)` (which hits the `data == NULL` no-op in `png_write_chunk_data`), then `mode |= PNG_HAVE_IEND`.\n* **`png_write_data`** — pngwio.c:31-41. `write_data_fn != NULL` → call it; **else `png_error(\"Call to NULL write function\")`**. Only reachable if the app calls `png_set_write_fn(png_ptr, ptr, NULL, ...)` in a `!PNG_STDIO_SUPPORTED` build; with STDIO the default is substituted (pngwio.c:128-133).\n* **`png_default_write_data`** — pngwio.c:49-60: `png_ptr == NULL` → return; `fwrite != length` → `png_error(\"Write Error\")`.\n* **`png_save_uint_32` / `png_save_uint_16`** — pngwutil.c:40-58, branchless.\n\n---\n\n# 11. Unknown chunks on write\n\n## 11a. `png_set_unknown_chunks` — pngset.c:1421-1522\n* `:1427-1429` `png_ptr == NULL || info_ptr == NULL || num_unknowns <= 0 || unknowns == NULL` → silent return.\n* `:1446-1450` `png_realloc_array` failure → `png_chunk_report(..., PNG_CHUNK_WRITE_ERROR)` (on a write struct → `png_app_error` → fatal here) + return.\n* Per-chunk loop `:1486-1519`: copies `name` (NUL-terminated at index 4), `np->location = check_location(png_ptr, unknowns->location)`, then `unknowns->size == 0` → `data = NULL, size = 0` (:1492-1496) **else** malloc + copy (:1498-1516, with an OOM `png_chunk_report` + `continue` that leaves `unknown_chunks_num` un-incremented).\n\n## 11b. `check_location` — pngset.c:1385-1419\n* `:1387` `location &= (PNG_HAVE_IHDR(0x01) | PNG_HAVE_PLTE(0x02) | PNG_AFTER_IDAT(0x08))` — **`PNG_HAVE_IDAT (0x04)` is masked out, so a chunk can never be stored \"at IDAT\".**\n* `:1393-1401` `location == 0 && write struct` → `png_app_warning(\"png_set_unknown_chunks now expects a valid location\")` (**fatal in this build unless benign errors are enabled**) then `location = mode & (HAVE_IHDR|HAVE_PLTE|AFTER_IDAT)`. Because `png_write_IHDR` assigns `mode = PNG_HAVE_IHDR`, the recovered location is: before `png_write_info` → 0 (→ `png_error` at :1407); after `png_write_info` → `PNG_HAVE_IHDR`; after IDAT → `PNG_AFTER_IDAT`.\n* `:1406-1407` `location == 0` → `png_error(\"invalid location in png_set_unknown_chunks\")`.\n* `:1412-1413` `while (location != (location & -location)) location &= ~(location & -location);` — **reduces to the single highest set bit**. So `HAVE_IHDR|AFTER_IDAT` becomes `AFTER_IDAT` only.\n\n## 11c. `png_set_unknown_chunk_location` — pngset.c:1526-1549\n* Guard `png_ptr != NULL && info_ptr != NULL && chunk >= 0 && chunk < info_ptr->unknown_chunks_num` (:1531-1532) — otherwise silent no-op.\n* `:1534-1545` `(location & (HAVE_IHDR|HAVE_PLTE|AFTER_IDAT)) == 0` → `png_app_error(\"invalid unknown chunk location\")` (fatal here) then the \"fake out pre-1.6.0\" recovery: `if (location & PNG_HAVE_IDAT) location = PNG_AFTER_IDAT; else location = PNG_HAVE_IHDR;`\n* `:1547-1548` `location = check_location(png_ptr, location)`.\n\n## 11d. `write_unknown_chunks` — pngwrite.c:22-70\nCalled at three sites: `PNG_HAVE_IHDR` (pngwrite.c:140, first thing after IHDR), `PNG_HAVE_PLTE` (:382, last thing in `png_write_info`), `PNG_AFTER_IDAT` (:483, inside the `info_ptr != NULL` block of `png_write_end`).\n\n* `:26` `if (info_ptr->unknown_chunks_num != 0)`.\n* `:35` `if ((up->location & where) != 0)` — since locations are single-bit, each chunk matches exactly one site.\n* `:41` `keep = png_handle_as_unknown(png_ptr, up->name)` (png.c:931-961: `num_chunk_list == 0` → `PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_AS_DEFAULT (0)`; else linear search of 5-byte records; not found → `AS_DEFAULT`).\n* `:55-59` **the write predicate**:\n  ```c\n  keep != PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_NEVER &&\n  ((up->name[3] & 0x20) /* safe-to-copy */ ||\n   keep == PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_ALWAYS ||\n   (keep == PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_AS_DEFAULT &&\n    png_ptr->unknown_default == PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_ALWAYS))\n  ```\n  With defaults (`num_chunk_list == 0`, `unknown_default == 0 == AS_DEFAULT`): **only safe-to-copy chunks (4th byte lowercase) are written.** Note `PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_IF_SAFE (2)` behaves identically to `AS_DEFAULT` here for unsafe-to-copy chunks (both fail all three disjuncts), and the comment at :50-53 flags that there is no way to *suppress* a safe-to-copy chunk.\n* `:63-64` `if (up->size == 0) png_warning(\"Writing zero-length unknown chunk\")` — **non-fatal, reachable with valid input**, then the chunk is still written.\n* `:66` `png_write_chunk(png_ptr, up->name, up->data, up->size)`.\n\n**→ unknown-chunk matrix: `location ∈ {HAVE_IHDR, HAVE_PLTE, AFTER_IDAT, HAVE_IDAT(→dropped), 0(→app_warning/error), multi-bit(→reduced)}` × `name[3] ∈ {lowercase, uppercase}` × `keep ∈ {AS_DEFAULT, NEVER, IF_SAFE, ALWAYS}` (via `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks` per-chunk) × `unknown_default ∈ {AS_DEFAULT, NEVER, IF_SAFE, ALWAYS}` (via `num_chunks_in == 0`) × `size ∈ {0, >0}`.** `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks` itself (pngset.c:1599-…) has branches: `keep < 0 || keep >= PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_LAST(4)` → `png_app_error`; `num_chunks_in == 0` → set `unknown_default` and return; `num_chunks_in < 0` → apply `keep` to the built-in 21-entry `chunks_to_ignore` list; `num_chunks_in > 0 && chunk_list == NULL` → `png_app_error`; `num_chunks + old > UINT_MAX/5` → `png_app_error`.\n\n---\n\n# 12. Error/warning-only branches reachable with **valid** configuration\n\nGrouped by severity in *this* build (remember §0: `png_app_*` and `png_benign_error` are fatal by default on write; `png_set_benign_errors(png_ptr, 1)` demotes them to warnings).\n\n**Non-fatal `png_warning` (always just a warning):**\n1. pngwutil.c:773 — `compression_type != 0` in IHDR (value silently coerced).\n2. pngwutil.c:796 — invalid filter_type in IHDR (coerced to 0).\n3. pngwutil.c:804 — invalid interlace_type in IHDR (coerced to **ADAM7**).\n4. pngwrite.c:99 — MNG features requested but a PNG signature was written; `mng_features_permitted` zeroed.\n5. pngwrite.c:1270 / 1276 — `png_set_compression_window_bits` out of 8..15.\n6. pngwrite.c:1295 — `png_set_compression_method(method != 8)` (stored anyway → later zlib failure).\n7. pngwrite.c:1349 / 1355 / 1371 — the `png_set_text_compression_*` equivalents.\n8. pngset.c:1823 / 1832 / 1843 — `png_set_compression_buffer_size` in-use / above `ZLIB_IO_MAX` / below 6.\n9. pngwutil.c:884 — `png_write_PLTE` with a bad count on a **non-palette** image (suggested palette) → warn + skip.\n10. pngwutil.c:891 — PLTE requested on a grayscale image → warn + skip.\n11. pngwutil.c:1107 — `srgb_intent >= 4` (chunk still written).\n12. pngwutil.c:1254 / 1268 / 1280 — `png_write_sBIT` out-of-range red/green/blue, gray, or alpha → warn + **chunk omitted**. Very easy to hit: e.g. GRAY@8 with `sig_bit.gray = 9`, or PALETTE with `sig_bit.red = 9` (maxbits is fixed at 8 for palette).\n13. pngwutil.c:1401 / 1420 / 1434 — `png_write_bKGD` bad palette index / 16-bit values at bit_depth 8 / gray out of range → warn + omit.\n14. pngwutil.c:1550 — `png_write_hIST` with `num_hist > num_palette` → warn + omit. Note `png_write_info` passes `info_ptr->num_palette`, so this only fires if PLTE was rejected/absent.\n15. pngwutil.c:1771 — `png_write_oFFs` unit_type ≥ 2 (written anyway).\n16. pngwutil.c:1862 — `png_write_sCAL_s` with `strlen(w)+strlen(h)+2 > 64` → warn + **omit**.\n17. pngwutil.c:1887 — `png_write_pHYs` unit_type ≥ 2 (written anyway).\n18. pngwutil.c:1912 — `png_write_tIME` invalid month/day/hour/second → warn + omit.\n19. pngwrite.c:64 — zero-length unknown chunk (still written).\n20. pngwutil.c:413 — `deflateEnd failed (ignored)` in `png_deflate_claim` (practically unreachable).\n21. pngset.c:2040 / 2042-2051 — `png_check_keyword` \"keyword truncated\" / \"bad character '0x@2'\". Reachable from tEXt/zTXt/iTXt/iCCP/sPLT/pCAL with any key that has a leading/trailing/double space, a control char, 0x80–0xA0, or is > 79 chars.\n22. pngset.c:1253-1254 — `png_set_tRNS` \"tRNS chunk has out-of-range samples for bit_depth\".\n23. pngwrite.c:346 / 360 / 375 and 444 / 457 / 470 — \"Unable to write international/compressed/uncompressed text\" — **dead in this build**.\n24. pngwrite.c:768-799 — the seven \"PNG_WRITE_X_SUPPORTED is not defined\" first-row warnings — **all dead in this build**.\n\n**`png_app_warning` / `png_app_error` / `png_benign_error` — fatal by default here, warning after `png_set_benign_errors(png_ptr, 1)`; all reachable with well-formed input:**\n25. pngwrite.c:1140 — `png_set_filter: UP/AVG/PAETH cannot be added after start` (start with NONE/SUB, write a row, then add UP).\n26. pngwrite.c:1078 — `Unknown row filter for method 0` for `filters & 0xFF ∈ {5,6,7}`.\n27. pngwutil.c:1331 — `Invalid number of transparent colors specified` (palette tRNS with `num_trans > num_palette`, e.g. `png_set_tRNS` before `png_set_PLTE`, or 4 entries against a 2-entry palette).\n28. pngwutil.c:1346 — gray tRNS out of range for bit_depth.\n29. pngwutil.c:1368 — RGB tRNS with high bytes set at bit_depth 8.\n30. pngwutil.c:1378 — `Can't write tRNS with an alpha channel` (GRAY_ALPHA/RGB_ALPHA + `png_set_tRNS`).\n31. pngtrans.c:202 — `png_set_filler is invalid for low bit depth gray output` (GRAY@1/2/4, **or any call before `png_write_info` when color_type/bit_depth are still 0**).\n32. pngtrans.c:209 — `png_set_filler: inappropriate color type` (PALETTE, GRAY_ALPHA, RGB_ALPHA).\n33. pngtrans.c:114 — `png_set_shift: invalid shift values` (any channel 0 or > `png_ptr->bit_depth`; note this validates against `bit_depth`, whereas `png_write_sBIT` validates against `usr_bit_depth`).\n34. pngwrite.c:1417 — `no rows for png_write_image to write` (`png_write_png` without `png_set_rows`).\n35. pngwrite.c:1472 — `PNG_TRANSFORM_STRIP_FILLER: BEFORE+AFTER not supported`.\n36. pngset.c:1396 — `png_set_unknown_chunks now expects a valid location` (location 0 on a write struct).\n37. pngset.c:1539 — `invalid unknown chunk location`.\n38. pngset.c:1610 / 1667 / 1685 — `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks` invalid keep / no chunk list / too many chunks.\n39. pngwrite.c:405 — **`Wrote palette index exceeding num_palette`** (`png_benign_error`) — the single most likely \"surprise fatal\" for a valid-looking palette write; guard with `png_set_check_for_invalid_index(png_ptr, 0)`.\n\n**Hard `png_error` reachable from ordering / configuration (not data corruption):**\n40. pngwrite.c:241 — `Valid palette required for paletted images` (PALETTE IHDR without `PNG_INFO_PLTE`).\n41. pngwrite.c:400 — `No IDATs written into file` (`png_write_end` with zero rows written).\n42. pngwrite.c:762 — `png_write_info was never called before png_write_row`.\n43. pngwrite.c:918 — `internal write transform logic error` (net transformed `pixel_depth` ≠ IHDR `pixel_depth`; e.g. `png_set_packing` without a sub-8-bit IHDR-vs-usr mismatch, or `png_set_filler` on a colour type where `png_do_strip_channel` bails out).\n44. pngwrite.c:1180 — `Unknown custom filter method` (`method ∉ {0}`, or `∉ {0,64}` with MNG).\n45. pngset.c:1407 — `invalid location in png_set_unknown_chunks` (location 0 called before `png_write_info`).\n46. pngset.c:1805 — `invalid compression buffer size` (0 or > 2^31−1).\n47. pngutil.c:1628 — `zTXt: invalid compression type`; :1692 `iTXt: invalid compression`; :1797 `Unrecognized equation type for pCAL chunk` (type ≥ 4); :1580/:1633/:1676/:1194/:1154 `<chunk>: invalid keyword` (all-whitespace or empty key).\n48. pngwutil.c:339 — `\"<chunk>: <owner> using zstream\"` (`png_deflate_claim` while the stream is claimed). **Only reachable via an internal ordering bug**, since `png_compress_IDAT` releases `zowner` on `Z_FINISH` — but note that after a `Z_SYNC_FLUSH` (`png_write_flush`) `zowner` remains `png_IDAT`, so **writing a text/iCCP chunk between rows is not possible and would trip this**. Worth one explicit negative row.\n49. pngwrite.c:2156 / 2045 / 2049 / 2053 / 2072 — simplified-API-only errors (`png_image_write_main`).\n\n---\n\n## Summary of the principal orthogonal axes for the matrix\n\n1. `(color_type, bit_depth)` — 15 valid rows (§1a).\n2. `interlace_type` × `PNG_INTERLACE` transformation set/unset — 3 combinations, × the 7-pass/empty-pass shapes (§9).\n3. Image shape: `1×1`, `1×N`, `N×1`, `N×M`, plus `rowbytes` straddling 32768 and total size straddling 16384 (§4d).\n4. `do_filter`: never-set (IHDR defaults, 2 outcomes), `PNG_NO_FILTERS`, each single mask bit, `PNG_FAST_FILTERS`, `PNG_ALL_FILTERS`, mixed sets, and the `PNG_FILTER_VALUE_*` (1..4) quirk (§1d, §2b).\n5. `png_set_filter` call time: before `png_write_info` / after `png_write_info` / after the first row (§2c).\n6. `method`: 0, 64-with-MNG, 64-without-MNG, other (§2a).\n7. zlib IDAT params: `level ∈ {0,1,6,9,-1}`, `mem_level ∈ {1,8,9}`, `strategy ∈ {unset, 0,1,2,3,4}`, `window_bits ∈ {7(clamped),8,9,15,16(clamped)}`, `method ∈ {8, other}`, `zbuffer_size ∈ {5(rejected),6,1024,8192,65536}` (§4a).\n8. Same again for the `text_*` set, plus whether it differs from the IDAT set (`deflateEnd`+`Init2` vs `deflateReset`) (§4b).\n9. Transform set: the 10 transforms of §5b, individually and in the no-op / interacting combinations of §5c, × set-before vs set-after `png_write_info`.\n10. Chunk presence: each `PNG_INFO_*` flag independently, plus the per-writer boundary values of §7c, plus `png_write_end(info_ptr)` vs `png_write_end(NULL)`.\n11. Unknown chunks: location × safe-to-copy bit × `keep` × `unknown_default` × size (§11d).\n12. `png_set_flush(nrows)` ∈ {−1, 0, 1, 2, height, height+1} and manual `png_write_flush` at each row index (§10).\n13. `png_set_sig_bytes` ∈ {0, 3, 8} (§10, and gates MNG filter-64).\n14. `png_set_benign_errors` ∈ {not called, 1, 0} — flips 15 branches from fatal to warning (§0, §12).\n15. `png_set_check_for_invalid_index` ∈ {not called (on), 1, 0} (§7d, §9c).\n16. `png_write_png` `transforms` bitmask: the 9 honoured flags of §8 plus the 7 silently-ignored read-only flags."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":994,"cache_read_input_tokens":158059,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":994,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01GD1ZzWADnHpQWVxV5zsaUn","session_id":"e3091878-9949-4689-ad83-c0c41e6641a2","uuid":"f6f8afc6-9f05-4022-8597-fd2a70da2813","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:27:04.269Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Map write pipe