.md` FIRST, then skim `translation/tests/common/mod.rs`, `translation/tests/common/types.rs` and `translation/tests/t03_write.rs` (which shows the write-pipeline driver pattern including a big option enum with all the chunk setters already wired up).\n\nYOUR TASK: create ONE new file `translation/tests/t04_chunks.rs` that differentially tests EVERY ancillary-chunk setter/getter pair through both `.so`s.\n\nFor each of the chunk types below, for a representative set of base images (at minimum: GRAY@8, PALETTE@4, RGB@8, RGB_ALPHA@16, GRAY_ALPHA@8), do BOTH of these:\n1. **write side**: set the chunk on the write struct, run the full write pipeline (png_set_IHDR -> setters -> png_write_info -> png_write_image -> png_write_end), and assert the produced PNG bytes are IDENTICAL between C and Rust, and that the captured `Diag` (warnings+errors) is identical.\n2. **read side**: read the produced bytes back with `png_read_info` + `png_read_image` + `png_read_end` and assert every corresponding `png_get_*` getter returns identical values (return code AND all out-parameters, including strings and byte arrays) between C and Rust, plus identical `png_get_valid` masks and identical `Diag`.\n\nChunks / setter+getter pairs to cover (all are exported; see `c_src/include/png.h`):\ngAMA (`png_set_gAMA`/`_fixed`, `png_get_gAMA`/`_fixed`), cHRM (`png_set_cHRM`/`_fixed`/`_XYZ`/`_XYZ_fixed` and all four getters), sRGB (`png_set_sRGB`, `png_set_sRGB_gAMA_and_cHRM`, `png_get_sRGB`), iCCP (`png_set_iCCP`/`png_get_iCCP`) — include a real minimal 132-byte-plus ICC profile header so it passes `png_icc_check_*`, and also a deliberately short/garbage profile, sBIT, PLTE, tRNS (all three colour-type forms), bKGD, hIST, pHYs (+ `png_get_pHYs_dpi`, `png_get_x_pixels_per_inch`, `png_get_y_pixels_per_inch`, `png_get_pixels_per_inch`, `png_get_pixel_aspect_ratio`(+`_fixed`)), oFFs (+ `png_get_x_offset_microns`/`_inches`(+`_fixed`)/`_pixels`, same for y), sCAL (`png_set_sCAL`/`_fixed`/`_s`, `png_get_sCAL`/`_fixed`/`_s`), pCAL, tIME, tEXt/zTXt/iTXt via `png_set_text`/`png_set_text_2`/`png_get_text` with every `PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_*` / `PNG_ITXT_COMPRESSION_*` value, sPLT, eXIf (`png_set_eXIf_1`/`png_get_eXIf_1`), cICP, cLLI (`png_set_cLLI`/`_fixed`, `png_get_cLLI`/`_fixed`), mDCV (`png_set_mDCV`/`_fixed`, `png_get_mDCV`/`_fixed`), and unknown chunks (`png_set_unknown_chunks`, `png_set_unknown_chunk_location`, `png_get_unknown_chunks`, `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks`, `png_handle_as_unknown` with each `PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_*`).\n\nAlso cover: `png_get_IHDR`/`png_get_PLTE`/`png_get_bit_depth`/`_color_type`/`_channels`/`_rowbytes`/`_image_width`/`_image_height`/`_interlace_type`/`_compression_type`/`_filter_type`/`_signature`/`_palette_max`/`_valid` and `png_free_data`/`png_data_freer` with each `PNG_FREE_*` mask.\n\nUse MANY randomized values per chunk (a deterministic `Rng` with a fixed seed), not one hand-picked value — include boundary values (0, 1, max, negative where the type is signed).\n\nRequirements:\n- Use `guard(...)` around every call that can `png_error`.\n- Compare `Diag` as well as values.\n- Keep the file self-contained (`mod common; use common::*;`) — do NOT modify `tests/common/*` or any other existing test file, and do NOT modify anything in `c_src/`.\n- It MUST compile and the test MUST pass: iterate with\n  `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-kk7Dev/translation && cargo test --offline --release --test t04_chunks`\n  until green. Use `timeout 600` on every cargo command.\n- If a test reveals a REAL divergence between C and Rust, the Rust translation\n  (`translation/src/*.rs`) is the thing that is wrong — but do NOT fix it\n  yourself. Instead leave the failing assertion in place, mark the test\n  `#[ignore]` with a `// DIVERGENCE:` comment describing exactly what differs\n  (function, inputs, C value vs Rust value), and report it prominently.\n- If a case is C undefined behaviour (pointer dereferenced before a null check, buffer read past the end), do NOT test it; note it in a comment.\n\nReport back: the list of test functions you wrote, the pass/fail status of the final run, and any `// DIVERGENCE:` findings with full detail.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-jhH7E9/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-kk7Dev/e3091878-9949-4689-ad83-c0c41e6641a2/tasks/a2ad59482221d9fff.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
