{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01GDGBnNByinKwXBJG2ZpiBb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Differential-test harness (read this before adding tests)\n2\t\n3\tLayout:\n4\t* `tests/common/types.rs`  — all public libpng types/constants, redeclared\n5\t  (the crate is a `cdylib`, tests never link it).\n6\t* `tests/common/api.rs`    — AUTO-GENERATED `struct Api` with one field per\n7\t  exported symbol (all 384), each an `unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn` pointer.\n8\t  `Api::load(path, name)` dlopens a `.so` and resolves every symbol.\n9\t* `tests/common/mod.rs`    — the harness proper.\n10\t\n11\tUse it like this:\n12\t\n13\t```rust\n14\tmod common;\n15\tuse common::*;\n16\t\n17\t#[test]\n18\tfn my_test() {\n19\t    for api in both() {            // [c_api(), rs_api()]\n20\t        unsafe {\n21\t            set_current_api(api);  // REQUIRED before any IO/error callback fires\n22\t            diag_reset();\n23\t            let s = WriteSess::new(api);          // or ReadSess::new(api, &bytes)\n24\t            let ok = guard(|| { /* calls that may png_error */ }).is_some();\n25\t            let d = diag_take();                  // captured warnings + errors\n26\t            let out = std::mem::take(&mut s.sink.buf);  // bytes written\n27\t        }\n28\t    }\n29\t}\n30\t```\n31\t\n32\tKey facts:\n33\t* `guard(f) -> Option<T>`: `png_error` in either library unwinds as a Rust\n34\t  panic (all entry points are `extern \"C-unwind\"`); `guard` catches it and\n35\t  returns `None`.  ALWAYS wrap anything that can error.\n36\t* `Diag { warnings: Vec<String>, errors: Vec<String> }` — compare these between\n37\t  the two libraries, not just success/failure.\n38\t* `ReadSess`/`WriteSess` own the png_struct + info_struct and destroy them on\n39\t  drop.  `WriteSess.sink.buf` is the produced byte stream, `.sink.flushes` the\n40\t  flush count.  `ReadSess.src` is the memory source.\n41\t* Helpers: `cs(&str) -> CString`, `rs_str(ptr) -> Option<String>`,\n42\t  `ver() -> CString` (PNG_LIBPNG_VER_STRING), `Rng::new(seed)` (deterministic\n43\t  xorshift: `.u8() .u32() .below(n) .range(lo,hi) .bytes(n) .bool()`),\n44\t  `rowbytes(pixel_depth, width)` (= PNG_ROWBYTES), `channels_of(color_type)`,\n45\t  `legal_ihdr() -> Vec<(color_type, bit_depth)>`, `assert_bytes_eq(label,c,r)`,\n46\t  `PNG_PASS_INC/_ROW_INC/_START_ROW/_START_COL`.\n47\t\n48\tRules:\n49\t* NEVER call the Rust crate directly; always go through `c_api()`/`rs_api()`.\n50\t* NEVER modify anything under `c_src/`.\n51\t* The C is ground truth.  If the two diverge, the *Rust* (`src/*.rs`) is wrong.\n52\t* Some C paths dereference a pointer before checking it (e.g. `png_muldiv`'s\n53\t  `res`, `png_do_bgr`'s `row`, `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer`'s `ptime`).\n54\t  Those are C UB, not error paths -- do not test them.\n55\t* Rows handed to the write path must be over-allocated when a transform makes\n56\t  libpng consume more application bytes per row than PNG_ROWBYTES (filler,\n57\t  packing), otherwise both libraries read past the buffer and results are\n58\t  nondeterministic.\n59\t* Build/run with:\n60\t  `cargo build --offline --release && cargo test --offline --release --test <name>`\n61\t  (the release cdylib at `target/release/liblibpng.so` is what gets loaded).\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01US2dipoeTMiontFWYLFvv8","session_id":"e3091878-9949-4689-ad83-c0c41e6641a2","uuid":"f64d4845-405b-4c7d-ab61-08ec161bf099","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:27:17.524Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write chunk round-trip tests"}
