{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01LxuZXL6sNbQ2Xhq96XENgz","type":"tool_result","content":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-kk7Dev/translation/tests/:\ntotal 96\ndrwxr-xr-x. 3 scheschb amazon   149 Aug 31 13:26 .\ndrwxr-xr-x. 7 scheschb amazon 16384 Aug 31 13:26 ..\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon  2886 Aug 31 13:26 HARNESS.md\ndrwxr-xr-x. 2 scheschb amazon    66 Aug 31 13:18 common\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon  2624 Aug 31 13:13 t00_smoke.rs\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon 23106 Aug 31 13:19 t01_utility.rs\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon 14922 Aug 31 13:22 t02_rowops.rs\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon 29151 Aug 31 13:26 t03_write.rs\n\n/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-kk7Dev/translation/tests/common/:\ntotal 104\ndrwxr-xr-x. 2 scheschb amazon    66 Aug 31 13:18 .\ndrwxr-xr-x. 3 scheschb amazon   149 Aug 31 13:26 ..\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon 68691 Aug 31 13:14 api.rs\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon 13475 Aug 31 13:18 mod.rs\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon 18345 Aug 31 13:25 types.rs","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01US2dipoeTMiontFWYLFvv8","session_id":"e3091878-9949-4689-ad83-c0c41e6641a2","uuid":"54b7c321-770d-4639-ad06-37dcdf55b0ab","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:27:18.551Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write chunk round-trip tests"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ivdbi2xqecocvwkffolb4wabb64f5yknihctyhpnz2ia7irkguda","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# libpng 1.6.59 Sequential-Read Configuration Surface\n\n**Build facts that gate everything (from `include/pnglibconf.h`):**\n\n| Fact | Consequence |\n|---|---|\n| `PNG_DISABLE_ADLER32_CHECK_SUPPORTED` **not** defined | `PNG_IGNORE_ADLER32` is **not** `#define`d (`png.h:3473-3475`), and the `inflateValidate` block at `pngrutil.c:497-501` is compiled out. `png_set_option(p, 8, on)` still *succeeds* (stores bits) but has **zero** effect. |\n| `PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_BASE_TYPE == PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_BETA` (2) < `RC` (3) | `PNG_RELEASE_BUILD == 0` (`pngpriv.h:447`). Two live consequences: (a) `pngread.c:67-69` does **not** set `PNG_FLAG_APP_WARNINGS_WARN` → app warnings are **fatal** by default; (b) `pngrutil.c:426-431` uses `png_chunk_error` (not warning) when the zstream is already owned. |\n| `ZLIB_VERNUM == 0x12b0` (≥ 0x1240) | `inflateInit2/inflateReset2` path live; `PNG_INFLATE` == `png_zlib_inflate` (`pngpriv.h:1729`) → the `zstream_start` CINFO check at `pngrutil.c:527-536` is live; `PNG_MAXIMUM_INFLATE_WINDOW` is live. |\n| `PNG_SET_USER_LIMITS_SUPPORTED` defined | `png_chunk_max(p)` == `p->user_chunk_malloc_max` (`pngpriv.h:1126`), i.e. runtime-settable. Default 8000000. |\n| `PNG_sRGB_PROFILE_CHECKS 2` and `PNG_SKIP_sRGB_CHECK_PROFILE` | **dead in this build** — grep shows zero references in `src/`. See §12. |\n| `PNG_USER_CHUNK_CACHE_MAX 1000`, `PNG_USER_WIDTH_MAX/HEIGHT_MAX 1000000`, `PNG_IDAT_READ_SIZE == PNG_ZBUF_SIZE == 8192`, `PNG_INFLATE_BUF_SIZE 1024` | seeds for §8 |\n| `PNG_ALIGNED_MEMORY_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_ALIGN_TYPE != NONE` | selects the aligned `row_buf` arithmetic (`pngrutil.c:4626-4634`) and the 16/32-bit copy loops in `png_combine_row` (`pngrutil.c:3576-3672`). |\n| No `PNG_FILTER_OPTIMIZATIONS`, no `PNG_ARM_NEON_IMPLEMENTATION` / `PNG_RISCV_RVV_IMPLEMENTATION` | §6 has only the 5 generic C filter functions; `png_read_destroy`'s `riffled_palette` free (`pngread.c:815-820`) is compiled out. |\n\nEverything below `pngread.c:1073` is simplified API — excluded as requested.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Struct creation, I/O and signature\n\n### `png_create_read_struct` — `pngread.c:24-35`\nBecause `PNG_USER_MEM_SUPPORTED` is defined, this function body is *entirely* a tail-call to `_2` (line 33). The `#ifndef` branch at line 30 is dead. **One row only.**\n\n### `png_create_read_struct_2` — `pngread.c:40-80`\nBranches:\n1. `png_create_png_struct` returns NULL → returns NULL immediately (`if (png_ptr != NULL)` at 50 false). Reachable via a failing `malloc_fn`.\n2. Success path sets `mode = PNG_IS_READ_STRUCT` (52), `IDAT_read_size = PNG_IDAT_READ_SIZE` (58), `flags |= PNG_FLAG_BENIGN_ERRORS_WARN` (62) — **note: read structs default benign errors to WARN**, then unconditionally calls `png_set_read_fn(png_ptr, NULL, NULL)` (76).\n3. `mem_ptr/malloc_fn/free_fn` all-NULL vs all-supplied vs partially supplied (validated inside `png_create_png_struct`, `png.c:~250-320`).\n4. `user_png_ver` mismatch → `png_user_version_check` sets `PNG_FLAG_LIBRARY_MISMATCH`; version string NULL vs `PNG_LIBPNG_VER_STRING` (\"1.6.59.git\") vs wrong-major.\n5. `error_fn == NULL` / `warn_fn == NULL` → defaults installed by `png_set_error_fn` (`png.c:311`).\n\nDistinct rows: {ok, alloc-fail, custom-mem, custom-error-fn, version-mismatch}.\n\n### `png_read_init` variants\n**None exist in this build.** There is no `png_read_init`, `_2`, or `_3` in `pngread.c` (confirmed by the function list — 1.6 removed them). Do not write rows for them.\n\n### `png_set_read_fn` — `pngrio.c:86-118`\nBranches:\n- `png_ptr == NULL` → no-op (89).\n- `PNG_STDIO_SUPPORTED` is defined, so: `read_data_fn != NULL` → install it (95); `read_data_fn == NULL` → install `png_default_read_data` (98). **This is why `png_create_read_struct_2` line 76 leaves a working stdio reader.**\n- `png_ptr->write_data_fn != NULL` (i.e. this was a write struct) → NULLs it + `png_warning` (104-111).\n- `output_flush_fn = NULL` (116) since `PNG_WRITE_FLUSH_SUPPORTED`.\n- `io_ptr` may be NULL with the default fn → `fread(…, NULL)` UB; the guard is only in `png_read_data` (`pngrio.c:35-40`) for a NULL `read_data_fn`.\n\nRows: {custom read_fn + io_ptr}, {NULL read_fn → stdio default + FILE\\* io_ptr}, {called on write struct}, {`png_init_io` instead}.\n\n### `png_set_read_status_fn` — `pngread.c:855-862`\nTwo rows: NULL (no per-row callback) and non-NULL (invoked at `pngread.c:522-523` **after** `png_read_finish_row`, so `row_number`/`pass` are already advanced). Note it is *not* called on the interlace-skip early-return paths (§4).\n\n### `png_set_error_fn` — `pngerror.c:718…`\nRows: {default error+warn}, {custom error_fn with longjmp}, {custom error_fn that returns (→ `PNG_ABORT`)}, {warn_fn NULL}, {`error_ptr` non-NULL retrievable by `png_get_error_ptr`}.\n\n### `png_set_sig_bytes(0..8)` — `png.c:53-70`\nBranches in the setter:\n- `num_bytes < 0` → clamped to `nb = 0` (62-63).\n- `nb > 8` → `png_error(\"Too many bytes for PNG signature\")` (65-66).\n- otherwise stored.\n\nBranches in the consumer `png_read_sig` (`pngrutil.c:116-145`):\n- `sig_bytes >= 8` → **return immediately, no read at all** (121-122). So `png_set_sig_bytes(8)` requires the caller to have already consumed 8 bytes; note `mode` does **not** get `PNG_HAVE_PNG_SIGNATURE` in this case, which matters for MNG (§10).\n- `sig_bytes` 0..7 → reads `8 - sig_bytes` bytes into `info_ptr->signature[num_checked]`, sets `sig_bytes = 8`.\n- `png_sig_cmp != 0`: sub-branch `num_checked < 4 && png_sig_cmp(…, num_to_check-4) != 0` → `png_error(\"Not a PNG file\")`; else → `png_error(\"PNG file corrupted by ASCII conversion\")` (135-142). **The second message is only reachable with `sig_bytes` 0..3.**\n- `num_checked < 3` → sets `PNG_HAVE_PNG_SIGNATURE` (143-144). **Note: `sig_bytes` of 3..7 leaves `PNG_HAVE_PNG_SIGNATURE` clear**, which silently enables MNG filter 64 acceptance in `png_set_IHDR` (`png.c:2089-2110`). This is a genuine, non-obvious configuration axis.\n\nRows: sig_bytes ∈ {0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 7, 8}, ×{valid sig, corrupt sig}, plus {negative}, {9}.\n\n---\n\n## 2. `png_read_info` dispatch loop and every chunk handler\n\n### The loop itself — `pngread.c:93-167`\nDistinct branches per iteration:\n1. `png_ptr == NULL || info_ptr == NULL` → return (101). **`png_read_info` with NULL info_ptr is a silent no-op**, unlike `png_read_end`.\n2. `png_read_sig` (105) — see §1.\n3. `chunk_name == png_IDAT` (115): three sub-errors — no IHDR → `png_chunk_error(\"Missing IHDR before IDAT\")` (118); palette PNG without PLTE → `png_chunk_error(\"Missing PLTE before IDAT\")` (122); `PNG_AFTER_IDAT` already set → `png_chunk_benign_error(\"Too many IDATs found\")` (125). Then `mode |= PNG_HAVE_IDAT`.\n4. else if `PNG_HAVE_IDAT` set (130) → sets `PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_AFTER_IDAT | PNG_AFTER_IDAT`.\n5. `IHDR` → `png_handle_chunk` (137); `IEND` → `png_handle_chunk` (140) — **these two bypass the unknown-handling override**, so `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks` can never divert IHDR/IEND.\n6. `png_chunk_unknown_handling(png_ptr, chunk_name) != 0` (143) → `png_handle_unknown(…, keep)`; if the chunk was `PLTE` set `PNG_HAVE_PLTE` (147-148); if it was `IDAT`, `idat_size = 0` and **`break`** (150-154) — i.e. IDAT forced to unknown handling terminates `png_read_info` having already consumed the whole first IDAT.\n7. plain `IDAT` (158) → `idat_size = length`, `break` — the normal exit.\n8. everything else → `png_handle_chunk` (165).\n\nRows: {IDAT-first}, {palette w/o PLTE}, {duplicate IDAT block}, {ancillary chunk after IDAT before IEND}, {IDAT marked keep}, {PLTE marked keep}.\n\n### `png_handle_chunk` — the table-driven gate, `pngrutil.c:3106-3217`\nThis is the single most important axis: every handler is preceded by table checks. Table at `pngrutil.c:2986-3083`; per-chunk constants at 3041-3078.\n\nBranch order:\n1. `chunk_index == PNG_INDEX_unknown || handler == NULL` → `png_handle_unknown(…, PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_AS_DEFAULT)` (3123-3128). In this build the `handler == NULL` chunks are exactly **`IDAT` (`#define png_handle_IDAT NULL`, line 1082), `acTL`, `fcTL`, `fdAT` (lines 2971-2973)** — all APNG chunks route to unknown handling by design.\n2. non-IHDR with `PNG_HAVE_IHDR` clear → `png_chunk_error(\"missing IHDR\")` (3133-3135), NORETURN.\n3. position check: `(mode & pos_before) != 0 || (mode & pos_after) != pos_after` → `errmsg = \"out of place\"` (3138-3143).\n4. `multiple == 0 && png_file_has_chunk(index)` → `errmsg = \"duplicate\"` (3148-3152). `chunks` bitmask in `png_struct` (`pngstruct.h:190`), set only at 3213 when `handled >= handled_saved`.\n5. `length < min_length` → `errmsg = \"too short\"` (3154).\n6. `max_length` switch (3167-3192): `Limit` (0x802) → compare against `png_chunk_max(png_ptr)` else `\"length exceeds libpng limit\"`; `NoCheck` (0x801) → straight to handler; numeric → `length <= max` else `\"too long\"`.\n7. error disposition (3198-3208): critical → `png_chunk_error`; ancillary → `png_crc_finish(length)` + `png_chunk_benign_error`.\n8. success and `handled >= handled_saved` → `png_file_add_chunk` (3210-3214).\n\n**Per-chunk table values (each is a distinct \"too short\"/\"too long\"/\"out of place\"/\"duplicate\" test row):**\n\n| chunk | max | min | pos_before | pos_after | multiple |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| IHDR | 13 | 13 | HAVE_IHDR | 0 | no |\n| PLTE | NoCheck | 0 | — | HAVE_IHDR | **yes** |\n| IDAT | NoCheck | 0 | AFTER_IDAT | HAVE_IHDR | yes |\n| IEND | NoCheck | 0 | — | AFTER_IDAT | no |\n| tRNS | 256 | 0 | HAVE_IDAT | HAVE_IHDR | no |\n| cHRM | 32 | 32 | PLTE\\|IDAT | HAVE_IHDR | no |\n| gAMA | 4 | 4 | PLTE\\|IDAT | HAVE_IHDR | no |\n| iCCP | NoCheck | 3+11=14 | PLTE\\|IDAT | HAVE_IHDR | no |\n| sBIT | 4 | 1 | PLTE\\|IDAT | HAVE_IHDR | no |\n| sRGB | 1 | 1 | PLTE\\|IDAT | HAVE_IHDR | no |\n| cICP | 4 | 4 | PLTE\\|IDAT | HAVE_IHDR | no |\n| mDCV | 24 | 24 | PLTE\\|IDAT | HAVE_IHDR | no |\n| eXIf | Limit | 4 | — | HAVE_IHDR | no |\n| cLLI | 8 | 8 | PLTE\\|IDAT | HAVE_IHDR | no |\n| tEXt | NoCheck | 2 | — | HAVE_IHDR | yes |\n| zTXt | Limit | 14 | — | HAVE_IHDR | yes |\n| iTXt | NoCheck | 6 | — | HAVE_IHDR | yes |\n| bKGD | 6 | 1 | HAVE_IDAT | HAVE_IHDR | no |\n| hIST | 1024 | 0 | HAVE_PLTE | HAVE_IHDR | no |\n| pHYs | 9 | 9 | HAVE_IDAT | HAVE_IHDR | no |\n| sPLT | NoCheck | 3 | HAVE_IDAT | HAVE_IHDR | **yes** |\n| tIME | 7 | 7 | — | HAVE_IHDR | no |\n| acTL | 8 | 8 | HAVE_IDAT | HAVE_IHDR | no |\n| fcTL | 25 | **26** | — | HAVE_IHDR | yes |\n| fdAT | Limit | 4 | HAVE_IDAT | HAVE_IHDR | yes |\n| oFFs | 9 | 9 | HAVE_IDAT | HAVE_IHDR | no |\n| pCAL | NoCheck | 14 | HAVE_IDAT | HAVE_IHDR | no |\n| sCAL | Limit | 4 | HAVE_IDAT | HAVE_IHDR | no |\n\nNote `hIST` `pos_before = HAVE_PLTE` — a *bug-shaped* rule (hIST must follow PLTE, but the table says it must come *before* PLTE was seen), which means **hIST is always rejected \"out of place\" for palette PNGs** via `png_handle_chunk`. Worth a dedicated test row. Also `CDfcTL` has `max_length 25 < min_length 26` — always \"too short\".\n\n### `png_handle_IHDR` — `pngrutil.c:900-973`\nValid branches: the `switch (color_type)` channel count — `GRAY`/`PALETTE`→1 (940-943), `RGB`→3 (945), `GRAY_ALPHA`→2 (949), `RGB_ALPHA`→4 (953). Then `pixel_depth = bit_depth*channels`, `rowbytes = PNG_ROWBYTES(...)`, then `png_set_IHDR` does all validation (`png.c:~1990-2122`): 0 width, 0 height, >2^31, > `user_width_max`/`user_height_max`, bit_depth ∉ {1,2,4,8,16}, colour-type/bit-depth combination table, `interlace_type >= 2`, `compression_type != 0`, `filter_type != 0` (with the MNG-64 exception, §10). Every invalid case is `png_warning` + `error=1` → single `png_error(\"Invalid IHDR data\")`.\n**Valid-input matrix: 5 colour types × legal bit depths (GRAY:1,2,4,8,16; PALETTE:1,2,4,8; RGB/GA/RGBA:8,16) × interlace ∈{0,1} = 29 combos.**\n\n### `png_handle_PLTE` — `pngrutil.c:980-1077`\nError branches (each distinct): \"duplicate\" (992), \"out of place\" (HAVE_IDAT, 995), \"ignored in grayscale PNG\" (998), \"invalid\" (`length > 768 || length%3`, 1001), \"out of place\" (non-palette colour type where tRNS or bKGD already seen, 1015-1017).\nValid branch (1019-1057): `max_palette_length` = `1<<bit_depth` for PALETTE else 256 (1026-1028); `num` clamped, **silent truncation** when `length > 3*max_palette_length` (1033-1034); `png_crc_read(num*3)` then `png_crc_finish_critical(length - 3*num, /*ancillary if not palette*/)` (1041-1044).\nError disposition split at 1061-1071: colour type PALETTE → `png_crc_finish` + `png_chunk_error`; otherwise → `png_crc_finish_critical(…, 1)` + `png_chunk_benign_error`. **→ benign-error-gated for non-palette PNGs only.**\nRows: palette bit_depth 1/2/4/8 with exact-size palette; oversize-but-≤256 palette (truncation); PLTE in RGB PNG (allowed, \"suggested palette\"); PLTE in RGB PNG after tRNS; PLTE in gray PNG; duplicate PLTE; `length%3 != 0`.\n\n### `png_handle_IEND` — `pngrutil.c:1084-1098`\nSets `PNG_AFTER_IDAT|PNG_HAVE_IEND` (1089); `length != 0` → `png_chunk_benign_error(\"invalid\")` (1091-1092) **benign-gated**; then `png_crc_finish_critical(length, 1/*as ancillary*/)` (1094) — so a bad IEND CRC is only a warning by default. Rows: {length 0}, {length > 0}, {bad CRC}.\n\n### `png_handle_gAMA` — `pngrutil.c:1101-1134`\nBranches: CRC error → `handled_error` (1111); `ugamma > PNG_UINT_31_MAX` → benign \"invalid\" (1116-1120); else `png_set_gAMA_fixed`; then **`chunk_gamma == 0` → set it** (1128-1129) — i.e. gAMA is only honoured for gamma if no cICP/sRGB already set it. Rows: {gamma 45455}, {gamma 100000}, {gamma 0}, {gamma > 2^31}, {gAMA after sRGB → chunk_gamma unchanged}, {gAMA before sRGB}.\n\n### `png_handle_sBIT` — `pngrutil.c:1140-1202`\n`truelen`/`sample_depth` selection:\n- `PALETTE` → `truelen = 3`, `sample_depth = 8` (1149-1153)\n- else → `truelen = channels`, `sample_depth = bit_depth` (1157-1158) → GRAY:1, GRAY_ALPHA:2, RGB:3, RGB_ALPHA:4\n`length != truelen` → benign \"bad length\" (1161-1166). `buf[]` pre-filled with `sample_depth` (1168). Per-sample validation `buf[i]==0 || buf[i] > sample_depth` → benign \"invalid\" (1176-1180).\nStorage split at 1183: `COLOR_MASK_COLOR` set → red/green/blue/alpha = buf[0..3]; grayscale → `gray=red=green=blue=buf[0]`, `alpha=buf[1]` (1193-1197).\n**5 valid rows (one per colour type) plus: length mismatch per type, sig bit 0, sig bit > depth.**\n\n### `png_handle_cHRM` — `pngrutil.c:1226-1275`\nFixed 32 bytes. `png_get_int_32_checked` (1208-1224) sets `error` only for the single value `0x80000000` → benign \"invalid\" (1249-1253). Valid → `png_set_cHRM_fixed`, then `!png_has_chunk(mDCV)` → `png_ptr->chromaticities = xy` (1267-1270) for RGB-to-gray. Rows: {sRGB-like chromaticities}, {negative values}, {0x80000000 value}, {cHRM after mDCV → chromaticities not overwritten}, {cHRM before mDCV}.\n\n### `png_handle_sRGB` — `pngrutil.c:1281-1320`\n1 byte. `intent > 3` → benign \"invalid\" (1298-1302). **Valid intents 0,1,2,3 are four rows** (`png_set_sRGB` at `pngset.c` stores it and drives colorspace). Then `!png_has_chunk(cICP) || chunk_gamma == 0` → `chunk_gamma = PNG_GAMMA_sRGB_INVERSE` (45455) (1314-1315). Rows: intent 0/1/2/3, intent 4 (invalid), intent 255, sRGB+gAMA both present (order matters), sRGB+iCCP both present (explicitly allowed now, comment 1335-1338).\n\n### `png_handle_iCCP` — `pngrutil.c:1326-1544`\nDeeply nested; each level is a distinct row.\n- keyword read: `read_length = min(81, length)` (1346-1348); `length < LZ77Min (11)` after subtracting → benign \"too short\" (1353-1357).\n- `keyword_length` scan capped at 80 (1360-1363); `keyword_length < 1 || > 79` → \"bad keyword\" (1532-1533).\n- `keyword[keyword_length+1] != PNG_COMPRESSION_TYPE_BASE` or `keyword_length+1 >= read_length` → \"bad compression method\" (1528-1529).\n- `png_inflate_claim(png_iCCP)` fails → `errmsg = zstream.msg` (1524-1525).\n- 132-byte header inflate (1384-1386, `finish = 0`); `size != 0` → \"profile truncated\" (1517-1518).\n- `png_icc_check_length` (`png.c:1593-1608`): `profile_length < 132` → \"too short\"; `profile_length > png_chunk_max` → \"profile too long\". **This is where `png_set_chunk_malloc_max` bites iCCP.**\n- `png_icc_check_header` (`png.c:1613-1791`) — distinct sub-branches, each an error unless noted:\n  - `profile[0..3] != profile_length` → \"length does not match profile\"\n  - `profile[8] > 3 && (profile_length & 3)` → \"invalid length\"\n  - tag count `> 357913930` or `profile_length < 132+12*count` → \"tag count too large\"\n  - rendering intent `>= 0xffff` → \"invalid rendering intent\"; `>= PNG_sRGB_INTENT_LAST (4)` → **warning only**, continues\n  - signature at +36 != `'acsp'` → \"invalid signature\"\n  - PCS illuminant at +68 != D50 → **warning only**, continues\n  - data colour space at +16: `'RGB '` on grayscale PNG → error; `'GRAY'` on colour PNG → error; anything else → \"invalid ICC profile color space\". **Valid rows: `'RGB '` with colour types 2/3/6; `'GRAY'` with colour types 0/4.**\n  - profile class at +12: `'scnr'`/`'mntr'`/`'prtr'`/`'spac'` → OK (4 valid rows); `'abst'` → error; `'link'` → error; `'nmcl'` → **warning only**; anything else → **warning only**\n  - PCS at +20: `'XYZ '` or `'Lab '` → OK (2 valid rows); else \"unexpected ICC PCS encoding\"\n- tag-table inflate (1420-1422); `size != 0` → \"profile truncated\" (1503-1504)\n- `png_read_buffer(profile_length)` returns NULL → \"out of memory\" (1507-1508)\n- `png_icc_check_tag_table` (`png.c:1797…`) failure — emits its own error\n- final body inflate with `finish = 1` (1438-1441). Then **the benign-errors interaction at 1443-1445**: `length > 0 && !(flags & PNG_FLAG_BENIGN_ERRORS_WARN)` → `errmsg = \"extra compressed data\"` (hard error); else if `size == 0` and `length > 0` → `png_chunk_warning(\"extra compressed data\")` and **continue to success** (1450-1457). This is the only place in the codebase where the benign-error flag changes *control flow* rather than just severity.\n- `info_ptr != NULL` → profile \"stolen\" into `info_ptr->iccp_profile` with `read_buffer = NULL` (1463-1485); `iccp_name` malloc failure → \"out of memory\". `info_ptr == NULL` → profile stays in `read_buffer` and is reused (comment 1487-1490).\n- **`PNG_sRGB_PROFILE_CHECKS` and `PNG_SKIP_sRGB_CHECK_PROFILE` play no part** — the sRGB-profile-comparison code that existed in older 1.6.x is gone from `png.c` in this tree (grep confirms zero references outside `png.h`/`pnglibconf.h`).\n\n### `png_handle_sPLT` — `pngrutil.c:1550-1680`\n- **chunk-cache gate at 1566-1582**: `user_chunk_cache_max == 1` → silent discard; `--max == 1` → `png_warning(\"No space in chunk cache for sPLT\")` + discard. (Note: `png_warning`, not benign error, unlike tEXt/zTXt/iTXt.)\n- `png_read_buffer(length+1) == NULL` → benign \"out of memory\" (1585-1590)\n- name scan (1604-1607) then `length < 2 || entry_start > buffer + length-2` → `png_warning(\"malformed sPLT chunk\")` (1610-1614)\n- **`new_palette.depth == 8` → `entry_size = 6`; else → `entry_size = 10`** (1617). Note: **any depth other than 8 is treated as 16** — no validation of depth ∈ {8,16}. Two valid rows plus a \"depth = 5 behaves as 16\" row.\n- `data_length % entry_size != 0` → `png_warning(\"sPLT chunk has bad length\")` (1624-1628)\n- `dl > PNG_SIZE_MAX/sizeof(png_sPLT_entry)` → `png_warning(\"sPLT chunk too long\")` (1633-1637)\n- `png_malloc_warn` fails → `png_warning(\"sPLT chunk requires too much memory\")` (1644-1648)\n- per-entry read: depth-8 path 4×byte + 16-bit frequency (1656-1659); depth-16 path 4×uint16 + frequency (1664-1667)\n- multiple sPLT allowed (`multiple = 1` in the table).\n\n### `png_handle_tRNS` — `pngrutil.c:1686-1765`\nFour colour-type branches:\n- `GRAY` (1693): `length != 2` → benign \"invalid\"; else `num_trans=1`, `trans_color.gray = uint16`\n- `RGB` (1709): `length != 6` → benign \"invalid\"; else `num_trans=1`, r/g/b\n- `PALETTE` (1727): `!(mode & HAVE_PLTE)` → benign \"out of place\"; `length > num_palette || length > 256 || length == 0` → benign \"invalid\"; else `num_trans = length`, alpha array in `readbuf`\n- `GRAY_ALPHA`/`RGB_ALPHA` (1749) → benign \"invalid with alpha channel\"\nThen a shared `png_crc_finish(0)`: **on CRC error `num_trans` is reset to 0** (1756-1760).\nNote `readbuf` is **uninitialized** for the GRAY/RGB paths but still passed to `png_set_tRNS` (1762) — harmless because `num_trans==1` and `png_set_tRNS` only reads the array for palette images, but worth pinning.\nRows: 5 colour types × {correct length, wrong length}; palette w/o PLTE; palette length 0; palette length > num_palette; bad CRC.\n\n### `png_handle_bKGD` — `pngrutil.c:1771-1876`\n`truelen` selection: `PALETTE` → 1 (with `!(mode & HAVE_PLTE)` → benign \"out of place\" first, 1782-1787); `COLOR_MASK_COLOR` set → 6 (1792); else → 2 (1796). `length != truelen` → benign \"invalid\" (1798-1803).\nThree value-decode branches:\n- PALETTE (1815): `index = buf[0]`; `info_ptr != NULL && info_ptr->num_palette != 0` → `buf[0] >= num_palette` → benign \"invalid index\" (1821-1825), else RGB copied from `png_ptr->palette`; **`info_ptr == NULL` or `num_palette == 0` → RGB set to 0** (1832-1833). This is a real config axis: bKGD validity depends on whether the palette is in `info_ptr`.\n- GRAY (1838): `bit_depth <= 8` → `buf[0] != 0 || buf[1] >= (1<<bit_depth)` → benign \"invalid gray level\" (1842-1846). **No check at bit_depth 16.**\n- COLOUR (1856): `bit_depth <= 8` → `buf[0]|buf[2]|buf[4]` must be 0 → benign \"invalid color\" (1860-1864). **No check at bit_depth 16.**\nRows: palette (valid index / out-of-range index / `info_ptr==NULL`); gray 1/2/4/8 in-range and out-of-range; gray 16; RGB 8 with clean/dirty high bytes; RGB 16; each with wrong length; GRAY_ALPHA (truelen 2) and RGB_ALPHA (truelen 6) also valid.\n\n### `png_handle_cICP` — `pngrutil.c:1882-1915`\nFixed 4 bytes, no validation here — `png_set_cICP` does it. The RGB-to-gray chromaticities update is a **TODO stub** (1900) and the gamma update is a **TODO** (1910) — so cICP currently has *no* effect on `chunk_gamma` despite the precedence comments in gAMA/sRGB. Rows: {valid 4 bytes}, {each of the 4 fields at boundary values that `png_set_cICP` rejects — check `pngset.c`}, {cICP + gAMA}, {cICP + sRGB}.\n\n### `png_handle_cLLI` — `pngrutil.c:1921-1938`\nFixed 8 bytes → `png_set_cLLI_fixed(maxCLL, maxFALL)`; all validation deferred to the setter. Rows: {both 0}, {maxFALL > maxCLL}, {max values}.\n\n### `png_handle_mDCV` — `pngrutil.c:1944-1992`\nFixed 24 bytes. 8 × `uint16 << 1` (note the /50000 vs /100000 scaling and the R,G,B,W ordering vs cHRM's W,R,G,B — comment 1961-1966), then peak/min luminance from +16/+20. **Unconditionally overwrites `png_ptr->chromaticities`** (1987) — unlike cHRM/cICP which check `png_has_chunk(mDCV)`. Rows: {mDCV alone}, {cHRM then mDCV}, {mDCV then cHRM}, {luminance 0}.\n\n### `png_handle_eXIf` — `pngrutil.c:1998-2036`\n`png_read_buffer(length)` NULL → benign \"out of memory\" (2007-2012) — **reachable via `png_set_chunk_malloc_max`** since the table uses `Limit`. Header check: first 4 bytes must be `0x49492A00` (\"II\\*\\0\") or `0x4D4D002A` (\"MM\\0\\*\") else benign \"invalid\" (2027-2031). Rows: {II little-endian}, {MM big-endian}, {bad magic}, {length exactly 4}, {length > chunk_max}.\n\n### `png_handle_hIST` — `pngrutil.c:2042-2080`\n`num = length/2`; `length != num*2 || num != num_palette || num > 256` → benign \"invalid\" (2058-2065). Per-entry 2-byte `png_crc_read` in a loop (2067-2073) — note **one CRC read call per entry**, unlike other handlers. Valid row requires `num_palette` entries exactly. **But see the `pos_before = HAVE_PLTE` table bug above — for a palette PNG `png_handle_chunk` rejects hIST \"out of place\" before the handler runs.** Test both `png_handle_chunk`-mediated and (progressive) direct paths.\n\n### `png_handle_pHYs` — `pngrutil.c:2086-2106`\nFixed 9 bytes. `unit_type = buf[8]`. Rows: unit 0 (unknown), unit 1 (metre), unit ≥ 2 (validated in `png_set_pHYs`), res 0.\n\n### `png_handle_oFFs` — `pngrutil.c:2112-2132`\nFixed 9 bytes, **signed** offsets via `png_get_int_32` (which returns 0 for `0x80000000`, `pngrutil.c:79-94`). Rows: unit 0 (pixel), unit 1 (micrometre), negative offsets, `0x80000000` offset.\n\n### `png_handle_pCAL` — `pngrutil.c:2139-2256`\n- `png_read_buffer(length+1)` NULL → benign \"out of memory\"\n- purpose-string scan (2173-2174); `endptr - buf <= 12` → benign \"invalid\" (2181-2185)\n- **equation-type × nparams check (2198-2205)** — each is a distinct row:\n  - `PNG_EQUATION_LINEAR (0)` requires nparams == 2\n  - `PNG_EQUATION_BASE_E (1)` requires nparams == 3\n  - `PNG_EQUATION_ARBITRARY (2)` requires nparams == 3\n  - `PNG_EQUATION_HYPERBOLIC (3)` requires nparams == 4\n  - mismatch → benign \"invalid parameter count\"\n  - `type >= PNG_EQUATION_LAST (4)` → benign \"unrecognized equation type\" **and then continues** (2207-2210) — i.e. non-fatal when benign-errors warn.\n- parameter-pointer walk (2227-2243): `buf > endptr` → free + benign \"invalid data\"\n- `png_malloc_warn(nparams * sizeof(png_charp))` NULL → benign \"out of memory\" (2220-2224). Note `nparams == 0` (type ≥ 4) → zero-size malloc.\n- `png_set_pCAL` may itself `png_chunk_report` (see the acknowledged TODO/BUG comment at 2248-2253).\nRows: 4 valid equation types with correct nparams; each with wrong nparams; type 4/255; purpose string too long; missing parameter separators; truncated last parameter.\n\n### `png_handle_sCAL` — `pngrutil.c:2263-2331`\n- `png_read_buffer(length+1)` NULL → benign \"out of memory\"\n- **`buffer[0] != 1 && buffer[0] != 2` → benign \"invalid unit\"** (2290-2294). Two valid unit rows: 1 = metre, 2 = radian.\n- width string: `png_check_fp_number(buffer, length, &state, &i) == 0 || i >= length || buffer[i++] != 0` → benign \"bad width format\" (2302-2304)\n- `PNG_FP_IS_POSITIVE(state) == 0` → benign \"non-positive width\" (2306-2307)\n- height string: parse failure or `i != length` → benign \"bad height format\" (2314-2316)\n- non-positive height → benign \"non-positive height\" (2318-2319)\n- **single success path** → `png_set_sCAL_s` (2324-2326)\nString-form rows worth enumerating (all go through `png_check_fp_number`, `png.c:~2130+`): `\"1\"`, `\"1.5\"`, `\"1e2\"`, `\"1.5e-3\"`, `\"+1\"`, `\"-1\"` (non-positive), `\"0\"` (non-positive), `\".5\"`, `\"1.\"`, `\"1e\"` (bad), `\"\"` (bad), embedded extra NUL, missing trailing NUL, height field absent.\n\n### `png_handle_tIME` — `pngrutil.c:2337-2367`\nFixed 7 bytes. Note the odd `mode |= PNG_AFTER_IDAT` at 2349-2350 (with a TODO admitting it's misplaced). `png_set_tIME` validates month 1-12, day 1-31, hour ≤ 23, minute ≤ 59, second ≤ 60. Rows: {valid}, {month 0}, {month 13}, {day 0/32}, {hour 24}, {second 60 (leap)}, {second 61}, {tIME before IDAT}, {tIME after IDAT}.\n\n### `png_handle_tEXt` — `pngrutil.c:2374-2439`\n- **chunk-cache gate (2385-2401)**: `==1` → silent discard; `--max==1` → benign \"no space in chunk cache\" + discard.\n- `png_read_buffer(length+1)` NULL → benign \"out of memory\"\n- key/text split at first NUL (2420-2424); **`text != key + length` → `text++`**, i.e. a tEXt with no NUL separator yields `text` pointing at the terminating NUL (empty text) rather than an error.\n- `png_set_text_2 != 0` → benign \"out of memory\" (2437)\n- `compression = PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_NONE`, `text_length = strlen(text)`\n- `multiple = 1`, `min_length = 2`\nRows: {key + text}, {key only, no separator}, {key + empty text}, {embedded NULs in text (truncated by strlen)}, {79-char key}, {80-char key}, {chunk cache exhausted}, {many tEXt chunks growing `info_ptr->text` array in 8-slot steps, `pngset.c` `png_set_text_2`}.\n\n### `png_handle_zTXt` — `pngrutil.c:2446-2555`\n- chunk-cache gate (2455-2471), identical to tEXt\n- `png_read_buffer(length)` — note **no `+1`** (2477), with the rationale comment at 2473-2476\n- keyword scan; `keyword_length > 79 || < 1` → \"bad keyword\" (2497-2498)\n- `keyword_length + 3 > length` → \"truncated\" (2504-2505)\n- `buffer[keyword_length+1] != PNG_COMPRESSION_TYPE_BASE` → \"unknown compression type\" (2507-2508)\n- `png_decompress_chunk(png_ptr, length, keyword_length+2, &uncompressed_length /*=PNG_SIZE_MAX*/, 1 /*terminate*/)`:\n  - `!= Z_STREAM_END` → `errmsg = zstream.msg` (2550)\n  - `== Z_STREAM_END` but `read_buffer == NULL` → \"Read failure in png_handle_zTXt\" (2523-2524)\n  - success → `text.compression = PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt`, `text_length = uncompressed_length`\n- `png_set_text_2 != 0` → \"out of memory\"\n- table `max_length = Limit` → `png_set_chunk_malloc_max` gates the *compressed* size; `png_decompress_chunk` gates the *uncompressed* size (§7).\nRows: {valid}, {empty text expanding to 0 bytes}, {keyword 1 char}, {keyword 79}, {keyword 80}, {compression method 1}, {truncated LZ}, {corrupt LZ}, {extra compressed data → \"extra compressed data\" benign error from `png_decompress_chunk:789`}, {uncompressed size > `chunk_max`}, {chunk cache exhausted}.\n\n### `png_handle_iTXt` — `pngrutil.c:2562-2704`\n- chunk-cache gate (2571-2587)\n- `png_read_buffer(length+1)` NULL → benign \"out of memory\"\n- keyword scan; `prefix_length > 79 || < 1` → \"bad keyword\" (2610-2611)\n- `prefix_length + 5 > length` → \"truncated\" (2617-2618)\n- **compression-flag/method gate at 2620-2622**: accepted iff `buffer[pl+1] == 0` (uncompressed, method byte ignored) **or** (`buffer[pl+1] == 1 && buffer[pl+2] == PNG_COMPRESSION_TYPE_BASE`). Anything else → \"bad compression info\" (2698-2699). Note **flag 0 does not validate the method byte at all**.\n- `compressed = buffer[pl+1] != 0` (2624)\n- language tag scan (2632-2634) then translated-keyword scan (2639-2641), `prefix_length` advanced past both\n- **uncompressed branch** (2650-2651): `prefix_length <= length` → `uncompressed_length = length - prefix_length`; else → \"truncated\" (2670)\n- **compressed branch** (2653-2667): `prefix_length < length` → `uncompressed_length = PNG_SIZE_MAX`, `png_decompress_chunk(…, prefix_length, …, 1)`; `Z_STREAM_END` → `buffer = read_buffer`; else `errmsg = zstream.msg`\n- success: `text.compression = PNG_ITXT_COMPRESSION_NONE` or `PNG_ITXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt`, `itxt_length = uncompressed_length`, `text_length = 0`, `lang`/`lang_key` pointers into buffer\nRows: {uncompressed with lang+translated}, {uncompressed with empty lang and empty translated}, {compressed with lang}, {compressed, empty text}, {flag 0 with method byte 1 (accepted!)}, {flag 1 method 1 (rejected)}, {flag 2 (rejected)}, {missing translated-keyword NUL → prefix_length runs past length → \"truncated\"}, {keyword 0/1/79/80}, {chunk cache exhausted}, {`Limit`/`chunk_max`}.\n\n### Benign-error-gated handlers (summary for §11)\nEvery handler above that calls `png_chunk_benign_error` changes severity with `png_set_benign_errors`: **PLTE (non-palette only), IEND, gAMA, sBIT, cHRM, sRGB, iCCP, tRNS, bKGD, eXIf, hIST, pCAL, sCAL, tEXt, zTXt, iTXt, `png_handle_chunk`'s generic ancillary error path (3206), `png_handle_unknown`'s \"unknown chunk exceeds memory limits\" (2745) and \"no space in chunk cache\" (2912), `png_read_info`'s \"Too many IDATs found\" (125), `png_read_end`'s two \"Too many IDATs\" messages (729, 747), `png_read_end`'s \"Read palette index exceeding num_palette\" (697, via `png_benign_error`), `png_read_IDAT_data`'s \"Extra compressed data\" (4276) / \"Too much image data\" (4304) / zstream error while checking (4289), and `png_decompress_chunk`'s \"extra compressed data\" (789).** `png_handle_sPLT` is the odd one out — it uses plain `png_warning` (1577, 1612, 1626, 1635, 1646) so it is **not** benign-error-gated.\n\n---\n\n## 3. `png_read_update_info` vs `png_start_read_image`\n\n### `png_read_update_info` — `pngread.c:171-194`\n- `png_ptr == NULL` → no-op\n- `!(flags & PNG_FLAG_ROW_INIT)` → `png_read_start_row(png_ptr)` **then** `png_read_transform_info(png_ptr, info_ptr)` (183). The latter writes `png_ptr->info_rowbytes = info_ptr->rowbytes` (`pngrtran.c:2277`).\n- else → `png_app_error(\"png_read_update_info/png_start_read_image: duplicate call\")` (191-192). **Because `PNG_RELEASE_BUILD == 0`, `PNG_FLAG_APP_ERRORS_WARN` is unset by default → this is a FATAL error unless `png_set_benign_errors(1)` was called.** Major test axis.\n\n### `png_start_read_image` — `pngread.c:202-217`\nSame `PNG_FLAG_ROW_INIT` gate but **does not** call `png_read_transform_info` → `info_rowbytes` stays 0 → the consistency check in `png_combine_row` (`pngrutil.c:3249-3251`, \"internal row size calculation error\") is **disabled**. Duplicate call → same `png_app_error`.\n\n### Ordering matrix (rows)\n1. neither called; `png_read_row` self-initializes via `pngread.c:301-302`\n2. `png_start_read_image` then `png_read_row`\n3. `png_read_update_info` then `png_read_row` (info_rowbytes check live)\n4. `png_read_update_info` twice → app_error\n5. `png_start_read_image` twice → app_error\n6. `png_read_update_info` then `png_start_read_image` → app_error\n7. `png_start_read_image` then `png_read_update_info` → app_error, **and `info_ptr` is never updated** (silent data mismatch for the app)\n8. transform set *after* `png_read_update_info` → ignored, likely \"internal sequential row size calculation error\" at `pngread.c:493`\n9. `png_read_image` after either (see §5, `pngread.c:626-645`)\n\n### `png_read_start_row` — `pngrutil.c:4407-4683`\nBranches:\n- `png_init_read_transformations` (4416)\n- interlaced (4418): `PNG_INTERLACE` clear → `num_rows = ceil(height/8)`; set → `num_rows = height` (4425); `iwidth` from pass-0 arrays. Non-interlaced (4433) → `num_rows = height`, `iwidth = width`.\n- `max_pixel_depth` computation — **each `#ifdef` block is a distinct configuration axis**: PACK (4452), EXPAND per colour type with/without tRNS (4457-4485), EXPAND_16 with/without EXPAND (**clears `PNG_EXPAND_16` if EXPAND absent**, 4502), FILLER per colour type (4507-4527), GRAY_TO_RGB with 5 sub-branches (4531-4567), USER_TRANSFORM depth override (4572-4579).\n- `row_bytes` = width rounded up to 8 pixels, `+1 + ((max_pixel_depth+7)>>3)`; `> 65536` only under `PNG_MAX_MALLOC_64K` (not set)\n- **buffer reuse gate at 4603**: `row_bytes + 48 > old_big_row_buf_size` → free + realloc; interlaced → `png_calloc`, non-interlaced → `png_malloc` (4609-4614). Re-entry with a smaller image reuses the old buffer.\n- aligned vs unaligned `row_buf`/`prev_row` placement (4626-4639)\n- `rowbytes > PNG_SIZE_MAX - 1` → `png_error(\"Row has too many bytes to allocate in memory\")` (4648)\n- `memset(prev_row, 0, rowbytes+1)` (4651)\n- **frees `read_buffer` unconditionally** (4665-4672)\n- `png_inflate_claim(png_IDAT)` failure → `png_error(zstream.msg)` (4679) — reachable with a bad deflate CINFO when `PNG_MAXIMUM_INFLATE_WINDOW` is off\n- sets `PNG_FLAG_ROW_INIT` (4682)\n\n### `png_read_finish_row` — `pngrutil.c:4356-4404`\n- `++row_number < num_rows` → return (4360-4362)\n- non-interlaced → falls through to `png_read_finish_IDAT` (4403)\n- interlaced (4364): `row_number = 0`, `memset(prev_row, 0, rowbytes+1)` (4371), then the pass-advance `do…while` (4373-4396):\n  - `++pass >= 7` → break\n  - recompute `iwidth` from `png_pass_inc`/`png_pass_start`\n  - `PNG_INTERLACE` **clear** → recompute `num_rows`, and the loop condition `num_rows == 0 || iwidth == 0` **skips empty passes**\n  - `PNG_INTERLACE` **set** → unconditional `break` at 4394 (\"libpng deinterlacing sees every row\"), so `num_rows` stays `height` and **all 7 passes are always iterated**\n  - `pass < 7` → return; else `png_read_finish_IDAT`\n\n### `png_read_finish_IDAT` — `pngrutil.c:4308-4354`\n- `!(flags & PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_ENDED)` → `png_read_IDAT_data(png_ptr, NULL, 0)` to swallow the LZ tail (4322), then force `PNG_AFTER_IDAT|PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_ENDED` if still unset (4328-4332)\n- `zowner == png_IDAT` → clear `next_in`/`avail_in`, `zowner = 0`, `png_crc_finish(png_ptr, idat_size)` (4338-4353). `idat_size > 0` means trailing garbage in the last IDAT is skipped here.\nRows: {stream ends exactly}, {truncated stream}, {trailing bytes in last IDAT}, {`png_read_end` called mid-image}, {called twice — idempotent because of the `zowner` and flag guards}.\n\n---\n\n## 4. `png_read_row` — `pngread.c:287-524`\n\nBranch inventory in order:\n\n1. `png_ptr == NULL` → return (292)\n2. `!(flags & PNG_FLAG_ROW_INIT)` → `png_read_start_row` (301-302) — the implicit-init path\n3. `row_info` built from `iwidth`, `color_type`, `bit_depth`, `channels`, `pixel_depth` (305-310)\n4. `row_number == 0 && pass == 0` warning block (313-351) — **all `#if` bodies are dead in this build** because every corresponding `PNG_READ_*_SUPPORTED` is defined. No rows.\n5. **Interlace-skip switch (361-440)**, gated on `interlaced != 0 && (transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) != 0`. Per pass, the skip condition and the display-combine sub-condition:\n\n| pass | skip when | dsp_row combined during skip |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | `row_number & 7` | always (if dsp_row) |\n| 1 | `(row_number & 7) \\|\\| width < 5` | always (if dsp_row) |\n| 2 | `(row_number & 7) != 4` | only if `row_number & 4` |\n| 3 | `(row_number & 3) \\|\\| width < 3` | always (if dsp_row) |\n| 4 | `(row_number & 3) != 2` | only if `row_number & 2` |\n| 5 | `(row_number & 1) \\|\\| width < 2` | always (if dsp_row) |\n| 6 (`default:`) | `(row_number & 1) == 0` | **never** — `row` and `dsp_row` both ignored |\n\n   Each skip path calls `png_read_finish_row` and returns **without** invoking `read_row_fn`.\n   Note the *empty-pass* conditions are width-based only: pass 1 empty for `width < 5`, pass 3 for `width < 3`, pass 5 for `width < 2`. Height-based emptiness is handled by `png_read_finish_row` **only when `PNG_INTERLACE` is off**. Test widths 1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8 and heights 1..8 crossed with interlace on/off.\n6. `!(mode & PNG_HAVE_IDAT)` → `png_error(\"Invalid attempt to read row data\")` (443-444)\n7. `row_buf[0] = 255` sentinel then `png_read_IDAT_data(row_buf, rowbytes+1)` (447-448)\n8. filter dispatch (450-457): `row_buf[0] == 0` → nothing; `1..4` → `png_read_filter_row`; `>= PNG_FILTER_VALUE_LAST (5)` → `png_error(\"bad adaptive filter value\")` (this catches the 255 sentinel when zlib produced no data)\n9. `memcpy(prev_row, row_buf, rowbytes+1)` (464) — **note it copies only the interlaced row length, not full `rowbytes`**\n10. MNG intrapixel (466-473): `(mng_features_permitted & PNG_FLAG_MNG_FILTER_64) && filter_type == PNG_INTRAPIXEL_DIFFERENCING` → `png_do_read_intrapixel` (`pngread.c:226-284`), which itself branches on `COLOR_MASK_COLOR`, `bit_depth == 8` vs `16`, and `RGB` (3/6 bytes) vs `RGB_ALPHA` (4/8 bytes) with an early `return` for anything else. **4 valid combinations.**\n11. **`png_ptr->transformations` gate (476-481)**: transforms run iff `transformations != 0` **or** `num_palette_max >= 0` (the latter only under `PNG_CHECK_FOR_INVALID_INDEX_SUPPORTED`, which is on). So a palette image with `png_set_check_for_invalid_index` enabled enters `png_do_read_transformations` even with zero transforms. Two rows: {transformations == 0, non-palette → skip}, {transformations == 0, palette with index checking → enter}.\n12. transformed-depth validation (485-493): first row sets `transformed_pixel_depth`; `> maximum_pixel_depth` → `png_error(\"sequential row overflow\")`; subsequent mismatch → `png_error(\"internal sequential row size calculation error\")`. Reachable by setting a transform after `png_read_update_info`.\n13. **de-interlace / combine (495-519)**:\n    - interlaced **and** `PNG_INTERLACE` set: `pass < 6` → `png_do_read_interlace(&row_info, row_buf+1, pass, transformations)` (500-502) — **pass 6 is skipped because it is already full-width**; then `dsp_row != NULL` → `png_combine_row(dsp_row, 1 /*display*/)`; then `row != NULL` → `png_combine_row(row, 0 /*row*/)`. **This is the sparkle (row, display=0) vs rectangle/block (dsp_row, display=1) split.**\n    - otherwise (513-519): `row != NULL` → `png_combine_row(row, -1)`; `dsp_row != NULL` → `png_combine_row(dsp_row, -1)`. Here `display` is ignored and `png_combine_row` degenerates to the `memcpy` at `pngrutil.c:3702`.\n14. `png_read_finish_row` (520)\n15. `read_row_fn != NULL` → callback (522-523)\n\n**`row`/`dsp_row` nullness matrix (4 rows) × interlace-handling-set (2) × interlaced-image (2) = 16 rows**, of which the interesting ones are: both NULL + interlaced + PNG_INTERLACE (data read and discarded, still advances), `row` NULL only, `dsp_row` NULL only, both non-NULL.\n\n**`png_combine_row` — `pngrutil.c:3226-3707`** sub-branches worth their own rows:\n- `pixel_depth == 0` → `png_error(\"internal row logic error\")` (3242)\n- `info_rowbytes != 0` mismatch → `png_error(\"internal row size calculation error\")` (3249) — only live after `png_read_update_info`\n- `row_width == 0` → `png_error(\"internal row width error\")` (3254)\n- `end_mask != 0` partial-last-byte preservation, with a PACKSWAP variant (3261-3276) and the restore at 3705-3706\n- interlace branch condition (3285-3289): requires `pass < 6` **and** (`display == 0` **or** (`display == 1 && (pass & 1) != 0`)) — so display copies on odd passes 1,3,5 only; even passes fall through to the whole-row `memcpy`\n- `row_width <= PNG_PASS_START_COL(pass)` → early return (3294)\n- `pixel_depth < 8` → compile-time mask path (3297-3470), indexed by `[PACKSWAP][depth 1/2/4][pass]` for sparkle and `[PACKSWAP][depth][pass>>1]` for display\n- `pixel_depth >= 8`: `pixel_depth & 7` → `png_error(\"invalid user transform pixel depth\")` (3477); then `bytes_to_copy` switch with cases **1, 2, 3, default** (3523-3688); `default` further splits into 32-bit-aligned, 16-bit-aligned, and `memcpy` paths (3582-3687)\n- non-interlace `memcpy` (3702)\n\nRows for `png_combine_row`: bit depths 1,2,4 × PACKSWAP on/off × display 0/1 × passes 0-6; byte depths 1 (gray8), 2 (gray16/GA8), 3 (RGB8), 4 (RGBA8), 6 (RGB16), 8 (RGBA16) × display 0/1 × misaligned buffer.\n\n**`png_do_read_interlace` — `pngrutil.c:3710-3950`**: four `pixel_depth` cases — 1 (3723), 2 (3786), 4 (3850), and `default` byte-wise (3913). Each of the first three has a PACKSWAP variant. `row == NULL || row_info == NULL` → whole body skipped (3715). Rows: depths 1,2,4 × PACKSWAP × passes 0-5; depths 8,16,24,32,48,64 × passes 0-5.\n\n---\n\n## 5. `png_read_rows`, `png_read_image`, `png_read_end`, destroy\n\n### `png_read_rows` — `pngread.c:552-591`\nFour branches:\n1. `png_ptr == NULL` → return (562)\n2. `row != NULL && display_row != NULL` → both advanced per row (567-574)\n3. `row != NULL` only → `png_read_row(rptr, NULL)` (576-582)\n4. `display_row != NULL` only → `png_read_row(NULL, dptr)` (584-590)\n5. **both NULL → the function does nothing at all; `num_rows` rows are NOT consumed.** This is a silent no-op, a good test row.\nAlso: `num_rows == 0`; `num_rows` greater than remaining rows (runs into \"Not enough image data\" from `png_read_IDAT_data`); individual `*rp` entries NULL (passed straight through to `png_read_row`).\n\n### `png_read_image` — `pngread.c:607-665`\nTwo top branches:\n- `!(flags & PNG_FLAG_ROW_INIT)` (620): `pass = png_set_interlace_handling(png_ptr)` (returns 7 if interlaced, 1 otherwise — `pngtrans.c:127-138`) **then** `png_start_read_image` (624)\n- else (627): if `interlaced && !(transformations & PNG_INTERLACE)` → `png_warning(\"Interlace handling should be turned on when using png_read_image\")` **and forcibly `num_rows = height`** (635-638); then `pass = png_set_interlace_handling(png_ptr)` again (644). The comment at 641-643 notes this second call also *turns on* the flag in the error case.\n- The `#else` at 646-652 (`png_error(\"Cannot read interlaced image -- interlace handler disabled\")`) is **dead** — `PNG_READ_INTERLACING_SUPPORTED` is defined.\n- loop: `pass` iterations × `height` rows, always `png_read_row(*rp, NULL)` (656-664) — **`display_row` is never used**, so the \"rectangle\" display path is unreachable through `png_read_image`.\nRows: {non-interlaced, fresh}, {interlaced, fresh}, {interlaced after `png_start_read_image` without interlace handling → warning + fix-up}, {interlaced after `png_read_update_info` without interlace handling}, {interlaced after explicit `png_set_interlace_handling` + `png_start_read_image`}, {called twice → \"Not enough image data\"}.\n\n### `png_read_end` — `pngread.c:673-755`\n- `png_ptr == NULL` → return\n- `png_chunk_unknown_handling(png_IDAT) == 0` → `png_read_finish_IDAT` (689-691). **If IDAT is registered for unknown handling, `png_read_finish_IDAT` is skipped entirely.**\n- palette-index check (693-698): `color_type == PALETTE && num_palette_max >= num_palette` → `png_benign_error(\"Read palette index exceeding num_palette\")`. Gated by `png_set_check_for_invalid_index`.\n- `do…while ((mode & PNG_HAVE_IEND) == 0)` loop; per iteration:\n  - non-IDAT → `mode |= PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_AFTER_IDAT | PNG_AFTER_IDAT` (705-711)\n  - `IEND` → `png_handle_chunk` (713-714)\n  - `IHDR` → `png_handle_chunk` (716-717)\n  - **`info_ptr == NULL` → `png_crc_finish(length)`, chunk discarded** (719-720). This is the \"read_end without info_ptr\" path: *all* ancillary chunks after IDAT are silently skipped, and only IEND/IHDR are processed.\n  - `keep != 0` → if IDAT, the two-part \"Too many IDATs\" benign check (725-730, message `\".Too many IDATs found\"`); then `png_handle_unknown`; PLTE sets `HAVE_PLTE` (731-733)\n  - `IDAT` → the same benign check (message `\"..Too many IDATs found\"`, 745-747) then `png_crc_finish` (749)\n  - else → `png_handle_chunk` (753)\n- **No IEND → infinite loop terminated by `png_read_chunk_header`'s `png_read_data` hitting EOF** (`png_default_read_data`'s `check != length` → `png_error(\"Read Error\")`).\nRows: {info_ptr non-NULL, tEXt+tIME after IDAT}, {info_ptr NULL}, {zero-length IDAT after last IDAT (legal)}, {non-zero IDAT after last IDAT}, {IDAT after a non-IDAT chunk}, {IHDR after IDAT → \"duplicate\"/\"out of place\" via table}, {missing IEND}, {`png_read_end` immediately after `png_read_info` (skips all rows)}, {IDAT in the keep list}.\n\n### `png_read_destroy` — `pngread.c:759-826`\nFrees (each conditional a row if you're testing leak-freedom): gamma tables (765), `big_row_buf`/`big_prev_row`/`read_buffer` (768-773), `palette_lookup`/`quantize_index` (776-779), `palette` (785), `trans_alpha` (793), `inflateEnd` (797), `save_buffer` (800), `unknown_chunk.data` (806), `chunk_list` (811). `riffled_palette` (818) is compiled out.\n\n### `png_destroy_read_struct` — `pngread.c:829-853`\nBranches: `png_ptr_ptr == NULL` → return (837-841); `*png_ptr_ptr == NULL` → return; `end_info_ptr_ptr` NULL vs non-NULL; `info_ptr_ptr` NULL vs non-NULL (both go to `png_destroy_info_struct`). Ordering: end_info destroyed first (847). **Note `*png_ptr_ptr = NULL` happens before `png_read_destroy`** (850-851), so an error inside destroy leaves a leak, not a dangling pointer.\nRows: {all three pointers}, {info only}, {none}, {called twice}, {called after a longjmp out of `png_read_row`}.\n\n---\n\n## 6. `png_read_filter_row` — `pngrutil.c:4153-4168`\n\n- `filter <= PNG_FILTER_VALUE_NONE (0) || filter >= PNG_FILTER_VALUE_LAST (5)` → **silent no-op** (4161). Note `png_read_row` already screens this at `pngread.c:450-457`, so the NONE case never reaches here from the sequential reader.\n- `pp->read_filter[0] == NULL` → `png_init_filter_functions(pp)` (4163-4164) — lazy, once per image (`read_filter[]` is not reset by `png_read_start_row`, so a second image in the same struct keeps the first image's Paeth variant — a genuine latent axis if a struct is reused).\n- dispatch `pp->read_filter[filter-1](row_info, row, prev_row)` (4166)\n\n`png_init_filter_functions` — `pngrutil.c:4116-4151`: `bpp = (pixel_depth+7)>>3`; installs SUB, UP, AVG unconditionally; **`bpp == 1` → `png_read_filter_row_paeth_1byte_pixel`, else `png_read_filter_row_paeth_multibyte_pixel`** (4133-4138). `PNG_FILTER_OPTIMIZATIONS` is not defined → no hardware override. **No `png_read_filter_row_*` specializations beyond these five functions.**\n\nThe five implementations:\n| filter | function | line | bpp dependence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| NONE (0) | — (no-op) | — | none |\n| SUB (1) | `png_read_filter_row_sub` | 3953 | loops `i = bpp … rowbytes`; **when `rowbytes <= bpp` the loop body never runs** |\n| UP (2) | `png_read_filter_row_up` | 3971 | none — pure byte-wise add over `rowbytes` |\n| AVG (3) | `png_read_filter_row_avg` | 3987 | first `bpp` bytes use `prev/2` only; `istop = rowbytes - bpp` — **underflows if `rowbytes < bpp`** |\n| PAETH (4) | `png_read_filter_row_paeth_1byte_pixel` | 4014 | bpp == 1 only; carries `a`/`c` across iterations |\n| PAETH (4) | `png_read_filter_row_paeth_multibyte_pixel` | 4065 | bpp > 1; first pixel handled as UP |\n\n`bpp` values reachable: 1 (bit_depth 1/2/4/8 gray or palette), 2 (gray16 or GA8), 3 (RGB8), 4 (RGBA8 or GA16), 6 (RGB16), 8 (RGBA16). **Test matrix: 5 filter types × 6 bpp values = 30 rows**, plus per-bpp: first row (all-zero `prev_row`), narrow interlaced rows where `rowbytes < bpp` (pass 0 of a 1-pixel-wide 16-bit RGBA image → `rowbytes = 8`, bpp = 8 → `istop = 0`), and the `PNG_USE_ABS` variant (not defined here → the ternary branches at 4042-4044 / 4100-4102 are live).\n\n---\n\n## 7. Decompression, CRC, chunk header\n\n### `png_inflate_claim` — `pngrutil.c:413-515`\n- `zowner != 0` → builds a `\"<chunk> using zstream\"` message; **`PNG_RELEASE_BUILD == 0` → `png_chunk_error` (430), so this is FATAL in this build**. Reachable e.g. by a zTXt inside the IDAT stream region.\n- `PNG_MAXIMUM_INFLATE_WINDOW` (option 2) **ON** → `window_bits = 15`, `zstream_start = 0` (455-458); **OFF/UNSET** → `window_bits = 0`, `zstream_start = 1` (462). With `window_bits == 0` zlib may skip CINFO validation, so `png_zlib_inflate` (`pngrutil.c:524-539`) adds the manual check: `(*next_in >> 4) > 7` → `Z_DATA_ERROR` with `msg = \"invalid window size (libpng)\"`. **With the option ON, that check is bypassed entirely.**\n- `PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_INITIALIZED` set → `inflateReset2(window_bits)` (479); unset → `inflateInit2(window_bits)` (488) and set the flag on success\n- the `inflateValidate` / `PNG_IGNORE_ADLER32` block (497-501) is **compiled out**\n- `ret == Z_OK` → `zowner = owner`; else `png_zstream_error`\nRows: {MAXIMUM_INFLATE_WINDOW off + valid CINFO}, {off + CINFO 8..15 → libpng rejects}, {on + CINFO 8..15 → accepted}, {first claim vs re-claim}, {claim while owned}.\n\n### `png_decompress_chunk` — `pngrutil.c:680-827`\n- `limit = png_chunk_max(png_ptr)`; `limit < prefix_size + terminate` → `Z_MEM_ERROR` + `png_zstream_error` (821-826)\n- `limit -= prefix_size + terminate`; `limit < *newlength` → `*newlength = limit` (701-702) — **this is where `png_set_chunk_malloc_max` caps the uncompressed size**\n- `png_inflate_claim` failure → returned (815-816)\n- **first pass**: `png_inflate(finish=1, output=NULL)` to measure (711-713); `!= Z_STREAM_END` → error path; `== Z_OK` → `PNG_UNEXPECTED_ZLIB_RETURN` (808-809)\n- `inflateReset` failure → `PNG_UNEXPECTED_ZLIB_RETURN` (800-805)\n- `png_malloc_base(prefix + new_size + terminate)` NULL → `Z_MEM_ERROR` (792-797)\n- **second pass** into the real buffer (741-743); `*newlength != new_size` → `PNG_UNEXPECTED_ZLIB_RETURN` (\"size changed on second read\", 764-773); `Z_OK` → `PNG_UNEXPECTED_ZLIB_RETURN` (776-777)\n- success: terminator written (749-750), prefix copied (752-753), `read_buffer` swapped (756-761)\n- **`chunklength - prefix_size != lzsize` → `png_chunk_benign_error(\"extra compressed data\")`** (787-789)\n- `zowner = 0` (812)\nRows: {clean}, {uncompressed size == chunk_max exactly}, {uncompressed size > chunk_max}, {trailing bytes after the LZ stream}, {truncated LZ}, {zlib dictionary error}, {`chunk_malloc_max` set to 1}, {`prefix_size + 1 > chunk_max`}.\n\n### `png_inflate` — `pngrutil.c:555-671`\n- `zowner != owner` → `msg = \"zstream unclaimed\"`, `Z_STREAM_ERROR` (662-670)\n- `output != NULL` → direct write; `output == NULL` → 1024-byte `local_buffer` reused each round (614-622)\n- input chunked to `ZLIB_IO_MAX` per iteration (601-607)\n- flush choice: `avail_out > 0` → `Z_NO_FLUSH`; else `finish ? Z_FINISH : Z_SYNC_FLUSH` (636-637)\n- loop until `ret != Z_OK`; sizes clawed back (645-655)\n\n### `png_inflate_read` (iCCP only) — `pngrutil.c:835-895`\n- `zowner != chunk_name` → `Z_STREAM_ERROR` (890-894)\n- refills input from the chunk via `png_crc_read` when `avail_in == 0` (850-861), `read_size` clamped to `*chunk_bytes`\n- flush: `*chunk_bytes > 0` → `Z_NO_FLUSH`; else `finish ? Z_FINISH : Z_SYNC_FLUSH` (877-878)\n\n### `png_read_chunk_header` — `pngrutil.c:182-222`\n- sets `io_state = READING|CHUNK_HDR` then `READING|CHUNK_DATA` (188-190, 217-219) — testable via `png_get_io_state`\n- `png_read_data(buf, 8)` — a short read is a hard error from the read function\n- `length = png_get_uint_31(...)` → `> PNG_UINT_31_MAX` → `png_error(\"PNG unsigned integer out of range\")` (`pngrutil.c:45-46`)\n- `chunk_name` set **before** validation so `png_chunk_error` can name it (198)\n- `png_reset_crc` + `png_calculate_crc(name, 4)` (201-202)\n- `buf[0] >= 0x80` → `png_chunk_error(\"bad header (invalid length)\")` (210-211) — note this is redundant with `png_get_uint_31` but produces a different message; unreachable in practice\n- `!check_chunk_name(chunk_name)` → `png_chunk_error(\"bad header (invalid type)\")` (214-215). `check_chunk_name` (`pngrutil.c:152-177`) requires every byte in `[A-Za-z]` ignoring bit 5 except the reserved byte. Rows: lowercase/uppercase mixes (valid), digit in the name, space, high-bit byte, all-zero name.\n\n### `png_crc_read` — `pngrutil.c:225-233`\n`png_ptr == NULL` → return; else `png_read_data` + `png_calculate_crc`. `png_calculate_crc` (`png.c`) itself has a `crc_started` fast path.\n\n### `png_crc_error` — `pngrutil.c:238-299` and `png_crc_finish_critical` / `png_crc_finish` — `pngrutil.c:311-363`\nThe full flag matrix (documented in the comment at 245-270):\n\n**Ancillary** (or `handle_as_ancillary != 0`):\n| ANCILLARY_USE | ANCILLARY_NOWARN | behaviour | set by |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 0 | compute CRC; on error `png_chunk_error` | default / `PNG_CRC_DEFAULT` / `PNG_CRC_WARN_DISCARD` |\n| 1 | 0 | compute CRC; on error `png_chunk_warning`, keep data | `PNG_CRC_WARN_USE` |\n| 0 | 1 | compute CRC; on error `png_chunk_error` | `PNG_CRC_ERROR_QUIT` |\n| 1 | 1 | **no CRC computation at all** (`need_crc = 0`, 275) | `PNG_CRC_QUIET_USE` |\n\n**Critical**:\n| CRITICAL_USE | CRITICAL_IGNORE | behaviour | set by |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 0 | compute; on error `png_chunk_error` | default / `PNG_CRC_ERROR_QUIT` / `PNG_CRC_DEFAULT` / `PNG_CRC_WARN_DISCARD` (+warning) |\n| 1 | 0 | compute; on error `png_chunk_warning` | `PNG_CRC_WARN_USE` |\n| 1 | 1 | **no CRC computation** | `PNG_CRC_QUIET_USE` |\n\n`png_crc_finish_critical` extra rule at 336-338: if `handle_as_ancillary` was requested but `CRITICAL_IGNORE` is set, `handle_as_ancillary` is forced back to 0 (because `png_crc_read` never computed a CRC). The severity selector at 345-347 then picks ancillary-NOWARN-clear → warning, else error.\n\nThe **skip loop** (318-329) reads in `PNG_INFLATE_BUF_SIZE` (1024) chunks through `png_crc_read`, so skipped data still contributes to the CRC.\n\nCallers using `handle_as_ancillary = 1`: `png_handle_PLTE` (1042-1044 with `color_type != PALETTE`, and 1069) and `png_handle_IEND` (1094). Everything else uses `png_crc_finish`.\n\nRows: `png_set_crc_action(crit, ancil)` over the 5×5 grid (NO_CHANGE / DEFAULT / WARN_USE / QUIET_USE / ERROR_QUIT / WARN_DISCARD), × {good CRC, bad CRC on critical chunk, bad CRC on ancillary chunk, bad CRC on PLTE in an RGB image, bad CRC on IEND}.\n\n### `png_read_IDAT_data` — `pngrutil.c:4171-4306`\n- `output == NULL` → `avail_out = 0`, output into `tmpbuf`, \"checking\" mode (4179-4180, 4243-4247)\n- `avail_in == 0` refill: `while (idat_size == 0)` → `png_crc_finish(0)` then `png_read_chunk_header`; **`chunk_name != png_IDAT` → `png_error(\"Not enough image data\")`** (4192-4202). Zero-length IDATs in the middle are therefore transparently skipped.\n- `avail_in` clamped to `IDAT_read_size` (8192), then `png_chunk_max`, then `idat_size` (4204-4210)\n- `png_read_buffer` NULL → `png_chunk_error(\"out of memory\")` (4221-4222)\n- `Z_STREAM_END` (4267): `mode |= PNG_AFTER_IDAT`, `flags |= PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_ENDED`; leftover `avail_in > 0 || idat_size > 0` → benign \"Extra compressed data\" (4275-4276); `break`\n- `ret != Z_OK` (4280): `output != NULL` → `png_chunk_error(zstream.msg)`; `output == NULL` → benign error + `return`\n- loop exits with `avail_out > 0` (4295): `output != NULL` → `png_error(\"Not enough image data\")`; else → benign \"Too much image data\"\nRows: {single IDAT}, {many small IDATs}, {zero-length IDAT interleaved}, {IDAT larger than 8192}, {`IDAT_read_size` vs `chunk_malloc_max` smaller}, {truncated deflate}, {corrupt deflate}, {extra bytes after Z_STREAM_END}, {non-IDAT chunk mid-stream}, {`chunk_malloc_max` = 1}.\n\n`png_push_*` — correctly out of scope (`pngpread.c`).\n\n---\n\n## 8. User limits\n\n| API | line | field | enforced at |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `png_set_user_limits(w,h)` | `pngset.c:1869-1884` | `user_width_max`, `user_height_max` | `png_set_IHDR` → `png.c:2012` (\"Image width exceeds user limit in IHDR\"), `png.c:2034` (height). Both are `png_warning` + `error=1` → one `png_error(\"Invalid IHDR data\")`. Also `png.c:~2007` \"Image width is too large for this architecture\". |\n| `png_set_chunk_cache_max(n)` | `pngset.c:1887-1893` | `user_chunk_cache_max` | **decremented in 5 places**: `png_handle_sPLT` (`pngrutil.c:1567-1581`), `png_handle_tEXt` (2386-2400), `png_handle_zTXt` (2456-2470), `png_handle_iTXt` (2572-2586), and `png_handle_unknown`'s store path (2908-2933). **Semantics: 0 = unlimited; 1 = \"already exhausted, silently discard\"; 2 = \"one more then warn\"; the counter is decremented and the warning fires when it *reaches* 1.** So `n` allows roughly `n-1` cached chunks. `png_handle_unknown`'s version uses a `switch` with fallthrough (case 2 → set to 1 + benign error → case 1 → break; default → decrement → case 0 → store). |\n| `png_set_chunk_malloc_max(n)` | `pngset.c:1897-1921` | `user_chunk_malloc_max`; **`n == 0` is remapped to `PNG_SIZE_MAX`** (1909-1915) | via `png_chunk_max()` (`pngpriv.h:1126`) in: `png_read_buffer` (`pngrutil.c:380`, returns NULL → each caller's \"out of memory\" benign error), `png_decompress_chunk` (693, 699-702), `png_cache_unknown_chunk` (2714, 2722), `png_handle_chunk`'s `Limit` case (3174), `png_read_IDAT_data` (4206-4207), `png_icc_check_length` (`png.c:1602`). |\n| `png_get_user_width_max` / `_height_max` | `pngget.c:1315`, `1321` | | return 0 if `png_ptr == NULL` |\n| `png_get_user_chunk_cache_max` | `pngget.c:~1328` | | |\n| `png_get_user_chunk_malloc_max` | `pngget.c:~1335` | | **returns the remapped value, not the 0 you set** |\n\nRows: `{width_max, height_max}` = {0, 1, exact image dim, dim-1, 0x7fffffff}; `chunk_cache_max` = {0, 1, 2, 3, 1000}; `chunk_malloc_max` = {0, 1, 11, 132, 8000000, PNG_SIZE_MAX} × {eXIf, zTXt, iTXt, iCCP, sCAL, sPLT, unknown chunk, IDAT}.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Unknown-chunk handling\n\n### `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks(keep, chunk_list, num_chunks_in)` — `pngset.c:1600-1712`\nBranches:\n- `png_ptr == NULL` → return\n- `keep < 0 || keep >= PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_LAST (4)` → `png_app_error(\"invalid keep\")` (1609-1614) — **fatal in this build unless `png_set_benign_errors(1)`**\n- `num_chunks_in <= 0` → `unknown_default = keep` (1618); `num_chunks_in == 0` → **return here** (list untouched)\n- `num_chunks_in < 0` → uses the built-in 21-entry `chunks_to_ignore` table (1624-1652), covering bKGD cHRM cICP cLLI eXIf gAMA hIST iCCP iTXt mDCV oFFs pCAL pHYs sBIT sCAL sPLT sTER sRGB tEXt tIME zTXt. **Note `sTER` is in the list but has no handler; note tRNS/PLTE/IHDR/IDAT/IEND are deliberately absent.**\n- `num_chunks_in > 0 && chunk_list == NULL` → `png_app_error(\"no chunk list\")` + return (1663-1668)\n- `num_chunks + old_num_chunks > UINT_MAX/5` → `png_app_error(\"too many chunks\")` (1679-1683)\n- `keep != 0` → allocate a new 5-byte-per-entry list and copy the old; `keep == 0` with an existing list → reuse in place; `keep == 0` with no list → `new_list = NULL` and the add loop is skipped (1690-1698)\n- `add_one_chunk` (`pngset.c:1572-1597`): updates in place if present; appends only when `keep != PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_AS_DEFAULT` — so setting AS_DEFAULT *removes the effect* without shrinking the list\n\n**Test matrix (each a row):** keep ∈ {AS_DEFAULT 0, NEVER 1, IF_SAFE 2, ALWAYS 3, 4 (invalid), -1 (invalid)} × num_chunks_in ∈ {-1, 0, 1, 2} × chunk_list ∈ {NULL, valid, duplicate entries}. Plus: global default only (`num_chunks_in == 0`) vs per-chunk only vs both with conflicting values.\n\n### `png_handle_as_unknown` — `png.c:930-971`\n- `png_ptr == NULL || chunk_name == NULL || num_chunk_list == 0` → `PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_AS_DEFAULT` (936-937)\n- reverse linear scan of 5-byte records (949-960); match → `p[4]`; no match → `AS_DEFAULT` (967)\n`png_chunk_unknown_handling` (`png.c:964-972`) is the internal `png_uint_32`-keyed wrapper.\n\n### `png_set_read_user_chunk_fn` — `pngset.c:1761-1774`\nStores `read_user_chunk_fn` and `user_chunk_ptr`. Retrieve with `png_get_user_chunk_ptr` (`pngget.c:1282`, returns NULL if `png_ptr == NULL`).\n\n### `png_handle_unknown` decision tree — `pngrutil.c:2760-2960`\nOrder of operations (each numbered item is a distinct row):\n1. `keep` arrives from `png_chunk_unknown_handling` (or `AS_DEFAULT` from `png_handle_chunk:3127`).\n2. **`read_user_chunk_fn != NULL` takes precedence** (2794):\n   - `png_cache_unknown_chunk` returns 0 (length > `chunk_max`, or `png_malloc_warn` failed) → `keep = PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_NEVER` (2852) and **the callback is never invoked**\n   - callback `ret < 0` → `png_chunk_error(\"error in user chunk\")` (2811-2812)\n   - callback `ret == 0` → if `keep < IF_SAFE` then: if `unknown_default < IF_SAFE` → `png_chunk_warning(\"Saving unknown chunk:\")` **plus** `png_app_warning(\"forcing save of an unhandled chunk; please call png_set_keep_unknown_chunks\")` (2832-2836) — **and `png_app_warning` is FATAL in this non-release build**; then `keep = IF_SAFE` (2839)\n   - callback `ret > 0` → `handled = handled_ok`, `keep = PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_NEVER` (2845-2847)\n3. else (`PNG_SAVE_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS_SUPPORTED` block, 2859-2879):\n   - `keep == AS_DEFAULT` → `keep = png_ptr->unknown_default` (2866-2867)\n   - `keep == ALWAYS` **or** (`keep == IF_SAFE && PNG_CHUNK_ANCILLARY(name)`) → `png_cache_unknown_chunk`; failure → `keep = NEVER` (2869-2875)\n   - otherwise → `png_crc_finish(length)` and the chunk is dropped (2878)\n4. store step (`PNG_STORE_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS_SUPPORTED`, 2899-2938): same `ALWAYS || (IF_SAFE && ancillary)` test, then the chunk-cache `switch` (§8), then `png_set_unknown_chunks` + `handled = handled_saved`\n5. `unknown_chunk.data` freed (2944-2946)\n6. **`handled < handled_saved && PNG_CHUNK_CRITICAL(name)` → `png_chunk_error(\"unhandled critical chunk\")`** (2956-2957)\n\n**The full keep × chunk-class grid** (`PNG_CHUNK_ANCILLARY(c) == bit 29`, `PNG_CHUNK_SAFE_TO_COPY(c) == bit 5`):\n\n| keep | critical (e.g. `abCD` uppercase 1st) | ancillary, unsafe-to-copy (`aBCD`) | ancillary, safe-to-copy (`aBCd`) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| AS_DEFAULT | resolves to `unknown_default` | same | same |\n| NEVER | `crc_finish` then **`png_chunk_error(\"unhandled critical chunk\")`** | skipped, `handled_discarded` | skipped, `handled_discarded` |\n| IF_SAFE | not cached → **`png_chunk_error`** | **cached and saved** | **cached and saved** |\n| ALWAYS | cached and saved → `handled_saved`, no error | cached and saved | cached and saved |\n\nImportant: **`PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_IF_SAFE` in libpng 1.6 tests `PNG_CHUNK_ANCILLARY`, not `PNG_CHUNK_SAFE_TO_COPY`** (2870-2871 and 2904-2905). The safe-to-copy bit is *not* consulted in the read path at all — a common misconception worth an explicit test row. (`png_set_unknown_chunks` / `png_set_unknown_chunk_location` in `pngset.c:~1700-1760` handle the write-side location semantics.)\n\n`png_cache_unknown_chunk` — `pngrutil.c:2711-2756`: frees any previous `data` (2716-2720); `length > png_chunk_max` → skips allocation; `length == 0` → `data = NULL` **and returns 1** (2730-2731, 2749-2754); `png_malloc_warn` failure with `length > 0` → `png_crc_finish` + benign \"unknown chunk exceeds memory limits\" + return 0 (2741-2747). `unknown_chunk.location = (png_byte)png_ptr->mode` (2728) — so location encodes HAVE_IHDR/HAVE_PLTE/HAVE_IDAT/AFTER_IDAT.\n\nRows: user-chunk-fn returning -1/0/+1 × keep ∈ {AS_DEFAULT, NEVER, IF_SAFE, ALWAYS} × `unknown_default` ∈ {AS_DEFAULT, NEVER, IF_SAFE, ALWAYS} × chunk class {critical, ancillary-unsafe, ancillary-safe} × length ∈ {0, small, > chunk_max}; plus no-callback rows for the same grid; plus `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks` on a *known supported* chunk (e.g. `gAMA`) to divert it from `png_handle_gAMA` to `png_handle_unknown` (this is the `pngread.c:143` path); plus IDAT and PLTE diverted.\n\n---\n\n## 10. `png_permit_mng_features`\n\n`pngset.c:1556-1567`: `png_ptr == NULL` → return 0; else `mng_features_permitted = mng_features & PNG_ALL_MNG_FEATURES (0x05)` and return it. So bits other than `PNG_FLAG_MNG_EMPTY_PLTE (0x01)` and `PNG_FLAG_MNG_FILTER_64 (0x04)` are silently dropped — a row: pass `0xFF`, expect `0x05` back.\n\nRead-path branch points:\n1. **`png.c:2089-2091`** — `(mode & PNG_HAVE_PNG_SIGNATURE) != 0 && mng_features_permitted != 0` → `png_warning(\"MNG features are not allowed in a PNG datastream\")`. **Whether `PNG_HAVE_PNG_SIGNATURE` is set depends on `png_set_sig_bytes` (< 3 sets it, ≥ 3 does not)** — see §1. This is the cross-axis coupling.\n2. **`png.c:2093-2110`** — `filter_type != PNG_FILTER_TYPE_BASE`: accepted only if all of `FILTER_64 permitted`, `filter_type == PNG_INTRAPIXEL_DIFFERENCING (64)`, `!(mode & HAVE_PNG_SIGNATURE)`, and `color_type ∈ {RGB, RGB_ALPHA}`. Otherwise `png_warning(\"Unknown filter method in IHDR\")` + error. A second check adds `png_warning(\"Invalid filter method in IHDR\")` if the signature *was* seen.\n3. **`pngset.c:778-785`** (`png_set_PLTE`) — `num_palette == 0 && !(mng_features_permitted & PNG_FLAG_MNG_EMPTY_PLTE)` → `png_error(\"Invalid palette\")`. With EMPTY_PLTE permitted, a zero-entry PLTE is accepted. Note `png_handle_PLTE` computes `num = length/3 = 0` for a zero-length PLTE and reaches `png_set_PLTE` with `num == 0`.\n4. **`pngread.c:466-473`** — the `png_do_read_intrapixel` call in `png_read_row`, gated on `FILTER_64 permitted && filter_type == 64`. Note `png_ptr->filter_type` is only stored when `PNG_MNG_FEATURES_SUPPORTED` (`pngrutil.c:931-933`).\n5. There is **no** `PNG_FLAG_MNG_EMPTY_PLTE` check anywhere in `pngrutil.c` — the empty-PLTE acceptance is entirely inside `png_set_PLTE`.\n\nRows: `mng_features` ∈ {0, 0x01, 0x04, 0x05, 0xFF} × `png_set_sig_bytes` ∈ {0, 4, 8} × `filter_type` ∈ {0, 64} × `color_type` ∈ {RGB, RGBA, GRAY, PALETTE} × `bit_depth` ∈ {8, 16} × PLTE length ∈ {0, 3}.\n\n---\n\n## 11. `png_set_benign_errors`\n\n`pngset.c:1925-1941`. `allowed != 0` → sets `PNG_FLAG_BENIGN_ERRORS_WARN | PNG_FLAG_APP_WARNINGS_WARN | PNG_FLAG_APP_ERRORS_WARN`; `allowed == 0` → clears all three. **Note: no NULL check on `png_ptr`.**\n\nCrucial default state for read structs in this build:\n- `PNG_FLAG_BENIGN_ERRORS_WARN` is **set** by `png_create_read_struct_2:62`\n- `PNG_FLAG_APP_WARNINGS_WARN` is **not** set (because `PNG_RELEASE_BUILD == 0`, line 67-69)\n- `PNG_FLAG_APP_ERRORS_WARN` is **not** set\n\nSo the three distinct states worth testing are:\n| state | benign errors | app warnings | app errors |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| default (no call) | warning | **fatal** | **fatal** |\n| `png_set_benign_errors(1)` | warning | warning | warning |\n| `png_set_benign_errors(0)` | **fatal** | **fatal** | **fatal** |\n\nConsumers (`pngerror.c`): `png_benign_error` (routes to `png_chunk_warning`/`png_chunk_error` when `mode & PNG_IS_READ_STRUCT && chunk_name != 0`, else `png_warning`/`png_error`), `png_chunk_benign_error`, `png_app_warning`, `png_app_error`.\n\n**Handlers/functions whose behaviour changes** (full list, from §2's summary plus):\n- `png_handle_PLTE` (non-palette colour types only — palette PLTE errors are always fatal, `pngrutil.c:1064`)\n- `png_handle_IEND` (length != 0)\n- `png_handle_gAMA`, `png_handle_sBIT` (×2 sites), `png_handle_cHRM`, `png_handle_sRGB`\n- `png_handle_iCCP` — **the only place where the flag changes control flow**, `pngrutil.c:1443-1445` vs `1450-1457`\n- `png_handle_tRNS` (×4), `png_handle_bKGD` (×4), `png_handle_eXIf` (×2), `png_handle_hIST`\n- `png_handle_pCAL` (×4, including the non-fatal \"unrecognized equation type\"), `png_handle_sCAL` (×5)\n- `png_handle_tEXt` (×2), `png_handle_zTXt` (×2 + the shared 2553), `png_handle_iTXt` (×2 + 2702)\n- `png_handle_chunk`'s generic ancillary path (`pngrutil.c:3206`)\n- `png_handle_unknown` (`pngrutil.c:2745`, `2912`) **and its `png_app_warning` at 2833** — this is the one that surprises people: with default flags, a user-chunk callback returning 0 without a prior `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks` is a **fatal** error.\n- `png_read_info` line 125; `png_read_end` lines 697, 729, 747\n- `png_read_IDAT_data` lines 4276, 4289, 4304\n- `png_decompress_chunk` line 789\n- `png_read_update_info` / `png_start_read_image` duplicate-call `png_app_error` (`pngread.c:191`, `214`)\n- `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks`'s three `png_app_error`s (`pngset.c:1611`, `1665`, `1681`)\n- `png_handle_unknown`'s `\"no unknown chunk support available\"` (2893) — dead here since SAVE_UNKNOWN is on\n- `png_set_pCAL` / `png_set_text_2` / `png_set_unknown_chunks` internal `png_chunk_report` calls in `pngset.c`\n- `png_icc_profile_error` (`png.c:~1570`) ends in `png_chunk_benign_error` → **all ICC validation failures are benign-gated**, including the \"warning only\" ones\n\nAlso `png_ptr->flags & PNG_FLAG_CRC_*` is independent — the `png_chunk_warning`/`png_chunk_error` choice in `png_crc_finish_critical` (`pngrutil.c:345-351`) is **not** affected by the benign flag.\n\n---\n\n## 12. `png_set_option` — every option in this build\n\n`png.c:3768-3784`. Acceptance test: `png_ptr != NULL && option >= 0 && option < PNG_OPTION_NEXT (16) && (option & 1) == 0`. Returns the **previous** 2-bit state (`PNG_OPTION_UNSET 0` / `PNG_OPTION_OFF 2` / `PNG_OPTION_ON 3`) or `PNG_OPTION_INVALID (1)`.\n\n| macro | value | `#define`d here? | read anywhere? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `PNG_ARM_NEON` | 0 | **no** (`PNG_ARM_NEON_API_SUPPORTED` unset) | no |\n| `PNG_MAXIMUM_INFLATE_WINDOW` | 2 | **yes** | **YES** — `pngrutil.c:453` |\n| `PNG_SKIP_sRGB_CHECK_PROFILE` | 4 | **yes** | **no** — zero references in `src/` |\n| `PNG_MIPS_MSA` | 6 | no | no |\n| `PNG_IGNORE_ADLER32` | 8 | **no** (`PNG_DISABLE_ADLER32_CHECK_SUPPORTED` unset) | reference exists at `pngrutil.c:498` but is `#ifdef`-ed out |\n| `PNG_POWERPC_VSX` | 10 | no | no |\n| `PNG_MIPS_MMI` | 12 | no | no |\n| `PNG_RISCV_RVV` | 14 | no | no |\n\nSo: **exactly one option is functional** — `PNG_MAXIMUM_INFLATE_WINDOW` (2). `png_set_option` will nonetheless *accept and store* option values 0, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14 (all even and < 16) with no effect, and reject 1, 3, 15, 16, 17, -1, and any call with `png_ptr == NULL`.\n\nAnswering the specific question: **`PNG_DISABLE_ADLER32_CHECK_SUPPORTED` not being in `pnglibconf.h` means `PNG_IGNORE_ADLER32` is not a defined symbol** — code written as `png_set_option(p, PNG_IGNORE_ADLER32, PNG_OPTION_ON)` will **fail to compile**. Code written as `png_set_option(p, 8, 3)` compiles, returns `PNG_OPTION_UNSET` (0) the first time, and does absolutely nothing: the Adler32 check remains **enabled** inside zlib.\n\nRows: `png_set_option(2, ON)` before `png_read_info` / before `png_start_read_image` / after `png_read_start_row` (too late — `png_inflate_claim` for IDAT already happened); `png_set_option(2, OFF)`; option 0/4/8 (accepted no-op, verify return value); option 1/15/16/-1 (`PNG_OPTION_INVALID`); NULL png_ptr; repeated calls (verify the return is the previous state).\n\n---\n\n## 13. Other distinct configuration axes in these files\n\n1. **`PNG_IO_STATE_SUPPORTED` is on** — `io_state` is written at `pngrutil.c:128` (SIGNATURE), `189` (CHUNK_HDR), `218` (CHUNK_DATA), `285` (CHUNK_CRC). A `png_get_io_state`-checking read callback is a distinct test configuration and observes a strict 4-state sequence per chunk.\n2. **`PNG_CHECK_FOR_INVALID_INDEX_SUPPORTED` / `png_set_check_for_invalid_index`** (`pngset.c:~1950`) — sets `num_palette_max` to 0 (track) or -1 (don't). Consequences: the `transformations` gate at `pngread.c:476-480`, and the `png_read_end` benign error at `pngread.c:693-698` (`num_palette_max >= num_palette`).\n3. **`png_ptr->IDAT_read_size`** — initialised to `PNG_IDAT_READ_SIZE` (8192) at `pngread.c:58` and used at `pngrutil.c:4204`. There is no public setter in this build, but it interacts with `chunk_malloc_max` at 4206-4207 (whichever is smaller wins).\n4. **`read_buffer` lifecycle** — allocated by `png_read_buffer`, *stolen* by `png_handle_iCCP` (`pngrutil.c:1478`), *replaced* by `png_decompress_chunk` (756-761), *freed* by `png_read_start_row` (4665-4672), and reused as the IDAT input buffer (4219). A PNG with `iCCP → zTXt → IDAT → iTXt` exercises all four transitions; ordering bugs live here.\n5. **`read_filter[]` persistence across images** — `png_read_start_row` does not reset it, so reusing one `png_struct` for two images with different `bpp` keeps the first image's Paeth variant (§6).\n6. **`old_big_row_buf_size` buffer reuse** (`pngrutil.c:4603`) — reusing a struct for a smaller second image skips reallocation; the `interlaced → calloc` vs `non-interlaced → malloc` distinction (4609-4614) then does not re-apply.\n7. **`png_handle_chunk` vs direct handler invocation** — the sequential reader always goes through `png_handle_chunk`, so the table's length/position/duplicate rules always apply. The progressive reader (`pngpread.c`, out of scope) may differ. This matters for `hIST` (§2) which the table makes unreachable for palette PNGs.\n8. **`png_ptr->chunks` bitmask** (`pngstruct.h:114-120, 190`) — only 28 known chunks fit in 32 bits; the `png_file_add_chunk` at `pngrutil.c:3213` fires **only** when `handled >= handled_saved`, so a handler that returns `handled_error` leaves the \"seen\" bit clear and a *second* copy of that chunk is not rejected as a duplicate. Test: two malformed gAMA chunks (both accepted into the loop) vs one good + one malformed.\n9. **`PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_AFTER_IDAT` vs `PNG_AFTER_IDAT`** — set together in `png_read_info:132-133` and `png_read_end:710`, but `PNG_AFTER_IDAT` is also set by `png_handle_tIME` (2349-2350), `png_handle_IEND` (1089), `png_read_IDAT_data` (4272), and `png_read_finish_IDAT` (4330). A tIME before IDAT therefore sets `AFTER_IDAT` spuriously if `HAVE_IDAT` is set — cross-check with the `CDIEND pos_after = aIDAT` table rule.\n10. **`PNG_POINTER_INDEXING_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_USE_COMPILE_TIME_MASKS`** — select the `png_combine_row` mask tables (3376-3413) vs runtime masks (3415-3421). Verify which is active in your build (`pngpriv.h`).\n11. **`PNG_NO_MEMZERO`** (`pngrutil.c:396-398`) — if defined, `png_read_buffer` skips the `memset`, exposing uninitialised-memory bugs in handlers that read past the data they wrote (sPLT name, pCAL params, tRNS `readbuf`).\n12. **`png_reset_zstream`** (`png.c:~975`) — a public API that calls `inflateReset` and, per its own comment, \"resets the window bits to the maximum\". Calling it mid-read desynchronises `zowner`/`zstream_start` and is a legitimate hostile-configuration row.\n13. **setjmp configuration** — `PNG_SETJMP_SUPPORTED` is on; `png_set_longjmp_fn` / `png_jmpbuf` / `png_set_error_fn` with a non-longjmp handler are distinct error-recovery configurations that change what \"fatal\" means for every row above."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":595,"cache_read_input_tokens":165099,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":595,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_016VJrbbk6DYMFLdQ2eJNiJ7","session_id":"e3091878-9949-4689-ad83-c0c41e6641a2","uuid":"51081206-57dc-42cd-bc21-12d32cf2457e","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:27:20.977Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Map read pipeline branches"}
