{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_r5sce3upafhir23zamckhbscdy3nkyhdqdrvzg2fwmgo3eknrtqq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01UszytRUjreecfEd4AebzFf","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write progressive+simplified tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-kk7Dev\n\nContext: `c_src/` is libpng 1.6.59 (C, ground truth, NEVER modify). `translation/` is a Rust re-implementation exported as `translation/target/release/liblibpng.so`. Both are already built. A differential-test harness exists — READ `translation/tests/HARNESS.md` FIRST, then skim `translation/tests/common/mod.rs`, `translation/tests/common/types.rs` and `translation/tests/t03_write.rs` (write-pipeline driver pattern).\n\nYOUR TASK: create TWO new files.\n\n## 1. `translation/tests/t06_progressive.rs` — the PROGRESSIVE read API\nCover `png_set_progressive_read_fn`, `png_process_data`, `png_process_data_pause`, `png_process_data_skip`, `png_progressive_combine_row`, `png_get_progressive_ptr`, and the exported push helpers (`png_push_read_sig`, `png_push_read_chunk`, `png_push_read_IDAT`, `png_push_fill_buffer`, `png_push_save_buffer`, `png_push_restore_buffer`, `png_push_process_row`, `png_push_have_info`, `png_push_have_end`, `png_push_have_row`, `png_process_some_data`, `png_read_push_finish_row`) at least indirectly through the full progressive flow.\n\nMethod: first produce a valid PNG byte stream with the (already verified) sequential WRITE path — for every `legal_ihdr()` (colour type, bit depth) pair, both interlace types, several widths/heights (1x1, 1x9, 9x1, 13x7, 32x17), and a couple of ancillary chunks present (gAMA, tEXt, tRNS, bKGD) so the chunk handlers run. Then feed those bytes to BOTH libraries progressively and assert byte-identical results:\n- info callback: record every `png_get_*` value visible at that point\n- row callback: record (row bytes, row_num, pass) for every call\n- end callback: record it happened\nFeed the data in several chunk granularities: 1 byte at a time, 3 bytes, 7 bytes, 64 bytes, and the whole buffer at once — the results must be identical between C and Rust for each granularity.\nAlso test `png_process_data_pause` (both `save != 0` and `save == 0`), `png_process_data_skip`, and calling `png_progressive_combine_row` from the row callback with a display row buffer.\n\n## 2. `translation/tests/t07_simplified.rs` — the SIMPLIFIED API\nCover, differentially:\n- `png_image_begin_read_from_memory`, `png_image_begin_read_from_stdio`, `png_image_begin_read_from_file` (write a temp file under `std::env::temp_dir()`), `png_image_finish_read`, `png_image_free`\n- every `PNG_FORMAT_*` value: GRAY, GA, AG, RGB, BGR, RGBA, ARGB, BGRA, ABGR, LINEAR_Y, LINEAR_Y_ALPHA, LINEAR_RGB, LINEAR_RGB_ALPHA, and every `*_COLORMAP` variant\n- colormapped output (supply a colormap buffer, check `colormap_entries` and the colormap bytes) vs direct output\n- `png_image_finish_read` with a non-NULL `background` (`png_color`) and with NULL\n- positive AND negative `row_stride` (negative means bottom-up), plus a stride larger than the minimum\n- `png_image_write_to_memory` (both the size-query call with `memory == NULL` and the real call), `png_image_write_to_file`, `png_image_write_to_stdio`, with `convert_to_8bit` both 0 and 1, and every input format\n- the `PNG_IMAGE_*` size/row-stride macros' inputs implicitly, by checking the produced buffers match byte for byte\n- after each call assert `image.warning_or_error` and the `image.message` text are identical between C and Rust.\n\nSource images: generate with a deterministic `Rng` (fixed seed) over all `legal_ihdr()` combinations and several sizes; produce the PNG bytes with the sequential write path first.\n\nRequirements for BOTH files:\n- Use `guard(...)` around every call that can `png_error`.\n- Compare the captured `Diag` (warnings + errors) as well as the values/bytes.\n- Self-contained (`mod common; use common::*;`). Do NOT modify `tests/common/*`, any other existing test file, or anything in `c_src/`.\n- They MUST compile and pass. Iterate with\n  `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-kk7Dev/translation && timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test t06_progressive`\n  (and `--test t07_simplified`) until green.\n- If a test reveals a REAL divergence between C and Rust, the Rust translation is wrong, but do NOT fix it yourself: leave the assertion, mark that test `#[ignore]` with a `// DIVERGENCE:` comment giving function, inputs, C value and Rust value, and report it prominently.\n- If a case is C undefined behaviour (pointer dereferenced before a null check, read past a buffer), do NOT test it; note it in a comment.\n\nReport back: the test functions written per file, final pass/fail status of each, and any `// DIVERGENCE:` findings in full detail."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2649,"cache_read_input_tokens":205793,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2649,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e3091878-9949-4689-ad83-c0c41e6641a2","uuid":"2bb0664e-4806-44cd-b593-798ee5b218f3","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:27:37.449Z"}
