| 360-371 | `PNG_INFO_gAMA` | no validation; rows: 0, 45455, 100000, negative, `INT32_MAX` |\n| `png_set_invalid` | 1858-1863 | clears | see below |\n\n**Non-trivial:**\n\n1. **`png_set_cHRM_XYZ_fixed`** — `pngset.c:61-95`. Calls `png_xy_from_XYZ` (87); on failure → **`png_app_error(\"invalid cHRM XYZ\")`** (94), which is **fatal by default in this build**. Rows: valid sRGB XYZ → `PNG_INFO_cHRM` set; all-zero XYZ → conversion fails → app_error; `png_ptr`/`info_ptr` NULL → no-op; with `png_set_benign_errors(p,1)` → warning instead of fatal. 5 rows\n2. **`png_set_cHRM`** / **`png_set_cHRM_XYZ`** (float) — 98-129. Each argument goes through `png_fixed`, so **any out-of-range double raises `png_error`**. Rows: 8 (resp. 9) rows each poking one argument out of range; plus one all-valid row. Note the \"cHRM White X\" etc. text strings appear in the error message\n3. **`png_set_cICP`** — 135-157. Stores all four fields, **then** checks `matrix_coefficients != 0` → `png_warning(\"Invalid cICP matrix coefficients\")` and **returns without setting the valid bit** (150-154). So the fields are written but `png_get_cICP` returns 0. Rows: `matrix_coefficients == 0` → valid set; `== 1` → warning, fields written, **valid NOT set**; `== 255` → same. The write-then-reject asymmetry is the interesting row\n4. **`png_set_cLLI_fixed`** — 161-190. `maxCLL > 0x7FFFFFFF || maxFALL > 0x7FFFFFFF` → `png_chunk_report(..., PNG_CHUNK_WRITE_ERROR)` (182) → on a write struct this is `png_app_error` → **fatal by default**. Rows: both 0 → valid; both `0x7"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3414,"cache_read_input_tokens":206112,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3414,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01AHp7EWTH7PuSA4AaDJf2sf","session_id":"e3091878-9949-4689-ad83-c0c41e6641a2","uuid":"d31b1d6f-b8d5-4713-b29