 0 at 583-584 so the remaining slots are NULL — `png_free_data` handles that. Row\n    - the params array is `nparams + 1` entries (575) — NULL-terminated. Row asserting `params[nparams] == NULL`\n    - `X0`/`X1`: rows at `0`, `INT32_MIN`, `INT32_MAX`, and `X0 == X1` (degenerate but accepted — no validation)\n    - success → `PNG_INFO_pCAL` set (603), `free_me |= PNG_FREE_PCAL`\n    - **note: this setter does NOT call `png_free_data` first**, so calling it twice **leaks** the first allocation. Row documenting that (contrast with `png_set_iCCP` at 931 and `png_set_eXIf_1` at 350 which do)\n\n15. **`png_set_sCAL_s`** — 608-671. All three validation failures are **`png_error` (unconditionally fatal, not chunk_report)**:\n    - `png_ptr`/`info_ptr` NULL → no-op (616-617)\n    - **`unit != 1 && unit != 2`** → `png_error(\"Invalid sCAL unit\")` (622-623). Rows: `unit = 0` (`PNG_SCALE_UNKNOWN`) → **fatal**; `unit = 1` (`PNG_SCALE_METER`) → OK; `unit = 2` (`PNG_SCALE_RADIAN`) → OK; `unit = 3` → fatal. Note `PNG_SCALE_UNKNOWN` is rejected even though it is a named constant\n    - `swidth == NULL` → `png_error(\"Invalid sCAL width\")` (625-627)\n    - `strlen(swidth) == 0` → same error\n    - **`swidth[0] == '-'`** → same error (negatives forbidden). Row: `\"-1.5\"` → fatal\n    - `!png_check_fp_string(swidth, lengthw)` → same error. Rows: `\"abc\"`, `\"1.5x\"`, `\"1e\"`, `\".\"`, `\"+\"` → all fatal\n    - `\"+1.5\"` → leading `+` passes `png_check_fp_string` and is not `'-'` → **accepted**. Asymmetry row\n    - the same 5 failure classes for `sheight` → `png_error(\"Invalid sCAL height\")` (629-631)\n    - `png_malloc_warn` for `scal_s_width` fails → `png_warning(\"Memory allocation failed while processing sCAL\")`, return, nothing set\n    - `png_malloc_warn` for `scal_s_height` fails → **frees `scal_s_width` and NULLs it** (660-661) then warns. Clean-rollback row\n    - success → `free_me |= PNG_FREE_SCAL`, `valid |= PNG_INFO_sCAL`\n    - **does not `png_free_data` first** → calling twice leaks. Row\n    - valid value rows: `\"1\"`, `\"0\"` (zero is accepted here — the float/fixed wrappers reject it but the `_s` form does not!), `\"1.5\"`, `\".5\"`, `\"1e10\"`, `\"1e-10\"`, a 79-char numeric string\n\n16. **`png_set_sCAL`** (float) — 674-700. Rows:\n    - **`width <= 0`** → `png_warning(\"Invalid sCAL width ignored\")` and return (681-682). Rows: `0.0`, `-1.0`\n    - **`height <= 0`** → `png_warning(\"Invalid sCAL height ignored\")` (684-685)\n    - success → two `png_ascii_from_fp(…, PNG_sCAL_PRECISION = 5)` calls into `char[PNG_sCAL_MAX_DIGITS+1]` buffers, then `png_set_sCAL_s`. Rows: `1.0` → `\"1\"`; `1.5` → `\"1.5\"`; `0.00001` → whichever of `\"1E-5\"`/`\".00001\"` the exponent regime picks; `1e300` → `\"1E300\"`; `1e-300`. Each exercises a different `png_ascii_from_fp` arm from §4\n    - **buffer-too-small → `png_error(\"ASCII conversion buffer too small\")`**: needs `PNG_sCAL_MAX_DIGITS+1 < 5+5`. Check the value of `PNG_sCAL_MAX_DIGITS`; if it is ≥ 10 this is unreachable. Note either way\n    - `unit` invalid propagates to `png_set_sCAL_s`'s `png_error`. Row: `png_set_sCAL(p, i, 0, 1.0, 1.0)` → fatal\n    - note: no way to produce a negative string here, so the `swidth[0] == '-'` check in `_s` is unreachable via this path\n\n17. **`png_set_sCAL_fixed`** — 704-728. Same two `<= 0` warning guards; uses `png_ascii_from_fixed` instead. Rows: `width = 0` → warning; `width = -1` → warning; `100000` → `\"1\"`; `1` → `\".00001\"`; `INT32_MAX` → `\"21474.83647\"`; `150000` → `\"1.5\"`. Each hits a different `png_ascii_from_fixed` arm\n\n18. **`png_set_PLTE`** — 749-831. Rows:\n    - `png_ptr`/`info_ptr` NULL → no-op\n    - **`max_palette_length` selection** (761-762): `color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE` → `1 << bit_depth`; otherwise `PNG_MAX_PALETTE_LENGTH` (256). Rows: `(ct=3,bd=1)` → max 2; `(ct=3,bd=2)` → 4; `(ct=3,bd=4)` → 16; `(ct=3,bd=8)` → 256; `(ct=2,bd=8)` → 256\n    - **`num_palette < 0 || > max` with `ct == PALETTE`** → `png_error(\"Invalid palette length\")` — **fatal** (766-767). Rows: `(ct=3,bd=1,num=3)` → fatal; `(ct=3,bd=1,num=2)` → OK\n    - **same with `ct != PALETTE`** → `png_warning(\"Invalid palette length\")` and **return** (771-773) — non-fatal. Rows: `(ct=2,num=257)` → warning + no-op; `(ct=2,num=-1)` → warning\n    - **`num_palette > 0 && palette == NULL`** → `png_error(\"Invalid palette\")` (777, 784)\n    - **`num_palette == 0` and `PNG_FLAG_MNG_EMPTY_PLTE` NOT permitted** → `png_error(\"Invalid palette\")` (778-782). Row: `num_palette = 0` without MNG → fatal\n    - **`num_palette == 0` WITH `png_permit_mng_features(p, PNG_FLAG_MNG_EMPTY_PLTE)`** → **accepted**, empty PLTE. Row (requires `PNG_MNG_FEATURES_SUPPORTED`, on)\n    - the `safe_palette[256]` snapshot at 790-794 — **getter-to-setter aliasing row**: `png_get_PLTE` then feed the pointer straight back to `png_set_PLTE`. The snapshot happens *before* `png_free_data` at 796, so this is safe. Must-test\n    - **two independent 256-entry `png_calloc` allocations** (815-818): one for `png_ptr->palette`, one for `info_ptr->palette`. Rows: assert they are **different pointers**; assert both are fully zeroed beyond `num_palette` (the comment at 809-811 says the ARM NEON riffle reads all 256 entries); assert `png_ptr->num_palette == info_ptr->num_palette`\n    - `png_free(png_ptr, png_ptr->palette)` at 813 before reallocating → calling `png_set_PLTE` twice must not leak or double-free. Row\n    - `png_calloc` failure → `png_malloc` raises `png_error` → fatal, leaving `png_ptr->palette` freed-and-NULLed but `info_ptr->palette` possibly stale. Partial-state row\n    - success → `free_me |= PNG_FREE_PLTE`, `valid |= PNG_INFO_PLTE`\n    - boundary rows: `num_palette = 1`, `= 256`\n\n19. **`png_set_sRGB_gAMA_and_cHRM`** — 861-884. Rows: NULL guards; success → calls `png_set_sRGB` + `png_set_gAMA_fixed(PNG_GAMMA_sRGB_INVERSE)` (873) + `png_set_cHRM_fixed(31270, 32900, 64000, 33000, 30000, 60000, 15000, 6000)` (877-882). Assert all three of `PNG_INFO_sRGB|PNG_INFO_gAMA|PNG_INFO_cHRM` become valid, and that `png_get_cHRM_XYZ` on the result yields the documented sRGB Y coefficients (0.212639/0.715169/0.072192). Both `PNG_gAMA_SUPPORTED` and `PNG_cHRM_SUPPORTED` are on so neither `#ifdef` is skipped. 3 rows\n\n20. **`png_set_iCCP`** — 889-938. Rows:\n    - `png_ptr`/`info_ptr`/`name`/`profile` NULL → no-op (900-901)\n    - **`compression_type != PNG_COMPRESSION_TYPE_BASE (0)`** → `png_app_error(\"Invalid iCCP compression method\")` (903-904) — **fatal by default in this build**, and note **execution continues** if it's downgraded to a warning. Rows: `compression_type = 1` default (fatal); `= 1` with `png_set_benign_errors(p,1)` → warning then the profile is stored anyway\n    - `png_malloc_warn` for `iccp_name` fails → `png_benign_error(\"Insufficient memory to process iCCP chunk\")` (911) — read struct → warning, write struct → **fatal**. 2 rows\n    - `png_malloc_warn` for `iccp_profile` fails → frees `new_iccp_name` (922) then `png_benign_error(\"Insufficient memory to process iCCP profile\")`. Clean-rollback row\n    - success → `png_free_data(..., PNG_FREE_ICCP, 0)` at 931, then store `iccp_proflen = proflen`. Row: call twice, assert no leak\n    - **`proflen == 0`** → `png_malloc_warn(p, 0)` non-NULL, `memcpy(_, _, 0)` → succeeds with a 0-length profile. Then `png_get_iCCP` does `png_get_uint_32(iccp_profile)` on a 0-byte buffer → **out-of-bounds read**. Hazard row\n    - **`proflen` disagreeing with the embedded length**: store a 132-byte profile whose bytes 0-3 say 999 → `png_get_iCCP` reports `*proflen = 999` while `iccp_proflen == 132`. See getter #29. High-value row\n    - `name` empty string → `length = 1`, stored as `\"\"`. Row\n    - long `name` (>79 chars) → accepted here; only `png_write_iCCP` truncates via `png_check_keyword`. Row\n    - success → `free_me |= PNG_FREE_ICCP`, `valid |= PNG_INFO_iCCP`\n\n21. **`png_set_text`** — 942-951. Thin wrapper: `if (png_set_text_2(...) != 0) png_error(\"Insufficient memory to store text\")`. Rows: success → returns normally; `png_set_text_2` returns 1 → **fatal**. Note `png_ptr == NULL` makes `png_set_text_2` return 0, so `png_error(NULL, ...)` is never reached from that path\n\n22. **`png_set_text_2`** — 953-1151 (`PRIVATE`, the real implementation). Rows:\n    - `png_ptr`/`info_ptr` NULL, `num_text <= 0`, `text_ptr == NULL` → **return 0** (963-964). Note `num_text == 0` is a silent success\n    - **array-growth branch** `num_text > max_text - num_text` (971): first call always takes it; a second call that fits in the slack does **not**. 2 rows\n    - `max_text` rounding: `(old + num + 8) & ~7` (985) → rows at `num_text = 1` → `max_text = 8`; `= 8` → 16; `= 9` → 24?? (`(0+9+8)&~7 = 16`) — assert the exact multiple-of-8 behavior\n    - **`num_text > INT_MAX - max_text`** (979) → `new_text` stays NULL → `png_chunk_report(\"too many text chunks\")` and **return 1** (1000-1003). Rows: `num_text = INT_MAX` with `old_num_text = 1`\n    - `max_text >= INT_MAX-8` → clamped to `INT_MAX` (987-988). Unreachable in practice; note\n    - `png_realloc_array` returns NULL → same `png_chunk_report` + return 1\n    - **deferred old-array free**: `old_text = info_ptr->text` at 1009, freed at 1148 **after** the copy loop. **Getter-to-setter aliasing row**: `png_get_text` then feed the array straight back to `png_set_text`. Must-test\n    - **per-entry `text_ptr[i].key == NULL` → `continue`** (1025-1026), silently skipping that entry without incrementing `num_text`. Rows: all keys NULL → 0 entries added, returns 0; middle key NULL → the rest still added\n    - **`compression < PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_NONE (-1)` or `>= PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_LAST (3)`** → `png_chunk_report(\"text compression mode is out of range\")` and `continue` (1028-1034). Rows: `-2` (`PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt_WR`) → **rejected**; `-3` (`PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_NONE_WR`) → **rejected**; `3` → rejected; `4` → rejected\n    - **each valid `PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_*` is its own row** (constants at `png.h:584-590`):\n      - `PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_NONE (-1)` → `compression <= 0` at 1038 → `lang_len = lang_key_len = 0`; `textp->lang = textp->lang_key = NULL` (1120-1121); `text_length` stored in `text_length`, `itxt_length = 0` (1140-1141). tEXt chunk\n      - `PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt (0)` → also `<= 0` → same lang handling, `itxt_length = 0`. zTXt chunk. **Row asserting -1 and 0 take the same lang path but produce different chunk types on write**\n      - `PNG_ITXT_COMPRESSION_NONE (1)` → `> 0` → the iTXt block at 1045-1060 reads `lang`/`lang_key`; `textp->text_length = 0`, `itxt_length = text_length` (1133-1134)\n      - `PNG_ITXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt (2)` → same iTXt path\n    - **iTXt with `lang == NULL`** → `lang_len = 0` (1052-1053) but `memcpy(textp->lang, text_ptr[i].lang, 0)` at 1110 with a NULL source and 0 length — technically UB, practically fine. Row\n    - **iTXt with `lang_key == NULL`** → `lang_key_len = 0`, same shape (1055-1059)\n    - `PNG_iTXt_SUPPORTED` is on, so the `#else` at 1061-1067 (`png_chunk_report(\"iTXt chunk not supported\")`) is **not compiled**. Second config row if you can rebuild\n    - **`text == NULL` or `text[0] == '\\0'`** (1069) → `text_length = 0` **and the compression is downgraded**: `compression > 0` → `textp->compression = PNG_ITXT_COMPRESSION_NONE (1)` (1074); else → `PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_NONE (-1)` (1078). **Two high-value rows**: pass `compression = PNG_ITXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt (2)` with an empty text → stored compression becomes 1; pass `PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt (0)` with empty text → stored compression becomes -1\n    - `text` non-empty → `textp->compression = text_ptr[i].compression` verbatim (1084)\n    - **single allocation for all four strings**: `key_len + text_length + lang_len + lang_key_len + 4` (1087-1088) via `png_malloc_base` (not `png_malloc`, so no error on failure). The four pointers are carved out of it at 1109-1122. Row asserting `textp->lang`, `textp->lang_key`, `textp->text` all point inside the `textp->key` block, and that a single `png_free(textp->key)` releases everything (which is exactly what `png_free_data` does at `png.c:498, 507`)\n    - allocation failure → `png_chunk_report(\"text chunk: out of memory\")`, **`png_free(png_ptr, old_text)`** (1094) and **return 1** — note the old array *is* freed on this path but `info_ptr->text` already points at the new array. Row\n    - `key` with embedded NUL → `strlen` stops early. Row\n    - `key` empty string `\"\"` → `key_len = 0`, accepted; the write side will reject it via `png_check_keyword`. Row\n    - `info_ptr->num_text++` per successful entry (1144) → row asserting the count after a mix of accepted/skipped entries\n    - return 0 on success, 1 on the two failure paths\n\n23. **`png_set_tIME`** — 1155-1177. Rows:\n    - `png_ptr`/`info_ptr`/`mod_time` NULL → no-op (1161-1163)\n    - **`(png_ptr->mode & PNG_WROTE_tIME) != 0`** → no-op. Reachable after `png_write_end`; distinct row\n    - validation (1165-1168) — **note there is NO year check here**, unlike `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer`: `month == 0` → warning; `month > 12` → warning; `day == 0`; `day > 31`; `hour > 23`; `minute > 59`; `second > 60`. All → `png_warning(\"Ignoring invalid time value\")` and return. 7 rows\n    - **`year = 70000`** → **accepted** (no check), but `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer` will later reject it. Asymmetry row\n    - `second == 60` → accepted (leap second)\n    - success → `valid |= PNG_INFO_tIME`\n    - boundary rows: `{1,1,0,0,0}` month/day/h/m/s minimum; `{12,31,23,59,60}` maximum\n\n24. **`png_set_tRNS`** — 1181-1271. Rows:\n    - `png_ptr`/`info_ptr` NULL → no-op (1187-1189)\n    - **`trans_alpha == NULL && trans_color == NULL`** → both blocks skipped, but `info_ptr->num_trans = (png_uint_16)num_trans` still executes (1264) and if `num_trans != 0` the flags are set (1266-1270). **Row: `png_set_tRNS(p, i, NULL, 5, NULL)` sets `PNG_INFO_tRNS` and `num_trans = 5` with no data.** Genuine hazard\n    - **`trans_alpha != NULL` branch** (1191-1238):\n      - `num_trans > 0 && num_trans <= 256` → snapshot into `safe_trans[256]` (1198-1199) **before** `png_free_data` (1203). **Getter-to-setter aliasing row**\n      - `num_trans <= 0` or `> 256` → the snapshot is skipped but `trans_alpha = safe_trans` is still assigned (1201) — so `trans_alpha` now points at an **uninitialized stack array**. Then the `else` at 1233-1237 frees `png_ptr->trans_alpha` and NULLs it without copying. Rows: `num_trans = 0` with non-NULL `trans_alpha`; `num_trans = -1`; `num_trans = 257`\n      - success path allocates **two independent 256-byte buffers** (`info_ptr->trans_alpha` at 1211-1212, `png_ptr->trans_alpha` at 1228-1229), each `memset` to 0xff then overwritten with `num_trans` bytes (1213-1214, 1230-1231). Rows: assert the two pointers differ; assert bytes `[num_trans..255]` are `0xff`; assert `num_trans = 1` and `= 256` boundaries\n      - `png_malloc` failure → `png_error` → fatal, leaving `info_ptr->trans_alpha` set but `png_ptr->trans_alpha` stale. Partial-state row\n    - **`trans_color != NULL` branch** (1240-1262):\n      - `info_ptr->bit_depth < 16` → `sample_max = (1<<bit_depth)-1`; `ct == GRAY && gray > sample_max` → `png_warning(\"tRNS chunk has out-of-range samples for bit_depth\")`; `ct == RGB && (red|green|blue) > sample_max` → same warning. Rows: `(bd=8, ct=0, gray=256)` → warning; `(bd=8, ct=0, gray=255)` → OK; `(bd=1, ct=0, gray=2)` → warning; `(bd=8, ct=2, red=256)` → warning; `(bd=8, ct=2, green=256)`; `(bd=8, ct=2, blue=256)`; `(bd=16, anything)` → **no check at all**; `(bd=8, ct=3)` → no check (PALETTE isn't in either test); `(bd=8, ct=4)`/`(ct=6)` → no check. 10 rows. Guarded by `#ifdef PNG_WARNINGS_SUPPORTED` (1242) — on\n      - **`num_trans == 0` → forced to 1** (1260-1261). Row: `png_set_tRNS(p, i, NULL, 0, &color)` → `num_trans` becomes 1 and the flags are set\n      - `trans_color` is stored by value (1258), so no aliasing concern\n    - both non-NULL → both blocks run; `num_trans` from the alpha side survives (the `if (num_trans == 0)` at 1260 only fires if it was 0)\n    - final: `num_trans != 0` → `free_me |= PNG_FREE_TRNS`, `valid |= PNG_INFO_tRNS` (1266-1270). **Row: `num_trans == 0` with `trans_alpha == NULL` and `trans_color == NULL` → NOTHING is set, a clean no-op**\n    - interaction with `png_get_valid(PNG_INFO_tRNS)`: setting `num_trans = 0` via a direct poke makes the getter return 0 despite the valid bit (getter #1's special case)\n\n25. **`png_set_sPLT`** — 1275-1380. Rows:\n    - `png_ptr`/`info_ptr` NULL, `nentries <= 0`, `entries == NULL` → no-op (1292-1293)\n    - `png_realloc_array` fails → `png_chunk_report(\"too many sPLT chunks\")` and return (1302-1307)\n    - **deferred old-array free**: `old_spalettes` saved at 1312, freed at 1376. **Getter-to-setter aliasing row** via `png_get_sPLT`\n    - **`entries->name == NULL || entries->entries == NULL`** → `png_app_error(\"png_set_sPLT: invalid sPLT\")` (1327) — **fatal by default in this build** — then `continue`. Note the `continue` skips `++entries` (comment 1366-1368), so **the `do/while(--nentries)` loop re-examines the same entry forever if `nentries > 1`**… actually `--nentries` in the `while` still decrements, so it terminates but processes the *same* entry `nentries` times. Rows: `nentries = 1` with a NULL name (with benign errors on) → the loop exits, `nentries` becomes 0, no `png_chunk_report` at 1378; `nentries = 3` with entry[0].name NULL → the same bad entry is hit 3 times, 3 app_errors. **Genuine control-flow bug worth its own row**\n    - `png_malloc_base` for `np->name` fails → `break` out of the loop (1340-1341), leaving `nentries > 0` → `png_chunk_report(\"sPLT out of memory\")` at 1378-1379\n    - `png_malloc_array` for `np->entries` fails → frees `np->name`, NULLs it, `break` (1352-1357) → same report\n    - success per entry → `info_ptr->valid |= PNG_INFO_sPLT`, `++splt_palettes_num`, `++np`, `++entries` (1369-1372)\n    - `entries->nentries == 0` → `png_malloc_array(p, 0, ...)` → **`png_error(\"internal error: array alloc\")`** (pngmem.c:126). **Fatal, unconditionally.** High-value row\n    - `entries->nentries < 0` → same `png_error`\n    - `depth` field is copied verbatim (1332) with **no validation**. Rows: `depth = 8`, `16`, `0`, `255`\n    - `name` empty string → accepted\n    - appending to an existing set: call twice with 2 entries each → `splt_palettes_num == 4`. Row\n    - `nentries = 1`, `= 2`, `= 100` → 3 rows\n\n26. **`check_location`** (static) — `pngset.c:1384-1419`. Rows:\n    - masks with `(PNG_HAVE_IHDR|PNG_HAVE_PLTE|PNG_AFTER_IDAT)` (1387)\n    - **`location == 0` on a WRITE struct** → `png_app_warning(\"png_set_unknown_chunks now expects a valid location\")` (1396-1397) — **fatal by default** — then falls back to `png_ptr->mode & (IHDR|PLTE|AFTER_IDAT)` (1399-1400)\n    - **`location == 0` on a READ struct** → skips the warning, goes straight to 1406\n    - **`location == 0` still after the fallback** → `png_error(\"invalid location in png_set_unknown_chunks\")` — fatal. Row: write struct before `png_write_info` (mode has no IHDR bit) with `location = 0`\n    - the top-most-bit reduction loop at 1412-1413: rows for `location = PNG_HAVE_IHDR` alone; `PNG_HAVE_PLTE` alone; `PNG_AFTER_IDAT` alone; `IHDR|PLTE` → reduces to `PLTE`; `IHDR|PLTE|AFTER_IDAT` → reduces to `AFTER_IDAT`; `IHDR|AFTER_IDAT` → `AFTER_IDAT`. 6 rows\n    - bits outside the mask (e.g. `PNG_HAVE_IDAT`) → stripped at 1387\n\n27. **`png_set_unknown_chunks`** — 1421-1524. Rows:\n    - `png_ptr`/`info_ptr` NULL, `num_unknowns <= 0`, `unknowns == NULL` → no-op (1428-1430)\n    - the two `#if !defined(...)` guards at 1438-1455 are **both compiled out** (both `PNG_READ_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS_SUPPORTED` and `PNG_WRITE_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS_SUPPORTED` are defined). Note as unreachable\n    - `png_realloc_array` fails → `png_chunk_report(\"too many unknown chunks\")` and return (1466-1471)\n    - **deferred old-array free**: `old_unknowns` at 1476, freed at 1523. **Getter-to-setter aliasing row** via `png_get_unknown_chunks`\n    - `name` is copied with a fixed `sizeof np->name` (5 bytes) then force-terminated (1488-1489). Rows: 4-char name; a name whose 5th byte is non-NUL → truncated\n    - `check_location(png_ptr, unknowns->location)` per entry — all of #26's rows reachable here\n    - **`unknowns->size == 0`** → `np->data = NULL, np->size = 0` (1492-1496), **no allocation**. Row: assert `png_get_unknown_chunks` returns an entry with NULL data\n    - `size > 0` → `png_malloc_base`; failure → `png_chunk_report(\"unknown chunk: out of memory\")` then **`continue`** (1503-1508), which skips both `++np` and `++(info_ptr->unknown_chunks_num)` so the slot is reused by the next entry (comment 1515-1518). Row\n    - success → `++np`, `++unknown_chunks_num`, `free_me |= PNG_FREE_UNKN` (1479)\n    - `num_unknowns = 1`, `= 5` → 2 rows\n    - appending: two calls → `unknown_chunks_num` accumulates\n    - `PNG_STORE_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS_SUPPORTED` gate at 1383 — on\n\n28. **`png_set_unknown_chunk_location`** — 1526-1552. Rows:\n    - any of `png_ptr == NULL`, `info_ptr == NULL`, `chunk < 0`, `chunk >= unknown_chunks_num` → **silent no-op** (1535-1536). 4 rows\n    - **`(location & (IHDR|PLTE|AFTER_IDAT)) == 0`** → `png_app_error(\"invalid unknown chunk location\")` (1540) — **fatal by default** — then the pre-1.6.0 fake-out (1542-1546): if `location & PNG_HAVE_IDAT` → `PNG_AFTER_IDAT`, else → `PNG_HAVE_IHDR`. **Both \"undocumented\" per the comments.** Rows: `location = 0` → becomes `PNG_HAVE_IHDR`; `location = PNG_HAVE_IDAT` → becomes `PNG_AFTER_IDAT`. Requires benign errors on to observe\n    - valid location → `check_location` applied. All of #26's reduction rows\n    - `chunk == 0` with 1 stored chunk → OK; `chunk == 1` with 1 stored → no-op\n\n29. **`png_permit_mng_features`** — 1556-1567. Rows: `png_ptr == NULL` → returns 0; `mng_features = 0` → returns 0; `= PNG_FLAG_MNG_EMPTY_PLTE` → returns that bit; `= PNG_FLAG_MNG_FILTER_64` → returns that bit; `= PNG_ALL_MNG_FEATURES` → returns all; **`= 0xFFFFFFFF` → masked with `PNG_ALL_MNG_FEATURES`, returns only the known bits** (1564). Returns the stored value, so the return is the assertion. 6 rows. Feeds `png_check_IHDR`'s filter-64 branch (§3) and `png_set_PLTE`'s empty-PLTE branch (#18)\n\n30. **`add_one_chunk`** (static) — 1571-1597. Reached only from `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks`. Rows: chunk not in the list → appended, count+1; chunk already in the list → its `keep` code is **updated in place**, count unchanged; `keep == 0` (default) for a chunk not present → **not appended** (per the comment at 1686-1688)\n\n31. **`png_set_keep_unknown_chunks`** — 1599-1757. Rows:\n    - `png_ptr == NULL` → no-op\n    - **`keep < 0 || keep >= PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_LAST (4)`** → `png_app_error(\"png_set_keep_unknown_chunks: invalid keep\")` (1609-1614) — **fatal by default**. Rows: `keep = -1`, `= 4`, `= 100`\n    - **each valid `keep` is a row** (`png.h:2583-2586`): `PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_AS_DEFAULT (0)`, `PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_NEVER (1)`, `PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_IF_SAFE (2)`, `PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_ALWAYS (3)`\n    - **`num_chunks_in == 0`** → sets `unknown_default = keep` and **returns immediately** (1616-1623). Row: `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks(p, PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_ALWAYS, NULL, 0)` → `unknown_default` changed, list untouched\n    - **`num_chunks_in < 0`** → sets `unknown_default = keep` **and** substitutes the built-in 21-entry `chunks_to_ignore` list (1625-1656): bKGD, cHRM, cICP, cLLI, eXIf, gAMA, hIST, iCCP, iTXt, mDCV, oFFs, pCAL, pHYs, sBIT, sCAL, sPLT, sTER, sRGB, tEXt, tIME, zTXt. `num_chunks = sizeof/5 = 21`. Row: assert exactly those 21 names end up in the list with the given `keep`, and that IHDR/PLTE/tRNS/IDAT/IEND are **absent** (comment 1627-1628). Note `sTER` and `cICP`/`cLLI`/`mDCV` are in the list — a version-specific detail worth pinning\n    - **`num_chunks_in > 0 && chunk_list == NULL`** → `png_app_error(\"png_set_keep_unknown_chunks: no chunk list\")` (1660-1668) — fatal by default; \"prior to 1.6.0 this was silently ignored\"\n    - **`num_chunks + old_num_chunks > UINT_MAX/5`** → `png_app_error(\"...too many chunks\")` (1679-1684). Practically unreachable; note\n    - `png_ptr->chunk_list == NULL` → `old_num_chunks` forced to 0 (1674-1675) even if `num_chunk_list` was non-zero. Defensive; row\n    - **`keep != 0`** → a fresh `png_malloc` of `5*(num+old)` and the old list is `memcpy`'d in (1690-1696). `png_malloc` failure → `png_error` → fatal\n    - **`keep == 0 && old_num_chunks > 0`** → `new_list = png_ptr->chunk_list` — **reuses the existing buffer in place** (1699-1700). Row: setting `keep = 0` for an existing entry removes it without reallocating\n    - **`keep == 0 && old_num_chunks == 0`** → `new_list = NULL` → the whole `if (new_list != NULL)` block is skipped, `num_chunks = 0` (1745-1746). Row\n    - the compaction loop at 1723-1733 removes entries whose `inlist[4] == 0`. Row: add 3 chunks with `keep = ALWAYS`, then set one of them to `keep = AS_DEFAULT` → list shrinks to 2\n    - **all entries removed → `num_chunks == 0`** → `new_list` is freed (if it isn't the current list) and set to NULL (1736-1742). Row: assert `png_ptr->chunk_list == NULL` and `num_chunk_list == 0` afterwards\n    - the final pointer swap at 1750-1756 frees the old list only if it differs. Row: call twice with the same `keep` and assert no double-free\n    - observable via `png_handle_as_unknown` (`png.c:930-961`): rows for a chunk in the list (returns its code), a chunk not in the list (returns `PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_AS_DEFAULT`), `num_chunk_list == 0` (returns default), `chunk_name == NULL` (returns default), `png_ptr == NULL` (returns default). 5 more rows\n    - and via `png_chunk_unknown_handling` (`png.c:965-972`) which converts a `png_uint_32` chunk id to the 5-byte string with `PNG_CSTRING_FROM_CHUNK` then delegates. 1 row\n    - `PNG_HANDLE_AS_UNKNOWN_SUPPORTED` gate at 1570 — on\n\n32. **`png_set_read_user_chunk_fn`** — 1761-1772 (`PNG_READ_USER_CHUNKS_SUPPORTED`). Rows: `png_ptr == NULL` → no-op; both params set; `read_user_chunk_fn == NULL` with a non-NULL ptr; `user_chunk_ptr == NULL`. Observable via `png_get_user_chunk_ptr`. 4 rows\n\n33. **`png_set_rows`** — 1776-1793 (`PNG_INFO_IMAGE_SUPPORTED`). Rows:\n    - `png_ptr`/`info_ptr` NULL → no-op\n    - **`row_pointers != NULL` and different from the current** → `png_free_data(..., PNG_FREE_ROWS, 0)` first (1785-1787). Note this frees `height` rows, so **`info_ptr->height` must be correct** or you leak/overrun\n    - **`row_pointers == info_ptr->row_pointers`** (same pointer) → the free is **skipped** (1786). Self-assignment row\n    - **`row_pointers == NULL`** with a non-NULL current → the condition `info_ptr->row_pointers != NULL && (!= row_pointers)` is **true**, so the old rows ARE freed, then `row_pointers = NULL` and `PNG_INFO_IDAT` is **not** set (1791-1792). Row: this is the \"clear the rows\" idiom\n    - `row_pointers == NULL` with a NULL current → pure no-op\n    - success with non-NULL → `valid |= PNG_INFO_IDAT`. Note **`free_me` is NOT touched** — the caller retains ownership unless they call `png_data_freer`. High-value row: `png_set_rows` then `png_free_data(PNG_FREE_ROWS, -1)` frees nothing because the `free_me` bit was never set\n    - pair with `png_data_freer(p, i, PNG_DESTROY_WILL_FREE_DATA, PNG_FREE_ROWS)` → now the free works. 2-row pair\n\n34. **`png_set_compression_buffer_size`** — 1796-1856. Rows:\n    - `png_ptr == NULL` → no-op\n    - **`size == 0`** → `png_error(\"invalid compression buffer size\")` — fatal (1804-1805)\n    - **`size > PNG_UINT_31_MAX`** → same `png_error`. Rows: `0x80000000`; boundary `PNG_UINT_31_MAX` → accepted\n    - **READ struct** (`mode & PNG_IS_READ_STRUCT`, 1808) → `IDAT_read_size = size` and **return immediately** — none of the write-side checks apply. Rows: `size = 1` on a read struct → **accepted** (no minimum!); `size = PNG_UINT_31_MAX` → accepted. Contrast with the write side's minimum of 6. High-value asymmetry row\n    - **WRITE struct** (1816):\n      - `png_ptr->zowner != 0` → `png_warning(\"Compression buffer size cannot be changed because it is in use\")` and return (1818-1824). Reachable mid-write; row\n      - `size > ZLIB_IO_MAX` → `png_warning(\"Compression buffer size limited to system maximum\")` and `size = ZLIB_IO_MAX` (1830-1835). `ZLIB_IO_MAX` is `UINT_MAX` capped; on LP64 with `uInt` 32-bit this is only reachable if `PNG_UINT_31_MAX > ZLIB_IO_MAX`, which it isn't → note as unreachable. Gated by `#ifndef __COVERITY__`\n      - **`size < 6`** → `png_warning(\"Compression buffer size cannot be reduced below 6\")` and return (1838-1847). Rows: `size = 1` → warning, no change; `size = 5` → warning; `size = 6` → **accepted** (boundary)\n      - **`zbuffer_size != size`** → `png_free_buffer_list(&zbuffer_list)` then assign (1849-1853). Row: setting the same size twice → the second call does **not** free the buffer list\n    - observable via `png_get_compression_buffer_size` (getter #52). 8 rows total\n\n35. **`png_set_invalid`** — 1858-1863. `info_ptr->valid &= ~mask`. Rows: `png_ptr`/`info_ptr` NULL → no-op; `mask = 0` → no change; `mask = PNG_INFO_gAMA` → that bit cleared, others untouched; `mask = PNG_INFO_gAMA|PNG_INFO_cHRM` → both cleared; `mask = -1` (all bits) → `valid` becomes 0; **`mask` is an `int` but `valid` is wider** — `mask = 0x10000` (`PNG_INFO_eXIf`) works, `mask = PNG_INFO_mDCV (0x80000)` works. Rows for each of the 22 `PNG_INFO_*` bits if you want exhaustive coverage; 6 representative rows otherwise. Note this does **not** free the associated data, so `png_get_*` returns 0 while the memory is still allocated and `free_me` still set. Row asserting `png_free_data` still releases it afterwards\n\n36. **`png_set_user_limits`** — 1868-1883 (`PNG_SET_USER_LIMITS_SUPPORTED`). Rows: `png_ptr == NULL` → no-op; `(1000000, 1000000)` → the defaults restated; **`(0x7fffffff, 0x7fffffff)`** → \"accept any PNG datastream regardless of dimensions\" per the comment at 1875-1877; `(0, 0)` → every image is rejected by `png_check_IHDR`; `(1, 1)` → only 1×1 accepted; asymmetric `(1000, 1)`. Then cross with `png_check_IHDR`: width exactly at the limit → OK, limit+1 → warning+error. 6 rows. Observable via `png_get_user_width_max`/`png_get_user_height_max`\n\n37. **`png_set_chunk_cache_max`** — 1886-1893. Rows: `png_ptr == NULL` → no-op; `0` → stored as 0 (meaning unlimited to the consumers); `1`; `1000` (default); `0xFFFFFFFF`. **No normalization at all** — contrast with `png_set_chunk_malloc_max`. 5 rows. Observable via `png_get_chunk_cache_max`\n\n38. **`png_set_chunk_malloc_max`** — 1896-1920. Rows:\n    - `png_ptr == NULL` → no-op\n    - **`user_chunk_malloc_max == 0`** → **normalized to `PNG_SIZE_MAX`** (1909-1915), because `PNG_MAX_MALLOC_64K` is not defined. The comment at 1902-1906 explains why. Row: set 0, then `png_get_chunk_malloc_max` returns `PNG_SIZE_MAX`, **not 0**. High-value row — this is the only setter in the file that rewrites its argument\n    - non-zero → stored verbatim. Rows: `1`, `8000000` (the default), `PNG_SIZE_MAX`\n    - 4 rows\n\n39. **`png_set_benign_errors`** — 1925-1943. Covered in §10\n\n40. **`png_set_check_for_invalid_index`** — 1955-1965 (`PNG_CHECK_FOR_INVALID_INDEX_SUPPORTED`). **No NULL check on `png_ptr`.** Rows:\n    - **`allowed > 0`** → `num_palette_max = 0` (checking **enabled**)\n    - **`allowed <= 0`** → `num_palette_max = -1` (checking **disabled**). Rows: `allowed = 0`, `= -1`\n    - `allowed = 1`, `= 2`, `= 100` → all enable\n    - Observable via `png_get_palette_max` (getter #55) and by whether `png_do_check_palette_indexes` (`pngtrans.c:727-826`) updates the field. Row: disable, read a row with an out-of-range index, assert `png_get_palette_max` returns -1; enable, same read, assert it returns the actual max\n    - 4 rows\n\n41. **`png_check_keyword`** — 1980-2055. Covered in §8\n\n### Remaining items in area 11\n\n42. **`png_set_sig_bytes`** — `png.c:52-69` (`PNG_READ_SUPPORTED` only). Rows:\n    - `png_ptr == NULL` → no-op (59-60)\n    - **`num_bytes < 0`** → clamped to `nb = 0` (62-63). Rows: `-1`, `INT_MIN`\n    - **`nb > 8`** → `png_error(\"Too many bytes for PNG signature\")` (65-66) — **fatal**. Rows: `9`, `100`, `INT_MAX`\n    - valid: `0` through `8` → stored. **9 rows**, one per value. `8` means \"the whole signature is already consumed\" (comment 46-48) and makes `png_read_sig` return immediately (`pngrutil.c:121-122`)\n    - interaction with `png_read_sig`: `sig_bytes = 0` → 8 bytes read and full compare; `= 4` → 4 bytes read, `png_sig_cmp(sig, 4, 4)`; `= 3` → `num_checked < 4` so the fallback comparison at `pngrutil.c:137-138` distinguishes \"Not a PNG file\" from \"PNG file corrupted by ASCII conversion\"; `< 3` → sets `PNG_HAVE_PNG_SIGNATURE` in `mode` (`pngrutil.c:143-144`), which in turn changes `png_check_IHDR`'s MNG branch. **The `sig_bytes < 3` → `PNG_HAVE_PNG_SIGNATURE` → MNG-filter-rejection chain is a high-value cross-area row**\n43. **`png_get_sig_bytes`** — **does not exist in this tree.** grep finds no definition and no `PNG_EXPORT` for it. Drop the row (there is a `png_get_signature` at `pngget.c:490-497` which returns the 8 stored bytes, and `png_ptr->sig_bytes` is only readable internally)\n44. **`png_get_io_ptr`** — `png.c:690-697`. Rows: `png_ptr == NULL` → NULL; never set → NULL; after `png_init_io(p, fp)` → `(png_voidp)fp`; after `png_set_read_fn(p, my_ptr, fn)` → `my_ptr`; after `png_set_write_fn(p, my_ptr, fn, flush)` → `my_ptr`; after `png_set_read_fn(p, NULL, NULL)` → NULL (the create-struct default). 6 rows\n45. **`png_set_read_fn`** — `pngrio.c:85-118`. Covered in §12\n46. **`png_set_write_fn`** — `pngwio.c:120-166`. Covered in §12\n47. **`png_set_read_status_fn`** — `pngread.c:855-862`. Rows: `png_ptr == NULL` → no-op; a callback installed → invoked once per row by `png_read_finish_row`/`png_read_row`; `read_row_fn == NULL` → disables the callback. 3 rows. No validation, no branches beyond the NULL check\n48. **`png_set_write_status_fn`** — `pngwrite.c:1378-1386`. Same 3 rows; the callback receives `(png_ptr, row_number, pass)` per `pngwrite.c:950`\n49. **`png_set_flush`** — `pngwrite.c:955-965` (`PNG_WRITE_FLUSH_SUPPORTED`, on). `png_ptr->flush_dist = (nrows < 0 ? 0 : (png_uint_32)nrows)`. Rows: `png_ptr == NULL` → no-op; **`nrows < 0` → clamped to 0** (flushing off) — rows `-1`, `INT_MIN`; `nrows = 0` → off; `nrows = 1` → flush every row; `nrows = 10`; `nrows = INT_MAX`. 6 rows. Interacts with `png_write_flush` (`pngwrite.c:968+`) and `png_flush` (`pngwio.c:69-74`)\n\n---\n\n## 12. `pngrio.c` / `pngwio.c`\n\n### `png_read_data` — `pngrio.c:30-40` (`PRIVATE`)\n1. `read_data_fn != NULL` → dispatched\n2. **`read_data_fn == NULL`** → `png_error(\"Call to NULL read function\")` (39). Reachable only by `png_set_read_fn(p, ptr, NULL)` in a build **without** `PNG_STDIO_SUPPORTED` — but STDIO **is** on here, so `png_set_read_fn` always installs `png_default_read_data` as a fallback (`pngrio.c:98-99`). The only way to reach the error in this build is `png_set_write_fn` on a read struct, which NULLs `read_data_fn` at `pngwio.c:159`. **Row: `png_create_read_struct` → `png_set_write_fn(...)` → attempt a read → \"Call to NULL read function\"**\n3. `length == 0` → the callback is still invoked with 0\n\n### `png_default_read_data` — `pngrio.c:48-63` (`PNG_STDIO_SUPPORTED`, on; exported as `PNGCBAPI`)\n1. **`png_ptr == NULL`** → silent return (53-54)\n2. `fread` returns `length` → success\n3. **`fread` returns < `length`** → `png_error(\"Read Error\")` (61-62). Rows: EOF reached mid-read; a file shorter than requested; `length` larger than the remaining bytes\n4. `length == 0` → `fread(_, 1, 0, f)` returns 0, `check == length` → **success**, no error. Row\n5. **`png_ptr->io_ptr == NULL`** → `fread(_, _, _, NULL)` → **undefined/crash**. Reachable via `png_create_read_struct` (which installs `png_default_read_data` with `io_ptr = NULL` at `pngread.c:74`) followed by a read without calling `png_init_io`. **High-value hazard row** — this is exactly the `png_init_io(p, NULL)` trap\n6. `io_ptr` pointing at a `FILE*` opened write-only → `fread` fails → \"Read Error\"\n7. reading exactly to EOF then one more byte → the second call errors\n\n### `png_set_read_fn` — `pngrio.c:85-118`\n1. `png_ptr == NULL` → no-op (89-90)\n2. `io_ptr` stored unconditionally (92) — including NULL\n3. **`read_data_fn != NULL`** → installed (95-96)\n4. **`read_data_fn == NULL`** → **`png_default_read_data` installed instead** (98-99), because `PNG_STDIO_SUPPORTED` is on. Row: `png_set_read_fn(p, fp, NULL)` behaves like `png_init_io(p, fp)`. Without STDIO the `#else` at 101 would store NULL — second config row\n5. **`png_ptr->write_data_fn != NULL`** → it is NULLed and `png_warning(\"Can't set both read_data_fn and write_data_fn in the same structure\")` (104-113). Reachable via `png_set_write_fn` then `png_set_read_fn` on the same struct. Row asserting the warning fires and `write_data_fn` becomes NULL\n6. `write_data_fn == NULL` → no warning\n7. **`output_flush_fn` is unconditionally NULLed** (115-117, `PNG_WRITE_FLUSH_SUPPORTED` on). Row: `png_set_write_fn(p, ptr, w, f)` then `png_set_read_fn(p, ptr, r)` → assert `output_flush_fn == NULL`\n8. called twice → second wins\n9. Called from `png_create_read_struct_2` as `png_set_read_fn(png_ptr, NULL, NULL)` (`pngread.c:74`) → the default state is `io_ptr = NULL`, `read_data_fn = png_default_read_data`. Row asserting that on a fresh read struct\n\n### `png_write_data` — `pngwio.c:31-41` (`PRIVATE`)\n1. `write_data_fn != NULL` → dispatched, with `png_constcast` stripping the const (36-37) — the comment at 34 warns the callback must not modify the buffer\n2. **`write_data_fn == NULL`** → `png_error(\"Call to NULL write function\")` (40). Reachable in this build only via `png_set_read_fn` on a write struct (which NULLs `write_data_fn` at `pngrio.c:108`). Row\n3. `length == 0`\n\n### `png_default_write_data` — `pngwio.c:49-61` (`PNG_STDIO_SUPPORTED`; exported)\n1. **`png_ptr == NULL`** → silent return (54-55)\n2. `fwrite` returns `length` → success\n3. **`fwrite` returns < `length`** → `png_error(\"Write Error\")` (59-60). Rows: disk full; write to a read-only `FILE*`; write to a closed stream\n4. `length == 0` → `fwrite` returns 0 == length → success\n5. **`io_ptr == NULL`** → `fwrite(_,_,_, NULL)` → crash. Same `png_init_io(p, NULL)` trap as the read side. Note `png_create_write_struct_2` also installs the default write fn, so a write struct with no `png_init_io` is equally dangerous. Row\n\n### `png_flush` — `pngwio.c:69-74` (`PRIVATE`, `PNG_WRITE_FLUSH_SUPPORTED`)\n1. `output_flush_fn != NULL` → dispatched\n2. **`output_flush_fn == NULL`** → **silent no-op** (no `png_error`, unlike `png_write_data`). Row: `png_set_read_fn` NULLs it (`pngrio.c:116`), then `png_flush` is harmless\n\n### `png_default_flush` — `pngwio.c:77-87` (`PNG_WRITE_FLUSH_SUPPORTED && PNG_STDIO_SUPPORTED`, both on; exported)\n1. **`png_ptr == NULL`** → silent return (82-83)\n2. valid `io_ptr` → `fflush(io_ptr)`; return value **ignored**, so a failed flush is silent. Row asserting no error is raised on a failing flush (contrast with `png_default_write_data`)\n3. **`io_ptr == NULL`** → `fflush(NULL)` → **defined behavior**: flushes *all* open output streams. Row — this one is benign, unlike the `fread`/`fwrite` NULL cases\n\n### `png_set_write_fn` — `pngwio.c:120-166`\n1. `png_ptr == NULL` → no-op (124-125)\n2. `io_ptr` stored unconditionally (127)\n3. **`write_data_fn != NULL`** → installed (130-131)\n4. **`write_data_fn == NULL`** → `png_default_write_data` installed (133-134). Row\n5. **`output_flush_fn != NULL`** → installed (142-143)\n6. **`output_flush_fn == NULL`** → **`png_default_flush` installed** (145-146). Row: `png_set_write_fn(p, my_non_FILE_ptr, my_write, NULL)` → `png_default_flush` will `fflush` a non-`FILE*`. The doc comment at 115-118 explicitly warns \"This is not a good idea if io_ptr does not point to a standard *FILE structure.\" **High-value hazard row**\n7. **`png_ptr->read_data_fn != NULL`** → NULLed + `png_warning(\"Can't set both read_data_fn and write_data_fn in the same structure\")` (157-164). Row\n8. `read_data_fn == NULL` → no warning\n9. the 4-way cross of `(write_data_fn NULL?) × (output_flush_fn NULL?)` → 4 rows\n10. Without `PNG_WRITE_FLUSH_SUPPORTED` the `#else PNG_UNUSED(output_flush_fn)` at 152 would discard it; without `PNG_STDIO_SUPPORTED` the `#else` at 148-149 stores it raw. 2 more config rows if you can rebuild\n\n### `png_init_io` — `png.c:707-716` (`PNG_STDIO_SUPPORTED`, on)\nThe function body is just two branches:\n1. **`png_ptr == NULL`** → return (712-713)\n2. otherwise → `png_ptr->io_ptr = (png_voidp)fp` — **unconditionally, with no NULL check on `fp`**\nSo the \"NULL `FILE*` branch\" you asked about **does not exist inside `png_init_io`**. Rows:\n3. **`png_init_io(p, NULL)`** → **succeeds silently**, `io_ptr` becomes NULL, `png_get_io_ptr` returns NULL. The failure surfaces later in `png_default_read_data`'s `fread(..., NULL)` or `png_default_write_data`'s `fwrite(..., NULL)`. **This is the row to write: assert `png_init_io(p, NULL)` returns without error and that the subsequent I/O is what fails.**\n4. `png_init_io(NULL, fp)` → no-op, no crash\n5. `png_init_io(NULL, NULL)` → no-op\n6. valid `fp` → `png_get_io_ptr(p) == fp`\n7. **`png_init_io` does NOT install any `read_data_fn`/`write_data_fn`** — it relies on `png_create_*_struct` having installed the defaults. Row: `png_init_io` after `png_set_read_fn(p, ptr, my_fn)` leaves `my_fn` in place but replaces `io_ptr` with the `FILE*` → `my_fn` now receives a `FILE*` it didn't expect. Genuine hazard row\n8. called twice with different `FILE*` → second wins, first is not closed (no ownership)\n9. the TODO at `pngread.c:70-73` notes the default read fn *should* be installed lazily in `png_init_io`; it currently is not. Note\n\n---\n\n## Summary of items in your request that do not exist in this tree\n\n| Requested | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| `png_muldiv_warn` | **absent** — no definition, no declaration anywhere |\n| `png_colorspace_set_chromaticities` | **absent** |\n| `png_colorspace_set_endpoints` | **absent** |\n| `png_colorspace_set_sRGB` | **absent** |\n| `png_colorspace_set_gamma` | **absent** |\n| `png_colorspace_sync` | **absent** (only a stale comment at `pngwrite.c:122`) |\n| `png_check_sig` | present but a **macro** at `png.h:940`, marked DEPRECATED |\n| `png_get_io_chunk_name` | **removed** — `PNG_REMOVED(200, ...)` at `png.h:2655` |\n| `png_get_sig_bytes` | **absent** — no such API; use `png_get_signature` (`pngget.c:490`) |\n| `png_product2` | present at `png.c:2929` but **not compiled** (`#ifndef PNG_FLOATING_ARITHMETIC_SUPPORTED`) |\n| `png_log8bit` / `png_log16bit` / `png_exp` / `png_exp8bit` / `png_exp16bit` | present at `png.c:3047/3104/3196/3244/3259` but **not compiled** (same gate) |\n| `png_muldiv` 32/64-bit integer path | present at `png.c:2796-2876` but **not compiled** |\n| `png_set_strip_error_numbers` | present at `pngerror.c:749` but **not compiled** (`PNG_ERROR_NUMBERS_SUPPORTED` undefined); body is a no-op anyway |\n| `png_err` | present at `pngerror.c:51` but **not compiled** (`PNG_ERROR_TEXT_SUPPORTED` is on, so `png_error` is used) |\n| `PNG_ALIGNED_MEMORY_SUPPORTED` effect on memory | **none** — defined at `pnglibconf.h:19` but never referenced in `pngmem.c`; only `pngrutil.c:4618` and hardware-optimization gates in `pngpriv.h` |\n\n## Cross-area rows worth prioritizing\n\n1. `png_set_IHDR` with an invalid combination → error raised **after** fields are written → `png_get_IHDR` re-raises → `png_get_channels`/`png_get_rowbytes` return stale values (§11 #13)\n2. `png_get_cHRM_XYZ` returning 0 for a `valid` cHRM because `png_XYZ_from_xy` rejected it — makes every §3 failure class observable through the public API (§11 getter #23)\n3. `png_get_iCCP`'s `*proflen` coming from the profile bytes, not `iccp_proflen` (§11 getter #29)\n4. `png_get_mDCV_fixed`'s ×2 undoing `png_ITU_fixed_16`'s ÷2 → odd inputs lose their low bit (§11 getter #34 / setter #7)\n5. `png_data_freer(freer=1)` vs `(freer=2)` × each `PNG_FREE_*` bit, then `png_free_data` — 22 rows (§9)\n6. `png_free_data` with `num >= 0` on a `PNG_FREE_MUL` bit leaving `free_me` intact vs `num == -1` clearing it (§9 rows 3-4)\n7. Every getter-to-setter aliasing pattern: `png_set_PLTE`, `png_set_hIST`, `png_set_tRNS`, `png_set_text`, `png_set_sPLT`, `png_set_unknown_chunks` — each has an explicit snapshot or deferred-free fix in this version (§11 #18, #12, #24, #22, #25, #27)\n8. `png_app_error`/`png_app_warning` being **fatal by default** in this BETA build (`PNG_RELEASE_BUILD == 0`) — affects `png_set_shift`, `png_set_filler`, `png_set_sPLT`, `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks`, `png_set_unknown_chunk_location`, `png_set_iCCP`, `png_set_cHRM_XYZ_fixed`, and every `png_chunk_report` on a write struct (§0, §10)\n9. `png_init_io(p, NULL)` succeeding silently, with the failure deferred to `fread`/`fwrite` on a NULL `FILE*` (§12 #3)\n10. `png_set_write_fn(p, non_FILE_ptr, my_write, NULL)` installing `png_default_flush`, which will `fflush` a non-`FILE*` (§12 #6)\n11. `png_set_read_fn`/`png_set_write_fn` mutual exclusion warnings and the fields they NULL (§12)\n12. `png_sig_cmp(sig, 3, 5)` → `sig_bytes < 3` → `PNG_HAVE_PNG_SIGNATURE` → `png_check_IHDR` rejects MNG filter 64 (§5, §3, §11 #42)\n13. `png_set_sPLT` with a NULL name and `nentries > 1` re-processing the same entry `nentries` times (§11 #25)\n14. `png_set_compression_buffer_size` accepting `size = 1` on a read struct but rejecting anything below 6 on a write struct (§11 #34)\n15. `png_set_chunk_malloc_max(p, 0)` being rewritten to `PNG_SIZE_MAX` (§11 #38)\n16. `png_get_palette_max` returning -1 both for NULL args and for \"checking disabled\" (§11 getter #55)\n17. `png_set_text_2` downgrading `PNG_ITXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt` → `PNG_ITXT_COMPRESSION_NONE` for empty text (§11 #22)\n18. `png_check_fp_string(\"1e\", 2)` returning 0 because `png_fp_set` drops the non-sticky `SAW_DIGIT` — propagates into `png_set_sCAL_s` and `png_set_pCAL` (§4, §11 #14, #15)\n19. `png_do_bgr` with `color_type = 3` (PALETTE) passing the `PNG_COLOR_MASK_COLOR` test but matching neither inner arm → silent no-op (§6)\n20. `png_gamma_correct` with `bit_depth ∈ {1,2,4}` dispatching to the **16-bit** routine (§2)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":64065,"cache_read_input_tokens":209526,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":64065,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01AHp7EWTH7PuSA4AaDJf2sf","session_id":"e3091878-9949-4689-ad83-c0c41e6641a2","uuid":"5b1b2548-434c-443d-9e6f-4725cf3bd58f","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:38:41.593Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Map utility and memory functions"}
