{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01KLnB5qKMWAyG2TJvjMbNi8","type":"tool_result","content":"# ERRORS.md — the ERROR-SURFACE TABLE (Phase A, gates Phase C)\n\nMechanically derived from `c_src/src/*.c`: every `png_error` / `png_chunk_error`\n/ `png_app_error` / `png_benign_error` / `png_chunk_benign_error` /\n`png_chunk_report` / `png_warning` / `png_app_warning` / `png_chunk_warning`\ncall site, every rejecting `return -1` / `return 0` / `return NULL`, every\nexplicit range / null / overflow check and every min/max constant comparison.\nThere are **no `assert()`** calls anywhere in the library.\n\nOne row per distinct rejection.  The `[x]` column is ticked when a differential\ntest constructs that exact condition and asserts both libraries produce the\nsame error/rejection.\n\nNote on non-testable rows: a handful of C paths dereference a pointer *before*\nchecking it (`png_muldiv`'s `res`, `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer`'s `ptime`,\n`png_do_bgr`'s `row`, `png_get_io_state`'s `png_ptr`, ...).  Those are C\nundefined behaviour, not error paths, and are marked `n/a (C UB)`.\n\n\n## png.c / pngerror.c / pngmem.c / pngrio.c / pngwio.c\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | [x] |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|-----|\n| 1 | `png_set_sig_bytes` | `png_ptr == NULL` (`png.c:59`) | silent `return`, no state change | [ ] |\n| 2 | `png_set_sig_bytes` | `num_bytes < 0` (`png.c:62`) | silently clamped: `nb = 0`, `png_ptr->sig_bytes = 0` | [ ] |\n| 3 | `png_set_sig_bytes` | `nb > 8` i.e. more than 8 already-consumed signature bytes (`png.c:65`) | `png_error(png_ptr, \"Too many bytes for PNG signature\")` -> error, no return | [ ] |\n| 4 | `png_sig_cmp` | `num_to_check > 8` (`png.c:84`) | silently clamped to `num_to_check = 8` | [ ] |\n| 5 | `png_sig_cmp` | `num_to_check < 1` (`png.c:87`) | `return -1` (reject) | [ ] |\n| 6 | `png_sig_cmp` | `start > 7` (`png.c:90`) | `return -1` (reject) | [ ] |\n| 7 | `png_sig_cmp` | `start + num_to_check > 8` (`png.c:93`) | silently clamped: `num_to_check = 8 - start` | [ ] |\n| 8 | `png_sig_cmp` | `memcmp(&sig[start], &png_signature[start], num_to_check) != 0` (`png.c:96`) | returns non-zero (signature mismatch) | [ ] |\n| 9 | `png_zalloc` | `png_ptr == NULL` (`png.c:109`) | `return NULL` | [ ] |\n| 10 | `png_zalloc` | `size != 0 && items >= (~(png_alloc_size_t)0) / size` — `items*size` overflows `png_alloc_size_t` (`png.c:118`) | `png_warning(png_ptr, \"Potential overflow in png_zalloc()\")` then `return NULL` | [ ] |\n| 11 | `png_calculate_crc` | `(uInt)length == 0` after truncation of a `length` that is a non-zero multiple of `uInt` range (`png.c:182`) | defensive fixup `safe_length = (uInt)-1`; loop continues, no error | [ ] |\n| 12 | `png_user_version_check` | `user_png_ver == NULL` (`png.c:229`) | sets `PNG_FLAG_LIBRARY_MISMATCH` | [ ] |\n| 13 | `png_user_version_check` | `user_png_ver[i] != PNG_LIBPNG_VER_STRING[i]` up to the second `.` (`png.c:221`) | sets `PNG_FLAG_LIBRARY_MISMATCH` | [ ] |\n| 14 | `png_user_version_check` | `(png_ptr->flags & PNG_FLAG_LIBRARY_MISMATCH) != 0` (`png.c:232`) | `png_warning(png_ptr, \"Application built with libpng-<ver> but running with <ver>\")` then `return 0` (failure) | [ ] |\n| 15 | `png_create_png_struct` | `png_user_version_check(...) == 0` (`png.c:329`) | falls through to `return NULL` | [ ] |\n| 16 | `png_create_png_struct` | `png_malloc_warn(&create_struct, sizeof *png_ptr) == NULL` i.e. OOM for `png_struct` (`png.c:334`) | `png_warning(..., \"Out of memory\")` from `png_malloc_warn`, then `return NULL` | [ ] |\n| 17 | `png_create_png_struct` | user memory allocator calls `png_error`/longjmp back into `create_jmp_buf` (`png.c:314`) | `return NULL` | [ ] |\n| 18 | `png_create_info_struct` | `png_ptr == NULL` (`png.c:373`) | `return NULL` | [ ] |\n| 19 | `png_create_info_struct` | `png_malloc_base(png_ptr, sizeof *inf