s; bad signature; \"Invalid IHDR length\"; truncated/extra compressed data; ADLER32 mismatch; `png_process_data_skip` and `png_process_data_pause` misuse.\n- **Out-of-range enum values across FFI**: for every enum-typed parameter also pass a value with no valid variant (-1, LAST, LAST+1, 999, i32::MIN, i32::MAX).\n\nCRITICAL RULES:\n- Some C paths dereference a pointer BEFORE checking it, so NULL there is C undefined behaviour, not an error path. If a case segfaults in BOTH libraries, do NOT test it: remove it and leave a comment explaining why with the C file:line.\n- The C is ground truth. If C and Rust genuinely differ, do NOT change the Rust. Leave the assertion, mark that one `#[test]` `#[ignore]` with a `// DIVERGENCE:` comment naming function, inputs, C result, Rust result, and report it prominently.\n- Do NOT modify `tests/common/*`, any other test file, `ERRORS.md`, or anything under `c_src/`.\n- Iterate until green:\n  `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-kk7Dev/translation && timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test t12_errors_read -- --test-threads=1`\n\nReport back: the list of `#[test]` functions with an approximate case count each, the final pass/fail status, every case dropped as C UB (with C file:line), and any `// DIVERGENCE:` findings in full detail.","uuid":"6b0acdaf-1841-477c-bd5e-8c8fd140c839","session_id":"e3091878-9949-4689-ad83-c0c41e6641a2"}
