`; `png_write_image`/`png_write_rows` with a NULL row-pointer array; writing more rows than `height`; writing fewer rows and then `png_write_end` (\"Not enough image data\" / \"too few rows\"); `png_write_png` with no rows set; `png_set_rows` then `png_write_png` with a mismatched height; calling write functions on a READ struct and read functions on a WRITE struct.\n- **`png_write_IHDR` / `png_write_*` chunk writers called directly and out of order**: `png_write_sig` twice, `png_write_IHDR` with each invalid (width, height, bit_depth, color_type, interlace, compression, filter) combination, `png_write_PLTE` with num_pal 0 / 1 / 256 / 257 / >(1<<bit_depth) and on a non-palette image, `png_write_chunk_start` with a bogus chunk name / huge length, `png_write_chunk_data` with NULL data or length 0, `png_write_chunk_end` without a start, `png_write_IEND` twice, and each of `png_write_gAMA_fixed` / `png_write_cHRM_fixed` / `png_write_sRGB` / `png_write_iCCP` / `png_write_sBIT` / `png_write_tRNS` / `png_write_bKGD` / `png_write_hIST` / `png_write_pHYs` / `png_write_oFFs` / `png_write_sCAL_s` / `png_write_pCAL` / `png_write_tIME` / `png_write_tEXt` / `png_write_zTXt` / `png_write_iTXt` / `png_write_sPLT` / `png_write_eXIf` / `png_write_cICP` / `png_write_cLLI_fixed` / `png_write_mDCV_fixed` with out-of-range arguments.\n- **Compression parameter rejections**: `png_set_compression_level`/`_mem_level`/`_strategy`/`_window_bits`/`_method` and the `png_set_text_compression_*` twins, with out-of-range values (below minimum, above maximum, and far out: -100, 999, i32::MIN, i32::MAX); `png_set_compression_buffer_size` with 0 and with a huge value; `png_set_compression_buffer_size` called after writing has started.\n- **Filter rejections**: `png_set_filter` with an invalid method and with invalid mask bits (e.g. 0x01..0x07, 0xff, -1); `png_set_filter` on a palette / low-bit-depth image (which restricts the allowed filters); `png_set_filter_heuristics`/`_fixed` with an invalid method, num_weights < 0, and NULL weight/cost arrays.\n- **Text rejections**: `png_set_text` / `png_set_text_2` with every invalid `compression` value (-4, -3..2 boundaries, 3, 99), an empty key, a key that is only spaces, a key longer than 79 characters, a key with leading/trailing/consecutive spaces or control characters, NULL text with a compressed type, iTXt without lang/lang_key, and `png_write_iTXt` with a bad compression value.\n- **ICC profile rejections** (one test case per distinct check): `png_set_iCCP` and the exported `png_icc_check_length` / `png_icc_check_header` / `png_icc_check_tag_table` with: length 0, length < 132, length not a multiple of 4, length > the maximum, a declared profile size that disagrees with the passed length, a bad signature (\"acsp\"), an unsupported version, a bad colour space, a bad PCS, a tag count of 0, a tag count that overflows the profile, a tag with a bad offset/length, and a well-formed minimal profile (which must be ACCEPTED by both). Also test with `png_set_option(PNG_SKIP_sRGB_CHECK_PROFILE, ON)`.\n- **`png_check_keyword`** with all the invalid keyword forms.\n- **Simplified write API failures**: `png_image_write_to_memory` / `_to_file` / `_to_stdio` with version != PNG_IMAGE_VERSION, width or height 0, an invalid `format`, a NULL buffer, a too-small memory buffer, a NULL image, a NULL file name, and `convert_to_8bit` values other than 0/1.\n- **Out-of-range enum values across FFI**: for every enum-typed parameter also pass a value with no valid variant (-1, LAST, LAST+1, 999, i32::MIN, i32::MAX).\n\nCRITICAL RULES:\n- Some C paths dereference a pointer BEFORE checking it, so NULL there is C undefined behaviour, not an error path. If a case segfaults in BOTH libraries, do NOT test it: remove it and leave a comment explaining why, citing the C file:line.\n- Rows must be handed to the write path over-allocated whenever a transform makes libpng consume more application bytes per row than PNG_ROWBYTES (filler, packing), otherwise both libraries read past the buffer and the comparison is meaningless.\n- The C is ground truth. If C and Rust genuinely differ, do NOT change the Rust. Leave the assertion, mark that one `#[test]` `#[ignore]` with a `// DIVERGENCE:` comment naming function, inputs, C result, Rust result, and report it prominently.\n- Do NOT modify `tests/common/*`, any other test file, `ERRORS.md`, or anything under `c_src/`.\n- Iterate until green:\n  `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-kk7Dev/translation && timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test t13_errors_write -- --test-threads=1`\n\nReport back: the list of `#[test]` functions with an approximate case count each, the final pass/fail status, every case dropped as C UB (with C file:line), and any `// DIVERGENCE:` findings in full detail."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2645,"cache_read_input_tokens":333338,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2645,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e3091878-9949-4689-ad83-c0c41e6641a2","uuid":"a321654e-bc2e-4d63-a8c8-01bccfbb8705","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:45:33.408Z"}
