{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01WACjT42ve9CgEDEFa52iaj","type":"tool_result","content":"#!/bin/bash\n# Full verification driver: rebuild both shared objects, diff their exported\n# symbols, then run every differential test under every Cargo feature\n# combination (this crate declares no [features], so the default is the only\n# combination -- the loop is generated from Cargo.toml so it stays correct if\n# features are ever added).\nset -uo pipefail\nROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\" && pwd)\"\ncd \"$ROOT/translation\"\n\necho \"=== 1. build the reference C shared library ===\"\n( cd \"$ROOT/c_src\" && mkdir -p build && cd build \\\n  && cmake .. -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON >/dev/null \\\n  && cmake --build . >/dev/null ) || exit 1\nls -l \"$ROOT/c_src/build/libpng.so\"\n\necho\necho \"=== 2. build the Rust cdylib ===\"\ncargo build --offline --release || exit 1\nls -l target/release/liblibpng.so\n\necho\necho \"=== 3. exported-symbol parity (SYMBOLS.md) ===\"\nW=$(mktemp -d)\nnm -D --defined-only \"$ROOT/c_src/build/libpng.so\"      | awk '$2!=\"U\"{print $3}' | sort -u > \"$W/c.txt\"\nnm -D --defined-only target/release/liblibpng.so        | awk '$2!=\"U\"{print $3}' | sort -u > \"$W/rs.txt\"\necho \"C exports:    $(wc -l < \"$W/c.txt\")\"\necho \"Rust exports: $(wc -l < \"$W/rs.txt\")\"\necho \"--- in C but MISSING from Rust (must be empty) ---\"\ncomm -23 \"$W/c.txt\" \"$W/rs.txt\" | tee \"$W/missing.txt\"\necho \"--- in Rust but not in C (must be empty) ---\"\ncomm -13 \"$W/c.txt\" \"$W/rs.txt\" | tee \"$W/extra.txt\"\nMISSING=$(wc -l < \"$W/missing.txt\"); EXTRA=$(wc -l < \"$W/extra.txt\")\necho \"--- undefined non-libc symbols in the Rust .so (must be empty) ---\"\nnm -D --undefined-only target/release/liblibpng.so | awk '{print $2}' | sed 's/@.*//' | sort -u \\\n  | grep -E '^png_' || echo \"(none)\"\n\necho\necho \"=== 4. feature combinations ===\"\nFEATURES=$(python3 - <<'PY'\n=== CONFIGS head ===\n# CONFIGS.md — the CONFIGURATION-SURFACE TABLE (Phase A, gates Phase B)\n\nMechanically derived from `c_src/include/png.h` (the public API), every\n`#define`d option in `c_src/include/pnglibconf.h` (they are ALL on in this\nbuild) and the `if` / `switch` branches the C actually takes in\n`c_src/src/*.c`.\n\nOne row per meaningful COMBINATION of (options set x input shape) that the C\ntreats differently.  The axes are: colour type, bit depth, interlace, filter\nselection, compression knobs, every read/write transform, every ancillary\nchunk, every entry point (including the lowest-level ones -- not just the\none-shot wrappers), every runtime option/flag, and the memory/callback hooks.\n\nPhase B drives BOTH shared objects through each row with MANY randomized inputs\n(fixed seed) and asserts byte-identical output.  A row is ticked only after it\npasses across the randomized inputs.\n\n\n## A — WRITE pipeline (`png_create_write_struct` .. `png_write_end`)\n\nCovered by `tests/t03_write.rs`, `tests/t04_chunks.rs`.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1 | png_create_write_struct, png_set_write_fn, png_set_IHDR, png_write_info, png_write_image, png_write_end | GRAY / bit_depth 1, INTERLACE_NONE, no png_set_filter (png_write_IHDR defaults do_filter=PNG_FILTER_NONE because bit_depth<8), 8x8, PLTE absent | [ ] |\n| 2 | same write pipeline | GRAY / bit_depth 2, INTERLACE_NONE, default filters -> PNG_FILTER_NONE, 8x8 | [ ] |\n| 3 | same write pipeline | GRAY / bit_depth 4, INTERLACE_NONE, default filters -> PNG_FILTER_NONE, width 7 (partial last byte) | [ ] |\n| 4 | same write pipeline | GRAY / bit_depth 8, INTERLACE_NONE, default filters -> PNG_ALL_FILTERS (bit_depth>=8, non-palette), 8x8 | [ ] |\n| 5 | same write pipeline | GRAY / bit_depth 16, INTERLACE_NONE, default PNG_ALL_FILTERS, bpp=2 in png_write_find_filter | [ ] |\n| 6 | png_set_PLTE + write pipeline | PALETTE / bit_depth 1, PLTE with exactly 2 entries, default do_filter=PNG_FILTER_NONE (palette test), zlib strategy = PNG_Z_DEFAULT_NOFILTER_STRATEGY | [ ] |\nHARNESS.md\ncommon\nt00_smoke.rs\nt01_utility.rs\nt02_rowops.rs\nt03_write.rs\nt04_chunks.rs\nt05_read.rs\nt06_progressive.rs\nt07_simplified.rs\nt08_callbacks.rs\nt10_errors_core.rs","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01UszytRUjreecfEd4AebzFf","session_id":"e3091878-9949-4689-ad83-c0c41e6641a2","uuid":"174f5e0c-e56a-433f-a35e-a25fafeaf0d0","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:51:00.672Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write progressive+simplified tests"}
