{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_6mlnxzwvtnh5l2mkcndzy5iqnqjyr6mpeyapepd6ztw7pn6yvsga","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both files are written and green. Final report:\n\n## Files created\n\n### `translation/tests/t06_progressive.rs` — progressive (push) read API — **9 tests, all PASS**\n\n| test | what it drives |\n|---|---|\n| `progressive_all_formats` | all 15 `legal_ihdr()` pairs × both interlace types × 5 sizes (1x1, 1x9, 9x1, 13x7, 32x17) × 5 feed granularities (1, 3, 7, 64 bytes, whole buffer), with gAMA/tEXt/tRNS/bKGD present. Compares the full `png_get_*` snapshot at info time (before *and* after `png_start_read_image`), every `(row bytes, row_num, pass, png_get_current_row_number, png_get_current_pass_number)` tuple, the end-callback snapshot, `Diag`, and asserts the result is granularity-independent plus a source-image round-trip. 1295+ decodes per library. |\n| `progressive_bare_and_update_info` | bare IHDR/IDAT/IEND streams, `png_read_update_info` instead of `png_start_read_image` |\n| `progressive_without_interlace_handling` | no `png_set_interlace_handling` → unexpanded per-pass rows (row length computed from `PNG_PASS_COLS`) |\n| `progressive_combine_row` | `png_progressive_combine_row` with a per-row display buffer; also checks the final blocky display reproduces the source (padding bits masked, since `png_combine_row` deliberately preserves the destination's tail bits) |\n| `process_data_pause` | `png_process_data_pause` with `save != 0` **and** `save == 0`, from the info and the end callback, at 3 granularities; verifies the returned byte count, that re-supplying the reported bytes resumes correctly, and that pausing does not change the decode |\n| `process_data_skip` | `png_process_data_skip` — fatal by default, warning with `png_set_benign_errors(1)`; return value + message compared |\n| `push_buffer_helpers` | `png_push_restore_buffer` / `png_push_fill_buffer` / `png_push_save_buffer` driven directly, including a read that straddles the save/current-buffer boundary, an over-long request, and the NULL-`png_ptr` early return |\n| `push_state_machine_direct` | `png_push_read_sig`, `png_push_read_chunk`, `png_push_read_IDAT`, `png_process_some_data` called by hand; result compared against the ordinary `png_process_data` driver |\n| `null_arguments` | documented NULL early-returns of `png_process_data`, `png_process_some_data`, `png_process_data_pause`, `png_get_progressive_ptr`, `png_set_progressive_read_fn`, `png_progressive_combine_row` |\n\n`png_push_process_row`, `png_push_have_info/_end/_row`, `png_read_push_finish_row` are covered indirectly by every flow above (`png_get_progressive_ptr` is additionally asserted inside all three callbacks).\n\n### `translation/tests/t07_simplified.rs` — simplified API — **12 tests, all PASS**\n\n`read_every_format_from_memory` (1295 cases, with non-vacuity guards: ≥95 % must decode, buffers/colormaps must actually be written), `read_every_format_with_background` (NULL and non-NULL `png_color`), `read_row_strides` (default / min / −min / +3 / −(+3) / +16 / one-too-small), `read_negative_stride_is_flipped` (proves bottom-up), `read_from_file_and_stdio` (memory ≡ file ≡ stdio), `read_colormap_without_buffer`, `write_every_format_to_memory` (size-query with `memory == NULL` + real call, `convert_to_8bit` 0/1, `flags` 0 / FAST / NOT_sRGB, colormap_entries 1/2/5/17/256), `write_to_file_and_stdio` (bytes ≡ memory form), `write_row_strides`, `write_to_memory_short_buffer`, `round_trip_read_then_write`, `simplified_error_paths` (17 recorded argument/version/junk/missing-file/no-colormap cases + `png_image_error`).\n\nAll 24 `PNG_FORMAT_*` values are covered (GRAY, GA, AG, RGB, BGR, RGBA, ARGB, BGRA, ABGR, LINEAR_Y, LINEAR_Y_ALPHA, LINEAR_RGB, LINEAR_RGB_ALPHA, plus GRAY/GA/AG/RGB/BGR/RGBA/ARGB/BGRA/ABGR/LINEAR_Y/LINEAR_RGB `_COLORMAP`). After every call the whole `png_image` (ret, `warning_or_error`, `message` text, version, w, h, format, flags, colormap_entries, `opaque == NULL`) plus the pixel buffer and the full 256-entry colormap buffer are compared. `fopen`/`fclose` are declared locally (no `libc` dev-dependency); temp files live under `std::env::temp_dir()` with per-test names and are removed.\n\n## DIVERGENCES\n\n**None found.** No test needed `#[ignore]`; the Rust translation matched C on every case in both files.\n\n## Deliberately untested (C undefined behaviour), documented in comments\n\n1. **`png_process_data_pause` from the *row* callback.** The row callback runs inside `png_process_IDAT_data`; when it returns, `png_push_read_IDAT` unconditionally executes `png_ptr->buffer_size -= save_size` on the `buffer_size` that the pause just set to 0, wrapping the `size_t`. With `idat_size == 0` this then lets `png_crc_finish` pull four bytes out of empty push buffers, i.e. uninitialised stack. The pause is therefore taken from the info and end callbacks, which libpng reaches from `png_push_read_chunk` where zeroing `buffer_size` terminates the loop cleanly.\n2. **`png_progressive_combine_row` on an interlaced image without `png_set_interlace_handling`.** `png_combine_row` degenerates to a `memcpy` of a *full* row out of a buffer holding only the pass' `iwidth` pixels → reads stale bytes.\n3. `png_process_data_skip(NULL)` — `png_app_warning` dereferences `png_ptr->flags` before any NULL check.\n\n## One non-functional behavioural note (not a value divergence)\n\nWhenever the simplified API takes an error path, the Rust cdylib's `png_safe_error` raises a Rust panic that its own (default) panic hook prints to stderr — e.g. `thread '<unnamed>' panicked at src/pngerror.rs:15:5: Box<dyn Any>` — where C libpng's `longjmp` is silent. The caught result, return values and `image.message` are identical, so no assertion was added; it is purely stderr noise from the translated library and may be worth suppressing in `src/pngerror.rs` (I did not modify `src/`).\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```\ncd translation && cargo test --offline --release --test t06_progressive   # 9 passed\ncd translation && cargo test --offline --release --test t07_simplified    # 12 passed\n```\nNothing under `tests/common/`, the other test files, or `c_src/` was modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1347,"cache_read_input_tokens":230759,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1347,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01UszytRUjreecfEd4AebzFf","session_id":"e3091878-9949-4689-ad83-c0c41e6641a2","uuid":"0d1d4e1d-ecef-4bdb-b53d-ae82f6cd3eae","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:51:42.731Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write progressive+simplified tests"}
