HA, LINEAR_RGB, LINEAR_RGB_ALPHA, plus GRAY/GA/AG/RGB/BGR/RGBA/ARGB/BGRA/ABGR/LINEAR_Y/LINEAR_RGB `_COLORMAP`). After every call the whole `png_image` (ret, `warning_or_error`, `message` text, version, w, h, format, flags, colormap_entries, `opaque == NULL`) plus the pixel buffer and the full 256-entry colormap buffer are compared. `fopen`/`fclose` are declared locally (no `libc` dev-dependency); temp files live under `std::env::temp_dir()` with per-test names and are removed.\n\n## DIVERGENCES\n\n**None found.** No test needed `#[ignore]`; the Rust translation matched C on every case in both files.\n\n## Deliberately untested (C undefined behaviour), documented in comments\n\n1. **`png_process_data_pause` from the *row* callback.** The row callback runs inside `png_process_IDAT_data`; when it returns, `png_push_read_IDAT` unconditionally executes `png_ptr->buffer_size -= save_size` on the `buffer_size` that the pause just set to 0, wrapping the `size_t`. With `idat_size == 0` this then lets `png_crc_finish` pull four bytes out of empty push buffers, i.e. uninitialised stack. The pause is therefore taken from the info and end callbacks, which libpng reaches from `png_push_read_chunk` where zeroing `buffer_size` terminates the loop cleanly.\n2. **`png_progressive_combine_row` on an interlaced image without `png_set_interlace_handling`.** `png_combine_row` degenerates to a `memcpy` of a *full* row out of a buffer holding only the pass' `iwidth` pixels → reads stale bytes.\n3. `png_process_data_skip(NULL)` — `png_app_warning` dereferences `png_ptr->flags` before any NULL check.\n\n## One non-functional behavioural note (not a value divergence)\n\nWhenever the simplified API takes an error path, the Rust cdylib's `png_safe_error` raises a Rust panic that its own (default) panic hook prints to stderr — e.g. `thread '<unnamed>' panicked at src/pngerror.rs:15:5: Box<dyn Any>` — where C libpng's `longjmp` is silent. The caught result, return values and `image.message` are i