{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ehggdserrrgadawdfjzwg6ttgylib4etlykmnehjsuk6e5geqhza","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `translation/tests/t04_chunks.rs` (3602 lines, 30 tests) is written and **all 30 tests pass**; the rest of the suite (t00–t10) still passes too, and nothing outside that one new file was touched.\n\n## Result of the final run\n\n```\ncargo test --offline --release --test t04_chunks\ntest result: ok. 30 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored\n```\n\n## No divergences found\n\n**There are zero `// DIVERGENCE:` findings.** Every one of the ~4,400 write+read round-trips (≈8,800 full pipeline runs) and the 4,000-case arithmetic fuzz produced byte-identical PNG streams, identical `Diag` (warnings *and* errors, in order), and identical values from every getter — including all out-parameters, strings, byte arrays, `f64`/`f32` bit patterns and `png_get_valid` masks.\n\nThe two failures I hit while iterating were both **bugs in my own probe**, not in the Rust translation (details in the \"Deliberately untested\" section below).\n\n## Test functions\n\n| Test | Covers |\n|---|---|\n`sanity_chunks_really_round_trip` | self-check: asserts every chunk tag really reaches the byte stream and comes back out (guards against the suite silently no-op'ing)\n`palette_max_and_invalid_index` | `png_get_palette_max` + `png_set_check_for_invalid_index`, with an asserted non-trivial tracked maximum\n`ihdr_and_basic_accessors` | `png_get_IHDR`/`_PLTE`/`_bit_depth`/`_color_type`/`_channels`/`_rowbytes`/`_image_width`/`_image_height`/`_interlace_type`/`_compression_type`/`_filter_type`/`_signature`/`_valid`\n`chunk_gAMA` | `png_set_gAMA`/`_fixed`, `png_get_gAMA`/`_fixed`\n`chunk_cHRM` | all four setters + all four getters (`cHRM`, `_fixed`, `_XYZ`, `_XYZ_fixed`)\n`chunk_sRGB` | `png_set_sRGB`, `png_set_sRGB_gAMA_and_cHRM`, `png_get_sRGB`\n`chunk_iCCP` | real 132+-byte profiles (6 sizes × 4 intents), all 8 ICC device classes / PCS encodings, wrong colour space, out-of-range intents, 16 short/garbage profiles, bad compression methods and invalid keywords\n`chunk_sBIT`, `chunk_PLTE`, `chunk_bKGD`, `chunk_hIST` | boundary + randomized values\n`chunk_tRNS` | all three colour-type forms (palette alpha array, grey value, RGB triple) plus the alpha-channel rejection\n`chunk_hIST_reordered` | byte-stream surgery to reach `png_handle_hIST`'s body\n`chunk_pHYs` | `png_get_pHYs`, `_dpi`, `x/y_pixels_per_meter`, `pixels_per_meter`, `x/y_pixels_per_inch`, `pixels_per_inch`, `pixel_aspect_ratio`(+`_fixed`)\n`chunk_oFFs` | `png_get_oFFs` + `x/y_offset_pixels`/`_microns`/`_inches`(+`_fixed`)\n`chunk_sCAL` | `png_set_sCAL`/`_fixed`/`_s` × `png_get_sCAL`/`_fixed`/`_s`, incl. malformed fp strings and overflow\n`chunk_pCAL` | all 4 equation types + out-of-range types, 0..4 params, malformed fp params, bad keywords, `X0 == X1`\n`chunk_tIME` | valid + every field out of range; both before IDAT and via `png_write_end`\n`chunk_text` | `png_set_text`/`png_set_text_2`/`png_get_text` with **every** `PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_*`/`PNG_ITXT_COMPRESSION_*` value plus out-of-range ones; multi-entry, NULL key/text, `num_text <= 0`; before and after IDAT\n`chunk_sPLT` | depths 8/16, 0..17 entries, invalid depths/keywords, multi-palette calls\n`chunk_eXIf` | `png_set_eXIf_1`/`png_get_eXIf_1` (+ the deprecated `png_set_eXIf`/`png_get_eXIf` warning), valid `II*\\0`/`MM\\0*` headers and invalid ones, before and after IDAT\n`chunk_cICP`, `chunk_cLLI`, `chunk_mDCV` | both fixed and floating setters/getters, incl. the `> 0x7FFFFFFF` and ITU-range rejections\n`chunk_unknown` | `png_set_unknown_chunks` × 6 locations × 6 names × 4 sizes, `png_set_unknown_chunk_location` (in- and out-of-range indices, 10 location values), `png_get_unknown_chunks`, location 0\n`keep_unknown_chunks_and_handle_as_unknown` | `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks` with every `PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_*` (+ `-1`, `99`), 7 chunk-list shapes, layered/reset calls, `png_handle_as_unknown` on 10 probe names\n`keep_unknown_chunks_on_read` | the same driving a real read, incl. `num_chunks_in < 0` (libpng's built-in ignore-all-known list — verified to route `gAMA` etc. through `png_handle_unknown`)\n`free_data_and_data_freer` | every `PNG_FREE_*` mask × every `PNG_DATA_FREER`/`PNG_*_WILL_FREE_DATA` value (+ invalid `4`/`-1`), with a full getter probe before, after, and after a second (idempotence) free\n`fuzz_fixed_and_floating_point_conversions` | 4,000 randomized cases across 6 magnitude bands through `png_fixed`/`png_float`/`png_muldiv`/`png_XYZ_from_xy`/`png_xy_from_XYZ`/`png_ascii_from_fp`/`atof`/`ppi_from_ppm` — 56,000 compared records and 6,179 warnings/errors spanning 8 distinct messages, all matching\n`all_chunks_at_once` | one PNG carrying every ancillary chunk, round-tripped per base image\n\nBase images: `GRAY@8`, `PALETTE@4`, `RGB@8`, `RGB_ALPHA@16`, `GRAY_ALPHA@8`. Every call that can `png_error` goes through `guard(...)`.\n\n## Two C-tree quirks worth flagging (both libraries agree — not divergences)\n\n1. **`hIST` can never round-trip in this tree.** `png_write_info` emits hIST *after* PLTE, but the read-side chunk table in `pngrutil.c` gives hIST `pos_before = PNG_HAVE_PLTE`, so it is always rejected with `\"hIST: out of place\"`. Moving it before PLTE (which `chunk_hIST_reordered` does) then fails the `num != png_ptr->num_palette` check, since `num_palette` is still 0. `png_handle_hIST`'s success path is therefore unreachable. Documented in a comment.\n2. **Small `iCCP` chunks are rejected as `\"too short\"`.** `png_handle_iCCP` reads up to 81 bytes into its keyword buffer and then requires the *remaining* length to be ≥ `LZ77Min` (11), so any iCCP chunk under ~92 bytes fails regardless of validity. The test's ICC profiles are filled with an incompressible pattern so the valid ones actually survive; the small ones still cover the rejection path.\n\n## Deliberately untested (C undefined behaviour, noted in comments in the file)\n\n- `png_get_sCAL`/`_fixed`/`_s`, `png_get_oFFs`, `png_get_PLTE`, `png_get_pCAL`, `png_get_eXIf_1` dereference some out-pointers without a NULL check → only called with non-NULL out-params.\n- `png_get_iCCP` unconditionally reads the profile's first 4 bytes and reports that as `proflen`; on a write struct the app supplies buffer and length independently, so no profile under 4 bytes is stored, and the profile body is only dumped after a *read* (where `png_handle_iCCP` has proven `proflen` == buffer size). **This was my first failure** — a genuine heap over-read in my probe, not a translation bug.\n- `png_free_data(.., PNG_FREE_TEXT|_SPLT|_UNKN, num)` with `num != -1` frees `text[num].key` but leaves `text[num].text` (same allocation) and `num_text` untouched, so any later `png_get_text` is a use-after-free → those masks use `num == -1` only. **This was my second failure**, again my probe rather than the translation.\n- `png_set_text_2` with `compression > 0` and NULL `lang`/`lang_key` reaches `memcpy(dst, NULL, 0)` → iTXt entries always carry non-NULL language strings.\n- `png_set_hIST` reads `info_ptr->num_palette` entries regardless of the caller's buffer → always passed a 256-entry buffer."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1223,"cache_read_input_tokens":289505,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1223,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01US2dipoeTMiontFWYLFvv8","session_id":"e3091878-9949-4689-ad83-c0c41e6641a2","uuid":"5f3dd3c9-94c2-4eba-a73f-f0ccf608c92d","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:52:47.373Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write chunk round-trip tests"}
