{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ucnhtvxbcvootbphldfhppbjosmwhbnua7g6hlq3g6nldyosfh4q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `translation/tests/t13_errors_write.rs` is the only file created; nothing else was touched.\n\n## Status: GREEN — 20 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored\n\n`cd translation && cargo test --offline --release --test t13_errors_write -- --test-threads=1` → `20 passed; 0 failed`.\n~6,100 differential cases total (each runs both `.so`s and compares return value + error/no-error + full `Diag` text, and for write-session probes also the exact bytes emitted before the abort and the flush count).\n\n## `#[test]` functions and approximate case counts\n\n| test fn | cases | ERRORS.md rows |\n|---|---|---|\n| `write_pipeline_ordering` | 69 | 976–979, 983, 984, 988, 989, 991, 992, 997–999, 1021–1024, 1026, 1128 |\n| `cross_struct_calls` | 11 | write fns on a read struct / read fns on a write struct |\n| `write_sig_and_ihdr` | 1988 | 1071–1079 |\n| `write_plte_rejections` | 210 | 1080–1082 |\n| `chunk_framing_rejections` | 30 | 1053–1058 + IEND twice |\n| `chunk_writer_rejections_simple` | 218 | 1086, 1105, 1116, 1119–1121 + gAMA/cHRM/cICP/cLLI/mDCV/eXIf |\n| `chunk_writer_rejections_sbit_trns_bkgd` | 1160 | 1095–1104 |\n| `chunk_writer_rejections_pcal_splt` | 546 | 1094, 1117, 1118 |\n| `compression_parameter_rejections` | 175 | 1005–1020, 1064, 1083–1085 + `png_set_compression_buffer_size` |\n| `filter_rejections` | 399 | 1000–1004, 1122 + the deprecated heuristics setters |\n| `check_keyword_rejections` | 27 | `png_check_keyword` (all invalid keyword forms) |\n| `text_rejections` | 297 | 1106, 1108–1112 + `png_set_text`/`_2` |\n| `icc_check_length_rejections` | 126 | 956, 957 |\n| `icc_check_header_rejections` | 90 | 958–972 + `PNG_SKIP_sRGB_CHECK_PROFILE` |\n| `icc_check_tag_table_rejections` | 30 | 973, 974 |\n| `write_iccp_rejections` | 111 | 1087–1093 (also via `png_set_iCCP` + `png_write_info`) |\n| `simplified_write_to_memory_rejections` | 33 | 1029–1042, 1035 |\n| `simplified_write_to_file_and_stdio_rejections` | 30 | 1043–1052 |\n| `row_transform_rejections` | 362 | 1124, 1128 |\n| `write_unknown_chunk_rejections` | 210 | 975 |\n\n## DIVERGENCES: none\n\nZero `#[ignore]`, zero `// DIVERGENCE:`. The Rust library matched C on every case, including exact `strerror` text (`\"No such file or directory\"`, `\"Is a directory\"`), the chunk-prefixed ICC warning format (`\"[00][00][00][00]: profile 'test profile': 'RGB ': RGB color space not permitted on grayscale PNG\"`), and byte-for-byte deflate output. The minimal well-formed ICC profile is accepted (all three checkers return 1) by both.\n\n## Cases dropped as C undefined behaviour\n\nEach is documented inline with a `NOTE (C UB, dropped)` comment and the C file:line. Four were found empirically (crashed the harness); the rest by source inspection.\n\n1. **`png_write_data(NULL, data, len)`** — pngwio.c:34 loads `png_ptr->write_data_fn` with no NULL guard. *Confirmed SIGSEGV.*\n2. **`png_read_row` / `png_read_image` on a write struct** — pngread.c:288-302, no \"is-read-struct\" guard; `png_read_start_row` sets `row_buf = big_row_buf + 32`, and the later `png_destroy_write_struct` `free()`s that interior pointer. *Confirmed glibc `free(): invalid pointer` abort.*\n3. **`png_image_write_*` with `image->width == 0`** — pngwrite.c:2044 evaluates `image->height > 0xffffffffU/png_row_stride` with `png_row_stride == 0` → integer division by zero / SIGFPE.\n4. **`png_image_write_*` with `row_stride == i32::MAX` or `i32::MIN`** — passes the guards at pngwrite.c:2038-2049 then walks the buffer in 2 GB steps (pngwrite.c:2166/2216). *Confirmed SIGSEGV.*\n5. **`png_write_image(png, NULL)` / `png_write_rows(png, NULL, n>0)`** — `*rp` is dereferenced in the caller at pngwrite.c:641 / 672. (`png_write_rows(png, NULL, 0)` *is* tested.)\n6. **`png_write_row(png, NULL)`** — `memcpy(row_buf+1, row, rowbytes)`, pngwrite.c:890.\n7. **`png_write_sig(NULL)`** — reads `png_ptr->sig_bytes`, pngwutil.c:78.\n8. **`png_write_chunk_start`/`png_write_chunk` with a NULL chunk name** — `PNG_CHUNK_FROM_STRING` loads all four bytes in the caller (pngwutil.c:131/215) before the callee's NULL check.\n9. **`png_write_PLTE(png, NULL, n)` with an in-range `n`** — `pal_ptr->red`, pngwutil.c:898.\n10. **`png_write_cHRM_fixed(png, NULL)`** — `xy->whitex`, pngwutil.c:1300.\n11. **`png_write_sBIT(png, NULL, ct)`** — `sbit->red`, pngwutil.c:1250.\n12. **`png_write_bKGD(png, NULL, ct)` / `png_write_tRNS(..., NULL, ...)`** — pngwutil.c:1400 / 1343.\n13. **`png_write_tIME(png, NULL)`** — `mod_time->month`, pngwutil.c:1908.\n14. **`png_write_sCAL_s` with NULL width/height** — `strlen(NULL)`, pngwutil.c:1852-1853.\n15. **`png_write_pCAL` with NULL `units`, or NULL `params` and `nparams > 0`** — pngwutil.c:1806 / 1818.\n16. **`png_write_sPLT(png, NULL)`** — `spalette->depth`, pngwutil.c:1180. (A NULL *name* is fine and is tested — `png_check_keyword` handles it.)\n17. **`png_check_keyword(png, NULL, NULL)`** — `*new_key = 0` before any check, pngset.c:1994.\n18. **`png_icc_check_*` with a NULL `name`** (walked by `png_safecat` in `png_icc_profile_error`, png.c:1546) or a NULL `profile` (`png_get_uint_32(profile+128)`, png.c:1802).\n19. **`png_do_write_interlace` with a negative `pass`** — indexes `png_pass_start[pass]` out of bounds (pngwutil.c:2117-2118); the out-of-bounds static read differs between builds.\n20. **`png_do_write_transformations(png, NULL)`** — `row_info->color_type`, pngwtran.c:507. (The NULL-`png_ptr` half, row 1128, *is* tested.)\n\n## Rows documented as unreachable in this build (not testable, explained in the file header)\n\n`pnglibconf.h` has **no** `PNG_BENIGN_WRITE_ERRORS_SUPPORTED` and `PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_BASE_TYPE == BETA`, so on a *write* struct `png_benign_error`, `png_app_warning` and `png_app_error` are all hard `png_error`s — that is what most of these rows actually observe. Every write transform and chunk writer is compiled in, so rows **980, 981, 982, 986, 993, 1002, 1025** (\"… is not defined\" / \"… not supported\") can never fire. Also unreachable: the `size > ZLIB_IO_MAX` branch of `png_set_compression_buffer_size` (the `> PNG_UINT_31_MAX` `png_error` fires first), and rows **1107, 1113, 1115, 1123** which need a >2 GB string / row.\n\nTwo extra debugging hooks mirror the existing `PNGTRACE` convention: `PNGTRACE=1` prints each case label, `PNGDUMP=1` prints the C-side result of every case."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":232,"cache_read_input_tokens":288722,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":232,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Q6dhGaVGZZaCU4yoFW14FN","session_id":"e3091878-9949-4689-ad83-c0c41e6641a2","uuid":"0724b999-28bc-4353-ab98-b281668bcdb9","timestamp":"2026-08-31T14:07:27.435Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Error tests: write + rutil paths"}
