{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_p2rmj6davt7bzpoxpby6uvpruhzbitycfxtqrevl6jpw4mexkega","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01WqEUg42sAoPRKCbCxZqrWL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"R=/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-kk7Dev; cd $R/translation && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nbody=open('../.work/configs_body.md').read().splitlines()\ntitles={\n 'A write':'A — WRITE pipeline (`png_create_write_struct` .. `png_write_end`)',\n 'B read':'B — sequential READ pipeline (`png_create_read_struct` .. `png_read_end`)',\n 'C progressive':'C — PROGRESSIVE read (`png_set_progressive_read_fn` / `png_process_data`)',\n 'D simplified':'D — SIMPLIFIED API (`png_image_*`)',\n 'E utility':'E — low-level / \"pure\" entry points',\n 'F memory':'F — memory management and application callbacks',\n}\ncovered_by={\n 'A write':'`tests/t03_write.rs`, `tests/t04_chunks.rs`, `tests/t09_internals.rs`',\n 'B read':'`tests/t05_read.rs`, `tests/t04_chunks.rs`, `tests/t09_internals.rs`',\n 'C progressive':'`tests/t06_progressive.rs`',\n 'D simplified':'`tests/t07_simplified.rs`, `tests/t09_internals.rs`',\n 'E utility':'`tests/t01_utility.rs`, `tests/t02_rowops.rs`, `tests/t09_internals.rs`',\n 'F memory':'`tests/t08_callbacks.rs`',\n}\nhdr = \"\"\"# CONFIGS.md — the CONFIGURATION-SURFACE TABLE (Phase A, gates Phase B)\n\nMechanically derived from `c_src/include/png.h` (the public API), the `#define`s\nin `c_src/include/pnglibconf.h`, and the `if` / `switch` / `#ifdef` branches the\nC actually takes in `c_src/src/*.c`.\n\nOne row per meaningful COMBINATION of (options set x input shape) that the C\ntreats differently, pruned to the combinations the code really distinguishes.\nThe axes are: colour type, bit depth, interlace, filter selection, compression\nknobs, every read/write transform, every ancillary chunk, every entry point\n(including the lowest-level ones, not just the one-shot wrappers), every runtime\noption/flag, and the memory/callback hooks.\n\nPhase B drives BOTH shared objects through each row with many randomized inputs\n(fixed seed) and asserts byte-identical output; a row is ticked only after it\npasses across those inputs.\n\n## Build-specific facts that shaped this table\n\nDerived from `pnglibconf.h` and the sources, and important when reading the rows:\n\n* `png_set_filter_heuristics` / `png_set_filter_heuristics_fixed` are\n  `PNG_UNUSED`-only stubs in this build and `png_write_find_filter` contains no\n  weighted-filter code, so those axes collapse to \"must have no observable\n  effect\".\n* `png_set_filter`'s trailing `do_filter = filters` overwrites its own\n  `PNG_FILTER_VALUE_*` switch, so passing 0..4 yields unfiltered rows rather\n  than the named filter.\n* `PNG_DISABLE_ADLER32_CHECK_SUPPORTED` is OFF, so `PNG_IGNORE_ADLER32` is not\n  `#define`d, and `PNG_SKIP_sRGB_CHECK_PROFILE` is unreferenced in the sources:\n  `PNG_MAXIMUM_INFLATE_WINDOW` is the only functional `png_set_option`.\n* `PNG_BENIGN_WRITE_ERRORS_SUPPORTED` is OFF and this is a BETA build\n  (`PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_BASE_TYPE == BETA`), so `png_app_error` / `png_app_warning`\n  / `png_benign_error` are FATAL by default on a write struct, and app errors are\n  fatal on a read struct too.  `png_set_benign_errors` is therefore a first-class\n  axis: it is the one flag that changes control flow (not just severity) inside\n  `png_handle_iCCP`.\n* `png_process_data_skip` is a warn-and-return-0 stub, and the progressive\n  reader hard-codes `display = 1`, so the \"sparkle\" combine path is unreachable.\n\"\"\"\nout=[hdr]\nn=0\ncounts={}\ncur=None\nfor line in body:\n    line=line.rstrip()\n    if line.startswith('<!-- SECTION:'):\n        cur=line.split(':',1)[1].replace('-->','').strip()\n        counts[cur]=0\n        out.append(\"\\n## %s\\n\"%titles.get(cur,cur))\n        out.append(\"Covered by %s.\\n\"%covered_by.get(cur,'the suite'))\n        out.append(\"| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\")\n        out.append(\"|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\")\n        continue\n    if line.startswith('| |'):\n        n+=1; counts[cur]=counts.get(cur,0)+1\n        b=line[3:].rstrip()\n        if b.endswith('|'): b=b[:-1].rstrip()\n        out.append(\"| %d |%s | [ ] |\"%(n,b))\nopen('CONFIGS.md','w').write('\\n'.join(out)+'\\n')\nprint(\"rows:\",n,counts)\nPYEOF\ngrep -c '^| [0-9]' CONFIGS.md","description":"Regenerate CONFIGS.md from final body"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":493,"cache_read_input_tokens":453677,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":493,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e3091878-9949-4689-ad83-c0c41e6641a2","uuid":"41893102-62f2-4720-8779-4aecc8b7d863","timestamp":"2026-08-31T14:09:47.881Z"}
