{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_kr7qifmzocku2up26nfe73ugoihh2dn5vgqchvpfkczharve2nkq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Created `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-kk7Dev/translation/tests/t11_errors_setget.rs` (5235 lines, 69 `#[test]` functions, **7481 differential `same!` cases**). Nothing else was modified; my throwaway scratch test file was deleted.\n\n## Status: **GREEN — 69 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored**\n\n```\ncd translation && timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test t11_errors_setget -- --test-threads=1\ntest result: ok. 69 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored\n```\n`t10_errors_core` still passes (20/20), so nothing shared was disturbed.\n\n## `#[test]` functions and case counts\n\n`pngget.c` (rows 287–409) — 25 tests, ~470 cases:\n`get_valid_rejections` 144 · `get_scalar_null_guards` 12 · `get_phys_rejections` 43 · `get_offs_rejections` 33 · `get_signature_rejections` 5 · `get_bkgd_rejections` 5 · `get_chrm_rejections` 13 · `get_gama_rejections` 5 · `get_srgb_rejections` 14 · `get_iccp_rejections` 5 · `get_splt_rejections` 5 · `get_cicp_rejections` 5 · `get_clli_rejections` 5 · `get_mdcv_rejections` 5 · `get_exif_rejections` 5 · `get_hist_rejections` 5 · `get_ihdr_rejections` 13 · `get_pcal_rejections` 5 · `get_scal_rejections` 12 · `get_plte_rejections` 5 · `get_sbit_rejections` 5 · `get_text_rejections` 5 · `get_time_rejections` 5 · `get_trns_rejections` 85 · `get_unknown_chunks_rejections` 5\n\n`pngset.c` (rows 410–529) — 30 tests, ~3450 cases:\n`set_bkgd` 8 · `set_chrm` 146 · `set_cicp` 604 · `set_clli` 218 · `set_mdcv` 308 · `set_exif` 14 · `set_gama` 25 · `set_hist` 15 · `set_ihdr_setget` 10 · `set_offs` 15 · `set_pcal` 258 · `set_scal` 191 · `set_phys` 14 · `set_plte` 516 · `set_sbit` 50 · `set_srgb` 40 · `set_iccp` 51 · `set_text` 137 · `set_time` 31 · `set_trns` 164 · `set_splt` 71 · `set_unknown_chunks` 88 · `set_unknown_chunk_location` 146 · `permit_mng_features` 23 · `set_keep_unknown_chunks` 287 · `set_read_user_chunk_fn` 3 · `set_rows` 6 · `set_compression_buffer_size` 29 · `set_invalid` 16 · `set_user_limits` 70 · `check_keyword` 563\n\n`pngtrans.c` (rows 530–568) — 10 tests, ~1730 cases:\n`trans_setter_null_guards` 26 · `trans_setter_gating` 780 · `do_invert` 72 · `do_swap` 40 · `do_packswap` 12 · `do_strip_channel` 320 · `do_bgr` 81 · `do_check_palette_indexes` 96 · `set_user_transform_info` 165 · `rtran_ordering_rejections` 142\n\nExtra (task brief, lives in `pngwrite.c`) — 3 tests, 1181 cases: `set_filter_rejections` 923 · `set_filter_heuristics_rejections` 126 · `set_compression_rejections` 132\n\n## Key technique: forced out-of-memory\nEvery OOM row (431, 436, 444–447, 452, 453, 469, 470, 474, 478, 491, 493–495, 501, 502) is reached with a **budget allocator** installed via `png_set_mem_fn` that fails the *N*th and every later allocation. I verified both libraries produce byte-identical diagnostics at each allocation site — including all four distinct pCAL messages (\"purpose\"/\"units\"/\"params\"/\"parameter\") — meaning the Rust translation's allocation *count and ordering* matches C exactly.\n\nI also verified out-of-band that the intended messages really fire (not vacuous parity): `fixed point overflow ignored`, `Invalid IHDR data`, `fixed point overflow in sCAL width`, `invalid cHRM XYZ`, `Invalid cICP matrix coefficients`, `cLLI light level exceeds PNG limit`, `mDCV chromaticities outside representable range`, `mDCV display light level exceeds PNG limit`, `Invalid palette size, hIST allocation skipped`, `Invalid pCAL equation type/parameter count/format`, `Invalid sCAL unit/width`, `Invalid sCAL width ignored`, `Invalid palette length`, `Invalid palette`, `Invalid iCCP compression method`, `text compression mode is out of range`, `png_set_unknown_chunks now expects a valid location` + `invalid location in png_set_unknown_chunks`, `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks: invalid keep / no chunk list / too many chunks`, `invalid compression buffer size`, `Compression buffer size cannot be reduced below 6`, `keyword truncated`, `keyword \"…\": bad character '0x01'`, `png_set_shift: invalid shift values`, `png_set_filler is invalid for low bit depth gray output`, `png_set_filler: inappropriate color type`, `info change after png_start_read_image or png_read_update_info`, `invalid after png_start_read_image or png_read_update_info`, `Unknown custom filter method`, `Unknown row filter for method 0`.\n\n## Cases dropped as C UB (each confirmed to segfault the **C** reference library)\n1. `png_get_PLTE` with `num_palette == NULL` while `PNG_INFO_PLTE` is set — `pngget.c:1140` stores through it; only `palette` is checked at `:1137`.\n2. `png_get_eXIf_1` with `num_exif == NULL` while `PNG_INFO_eXIf` is set — `pngget.c:910`; only `exif` is checked at `:908`.\n3. `png_get_sCAL_s` with NULL out-params while sCAL is valid — `pngget.c:1085-1087`.\n4. `png_get_sCAL_fixed` with NULL out-params while sCAL is valid — `pngget.c:1042-1049`.\n5. `png_get_sCAL` (double) with NULL out-params while sCAL is valid — `pngget.c:1067-1069`.\n6. `png_do_check_palette_indexes` on a `png_struct` with `row_buf == NULL` — `pngtrans.c:742`. The test therefore performs a real `png_write_row` first so `row_buf` exists; rows 562/563 are still fully covered.\n\nAlso, in `set_filter_rejections` I stop the write once a setter has raised `png_error`, because continuing is undefined by the libpng contract — and the C crashes: `png_set_filter(BASE, PNG_FILTER_UP)` mid-write stores the new mask at `pngwrite.c:1096` (switch `default:`) and *then* longjmps from the `png_app_warning` at `pngwrite.c:1141`, before `pngwrite.c:1143` masks UP/AVG/PAETH back out. `do_filter` is left as `UP` with `prev_row`/`try_row` still NULL, so the next `png_write_row` NULL-derefs in `png_write_find_filter`. This is documented in a comment at the call site.\n\n## Rows unreachable in this build configuration (documented in comments, not tested)\n- 477 `iTXt chunk not supported` — `PNG_iTXt_SUPPORTED` is defined, so `pngset.c:1061-1066` is not compiled.\n- 499 / 500 `no unknown chunk support on read/write` — both `PNG_{READ,WRITE}_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS_SUPPORTED` are defined (`pngset.c:1440-1445`, `:1449-1454`).\n- 517 `Compression buffer size limited to system maximum` — `ZLIB_IO_MAX` is `UINT_MAX` but `pngset.c:1804` already rejects everything above `PNG_UINT_31_MAX`, so `size > ZLIB_IO_MAX` is unreachable on this platform.\n- 543 / 546 `png_set_filler not supported on read/write` — both `PNG_{READ,WRITE}_FILLER_SUPPORTED` are defined (`pngtrans.c:171-173`, `:213-215`).\n\n## DIVERGENCES: **none**\nThe Rust re-implementation matched the C ground truth on every one of the 7481 cases — identical return values, identical out-parameter writes (including \"did not write\" vs \"wrote 0\", detected via pre-filled sentinels such as `0xdeadbeef`, `-12345`, and a `0x1` poison pointer), and identical warning/error message text and ordering. No `#[test]` needed `#[ignore]`.\n\nOne implementation note for future readers: because `png_error(NULL, …)` reaches `png_default_error` → `png_longjmp(NULL)` → `PNG_ABORT()` (process abort, not a catchable error), the tests deliberately pass only in-range values to `png_set_cHRM`/`_XYZ`/`png_set_gAMA`/`png_set_cLLI`/`png_set_mDCV` when `png_ptr == NULL`; the out-of-range/overflow variants of those rows are exercised with a real `png_ptr`. This is called out in a comment in `set_chrm_rejections`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":421,"cache_read_input_tokens":370234,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":421,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01K4AzBRHbaoF5qTYNXeCbTr","session_id":"e3091878-9949-4689-ad83-c0c41e6641a2","uuid":"3e34d12c-d255-487a-adbf-7d3984108063","timestamp":"2026-08-31T14:15:30.829Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Error tests: pngset/pngget/pngtrans"}
