{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ltuf4b337yx3sbrlhkp4fxrtzoq7ccxbzqlpmr63u576ntpfkccq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `translation/tests/t12_errors_read.rs` (140 KB, new file — nothing else was modified by me).\n\n## Final status\n\n`cd translation && cargo test --offline --release --test t12_errors_read -- --test-threads=1`\n→ **32 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored** (1.7 s). **9,285 differential cases** = 18,570 library invocations, each comparing (return value, error-or-not, full `Diag`) plus a hash of every observable field and every decoded row byte.\n\n## `#[test]` functions and case counts\n\n| cases | test | ERRORS.md rows |\n|---|---|---|\n| 24 | `create_read_struct_rejections` | 569 |\n| 30 | `null_pointer_guards` | 570,574,576,592,594,597,601-603,751,752,754,755,772,783-786 |\n| 816 | `out_of_order_calls` | 575,577,593,595 (7 init × 7 row-mode × ihand × 8 streams) |\n| 6 | `row_calls_before_read_info` | 588 |\n| 228 | `truncation_sequential` | every chunk boundary + spread of byte offsets, 4 formats |\n| 156 | `truncation_progressive` | same, gran 1/5/all |\n| 84 | `bad_signature` | 757,758 |\n| 163 | `crc_action_matrix` | 693-696 (9×9 crit/ancil incl. -1/6/999 × critical+ancillary broken CRC) |\n| 68 | `crc_corruption_every_chunk` | per-chunk CRC corruption, seq + progressive |\n| 375 | `ihdr_field_corruption` | zero/huge w+h, all bd/ct, comp/filt/il, bad+lying IHDR length, 578/579,764 |\n| 75 | `chunk_order_errors` | 571-573,599,600,760-763; dup IHDR/PLTE/IDAT/IEND, PLTE after IDAT, missing PLTE/IEND, empty PLTE ±MNG, IDAT-as-unknown, data after IEND (756) |\n| 76 | `chunk_header_errors` | non-alphabetic names, lengths past EOF / >2^31 |\n| 1071 | `ancillary_chunk_lengths` | all 21 ancillary chunks × 12 lengths × before/after IDAT × 2 colour types + progressive |\n| 400 | `idat_zlib_corruption` | 767,773-778: bad CMF/FLG, ADLER32, truncated/extra deflate, empty/short/long raw, IDAT split 1/2/3/7/1000, zero-length IDATs, ±IGNORE_ADLER32 |\n| 112 | `bad_filter_bytes` | 589,779 (filter 0-255, first and second row) |\n| 284 | `read_png_transform_masks` | 603,604 + all 18 transform flags + unknown/oversized masks |\n| 122 | `rtran_ok_gating` | 697-704,708,712,713,716,721-727 (15 setters × 8 call sites incl. write struct) |\n| 255 | `gamma_value_rejections` | 705-707,716-720 |\n| 110 | `alpha_mode_rejections` | 709-711 (incl. \"conflicting calls…\", both orders) |\n| 640 | `background_gamma_type_rejections` | 701,736 |\n| 630 | `rgb_to_gray_rejections` | 727,728,730,731,748,749 |\n| 7 | `rgb_to_gray_float_overflow` | see divergence below |\n| 122 | `quantize_argument_rejections` | 712-715 |\n| 46 | `user_limit_rejections` | user limits < image, chunk cache max, chunk malloc max |\n| 64 | `progressive_misuse` | 751-756,762,783-785 (pause save modes, skip, no interlace handling, combine) |\n| 60 | `progressive_malformed_streams` | 757-768,779 at gran 1/2/9/all |\n| 33 | `user_transform_row_size_errors` | 590,591,780,781 |\n| 9 | `transform_init_errors` | 746,747 |\n| 298 | `palette_index_and_shift_errors` | 598,737-745,750 |\n| 54 + 2767 | `simplified_read_begin_rejections`, `simplified_read_finish_rejections` | 620,625-640,645-657,687-692 |\n| 100 | `out_of_range_enum_values` | filler loc, keep, benign, check-index, option, mng features, pause save, interlace handling, read_png mask: -1/0/LAST/LAST+1/999/i32::MIN/i32::MAX |\n\n## DIVERGENCE found — `png_set_rgb_to_gray` (float entry point)\n\nC: `png_error \"fixed point overflow in rgb to gray green coefficient\"`; Rust (originally): `…red coefficient`. Inputs: read struct after `png_read_info`, `error_action=1`, `red=green=1e30` (also 1e300, `f64::MAX`, -1e30, 21475.0). Cause: `pngrtran.c:1122-1125` passes the two `png_fixed()` conversions as arguments of one call — unspecified evaluation order in C; gcc/x86-64 evaluates right-to-left so *green* errors first, Rust evaluates left-to-right.\n\n**Important:** I originally left the assertion in place and marked that one test `#[ignore]` with a `// DIVERGENCE:` block, as instructed — I did not touch `src/`. While my run was in flight, **another agent working concurrently in this same workspace edited `src/pngrtran_a.rs` (14:22) to bind the two conversions in gcc's order, and removed my `#[ignore]` / rewrote my comment**. The test therefore now passes and is enabled; the comment records the full divergence and that the Rust was changed by that other change (`tests/t14_argorder.rs`, same timestamp, appears to be its test).\n\n## Cases dropped as C undefined behaviour (each documented in-file at the drop site)\n\n- `png_set_read_user_transform_fn(NULL, fn)` — `pngrtran.c:1139` writes `png_ptr->transformations` with no NULL check. Verified SIGSEGV in both.\n- `png_process_data_skip(NULL)` — `pngpread.c:99` calls `png_app_warning`, which reads `png_ptr->flags` unconditionally.\n- `png_set_quantize` with `maximum_colors < 1` (and `num_palette > maximum_colors`, no histogram) — `while (num_new_palette > maximum_colors)` at `pngrtran.c:693` can never terminate (`num_new_palette` bottoms out at 1) while `max_d += 96` (`pngrtran.c:806`) makes `for (i = 0; i <= max_d; i++) hash[i]` (`pngrtran.c:725`) run off the 769-entry array from `pngrtran.c:678`. Infinite loop + OOB read (hit it: test hung >3 min).\n- `png_set_quantize` with `maximum_colors < 0` and a histogram — `for (i = num_palette-1; i >= maximum_colors; i--)` (`pngrtran.c:548`) indexes `quantize_sort[-1]`.\n- `png_set_quantize` with `num_palette < 0` or `> 256` — `memcpy(png_ptr->palette, palette, (unsigned)num_palette*3)` (`pngrtran.c:823-824`) into a 256-entry allocation; ~4 GB count when negative.\n- `png_set_user_transform_info` declaring a pixel depth *larger* than the image's — `png_combine_row` then copies `PNG_ROWBYTES(64,width)` bytes out of `png_ptr->row_buf`, of which only the real bytes were written (uninitialised `png_malloc`, `pngrutil.c:4592`); nondeterministic in both.\n- `png_image_finish_read` with an undefined `image->format` (e.g. `0xffffffff`) — the simplified API never validates format bits (`pngread.c:4091-4145` only tests individual flags); corrupts the heap in both (glibc `malloc(): invalid size`).\n- `png_read_png` at height exactly `PNG_UINT_32_MAX/8` (536,870,911, the largest value that *passes* row 604's check) — both then allocate a 4 GiB row-pointer array plus one buffer per row; OOM-aborted the process. Heights above the threshold are tested.\n- Uninitialised sub-byte padding bits of `png_read_png`'s `png_malloc`'d rows are masked out before comparison (same rule as `t05_read.rs`).\n\n## Rows with no observable rejection in this build (documented in the file header, driven through their supported path anyway)\n\n581-587 (all `PNG_READ_*_SUPPORTED` are defined), 596 (`PNG_READ_INTERLACING_SUPPORTED` on — row 595's warning *is* tested), 605-619 (all 14 `png_read_png` \"not supported\" app errors), 729 (`PNG_READ_EXPAND_SUPPORTED` on), 740 (\"Palette is NULL in indexed image\" — `png_set_PLTE` always `png_calloc`s a full 256-entry palette, even for the MNG zero-length PLTE, which is the only way `num_palette == 0` can survive `png_handle_PLTE`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":506,"cache_read_input_tokens":298296,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":506,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01BzwnoYDSYW86hqb9b58PMk","session_id":"e3091878-9949-4689-ad83-c0c41e6641a2","uuid":"f19fe4d7-519f-445e-96d5-0561a67ce1b6","timestamp":"2026-08-31T14:33:12.955Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Error tests: read paths"}
