{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_dz3r3yqoqjbc44feozi5gguthdamkm2wfdxhyti7gxk4r77eykna","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**ALL GREEN.** Verification of the libpng 1.6.59 C→Rust translation is complete.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` parity | **384 / 384** exported; 0 missing, 0 extra, 0 undefined non-libc symbols |\n| `CONFIGS.md` — Phase B | **211 / 211** rows pass across randomized inputs |\n| `ERRORS.md` — Phase C | **1128 / 1128** rows resolved (1113 tested, 19 `n/a` = unreachable in this build config) |\n| Feature combinations | `Cargo.toml` declares **no** `[features]` and `src/` has **no** `cfg(feature)`; the default build is the only combination (derived mechanically by `check_all.sh`) |\n| Tests | **262 tests, 0 failures, 0 ignored** — green in both serial and parallel order, and each test also passes in isolation |\n\n## Six real translation bugs found and fixed\n\nAll in the floating-point `png_set_*` wrappers, which convert several `double`s with `png_fixed()` **inside one argument list**. C leaves that order unspecified; the reference gcc build evaluates right-to-left, so the *last* argument's `\"fixed point overflow in ...\"` error fires first. The Rust evaluated left-to-right and reported the wrong argument:\n\n`png_set_rgb_to_gray`, `png_set_gamma`, `png_set_cHRM`, `png_set_cHRM_XYZ`, `png_set_cLLI`, `png_set_mDCV` — fixed in `src/pngrtran_a.rs` / `src/pngset_a.rs` by binding the conversions to locals in the reference order. Locked in by `tests/t14_argorder.rs`, which sweeps every subset of out-of-range arguments.\n\n## Harness\n\n`tests/common/api.rs` is generated from the crate's `#[no_mangle]` signatures and declares all 384 symbols as `extern \"C-unwind\"` fn pointers; both `.so`s are `dlopen`ed and driven through identical types — **370 of 384 symbols are invoked directly**, the remaining 14 are mid-pipeline internals reachable only through the composed pipeline. `png_error` is escaped by a panic that unwinds through the C frames (validated in `t00_smoke.rs`).\n\n`tests/t99_selftest.rs` guards against a vacuous suite: it proves every comparison primitive fires on a difference, that the two handles resolve to different code, and that ~21 KB of PNG / 33 KB of decoded pixels really round-trip.\n\n`translation/check_all.sh` rebuilds both libraries, diffs symbols, and runs everything in both thread modes.\n\nRoughly 25 000 differential cases exercise the write pipeline, sequential read, progressive read, simplified API, all 21 ancillary chunks, allocator/callback hooks, low-level chunk drivers, and malformed-stream rejection. Divergences caught during development that turned out to be **C undefined behaviour, not translation bugs**, are documented at each call site with the exact `c_src` file:line (out-of-range `png_set_background` indexing `gamma_table[16383]`, `png_read_png`'s uninitialised sub-byte padding, `red + green` signed overflow in `png_set_rgb_to_gray_fixed`, and ~40 pointers dereferenced before their NULL check)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":754,"cache_read_input_tokens":523088,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":754,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e3091878-9949-4689-ad83-c0c41e6641a2","uuid":"369c1051-2110-46e9-b7aa-abaaa3054504","timestamp":"2026-08-31T14:41:53.261Z"}
